      transcript:
        "Want smooth, flawless walls? Here\u2019s how to install drywall like a pro. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn every step to hang, tape, and finish drywall for a perfect paint-ready surface.\n\nFirst, clear your workspace and gather all your materials: drywall sheets, joint compound, screws, tape, and corner bead. Measure your walls or ceiling, mark the studs, and plan your sheet layout to minimize seams.\n\nNext, cut your drywall sheets to fit, making sure to stagger seams for strength. Hang the sheets on the studs using drywall screws, keeping edges tight and aligned.\n\nNow, tape all the seams with paper tape. Cover them with a first coat of joint compound, filling screw holes and corners. Let it dry completely.\n\nApply two more coats of joint compound, feathering the edges wider each time. Sand between coats and after the final coat for a smooth finish.\n\nFinally, inspect your work for any flaws, touch up as needed, and clean up the area. Your walls are now ready for paint or texture!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
