      transcript:
        "Is your heat pump not heating or cooling like it should? Let\u2019s walk through how to repair a heat pump step by step. First, always shut off the power before you start. Inspect the unit for any visible damage, check the thermostat settings, and listen for odd noises or look for error codes. Next, test the main components: check the electrical connections, capacitors, relays, and sensors. If you find a bad capacitor, contactor, or fuse, replace it with a new one. Don\u2019t forget to clean the coils and filters\u2014this helps your system run better. Now, reassemble the panels and turn the power back on. Run the heat pump through both heating and cooling cycles. Make sure the airflow feels strong, the temperature changes as it should, and the system responds to the thermostat. That\u2019s it! If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
