        "Did a storm wreck your roof? Here\u2019s how to fix it fast and right. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the exact steps and materials you need for a storm damage roof repair. \n\nFirst, assess the damage. Walk the roof safely, document all affected spots, and clear away debris. Set up safety gear before you start any work.\n\nNext, protect your home from more water damage. Cover broken areas with tarps or plastic sheeting. Make sure everything is tight and secure, especially if more bad weather is coming.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time for repairs. Remove damaged shingles, underlayment, and any broken flashing. Replace them with new asphalt shingles, roofing felt, nails, and flashing. Don\u2019t forget the drip edge and ice & water shield for extra protection. If the plywood decking is rotten, swap it out for new sheets. Always follow local building codes and manufacturer instructions.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Make sure everything is watertight. Clean up all debris and dispose of waste properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
