      transcript:
        "A burst pipe can flood your home in minutes\u2014do you know how to fix it fast? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair a burst copper pipe and prevent future leaks. \n\nFirst, shut off the main water supply and drain the lines. This stops more water from leaking and lets you work safely. Next, inspect the damaged pipe to see how much needs replacing.\n\nNow, cut out the burst section using a pipe cutter. Clean and dry the area around the break. Get your new copper pipe, couplings, and fittings ready. Use an emery cloth or brush to clean the pipe ends for a solid connection.\n\nFit the new pipe section in place. Apply flux, then solder the joints for a watertight seal. Once everything cools, turn the water back on and check for leaks. If it\u2019s dry, add pipe insulation to help prevent future bursts.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
