      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to swap out a sink trap without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to remove an old sink trap and install a new one, step by step. \n\nFirst, place a bucket under your sink to catch any water. Loosen the slip nuts on both ends of the old trap using channel locks or by hand. Carefully remove the trap and dump out any water. Wipe down the pipe ends so they\u2019re clean and ready for the new parts.\n\nNext, dry-fit your new P-trap kit. Adjust the PVC pipe length if needed, and slide on the slip joint washers and nuts. Make sure everything lines up with the sink drain and the wall pipe. Don\u2019t forget to use Teflon tape or pipe joint compound on the threads for a tight seal.\n\nNow, hand-tighten all the connections. Turn on the faucet and check for leaks. If you see drips, tighten the nuts a bit more. Once it\u2019s leak-free, clean up your workspace and dispose of the old trap properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
