      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to replace your home's air ducts? In this video, you'll learn the exact steps and materials needed for a smooth air duct replacement. \n\nFirst, assess your current ductwork. Spend 2 to 3 hours inspecting the old ducts, measuring each run, and making a list of what you need. Gather flexible ducting, clamps, foil tape, and hangers before you start.\n\nNext, remove the old ducts. This takes about 3 to 4 hours. Carefully disconnect each section, seal off vents to keep dust out of your home, and dispose of the old material according to your local rules.\n\nNow, install the new ducts. Plan for 6 to 7 hours. Fit each section, making sure the ducts are straight and connections are tight. Use duct clamps and foil tape to seal every joint. Hang the ducts securely with straps, following your local building codes.\n\nFinally, test your system. Spend 2 hours checking for airflow and leaks. Make any needed adjustments, then clean up your work area. Confirm everything meets your area's standards.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
