      transcript:
        "Did you know leaky air ducts can waste up to 30% of your heating and cooling? In this video, you'll learn how to seal your air ducts for better comfort and lower energy bills. \n\nFirst, inspect all accessible ductwork for leaks, gaps, or damage. Use duct cleaning supplies to wipe down the surfaces, and clear the area so you can work safely. \n\nNext, seal every joint, seam, and connection with mastic sealant or UL-listed foil tape. Make sure each joint is fully covered\u2014this is where most leaks happen. Let the mastic dry as recommended. \n\nAfter sealing, wrap the ducts with insulation if needed, and secure it with approved fasteners. Double-check for any missed spots and reinforce them. \n\nFinally, turn on your HVAC system to test for leaks and check airflow. Clean up your workspace and dispose of materials properly. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
