      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely replace a GFCI outlet in under an hour? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to swap out a faulty GFCI outlet and make sure it\u2019s working right. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker box for the outlet you\u2019re replacing. Double-check the power is off using a voltage tester. Remove the cover plate and unscrew the old GFCI outlet from the box.\n\nNext, disconnect the wires. Take note of which wires go to the LINE and LOAD terminals\u2014this is important for safety. Connect the wires to the new GFCI outlet, matching the LINE and LOAD positions. Tighten the screws, tuck the wires back in, and secure the new outlet to the box. Attach the new cover plate.\n\nNow, turn the breaker back on. Press the TEST and RESET buttons on the GFCI to make sure it\u2019s working. Plug in a device to confirm the outlet is live and safe.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
