      transcript:
        "Want to know how to install air ducts the right way, step by step? In this video, you'll learn how to plan, install, and seal air ducts for a smooth, energy-efficient HVAC system.\n\nFirst, start with planning and layout. Spend 3 to 4 hours measuring your space, checking HVAC needs, and designing a duct layout that meets local building codes. Good planning saves time and money later.\n\nNext, prepare your materials. Gather flexible and sheet metal ducts, insulation wrap, hangers, elbows, register boots, supply registers, and mastic sealant. Cut your ducts to size and label each section. This takes about 2 to 3 hours.\n\nNow, install the ducts. Over 18 to 20 hours, mount the main trunk lines and branch ducts. Use hangers or straps every few feet to support the ducts. Connect everything to the HVAC unit. Seal all joints and seams with mastic or tape to stop air leaks.\n\nAfter that, insulate and seal. Wrap the ducts with insulation and tape all seams. Make sure every connection is airtight. This step takes 4 to 5 hours and boosts energy efficiency.\n\nFinally, test the system and clean up. Spend 2 to 3 hours checking airflow, looking for leaks, and balancing the system. Clean up debris and make sure everything passes inspection.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
