      transcript:
        "Want to make your trim look brand new without hiring a pro? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to paint trim like a pro, from prep to cleanup. \n\nFirst, gather your supplies: trim paint, painter\u2019s tape, drop cloths, sandpaper, caulk, and a couple of 2 to 2.5-inch brushes. \n\nStart with surface prep. Clean the trim, fill any holes with caulk, sand it smooth, and tape off the walls and floors. This takes about 1 to 2 hours but makes a huge difference.\n\nNext, apply a coat of primer to all the trim. Let it dry fully\u2014this helps the paint stick and last longer. Plan for 1 to 1.5 hours here.\n\nNow, paint your first coat using smooth, even strokes. Take your time for even coverage. This step usually takes about 2 hours.\n\nOnce dry, add a second coat and touch up any missed spots or imperfections. Another 2 hours, but it\u2019s worth it for a flawless finish.\n\nFinally, remove the tape, clean your brushes, and reinstall any hardware. Cleanup takes about 30 minutes, and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
