        "Mold can destroy your home and your health\u2014here\u2019s how to get rid of it for good. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process to safely remove mold and prevent it from coming back.\n\nFirst, prepare the site. Seal off the affected area with 6 mil plastic sheeting and tape. Set up a HEPA air scrubber to create negative air pressure. Always wear N95 respirators, protective coveralls, and nitrile gloves to keep yourself safe.\n\nNext, remove any contaminated materials like drywall or carpet. Scrub all surfaces with a mold remediation cleaner. Use a HEPA vacuum to capture loose spores. Make sure you bag all debris in contractor-grade garbage bags and seal them tight.\n\nNow, dry out the area. Run air movers and dehumidifiers for 8 to 10 hours. Check moisture levels to be sure everything is dry\u2014mold loves moisture.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Look for any missed spots. Apply an antimicrobial treatment to prevent future growth. Fix any leaks or humidity issues to keep mold away for good.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
