      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely install a new circuit breaker in your home? Today, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process to get it done right and safely. \n\nFirst, always start by turning off the main power supply. Double-check with a voltage tester to make sure there\u2019s no electricity flowing. Put on your safety gear before opening the panel.\n\nNext, unscrew and remove the panel cover. Find an open slot that matches your new breaker. Make sure the breaker is compatible with your panel type.\n\nNow, insert the new breaker into the slot. Connect the circuit wires\u2014hot, neutral, and ground\u2014making sure each connection is tight and routed neatly. Use wire connectors and a grounding screw or bar as needed.\n\nOnce everything\u2019s secure, put the panel cover back on. Turn the main power back on and test your new breaker. Make sure it works and meets your local electrical codes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
