        "Is your shower faucet leaking or hard to turn? Let\u2019s fix it fast and save money! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a shower faucet by replacing the cartridge or washers, step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply to your shower. Open the faucet to relieve any pressure. Next, remove the handle and trim to expose the valve. This usually means unscrewing a few screws\u2014keep them safe!\n\nNow, inspect the cartridge or washers inside. If you see wear, corrosion, or mineral buildup, it\u2019s time to replace them. Take the old part to the store to get the right match. Before installing the new cartridge or washers, clean the valve area and apply plumber\u2019s grease to the O-rings. Wrap any threaded parts with Teflon tape for a tight seal.\n\nReassemble the trim and handle. Turn the water back on and test your shower. Check for leaks and make sure everything works smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
