      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to swap out an old toilet without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to remove an old toilet and fit a new one, step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply. Flush the toilet to drain the tank and bowl. Disconnect the water line, then unbolt the toilet from the floor. Carefully lift and remove the old toilet.\n\nNext, clean the flange on the floor. Check for any cracks or damage. Place a new wax ring on the flange to make a watertight seal.\n\nNow, lower your new toilet straight down onto the flange, lining up the bolts. Press down firmly to seat the wax ring. Tighten the mounting bolts, but don\u2019t overtighten. Reconnect the water supply line and turn the water back on. Check for leaks around the base and at the supply line. Finally, run a bead of caulk around the base for a clean finish.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
