      transcript:
        "Tired of noisy neighbors or city sounds invading your apartment? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to soundproof your apartment for peace and quiet. \n\nFirst, assess where the noise is coming from. Spend a few hours checking windows, doors, walls, and floors. Write down the worst spots so you know where to focus.\n\nNext, seal up all the gaps and cracks. Use acoustic caulk and weatherstripping around windows, doors, and baseboards. Fill every visible crack to block airborne noise.\n\nNow, install your soundproofing materials. Mount acoustic insulation batts inside walls, add resilient channels, and use soundproof drywall. Lay down thick rugs or carpets to help with floor noise. For extra protection, use door sweeps and window inserts.\n\nUpgrade your fixtures. Swap out hollow-core doors for solid-core ones. Hang heavy curtains or blinds, and consider adding bookshelves or another layer of drywall for even better sound isolation.\n\nFinally, test your results. Listen for any leftover noise and make adjustments as needed. Add more treatments if you have to until you get the quiet you want.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
