        "Want to install PEX pipe like a pro and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to install PEX piping for your next plumbing project. \n\nFirst, measure your pipe runs and mark where each fixture will go. Gather your materials: PEX pipe, fittings, crimp rings, a manifold, insulation, and pipe hangers. \n\nNext, cut your PEX pipe to the right lengths. Lay out the pipes along your planned routes, making sure to follow local plumbing codes for spacing and support. \n\nNow, connect your PEX fittings using crimp or clamp rings. Secure the pipes to the framing with hangers or clamps. Be careful to avoid sharp bends or kinks in the pipe. \n\nOnce everything is connected, it's time to pressure test the system. Pressurize the pipes, check every joint for leaks, and fix any issues you find. \n\nFinally, inspect your work. Label all pipes, clean up debris, and dispose of waste properly. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
