        "Want to make your tile floors last longer and look brand new? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to seal your tile and grout the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: tile sealer, applicator pads, painter\u2019s tape, and a good cleaning solution. You\u2019ll need about one gallon of sealer for every 100 square feet.\n\nStart by cleaning your tile and grout. Use a cleaning solution to scrub away dirt and debris. Let everything dry completely\u2014this is key for a good seal.\n\nNext, use painter\u2019s tape to protect any edges you don\u2019t want sealed. Pour some sealer into a tray. Using an applicator pad, brush, or roller, apply the sealer evenly over the tiles and grout. Make sure you cover every line and surface. Wipe away any extra sealer as you go, following the product\u2019s directions.\n\nLet the sealer dry for at least an hour, or as the manufacturer recommends. Once dry, inspect your work. Touch up any missed spots for a perfect finish.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
