      transcript:
        "Did you know a faulty pressure relief valve can turn your water heater into a ticking time bomb? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely replace a water heater pressure relief valve in just a few steps. \n\nFirst, turn off the water supply and shut off power or gas to your water heater. Let it cool down\u2014safety first! Next, attach a hose to the drain valve and drain water until it\u2019s below the relief valve level. This prevents spills. Use a wrench to carefully remove the old pressure relief valve.\n\nNow, wrap the threads of your new T&P valve with plumber\u2019s tape. Screw it in and tighten it securely. Reconnect the discharge pipe if needed. Turn the water and power back on. Check for leaks and make sure the new valve works by lifting the test lever\u2014water should flow out and stop when you release it.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
