        "Want to make your yard shine at night? Here\u2019s how to install landscape lighting like a pro.\n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to plan, wire, and install low-voltage landscape lights step by step.\n\nFirst, walk your outdoor space and decide where you want lights for safety and style. Mark each spot with a flag or stake. Choose low-voltage fixtures\u2014about 10 is a good start\u2014and make sure you have a transformer, 12/2 gauge wire, wire connectors, and ground stakes.\n\nNext, lay out your low-voltage wire along the planned route. Connect the wire to your transformer, but don\u2019t plug it in yet. Place each fixture at your marked spots and attach them to the wire using waterproof connectors. Secure each fixture with a ground stake.\n\nNow, connect the transformer to power and test each light. Adjust the angles so they highlight your plants or pathways. Double-check that all connections are tight and weatherproof.\n\nFinally, bury the wire a few inches underground, tidy up the area, and set your timer or smart controls. Walk around at night to make sure everything looks great and works right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
