      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to replace a toilet drain without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to do it step by step, so you can save money and avoid leaks. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply to your toilet. Flush to drain the tank, then disconnect the water line. Remove the toilet and set it aside to expose the drain opening. Make sure you have gloves, safety glasses, and all your tools ready.\n\nNext, check the drain pipe for any blockages or damage. Use a drain snake or auger to clear out any clogs. Clean the pipe thoroughly so your new drain parts fit tight and leak-free.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to reinstall. Place a new wax ring on the flange. Carefully set the toilet back in place, lining up the bolts. Press down to seal the wax ring. Reconnect the water supply, turn it on, and flush a few times to check for leaks. Tighten bolts if needed, and clean up your work area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
