      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely add more power to your home or shop? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a subpanel step by step, so you can expand your electrical system with confidence.\n\nFirst, plan your project. Pick the right spot for your subpanel, figure out your power needs, and get any permits required. Before you touch anything, shut off the main power for safety.\n\nNext, mount the subpanel securely on the wall. Run your feeder cable\u2014usually 6-gauge copper\u2014from the main panel to the subpanel. Install a grounding bar kit, and connect your ground and neutral wires as required by code. Label each circuit clearly to avoid confusion later.\n\nNow, install your breakers. For most homes, you\u2019ll use a mix of 15 and 20 amp breakers. Connect your branch circuits using 12-gauge copper wire. Make sure all connections are tight and wires are neat.\n\nFinally, schedule an inspection with your local authority. Fix any issues they find, then restore power. Test every circuit to make sure everything works as it should.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
