      transcript:
        "Is your hot water heater not working right? Let\u2019s fix it fast and safe. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a hot water heater step by step, from shut-off to testing. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at the breaker and close the cold water valve. Safety first\u2014never skip this step. Next, hook up a hose to the drain valve and empty the tank. Check for leaks, rust, or broken parts. Look closely at the heating elements and thermostat.\n\nNow, replace any bad parts. This could be the heating element, thermostat, or the T&P relief valve. Use plumber\u2019s tape on threads and tighten all connections. Make sure everything meets your local safety codes.\n\nWhen done, close the drain, refill the tank, and turn the power back on. Watch for leaks and make sure the heater works right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
