      transcript:
        "Want safe, reliable power outside? Here\u2019s how to install a weatherproof outdoor outlet in just a few steps. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to plan, wire, and mount a GFCI outdoor outlet that stands up to the weather.\n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker box. Safety first! Gather your tools and materials: a weatherproof GFCI outlet, outdoor-rated electrical box, cover, 12/2 UF-B wire, connectors, mounting hardware, and caulk.\n\nPick a spot on your exterior wall close to an existing indoor circuit. Mark and cut an opening for the new box. Mount the weatherproof box securely to the wall.\n\nNext, run the outdoor-rated wire from your indoor power source to the new box. Make sure the wire is rated for outdoor use and follow local code.\n\nConnect the wires to the GFCI outlet: black to brass, white to silver, ground to green. Secure the outlet in the box and attach the weatherproof cover. Seal around the box with caulk to keep out moisture.\n\nTurn the power back on and test your new outlet. It should trip and reset properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
