      transcript:
        "Want smooth, flawless walls? Drywall taping is the secret pros use for perfect finishes. \n\nIn this video, you'll learn how to tape drywall like a pro, step by step.\n\nFirst, prep your surface. Clean all drywall seams, wipe away dust, and make sure every screw is set just below the surface. Gather your joint compound, drywall tape, corner bead, and sanding sponges.\n\nNext, apply a thin layer of joint compound to each seam. Press drywall tape into the wet compound, then smooth out any extra with your taping knife. Don\u2019t forget to cover screw holes and corners too.\n\nOnce dry, add a second and third coat of joint compound. Each time, feather the edges wider for a seamless look. Let each coat dry fully before adding the next.\n\nFinally, sand all joints until smooth. Check for any bumps or gaps and touch up as needed. Clean up the dust, and your walls are ready for paint.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
