      transcript:
        "Want to upgrade your floors without glue or nails? Watch how to install a floating floor step by step! In this video, you'll learn how to prep, lay, and finish a floating floor like a pro.\n\nFirst, clear out all furniture and clean the subfloor. Make sure the surface is flat and dry. Fix any bumps or holes\u2014this is key for a smooth floor.\n\nNext, roll out your underlayment. Cut it to fit the room and tape the seams. This layer helps with moisture and sound.\n\nNow, start laying your floor planks along the longest wall. Use spacers to leave a small gap at the edges for expansion. Stagger the joints so the seams don\u2019t line up. Click or lock each plank together tightly as you go.\n\nOnce the floor is down, add your trim or quarter round to cover the gaps. Remove the spacers, check for any uneven spots, and clean up. Move your furniture back in and enjoy your new floor!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
