      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a leaking water line without calling a pro? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair a damaged water line safely and efficiently.\n\nFirst, shut off the main water supply and drain the lines. Find the exact spot where the pipe is leaking.\n\nNext, remove any wall, floor, or ground coverings to expose the damaged pipe. Check how much pipe needs replacing.\n\nNow, use a pipe cutter to remove the bad section. Measure and cut a new piece of 3/4\" PEX pipe. Attach brass couplings to both ends, and use Teflon tape on threaded connections. Secure everything tightly, following local plumbing codes. Add a new ball valve if needed, and use pipe hangers or clamps to support the line. Slide on pipe insulation to protect against temperature changes.\n\nTurn the water back on and check every joint for leaks. Make sure water flows smoothly.\n\nFinally, patch up any walls or floors you opened, clean up the area, and dispose of old materials properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
