        "Want to make your bathroom look brand new with just a few hours of work? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to paint your bathroom like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, prep your space. Remove any fixtures, cover the floor with drop cloths, and clean the walls. Fill holes or cracks with spackling compound, then sand smooth. Use caulk to seal any gaps. This takes about an hour.\n\nNext, tape off trim, edges, and fixtures with painter\u2019s tape. Apply a quality primer to all surfaces. This helps the paint stick and protects against moisture. Give yourself another hour for this step.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to paint. Use a roller kit for large areas and brushes for corners. Apply at least two coats of bathroom-grade paint to the walls and ceiling. Let each coat dry fully before adding the next. This part takes about two hours.\n\nFinally, remove the tape, reinstall fixtures, and clean up your supplies. Make sure the room is well-ventilated so the paint dries properly. That\u2019s it!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
