      transcript:
        "Want to make your old window frames look brand new? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to paint window frames like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, gather your supplies: exterior paint, primer, painter\u2019s tape, a drop cloth, sandpaper, and a good paint brush. You\u2019ll need about two hours per window.\n\nStart with surface preparation. Lay down your drop cloth to protect the floor. Clean the window frames with a damp cloth to remove dust and dirt. Use sandpaper to lightly sand the surface\u2014this helps the paint stick better.\n\nNext, apply painter\u2019s tape around the glass and any areas you don\u2019t want painted. If you see bare wood or repaired spots, brush on a coat of primer. Let it dry for a few minutes.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to paint. Use your brush to apply paint evenly along the frame. Don\u2019t overload the brush\u2014thin coats look better and dry faster. Let the paint dry, then carefully peel off the tape for a crisp, clean edge.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your window frames are refreshed and protected. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
