      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to get rid of that outdated popcorn ceiling without making a huge mess? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to safely and efficiently remove a popcorn ceiling and leave your room looking fresh. \n\nFirst, prep your space. Move out all furniture, cover floors and walls with plastic sheeting, and use painter\u2019s tape to seal the edges. Turn off power to any ceiling fixtures for safety.\n\nNext, fill a pump sprayer with water and lightly mist the ceiling. Let it soak for about 15 minutes\u2014this softens the texture. Then, use a wide scraper to gently remove the popcorn. Work in small sections and collect debris as you go.\n\nAfter scraping, check for any gouges or rough spots. Patch these with joint compound, let it dry, then sand the ceiling smooth using 120-150 grit sandpaper.\n\nNow, apply a stain-blocking primer to seal the surface. Once dry, finish with two coats of ceiling paint for a clean, modern look.\n\nDon\u2019t forget to wear a dust mask throughout the process for safety.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
