      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/mold-treatment/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Mold can destroy your home and your health\u2014here\u2019s how to get rid of it for good. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn the exact steps and materials you need to safely treat mold in any room.\n\nFirst, assess the area. Inspect every corner for mold and find the source of moisture. Gather your gear: N95 respirators, gloves, goggles, and mold cleaner. Seal off the work area with plastic sheeting to keep spores from spreading.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time for removal. Scrub all non-porous surfaces with mold remediation cleaner and a stiff brush. For porous materials like drywall or carpet, remove and bag them in heavy-duty trash bags\u2014they can\u2019t be saved. Use a HEPA vacuum on all surfaces to catch any loose spores.\n\nNow, dry out the area. Set up fans and dehumidifiers for at least two hours. Good airflow is key to stopping mold from coming back.\n\nFinally, prevent future problems. Apply a mold-resistant treatment, fix any leaks, and do a final inspection to make sure all mold is gone.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
