        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/irrigation-system-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your lawn full of dry spots or puddles? Let\u2019s fix your irrigation system fast! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to inspect, repair, and test your irrigation system step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the water supply. Walk each irrigation zone and look for leaks, broken sprinkler heads, or faulty valves. Write down every issue you find.\n\nNext, replace any damaged sprinkler heads and swap out bad valves. Use the right PVC pipe, couplings, and solvent cement for your system. If you spot a broken pipe, dig carefully to expose it. Cut out the damaged section, clean the ends, and glue in a new piece with couplings. Don\u2019t forget to use thread sealant tape on threaded parts.\n\nOnce repairs are done, flush the lines to clear debris. Make sure all connections are tight and watertight.\n\nFinally, turn the water back on. Test each zone, adjust spray patterns, and check for leaks or low pressure. Your system should now cover every area evenly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
