      transcript:
        "Want to give your walls a bold new look? Textured wall painting is easier than you think! In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to create a stunning textured finish, from prep to cleanup.\n\nFirst, get your materials ready: textured paint, primer, joint compound, painter\u2019s tape, drop cloths, and texture tools like rollers or trowels. For a 500 square foot room, you\u2019ll need about 6 gallons of textured paint, 3 gallons of primer, and 4 gallons of joint compound.\n\nStart with surface preparation. Clean your walls, patch any holes, and sand rough spots. Protect your floors and trim with drop cloths and painter\u2019s tape. This takes about 2 to 3 hours.\n\nNext, mix your joint compound. Apply it to the walls with a trowel or roller. Use your tools to create the texture pattern you want. Let it dry completely\u2014this step takes 4 to 6 hours.\n\nOnce dry, prime the textured surface. After the primer dries, paint the walls with your textured paint. Use a roller or brush for even coverage. This part takes 3 to 4 hours.\n\nFinally, let the paint cure for about 12 hours. Remove all tape and drop cloths, and clean your tools. Step back and enjoy your new textured walls!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
