        "Want to give your walls a pro-level finish with sheetrock texturing? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to texture sheetrock like a pro, from prep to cleanup. \n\nFirst, prep your surface. Clean the sheetrock, fix any dents or holes, and sand the joints smooth. Wipe away all dust\u2014this helps the texture stick evenly.\n\nNext, protect your space. Use plastic sheeting and painter\u2019s tape to cover floors, windows, and fixtures. This keeps everything clean from overspray.\n\nNow, mix your texture. Use premixed joint compound and add texture additive if needed. Mix until you get a thick, creamy consistency. Test your spray or hand pattern on scrap drywall to make sure you like the look.\n\nTime to apply! Use a sprayer or hand tools to spread the texture evenly, working in sections. Keep your pattern consistent for a pro finish.\n\nLet it dry for at least 6 hours. Once dry, carefully remove all masking and clean up your tools and space.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
