      transcript:
        "Did you know a hidden slab leak can destroy your home\u2019s foundation if left unchecked? In this video, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to find and fix a slab leak, step by step. \n\nFirst, use electronic leak detection tools or a dye test kit to pinpoint the leak under your slab. This usually takes 2 to 3 hours. Once you find the leak, clear the area\u2014move furniture, cover surfaces, and carefully cut through flooring and concrete to reach the pipe. This prep work takes about 3 to 4 hours.\n\nNext, remove the damaged copper pipe. Replace it with new Type L copper pipe and secure it with proper fittings. Make sure all connections are tight and meet local plumbing codes. This repair step can take 6 to 8 hours.\n\nAfter the pipe is fixed, backfill the hole, patch the concrete, and restore the flooring. Turn the water back on and check for leaks and water pressure. This final step takes about 3 hours.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
