      transcript:
        "Want to know what it really takes to install a central air conditioning unit? In this video, I\u2019ll walk you through every step, from prep to final inspection, so you can tackle the job with confidence. \n\nFirst, start with a site assessment. Check your existing ductwork, electrical supply, and make sure you have enough space. Clear the area and confirm you\u2019re following local building codes.\n\nNext, place and mount the units. Set the indoor air handler and the outdoor condenser in their spots. Use mounting brackets and vibration pads to keep things steady and quiet.\n\nNow, connect the ductwork and electrical. Attach new or existing ducts, run your copper refrigerant lines, and wire up the system. Seal and insulate all connections to keep your system efficient.\n\nAfter that, charge and test the system. Add the right amount of R410A refrigerant, check for leaks, and calibrate the thermostat. Make sure you have good airflow and cooling in every room.\n\nFinally, do a full inspection and cleanup. Double-check everything meets code, show the homeowner how it works, and clean up all debris. Dispose of packaging the right way.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
