      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a clogged drain fast, without calling a plumber? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to clear a blocked drain and get your sink or tub flowing again. \n\nFirst, check the drain. Look for standing water or slow drainage. Clear the area around the fixture and grab your tools: a plunger, drain snake, drain cleaner, gloves, and maybe a replacement P-trap.\n\nStart with the plunger. Place it over the drain and push up and down firmly for about 30 seconds. If that doesn't work, try a handheld drain snake. Feed it into the drain, twist, and pull out any debris. If you see hair or gunk, remove it by hand\u2014wear gloves!\n\nStill clogged? Use an enzyme or chemical drain cleaner, following the label instructions. Let it sit, then flush with hot water. If the clog is stubborn, you may need to remove the P-trap under the sink. Place a bucket underneath, unscrew the trap, and clean it out. Reinstall it with plumber\u2019s putty or Teflon tape for a tight seal.\n\nFinally, run water for several minutes to make sure the drain is clear. Clean up your tools and sanitize the area. Dispose of debris according to your local rules.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
