      transcript:
        "Want cleaner water for your whole home in just a few hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace a whole house water filter, step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off your main water supply. Open a faucet to relieve pressure, and put towels or a bucket under the filter housing to catch any water. \n\nNext, use the filter wrench to unscrew the housing. Take out the old filter. Clean the inside of the housing and the O-ring with warm, soapy water. Make sure the O-ring is in good shape and seated properly\u2014this stops leaks. \n\nNow, insert the new filter cartridge. Lightly lubricate the O-ring with food-grade silicone grease. Screw the housing back on, hand-tighten, and don\u2019t overdo it. \n\nSlowly turn the water supply back on. Check for leaks around the housing. Open a few faucets to flush the system for a few minutes, as recommended by your filter\u2019s instructions. \n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve got fresh, filtered water for your whole house. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
