      transcript:
        "Want to paint your bedroom like a pro, without the mess or stress? In this video, I\u2019ll show you every step to paint a 12x12 bedroom, from prep to cleanup. \n\nFirst, move all furniture away from the walls. Cover your floors and furniture with drop cloths. Use painter\u2019s tape to protect trim, outlets, and windows. This keeps paint only where you want it.\n\nNext, clean the walls to remove dust and stains. Fill any holes or cracks with spackling compound. Once dry, sand the spots smooth. Make sure the walls are dry before you start painting.\n\nIf you patched or have stains, apply primer to those areas. Then, use an angled brush to cut in along the edges, corners, and trim. This gives you sharp, clean lines.\n\nNow, grab your roller and paint tray. Roll paint onto the walls in sections. Let it dry, then add a second coat if needed for full coverage.\n\nWhen you\u2019re done, carefully remove the tape. Clean your brushes and rollers. Throw away the drop cloths if they\u2019re disposable. Move your furniture back once the paint is dry.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
