      name: "Building Demolition: Step-by-Step Guide & Cost Breakdown",
      description:
        "Calculate materials & costs to building demolition at https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/building-demolition/national-average\n\nThinking about tearing down a building? This video walks you through the entire building demolition process, from site assessment and permits to debris removal and final cleanup. Learn what materials you'll need\u2014like dumpsters, dust control, PPE, and fencing\u2014and get a clear idea of the labor and time involved for a 2,000 sq ft building. We break down each step so you know exactly what to expect, whether you're a contractor or a homeowner. Have questions or want more tips? Drop a comment below! Like and follow for more construction guides, and check out Contractor Plus for the best tools to run your contracting business.",
      thumbnailUrl:
        "https://contractor-plus-website.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/og-images/b6eb09e9-20b8-48d3-93f0-1804621c6d57.jpg",
      uploadDate: "2025-08-04",
      duration: "PT2M1S",
      contentUrl:
        "https://contractor-plus-website.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/reshub-how-to-vids/building-demolition.mp4",
      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/building-demolition/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to safely demolish a building? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process and what materials you'll need to get the job done right. \n\nFirst, start with a site assessment. Inspect the building, look for hazardous materials like asbestos, and get all the permits you need from your local authorities. This usually takes about 8 to 12 hours.\n\nNext, disconnect all utilities\u2014water, gas, and electricity. Put up temporary fencing and safety signs to keep the site secure. This step takes 6 to 8 hours.\n\nNow, remove anything salvageable and handle hazardous materials safely, following your area's environmental rules. This can take 16 to 20 hours.\n\nFor the main event\u2014structural demolition\u2014use the right machines and manual tools to bring down the building in a controlled way. This is the longest step, taking 60 to 70 hours.\n\nFinally, sort and load the debris into demolition dumpsters, clean up the site, and make sure it's ready for whatever comes next. This last step takes about 10 to 12 hours.\n\nYou'll need materials like two 30-yard dumpsters, plastic sheeting for dust control, heavy-duty contractor bags, PPE for your crew, and temporary fencing.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
