        "Thinking about installing a gas stove but worried about safety and cost? In this video, you'll learn exactly how to install a gas stove step by step, safely and efficiently.\n\nFirst, get your materials ready: a gas stove, flexible gas connector, shutoff valve, pipe fittings with sealant, and a range cord if your stove has electric ignition.\n\nStart with site preparation. Shut off the gas supply and unplug any electrical connections. Clear the area where you'll install the stove. Make sure the space is well-ventilated and double-check for any gas leaks before you begin.\n\nNext, place your stove in position. Connect the gas line using approved fittings and sealant. Install the shutoff valve if you don\u2019t have one already. Secure the stove as the manufacturer recommends. Always follow your local safety codes for gas connections.\n\nNow, turn the gas supply back on. Use a soapy water solution to check every connection for leaks\u2014look for bubbles. Test each burner to make sure they ignite and the flames look right. Once everything works, clean up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
