      transcript:
        "Want to fix your yard\u2019s drainage and get a smooth, level lawn? Here\u2019s how to grade your landscape the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process for landscape grading, from planning to finishing touches.\n\nFirst, assess your site. Walk the area, spot drainage problems, and mark high and low spots. Make a grading plan that follows local rules and directs water away from your house.\n\nNext, clear the area. Remove rocks, plants, and debris. Set up stakes and string lines to mark your new grade levels.\n\nNow, start excavation. Use a shovel or equipment to cut down high spots and fill in low ones. Always slope the ground away from buildings\u2014aim for at least a 2% slope for drainage.\n\nAfter shaping, compact the soil in layers. This stops future settling. Then, do a fine grade for a smooth finish. Double-check your slopes with a level or string.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Make sure it meets local codes and your plan. Clean up the site and get ready for sod, seed, or more landscaping.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
