      transcript:
        "Want to make your old cabinets look brand new without replacing them? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to refinish your cabinets like a pro. \n\nFirst, remove all hardware, doors, and drawers. Set them aside and label them if needed. Clean every surface with a strong degreaser to get rid of grease and grime\u2014this is key for a smooth finish.\n\nNext, sand all cabinet frames, doors, and drawers. Use assorted grit sandpaper to remove the old finish and smooth out any rough spots. Fill any holes or cracks with wood filler, then sand again for a flawless surface.\n\nNow, tape off areas you don\u2019t want painted and lay down drop cloths. Apply a quality primer to all surfaces. Let it dry completely. Then, use a brush or roller to apply your cabinet paint or stain in thin, even coats. Let each coat dry before adding another. Finish with a topcoat or sealer for durability.\n\nOnce everything is dry, reattach the hardware, doors, and drawers. Inspect your work for any touch-ups, and clean up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
