      transcript:
        "Is your tankless water heater leaving you in the cold? In this video, you'll learn how to repair a tankless water heater step by step, from diagnosis to testing. \n\nFirst, turn off the power and water supply to your unit. Safety comes first! Check the heater for error codes, leaks, or any visible damage. This helps you spot the real problem fast.\n\nNext, remove and clean the inlet filters. Use a descaling solution to flush out the heat exchanger\u2014this keeps your heater running smooth. Check the ignition and temperature sensors. If you find a faulty heating element, temperature sensor, or pressure relief valve, replace them with new parts. Use Teflon tape on all pipe fittings to prevent leaks.\n\nOnce repairs are done, reconnect the water and power. Purge any air from the lines. Turn on the heater and test for steady hot water. Check for leaks and make sure everything works as it should.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
