      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to remodel your basement from start to finish? In this video, you'll learn the exact steps, materials, and time needed to transform your basement into a beautiful, livable space. \n\nFirst, start with planning and design. Spend 30 to 40 hours assessing your basement, deciding how you want to use the space, drawing up plans, and getting the right permits for your area.\n\nNext, move to framing and utilities. Over 60 to 80 hours, frame new walls with about 600 board feet of lumber, add 1,000 square feet of R-13 insulation, and rough-in all electrical, plumbing, and HVAC. Make sure everything meets your local codes.\n\nThen, it's drywall and finishing. Hang 60 sheets of drywall, use 5 pounds of screws, tape, mud, sand, and then paint with about 8 gallons. Install 3 interior doors, hardware, and 250 feet of baseboard trim. This stage takes 80 to 100 hours.\n\nAfter that, install flooring and fixtures. Lay 800 square feet of laminate flooring with underlayment, set up 10 recessed lights, 12 outlets and switches, and finish with ceiling tiles and grid kits. This step takes 40 to 60 hours.\n\nFinally, schedule your inspection, fix any issues, and do a deep clean. This last step takes 20 to 30 hours. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
