      transcript:
        "Want to hang your curtains straight and strong the first time? In this video, you'll learn how to install a curtain rod like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, measure the width of your window. Decide how high and wide you want your rod, then use a level and pencil to mark where the brackets will go on the wall. Double-check your marks\u2014they need to be even!\n\nNext, drill pilot holes at your marks. If you\u2019re not hitting a stud, insert wall anchors to keep the brackets secure. Screw the brackets into place, making sure they\u2019re tight and level.\n\nNow, assemble your curtain rod and slide on your curtain panels. Place the rod onto the brackets. Adjust the curtains so they hang evenly and cover the window just right.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve installed a curtain rod that\u2019s ready for daily use. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
