      transcript:
        "Want to turn your roof into a living, green space? Watch this to learn how to install a green roof step by step.\n\nToday, I\u2019ll show you how to build a green roof, from prep to planting, so you can boost your home\u2019s value and help the environment.\n\nFirst, check your roof\u2019s structure. Make sure it can handle the extra weight. Clear off any debris and fix damage. Next, install a root barrier and waterproof membrane. This protects your building from leaks and roots.\n\nNow, lay down the drainage layer. This keeps water flowing and stops soil from washing away. Add filter fabric on top to keep the soil in place.\n\nSpread a lightweight growing medium evenly across the roof. Use about 25 cubic feet for every 100 square feet. Then, plant your vegetation mats or plants. Pick plants that fit your local climate. Water them well to help them settle in.\n\nInstall an irrigation system if your climate needs it. Secure edge restraints around the roof to keep soil and plants in place.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Check for leaks, drainage, and healthy plants. Set up a maintenance plan to keep your green roof thriving.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
