      transcript:
        "Want to make sure your tile project never leaks? Here\u2019s how to waterproof tiles like a pro. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the exact steps and materials you need to keep water out for good. \n\nFirst, prep your surface. Clean and dry all tile areas. Remove dust, debris, and fix any cracks or holes. This helps the waterproofing stick. \n\nNext, tape off edges with masking tape. Apply a primer to the tiles and let it dry. Now, roll or brush on a liquid waterproofing membrane. Cover every tile and grout line. For extra strength, press polyester reinforcing fabric into corners and joints while the membrane is wet. Add a second coat if the manufacturer says so. \n\nSeal all joints and edges with a waterproof sealant. Let everything cure for at least 6 hours. When dry, inspect for missed spots and touch up as needed. \n\nThat\u2019s it! Your tiles are now protected from water damage. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
