      transcript:
        "Want to give your staircase a fresh new look without hiring a pro? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to paint your staircase step by step, from prep to finish. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: interior paint, primer, painter\u2019s tape, drop cloths, sandpaper, paint brushes or rollers, and wood filler. You\u2019ll need about two gallons of paint and one gallon of primer for a standard staircase.\n\nStart with surface preparation. Clean the stairs, sand any rough spots, and fill holes or cracks with wood filler. Once dry, sand smooth. Lay down drop cloths and use painter\u2019s tape to protect areas you don\u2019t want painted.\n\nNext, apply a coat of primer to all stair surfaces. Let it dry completely\u2014this helps the paint stick and last longer.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to paint. Use a brush for edges and a roller for flat surfaces. Apply the first coat, let it dry, then add a second coat for even coverage. Choose a durable paint made for high-traffic areas.\n\nFinally, remove the tape, touch up any missed spots, and let the paint cure fully before using the stairs.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
