      transcript:
        "Want to make your old hardwood floors look brand new? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to sand and refinish hardwood floors like a pro. \n\nFirst, clear the room. Move out all furniture, rugs, and baseboards. Seal off doors and vents with plastic sheeting to keep dust contained.\n\nNext, start sanding. Use a drum sander with coarse-grit sandpaper to strip away the old finish and smooth out rough spots. Always sand along the wood grain. Vacuum up dust as you go.\n\nNow, tackle the edges and corners. Use an edge sander or hand sander with medium-grit paper. Make sure every spot is smooth and level.\n\nSwitch to fine-grit sandpaper for the final sanding. This gives you a silky finish. Vacuum and wipe down every surface with tack cloths to remove all dust.\n\nFinally, apply your floor finish. Use a brush or roller for an even coat. Let it dry fully and keep the area well-ventilated.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
