      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how easy it is to swap out a door knob yourself? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to remove an old door knob and install a new one, all in under 30 minutes. \n\nFirst, grab your new door knob set, strike plate, and mounting screws. You\u2019ll also need a screwdriver. \n\nStep one: Remove the old door knob. Unscrew both sides and gently pull them off. Don\u2019t forget to take out the latch and keep all the old hardware if you want to reuse or recycle it.\n\nStep two: Install the new latch. Slide it into the edge of the door and secure it with the screws provided. Next, line up both sides of the new knob, making sure the spindle fits through the latch. Tighten the screws until the knob feels secure.\n\nStep three: Test your work. Turn the knob and check that the latch moves smoothly and lines up with the strike plate. If it sticks, adjust the screws or reposition the plate until everything works perfectly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
