      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to patch drywall so well no one can spot the repair? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to patch drywall like a pro, from prep to a paint-ready finish. \n\nFirst, clear the area and remove any loose debris. Use a utility knife to square off the damaged section\u2014this helps your patch fit better. Clean the area so the new material sticks well.\n\nNext, place a drywall patch or mesh tape over the hole or crack. Spread joint compound smoothly over the patch, feathering the edges so it blends into the wall. Let the first coat dry completely\u2014this usually takes about an hour.\n\nOnce dry, sand the area until it's smooth. If needed, add a second coat of joint compound and sand again after it dries. Wipe away all dust so the surface is clean and ready for primer and paint.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
