      transcript:
        "Thinking about a new roof? Here\u2019s what it really takes to install one the right way. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process for a professional roof installation, including what materials you need and how long each step takes.\n\nFirst, clear the work area and protect your landscaping. Make sure all your roofing materials\u2014like asphalt shingles, underlayment, nails, drip edge, and vents\u2014are delivered and ready. Double-check you have the right tools and safety gear.\n\nNext, remove the old roof. Strip off the shingles, underlayment, and flashing. Inspect the roof decking for any damage. If you find rot or soft spots, repair them before moving on.\n\nNow, install the underlayment and flashing. Roll out the roofing felt, add ice and water shield where needed, and secure the drip edge along the roof\u2019s edges. Install flashing around chimneys, vents, and valleys to prevent leaks.\n\nTime for shingles. Start at the bottom edge, using starter strips, and work your way up. Nail each shingle according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions. Don\u2019t forget ridge cap shingles and roof vents for proper airflow.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Make sure everything is secure and meets local codes. Clean up all debris and check the gutters. Dispose of old materials properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
