      transcript:
        "Want to make your home's siding look brand new? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to paint your siding like a pro, from prep to cleanup. \n\nFirst, start with surface preparation. Clean the siding well, scrape off any loose paint, sand rough spots, and repair damaged areas. This takes about 6 to 8 hours but is key for a smooth finish.\n\nNext, mask off windows, doors, and landscaping with painter\u2019s tape and drop cloths. Then, apply primer to any bare wood or patched spots. This step takes 4 to 6 hours and helps the paint stick better.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to paint. Use high-quality exterior paint with brushes, rollers, or a sprayer. Work from top to bottom and make sure every spot is covered. This will take 12 to 14 hours for 1,000 square feet.\n\nAfter painting, check for missed spots. Add a second coat if needed and touch up trim or edges. This detailing takes 2 to 3 hours.\n\nFinally, remove all masking, clean your tools, and throw away debris. Do a final inspection to make sure everything looks great. Cleanup takes 1 to 2 hours.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
