        "Want to give your kitchen a fresh new look without breaking the bank? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to paint your kitchen cabinets step by step, so you get a pro finish every time.\n\nFirst, remove all cabinet doors, drawers, and hardware. Label each piece and store them safely, so reassembly is a breeze.\n\nNext, clean every surface with a degreaser to get rid of grease and grime. Then, sand the doors, drawers, and frames. This helps the paint stick and gives you a smooth finish.\n\nNow, tape off areas you don\u2019t want painted and lay down drop cloths. Apply a bonding, stain-blocking primer to all cabinet surfaces. Let it dry completely.\n\nTime to paint! Use high-quality acrylic or alkyd paint. Apply thin, even coats with a brush or roller. Let each coat dry before adding the next. Two coats usually do the trick.\n\nOnce dry, reattach the hardware, reinstall the doors and drawers, and clean up your workspace. Check for any touch-ups needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
