      transcript:
        "Did you know hail can destroy your roof in just minutes? In this video, you'll learn how to repair hail damage on your roof, step by step, and what materials you'll need. \n\nFirst, inspect your entire roof for dents, cracks, or missing shingles. Take photos and note every spot that needs repair. Next, buy the right materials: asphalt shingles, roofing felt, nails, sealant, drip edge, ice & water shield, and plywood for any decking repairs. Make sure your new shingles match your old ones.\n\nSet up your safety gear and tools. Carefully remove all damaged shingles and underlayment, but don't disturb the good areas. If you find soft spots, replace the decking underneath. Now, install new underlayment and shingles, following the pattern of your existing roof. Secure the drip edge and flashing, and use roofing sealant on all seams and nail heads. Double-check that everything meets local building codes.\n\nFinish with a final inspection. Make sure all repairs are watertight, then clean up debris and leftover materials.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
