        "Want to make your rooms look sharp with perfect trim? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to install trim like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, measure every wall, window, and door where you\u2019ll add trim. Mark your trim pieces and use a miter saw to cut each one to the right length and angle. This takes about 3 to 4 hours for a standard room.\n\nNext, dry fit each piece against the wall. Check the fit, make any small adjustments, and label each piece so you know where it goes. This step helps you avoid mistakes during installation.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install. Use finishing nails or a nail gun to attach the trim to the wall. Make sure your joints are tight and everything is level. Fill nail holes and seams with wood filler for a smooth look. This part usually takes 5 to 6 hours.\n\nFinally, caulk along the edges where the trim meets the wall. Let it dry, then sand and paint or stain your trim for a clean, finished appearance.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
