      transcript:
        "Did you know a simple cleaning can double your tankless water heater\u2019s life? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to maintain your tankless water heater step by step, so you save money and avoid cold showers. \n\nFirst, turn off the power and close the water valves to your heater. This keeps you safe while you work. Next, remove the cold water inlet filter. Rinse it under running water to clear out any debris. Now, grab your hose kit and connect it to the service valves. Place one hose in a bucket with descaling solution, and the other in an empty bucket. Use a small pump to circulate the solution through the heater for about 45 minutes to break down mineral buildup.\n\nAfter flushing, disconnect the hoses and run clean water through the system for a few minutes to rinse out any leftover solution. Check all connections for leaks. Replace the filter if needed, and use Teflon tape on any threaded fittings. Finally, turn the water and power back on. Test your heater to make sure it\u2019s working right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
