        "Ever wondered how to fix cracked or stained grout and make your tile look new again? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair grout like a pro. \n\nFirst, prep your surface. Clean the grout lines well, then use a grout removal tool to scrape out any loose or damaged grout. Vacuum up all the dust so the new grout sticks properly.\n\nNext, mix your grout\u2014follow the instructions on the bag or tub. Using a rubber grout float, press the grout firmly into the joints, making sure every gap is filled. Work in small sections for best results.\n\nAfter about 15 minutes, wipe away extra grout from the tile with a damp sponge. Shape the grout lines for a smooth, even look. Let it set for about an hour.\n\nFinally, let the grout cure as the package says\u2014usually a day. Then, apply a grout sealer to protect against stains and moisture. This keeps your repair looking great for years.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
