      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to replace a broken sprinkler head without calling a pro? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to swap out a sprinkler head in just a few easy steps. \n\nFirst, shut off your irrigation system. Find the sprinkler head that\u2019s not working and mark the spot so you don\u2019t lose it. \n\nNext, grab a small shovel and carefully dig around the head. You want to expose the riser\u2014the pipe the head screws onto\u2014without damaging it. Unscrew the old sprinkler head. Check the riser for cracks or dirt. If it\u2019s dirty, clean it out. If it\u2019s damaged, you may need a new fitting.\n\nNow, wrap Teflon thread seal tape around the riser threads. This helps prevent leaks. Screw on your new sprinkler head by hand until it\u2019s snug. Don\u2019t overtighten.\n\nTurn the water back on and test the spray. Make sure there are no leaks and the spray pattern looks good. Adjust if needed. Finally, backfill the soil and tidy up the area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
