        "Want to give your hardwood floors a stunning new look? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to stain hardwood floors like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, clear out all furniture and cover nearby surfaces with plastic sheeting. Use painter\u2019s tape to protect baseboards. Now, sand the floor down to bare wood using a drum sander for the main area and an edge sander for corners. Start with coarse sandpaper, then move to finer grits for a smooth finish. Vacuum and wipe with tack cloths to remove every bit of dust.\n\nNext, apply your wood stain with a brush or applicator pad. Work in small sections, following the wood grain. Wipe off any excess stain with a clean rag. Let the stain dry fully\u2014check the label for drying times based on your room\u2019s conditions.\n\nOnce dry, it\u2019s time to seal. Apply a thin coat of polyurethane finish. Let it dry, then lightly sand with fine sandpaper. Clean up the dust, then add one or two more coats, letting each dry completely.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your floors will look brand new. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
