      transcript:
        "Is your roof ready for the next big storm, or will leaks catch you off guard? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to waterproof your roof and keep your home dry. \n\nFirst, clear off all debris, dirt, and any old coatings from your roof. Make sure the surface is dry. Inspect for cracks or damaged spots\u2014these need fixing before you start waterproofing.\n\nNext, patch any cracks and seal all joints. Repair damaged areas with the right materials. Then, apply a primer to help the waterproofing stick better. Let it dry as recommended.\n\nNow, roll out polyester reinforcing fabric over the roof. Apply the liquid waterproofing membrane evenly with rollers or brushes. Cover every inch, and pay extra attention to edges and around pipes. Let the first coat dry, then add a second coat if the manufacturer says so.\n\nFinally, check the whole roof for even coverage. Clean up your tools and throw away waste safely. Your roof is now protected!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
