      transcript:
        "Did you know dirty vents can lower your air quality and spike your energy bills? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to clean your vents like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off your HVAC system. Gather your tools: a vent cleaning brush kit, HEPA vacuum filter, disinfectant spray, gloves, and drop cloths. Put on your gloves and cover nearby furniture to keep dust off your stuff.\n\nNext, unscrew and remove each vent cover. Wash them with soap and water, then let them dry completely. While they dry, use your vacuum and brush kit to clean inside the ducts. Scrub and loosen dust and debris, then vacuum it all out. Spray disinfectant inside the vent for a fresh finish.\n\nOnce the covers are dry, reinstall them. Put your furniture back, turn on the HVAC, and check that air flows from every vent.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
