      transcript:
        "Is your water heater not heating up? The thermostat could be the problem. \n\nIn this video, you'll learn how to safely replace a water heater thermostat step by step.\n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker panel. Double-check that the water heater is off\u2014safety first! Remove the access panel and pull back the insulation to see the thermostat.\n\nBefore touching any wires, take a clear photo of the wiring. This will help you reconnect everything later. Now, disconnect the wires from the old thermostat. Remove the old thermostat and set it aside.\n\nInstall the new thermostat in the same spot. Use your photo to reconnect the wires exactly as before. Make sure all connections are tight. Use wire connectors and a bit of electrical tape for safety.\n\nReplace the insulation and the access panel. Turn the power back on at the breaker. Set your new thermostat to the temperature you want. Wait a few minutes, then check if the water heater is working right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
