      transcript:
        "Is your garbage disposal jammed or leaking? Let\u2019s fix it fast and safe. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to troubleshoot, repair, and test your garbage disposal step by step. \n\nFirst, always turn off the power at the circuit breaker and unplug the unit. Clear out everything under your sink so you have room to work. \n\nNext, grab a hex key and insert it into the bottom of the disposal. Turn it back and forth to free up any jams. Use tongs or pliers to remove anything stuck inside\u2014never use your hands. \n\nNow, check the wiring connections and look for any loose or damaged wires. Inspect the mounting assembly and drain for leaks. Tighten any loose fittings and replace worn gaskets or splash guards if needed. Use plumber\u2019s putty to seal the flange if you see leaks. \n\nPlug the unit back in, restore power, and test the disposal. Listen for smooth operation and check for leaks. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
