      transcript:
        "Want to make your banister look brand new without hiring a pro? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to paint your banister for a smooth, lasting finish. \n\nFirst, gather your supplies: primer, interior or trim-grade paint, painter\u2019s tape, sandpaper, a drop cloth, and two angled brushes. For a 20-foot banister, you\u2019ll need about one quart of primer and two quarts of paint.\n\nStart with surface prep. Clean the banister well\u2014remove dust, dirt, and any sticky spots. Sand every surface with assorted grits until it feels smooth. Wipe away all dust so the paint sticks properly.\n\nNext, tape off areas you don\u2019t want painted, and lay down your drop cloth. Apply a coat of primer evenly over the whole banister. Let it dry fully\u2014this usually takes about an hour.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to paint. Use your angled brush for detail work and a small roller for flat areas. Apply the first coat, let it dry, then add a second coat for full coverage. Make sure to use paint made for trim or interior woodwork.\n\nOnce the final coat is dry, carefully remove the tape, reattach any hardware, and clean up your workspace. Your banister is ready to impress!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
