      transcript:
        "Is your lawn full of dry spots or puddles? Your sprinkler system might need a quick repair! In this video, you'll learn how to inspect, repair, and test your sprinkler system step by step.\n\nFirst, turn off the water supply. Walk around and check each sprinkler head, valve, and pipe for damage or leaks. Look for broken heads, clogged nozzles, or wet spots in the yard. Make a note of any zones that aren\u2019t working right.\n\nNext, replace any damaged sprinkler heads. Clean out clogged nozzles and swap out any faulty valves. Make sure the new parts match your system. Use Teflon tape on threaded connections to prevent leaks.\n\nNow, check the pipes. Dig carefully to find leaks in underground pipes. Cut out damaged sections and use PVC primer and cement to glue in new pipe and fittings. Tighten all connections and use couplings where needed.\n\nFinally, turn the water back on. Run each zone and watch for leaks or odd spray patterns. Adjust the heads for even coverage. Make sure every repair works before you finish.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
