        "https://contractor-plus-website.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/reshub-how-to-vids/fuse-box-replacement.mp4",
      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/fuse-box-replacement/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to replace a fuse box safely and up to code? In this video, you'll learn the exact steps and materials needed to swap out an old fuse box for a new one. \n\nFirst, always start by shutting off the main power supply. Double-check that all circuits are de-energized, and set up safety barriers around your work area. Safety comes first.\n\nNext, label every existing circuit in the old fuse box. Carefully disconnect all wiring, then remove the old box from its mount. Take your time\u2014this step usually takes two to three hours.\n\nNow, mount your new 100-amp fuse box. Connect each labeled circuit to the right breaker. Make sure all connections follow your local electrical codes. Install the grounding bar and run your copper ground wire as needed. Secure everything with wire connectors and mounting hardware. Finish by attaching the panel cover.\n\nFinally, restore power and test each circuit. Check for any faults. Clean up your work area and dispose of old materials according to local rules.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
