      transcript:
        "Want to make your trees look great and stay healthy? Here\u2019s how to trim a tree safely and efficiently, step by step.\n\nFirst, you\u2019ll learn how to assess your tree, trim it the right way, and clean up like a pro.\n\nStart with a site check. Look for dead or overgrown branches and any hazards, like power lines. Gather your tools: a tree trimming saw, loppers or pruning shears, a sturdy ladder, heavy-duty trash bags, and protective gear\u2014gloves, goggles, and a helmet. Set up your ladder on level ground and clear the area around the tree.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time to trim. Use your saw or loppers to cut away dead, diseased, or crossing branches. Always cut at a slight angle, just outside the branch collar. Shape the canopy to let in light and keep branches clear of walkways or roofs. Take your time\u2014this usually takes about two hours per tree.\n\nFinally, clean up. Gather all branches and leaves into trash bags. Dispose of them according to your local rules. Make sure the area is safe and tidy before you finish.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
