        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/install-cabinet/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to install cabinets like a pro and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to install kitchen cabinets, from prep to finishing touches. \n\nFirst, clear your workspace and mark the wall studs. Use a level to draw straight lines where your cabinets will go. This helps keep everything even.\n\nNext, install a ledger board or temporary support under where the cabinets will hang. This holds them up while you work. Start with the upper cabinets. Lift each one into place, line it up with your marks, and screw it into the studs. Make sure each cabinet is level and plumb before moving on.\n\nOnce all cabinets are up, align the faces so they look seamless. Clamp them together and fasten the sides. Adjust the doors and drawers so they open smoothly.\n\nFinally, add your hardware\u2014pulls, knobs, and hinges. Fill any gaps with caulk, touch up the surfaces, and clean up the area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
