      transcript:
        "Want a perfect green lawn with zero mowing? Here\u2019s how to install artificial turf like a pro. In this video, you\u2019ll learn every step to get a flawless, long-lasting turf yard.\n\nFirst, clear your area. Remove all grass, rocks, and debris. Dig down a few inches so you have room for the base. Make sure the ground is level and slopes slightly for drainage.\n\nNext, lay down a weed barrier fabric. This keeps weeds from poking through your turf later.\n\nNow, spread a layer of crushed stone or decomposed granite. Compact it well. This base gives your turf a solid, even surface and helps water drain away.\n\nRoll out your artificial turf. Make sure the grain faces the same way for a natural look. Trim the edges to fit your space. Use seam tape and adhesive to join pieces together.\n\nSecure the turf around the edges with landscape spikes or staples. Then, spread sand infill evenly across the turf. This helps the blades stand up and adds weight.\n\nFinally, brush the turf to lift the fibers and spread the infill. Check all seams and edges. Make sure water drains well and the surface looks clean.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
