        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/gas-line-leak-detection/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Did you know a hidden gas leak can put your home and family at serious risk? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely detect and fix gas line leaks step by step. \n\nFirst, safety comes first. Shut off the gas supply and open windows to ventilate the area. Make sure there are no open flames or sparks nearby. Put on protective gloves and a respirator mask before you start.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time to find the leak. Use a gas leak detector solution or an electronic gas leak meter. Apply the solution to all joints, fittings, and connections along the gas line. If you see bubbles forming, or your meter alerts, you\u2019ve found a leak.\n\nTo fix it, use pipe wrenches to tighten or replace any faulty fittings. Once repaired, retest the area with your solution or meter to make sure the leak is gone. When everything checks out, restore the gas supply and double-check all connections for safety.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
