      transcript:
        "Did you know you can replace a damaged garage door panel in just a few hours? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to safely swap out a broken panel and get your garage door working like new. \n\nFirst, disconnect your garage door opener and make sure the door can't move. Safety first! Gather your tools and the new replacement panel. \n\nNext, remove the hinges, rollers, and any hardware attached to the damaged panel. Carefully slide the old panel out of the frame. Take your time\u2014these panels can be heavy and awkward.\n\nNow, slide the new panel into place. Reattach all the hardware, including hinges, brackets, and rollers. Make sure everything lines up straight. Tighten all fasteners securely.\n\nFinally, reconnect the garage door opener and test the door. Open and close it a few times to check for smooth movement and proper alignment. If needed, adjust the hardware until the door works perfectly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
