      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to replace a broken tile without making a mess? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair a damaged floor tile like a pro. \n\nFirst, use a grout saw to carefully remove the grout around the broken tile. Take your time\u2014this helps prevent damage to nearby tiles. Next, use a hammer and chisel to break up the damaged tile. Remove all the pieces and scrape away any leftover adhesive. Clean the area so it\u2019s smooth and dust-free.\n\nNow, mix your thinset mortar and spread a thin, even layer on the exposed floor. Press your new tile into place, making sure it\u2019s level with the others. Use tile spacers to keep the grout lines straight.\n\nLet the adhesive set, then mix and apply grout around the new tile. Wipe away any excess grout with a damp sponge. Once it\u2019s dry, apply a sealer to protect your repair.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
