      transcript:
        "Want to get rid of kitchen smoke and odors for good? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a kitchen exhaust fan, step by step. \n\nFirst, mark where you want the fan on your wall or ceiling. Measure carefully, then cut the opening using a drywall saw or jigsaw. Make sure it lines up with where you\u2019ll vent outside.\n\nNext, mount the exhaust fan in the opening. Attach flexible ducting to the fan, and run it to the outside wall. Use duct clamps to secure the connections, and seal all joints with foil tape to stop air leaks.\n\nNow, turn off the power at your breaker. Connect the fan\u2019s wires to your home\u2019s electrical circuit using Romex wire and wire connectors. Double-check your connections, mount the fan cover, and turn the power back on to test it.\n\nFinally, install the exterior vent cap outside. Make sure it\u2019s sealed tight to keep out weather. Clean up your work area and check that air flows freely from inside to outside.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
