      transcript:
        "Want to paint a nursery that\u2019s safe, beautiful, and done right the first time? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to paint a nursery, from prep to cleanup, so you get pro results\u2014even if you\u2019re a beginner.\n\nFirst, clear out the room. Move furniture, take down wall hangings, and cover the floor and outlets with drop cloths. Use painter\u2019s tape to protect trim and edges.\n\nNext, clean the walls to remove dust and stains. Fill any holes or cracks with wall patch, then sand smooth. Wipe down the walls so the paint sticks well.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to prime. Use a low-VOC primer, especially on patched spots or if you\u2019re covering a dark color. With a brush, cut in around the edges, corners, and trim for sharp lines.\n\nGrab your roller and start painting the walls with a pastel, low-VOC paint. Roll on the first coat evenly. Let it dry, then add a second coat for full, even color.\n\nWhen you\u2019re done, peel off the tape, clean your brushes and rollers, and toss the drop cloths. Once the paint is dry, move the furniture and decor back in.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
