      transcript:
        "Ever wonder how to make a chipped tile disappear in under an hour? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to repair a chipped tile so it looks like new\u2014no need to replace the whole thing. \n\nFirst, clean the chipped area and the tile around it with a damp cloth. Make sure all dust and debris are gone, then let it dry completely. \n\nNext, grab your tile repair epoxy or filler. Mix it up or open it, following the instructions on the package. Use a putty knife to fill the chip, pressing the compound in and smoothing it out so it\u2019s level with the rest of the tile. If you have a color-matching pigment, mix it in now to match your tile\u2019s color. \n\nLet the repair dry as directed. Once it\u2019s dry, gently sand the area with fine sandpaper until it\u2019s flush with the tile. Wipe away any dust. \n\nFinally, apply a tile sealer or matching touch-up paint to blend the repair with the rest of the tile. Let it dry, and you\u2019re done! \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
