        "Want to stop water damage before it starts? Let\u2019s install roof gutters the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to measure, cut, mount, and test new aluminum gutters step by step.\n\nFirst, set up your ladders and gather all your tools. Measure the roof edges to figure out how much gutter you need. Mark where your downspouts will go, and check the fascia boards for any rot or damage.\n\nNext, cut your aluminum gutters to the right lengths. Attach end caps, and connect sections using gutter connectors. Pre-drill holes for your hangers and downspouts so everything lines up perfectly.\n\nNow, mount the gutter hangers to the fascia board, spacing them about every two feet. Hang the gutters with a slight slope\u2014about a quarter inch for every ten feet\u2014so water flows to the downspouts. Attach the downspouts and elbows, then seal all the joints with caulk.\n\nFinally, flush the gutters with water to check for leaks and make sure everything drains right. Tighten any loose screws, clean up your work area, and dispose of waste properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
