        "Did you know a small leak in your roof flashing can cause thousands in water damage? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to repair roof flashing step by step, so you can protect your home and save money. \n\nFirst, inspect your roof flashing for cracks, rust, or loose sections. Make sure your ladder is secure and gather your tools\u2014new flashing, roofing cement, nails, and a pry bar. Clean the area around the flashing so you have a clear workspace.\n\nNext, carefully remove the damaged flashing. Use a pry bar and utility knife, but be gentle\u2014don\u2019t tear the shingles or underlayment. Once the old flashing is out, cut your new flashing to size. Slide it into place, making sure it fits snugly. Secure it with roofing nails, then seal all the edges with roofing cement to keep water out.\n\nFinally, put back any shingles you removed. Press them down firmly and add more roofing cement over seams and nail heads for a watertight finish.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
