        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/drywall-finishing/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to get smooth, pro-level drywall finishes without the guesswork? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to finish drywall like a pro, from prep to final sanding. \n\nFirst, prep your surface. Check all drywall screws in your space\u2014make sure they\u2019re set just below the surface. Wipe away any dust or debris from seams and corners. This takes about 2 to 3 hours for 1,000 square feet.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time for taping and the first coat. Apply paper drywall tape to all seams. Then, cover the tape and screw holes with joint compound. Feather the edges for a smooth blend. This step usually takes 4 to 5 hours.\n\nAfter the first coat dries, apply your second and third coats of joint compound. Let each coat dry fully, and sand lightly between coats for a flawless finish. Plan for 6 to 8 hours, including drying time.\n\nFinally, do a thorough sanding and inspection. Smooth out any rough spots, touch up imperfections, and wipe down all surfaces to remove dust. Now you\u2019re ready for primer and paint!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
