      transcript:
        "Is your garage door making noise or getting stuck? It might be time to replace the rollers! In this video, you'll learn how to safely and easily replace garage door rollers yourself. \n\nFirst, disconnect your garage door opener so the door won't move unexpectedly. Lift the door and secure it in the open position using locking pliers or clamps on the tracks. Gather your new rollers, lubricant spray, and a socket wrench or screwdriver.\n\nNext, unbolt the hinges or brackets holding the old rollers. Carefully slide out each old roller. As you go, check the tracks for any damage or debris\u2014clean them out if needed.\n\nNow, insert the new rollers into the hinges. Reattach all hardware tightly. Spray a little lubricant on the rollers and tracks for smooth movement. Manually open and close the door to make sure everything works. Finally, reconnect the opener and test the door with the remote.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
