        "Is your shower leaking and you\u2019re worried about hidden water damage? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to find and fix a shower leak like a pro. \n\nFirst, inspect the shower. Turn off the water supply and clear the area. Look for signs of leaks\u2014like loose tiles, cracked grout, or water stains. Gather your tools, safety gear, and materials: silicone caulk, a shower pan liner patch, replacement tiles, grout, a waterproof membrane patch, and plumbing fittings.\n\nNext, remove any damaged materials. Carefully take off shower trim, tiles, or panels to reach the leak. Check all plumbing connections and the surrounding surfaces for damage.\n\nNow, repair and seal. Replace any faulty gaskets, pipes, or fittings. Apply waterproof sealant to all joints and seams. Make sure your repairs meet local plumbing codes.\n\nFinally, reassemble the shower. Put tiles or panels back, restore fixtures, and turn the water on. Test for leaks and clean up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
