      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/drywall-tape-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wonder how to fix peeling or cracked drywall tape so it looks brand new? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair drywall tape like a pro. \n\nFirst, clear the area and remove any loose or damaged tape. Lightly sand the surface so the new tape sticks well. This prep work is key for a smooth finish.\n\nNext, spread a thin layer of joint compound over the seam. Press new drywall tape into the compound, then smooth it out with a taping knife. Make sure there are no bubbles or wrinkles.\n\nOnce the first layer dries, add more joint compound over the tape. Feather the edges outward so it blends with the wall. Let each coat dry fully, and lightly sand between coats for a flat surface.\n\nFor the final touch, sand the last coat until smooth. Wipe away dust, then prime and paint to match your wall. That\u2019s it\u2014your repair is done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
