      transcript:
        "Want to make your old hardwood floors look brand new without replacing them? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to resurface hardwood floors like a pro. \n\nFirst, clear the room. Remove all furniture, rugs, and baseboards. Sweep and vacuum to get rid of dust and debris. This makes sure nothing gets trapped in your new finish.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time to sand. Use a drum sander for the main area and an edge sander for corners. Start with coarse sanding belts, then switch to finer grits for a smooth finish. After sanding, vacuum and wipe the floor with tack cloths to remove all dust.\n\nNow, fill any cracks or holes with wood filler. Let it dry, then sand those spots smooth. Tape off walls and cover vents with plastic sheeting to protect from dust and drips.\n\nApply your finish. If you want a new color, stain the wood first. Then, use a roller or brush to apply polyurethane or your chosen finish. Let it dry as recommended\u2014usually a few hours between coats.\n\nFinally, reinstall baseboards and move your furniture back in. Inspect the floor for any missed spots or imperfections. Now your floor is ready to shine!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
