        "Want to make your exterior wood look brand new and last for years? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to stain exterior wood the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, prep your surface. Clean the wood with a wood cleaner or mild detergent. Scrub off dirt, mildew, and any old stain. Let it dry completely\u2014this is key for a smooth finish.\n\nNext, sand the wood. Use sandpaper to smooth rough spots and open up the grain. This helps the stain soak in better. Then, mask off windows, hardware, and anything you don\u2019t want stained with painter\u2019s tape and drop cloths.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to stain. Use a brush, roller, or sprayer. Always follow the wood grain and work in small sections. Wipe off any extra stain as you go to avoid blotches.\n\nLet the stain dry fully\u2014usually 6 to 7 hours, but check the label. Once dry, inspect your work. Touch up any missed spots for a perfect finish.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
