      transcript:
        "Want to hang sheetrock like a pro and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to hang drywall, from prep to a smooth finish. \n\nFirst, clear your workspace and gather all your tools. Check the framing to make sure it's solid and ready for new sheetrock. \n\nNext, measure your walls and ceilings. Mark your drywall sheets and cut them to fit around outlets, windows, and doors. Take your time\u2014accurate cuts make a big difference.\n\nNow, it's time to hang the sheetrock. Lift each panel into place and fasten it to the studs or joists using drywall screws. Stagger the seams for extra strength and a better finish.\n\nOnce all panels are up, apply joint tape over the seams. Cover the tape and screw heads with a coat of joint compound. Let it dry completely before moving on.\n\nFinally, sand the dried compound until the surface is smooth. Check for any rough spots or imperfections, then clean up all dust and debris.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
