      transcript:
        "Want to make your trees healthier and safer in just a few hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to prune a tree step by step, using the right tools and techniques. \n\nFirst, assess your tree. Look for dead, diseased, or overgrown branches. Make sure you have a pruning saw, bypass pruners, loppers, a ladder, gloves, goggles, a tarp, and trash bags. Clear the area under the tree to keep it safe and tidy.\n\nNext, start pruning. Use your pruners and loppers to cut away small dead or crossing branches. For thicker limbs, use the pruning saw. Always cut at a slight angle, just outside the branch collar, to help the tree heal. Focus on shaping the tree and letting more air and light through the canopy.\n\nWhen you\u2019re done, gather all the branches and debris onto your tarp. Bag up the waste or compost it, following your local rules. Clean your tools and store them safely for next time.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
