      transcript:
        "Want to install a new ceiling light without calling an electrician? Watch this! In this video, you'll learn how to safely replace or install a ceiling light fixture step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker box. Double-check the light switch to make sure the power is off. Clear the area under the fixture so you have space to work safely.\n\nNext, remove the old light. Unscrew the fixture, gently lower it, and disconnect the wires. Inspect the electrical box and wiring to make sure they're in good shape and match your new fixture's requirements.\n\nNow, install your new ceiling light. Connect the fixture wires to the house wires\u2014usually black to black, white to white, and ground to ground. Use wire connectors for a secure fit. Attach the fixture to the electrical box with the mounting hardware. Add any covers or bulbs as needed.\n\nFinally, turn the power back on at the breaker. Flip the switch to test your new light. Clean up your workspace, and you're done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
