      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/gas-water-heater-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your gas water heater not heating or refusing to stay lit? In this video, you'll learn how to safely repair a gas water heater by replacing key parts and getting it running again. \n\nFirst, shut off the gas supply and the cold water inlet to your heater. Attach a hose to the drain valve and empty the tank completely\u2014this keeps things safe and dry while you work.\n\nNext, inspect the main components: the thermocouple, burner assembly, and gas control valve. Look for signs of wear, corrosion, or damage. If you spot a faulty part, swap it out with a manufacturer-approved replacement. Common parts include the thermocouple, gas control valve, flexible gas connector, igniter assembly, and pipe joint compound or Teflon tape for sealing connections.\n\nOnce repairs are done, reassemble all fittings. Turn the water and gas back on. Relight the pilot according to your heater\u2019s instructions. Check for gas or water leaks, and make sure the heater fires up and runs smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
