        "Did you know a small leak in your metal roof can lead to big problems fast? In this video, you'll learn how to repair a metal roof step by step, so you can protect your home and save money. \n\nFirst, inspect your roof. Look for rust, loose screws, and damaged panels. Clean the area well\u2014remove dirt, leaves, and any old sealant. This helps new materials stick better.\n\nNext, fix the damage. Replace or tighten any loose panels and fasteners. Patch holes or rust spots with metal patches and a quality roof sealant. Make sure everything is secure and weatherproof. Use flashing to cover seams and edges, and check that repairs meet your local building codes.\n\nNow, seal it up. Apply a high-quality metal roof sealant to all seams and repaired spots. Double-check your work\u2014look for missed areas and make sure everything is watertight. Clean up your tools and debris.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
