      transcript:
        "Tree roots can crack foundations and ruin your yard\u2014here\u2019s how to safely remove them. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process for removing tree roots, what tools you need, and how to restore your site when you\u2019re done.\n\nFirst, assess the area. Walk around and mark where roots are causing problems\u2014look for cracks, lifted pavement, or roots near pipes. Mark the removal zone clearly.\n\nNext, grab your excavation tools\u2014a shovel and pickaxe work best. Carefully dig around the marked roots. Go slow to avoid damaging nearby plants or underground utilities. Expose the roots fully so you can see what you\u2019re working with.\n\nNow, use a heavy-duty root saw or loppers to cut the exposed roots. Cut in sections for easier removal. Pull out the root pieces and place them in disposal bags. Always check for utility lines before cutting.\n\nOnce the roots are out, backfill the hole with soil. Compact it down and restore any landscaping. Dispose of the roots according to your local guidelines.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
