        "Want to give your bathroom a fresh look without a full remodel? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to paint your bathroom cabinets step by step, so you get a pro finish every time. \n\nFirst, remove all cabinet doors, drawers, and hardware. Clean every surface with a good degreaser to get rid of dirt and grease. This helps your paint stick and last longer.\n\nNext, lightly sand all cabinet surfaces. This roughs up the finish so the paint can grip. Wipe away dust, then use painter\u2019s tape to protect your walls and counters.\n\nNow, apply a high-quality primer. Cover every surface and let it dry completely. This step is key for a smooth, even paint job.\n\nOnce the primer is dry, paint your cabinets. Use a brush or roller for even coats. Let the first coat dry, then add a second coat for full coverage.\n\nFinally, reattach your hardware, put the doors and drawers back, and remove the tape. Clean up your workspace and let the cabinets dry fully before using them.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
