        "Is water sneaking in around your windows and causing damage? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to fix a leaking window step by step, so you can keep your home dry and protected. \n\nFirst, inspect the window frame, sill, and wall. Look for cracks, gaps, or old, damaged caulk. Remove any loose caulk or debris with a sealant remover and clean the area well. This helps the new sealant stick properly.\n\nNext, grab your exterior-grade caulk and, if needed, a backer rod for larger gaps. Apply the caulk smoothly around all seams, joints, and gaps. Use a caulk tool or your finger to smooth it out for a tight, watertight seal. If you spot damaged trim, replace it now.\n\nLet the caulk cure as directed. Then, test your work by spraying water around the window. Check inside for any leaks. If it\u2019s dry, you\u2019re done! Clean up your tools and dispose of waste safely.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
