        "Want to make your home the brightest on the block this holiday season? In this video, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to plan and install holiday lights like a pro. \n\nFirst, start with a site assessment. Walk around your property and talk through your design ideas. Look at your rooflines, trees, and walkways. Decide where you want the lights to go and measure the total length you\u2019ll need.\n\nNext, gather your materials. You\u2019ll need LED holiday light strands, outdoor extension cords, light clips or hooks, an outdoor timer, and weatherproof tape. Test every strand before you hang them\u2014nothing\u2019s worse than finding a dead section after you\u2019re done!\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install. Use clips or hooks to attach the lights securely to your roof, trees, and walkways. Keep the spacing even and make sure all connections are safe and weatherproof. Use extension cords and weatherproof tape to protect plugs and connections from the elements.\n\nOnce everything\u2019s up, plug in the lights and check for any dark spots or uneven sections. Make adjustments until you\u2019re happy with the look. Set your timer so your lights turn on and off automatically.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
