      transcript:
        "Is your well pump acting up? A faulty pressure switch could be the reason\u2014and you can fix it yourself! In this video, you'll learn how to safely replace a well pressure switch step by step.\n\nFirst, turn off power to the well pump at your breaker panel. Double-check with a voltage tester to make sure there\u2019s no electricity at the switch. Safety first!\n\nNext, disconnect the wires and the small pressure tube from the old switch. Unscrew the switch from the pressure tank. If the fitting is corroded, you might need a new pipe fitting.\n\nWrap the threads of the new switch with Teflon tape. Screw it onto the tank, then reconnect the pressure tube. Attach the wires to the new switch, following the manufacturer\u2019s diagram. Use wire connectors for a secure fit, and double-check all connections.\n\nTurn the power back on. Watch the pump cycle and check for leaks or odd noises. Adjust the pressure settings if needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
