      transcript:
        "Want to hang drywall like a pro and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to hang drywall, from prep to finish. \n\nFirst, clear your workspace and gather all your materials: 4x8 drywall sheets, drywall screws, joint tape, and joint compound. Measure your walls or ceilings and mark the stud locations. This makes hanging much easier.\n\nNext, cut your drywall sheets to fit. Lift each sheet into place and fasten it to the studs using drywall screws. Make sure to stagger the seams and keep everything lined up for a smooth finish.\n\nOnce all the sheets are up, it\u2019s time for taping. Apply joint tape over the seams, then cover with a first coat of joint compound. Smooth it out and let it dry.\n\nAfter it dries, add a second coat of joint compound, feathering the edges so it blends in. When that\u2019s dry, sand everything smooth. Now you\u2019re ready for paint or texture!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
