      transcript:
        "Want to stop drafts and leaks around your windows for good? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to caulk your windows like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, gather your supplies: exterior window caulk, painter\u2019s tape, a caulking gun, and backer rod if you have wide gaps. For five windows, you\u2019ll need about two tubes of caulk, a quarter roll of tape, and half a pack of backer rod.\n\nStart with surface preparation. Clean the window frame and the area around it. Scrape away any old caulk, dirt, or debris. This helps the new caulk stick well.\n\nNext, apply painter\u2019s tape along both sides of the seam to keep your lines neat. Cut the tip of your caulk tube at a 45-degree angle, load it into your caulking gun, and squeeze a steady bead along the seams. If you see any big gaps, push in some backer rod first, then caulk over it.\n\nNow, smooth the caulk with a wet finger or a caulking tool. Wipe away any extra before it dries. Remove the tape for crisp lines. Let the caulk dry as recommended for your local weather.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your windows are sealed and ready for any season. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
