      transcript:
        "Cracked or loose floor tiles? You can fix them like a pro in just a few hours. \n\nIn this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair a damaged tile floor, from removing old tiles to sealing the new ones.\n\nFirst, carefully pry up the broken or loose tiles using a chisel and hammer. Take your time\u2014work gently to avoid damaging nearby tiles. Once the tiles are out, scrape away any old adhesive and clean the area so it\u2019s smooth and debris-free.\n\nNext, check that your subfloor is level and dry. Spread a layer of thinset mortar with a notched trowel. This gives your new tiles a solid base.\n\nNow, press your replacement tiles firmly into place. Line them up with the surrounding tiles. Use tile spacers to keep your grout lines even. Let the adhesive set as recommended on the package.\n\nOnce the tiles are set, mix your grout and apply it between the tiles with a rubber float. Wipe away extra grout with a damp sponge. Let the grout cure fully, then apply a sealer to protect your new floor.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
