        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/under-sink-water-filter-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want cleaner water straight from your kitchen tap? Watch how easy it is to install an under sink water filter yourself! In this video, you\u2019ll learn the exact steps and tools you need to get the job done right.\n\nFirst, gather your materials: an under sink water filter kit, two flexible supply lines, a tee fitting, plumber\u2019s tape, and mounting screws or brackets. Clear out everything under your sink and lay down a towel to catch any drips.\n\nNext, turn off the cold water supply valve under the sink. Disconnect the supply line from the valve. Now, attach the tee fitting to the valve, then connect the filter\u2019s inlet and outlet fittings. Use plumber\u2019s tape on threaded connections to prevent leaks. Mount the filter unit securely to the cabinet wall using the provided screws or brackets.\n\nConnect the tubing from the filter to your faucet and the water supply. Double-check all connections. Turn the water back on slowly and look for leaks. Finally, flush the filter as recommended in the instructions before using the water.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
