      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/backsplash-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to give your kitchen a fresh new look in just one weekend? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a beautiful tile backsplash, step by step. \n\nFirst, prep your wall. Clean and dry the area, remove outlet covers, and patch any holes or bumps. A smooth surface is key for good tile adhesion.\n\nNext, plan your layout. Measure and mark straight guidelines. Dry-fit your tiles to see how they\u2019ll look, and use a tile cutter or wet saw to trim pieces for outlets and edges.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install. Spread thinset mortar evenly on the wall. Press each tile into place, using spacers for even gaps. Work in small sections so the adhesive doesn\u2019t dry out.\n\nOnce the tiles are set, remove the spacers. Mix and apply grout between the tiles, wiping away any excess with a damp sponge. Let the grout cure, then seal the lines to protect against moisture.\n\nFinish up by adding edge trim and caulking where the backsplash meets the countertop.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
