      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to replace old ductwork and boost your home's airflow? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process for a successful ductwork replacement, from planning to final inspection. \n\nFirst, start with a thorough assessment. Inspect your current ducts, measure each space, and make a list of what you need. Always check your local building codes before you begin.\n\nNext, remove the old ductwork. Disconnect all sections, take out registers and supports, and safely dispose of debris according to your area's rules.\n\nNow, it's time to install the new ducts. Cut and fit galvanized steel duct sections, making sure everything lines up. Use hangers or straps for support. Seal every joint with mastic and foil tape to prevent leaks. Wrap the ducts with R-6 insulation for energy savings.\n\nAfter installation, test the system. Check airflow, look for leaks, and balance the system by adjusting dampers and registers until every room gets the right amount of air.\n\nFinally, do a full inspection. Make sure everything meets code, clean up the workspace, and give maintenance tips to the occupants.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
