      "@type": "VideoObject",
      name: "How to Transplant a Tree: Step-by-Step Guide",
      description:
        "Calculate materials & costs to tree transplanting at https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/tree-transplanting/national-average\n\nIn this video, learn how to transplant a mature tree safely and successfully. We\u2019ll walk you through every step, from choosing the right new location and preparing the site, to digging the root ball, moving the tree, and giving it the aftercare it needs to thrive. You\u2019ll also find out what materials you need, like compost, mulch, staking kits, and watering bags. Whether you\u2019re a homeowner or a contractor, these tips will help you avoid common mistakes and give your tree the best chance to survive and grow. If you found this guide helpful, please like and follow for more practical construction tips. Contractors, don\u2019t forget to check out Contractor Plus for the best tools to run your business!",
      thumbnailUrl:
        "https://contractor-plus-website.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/og-images/280f7307-2529-4b97-8945-b1a3394e2d8b.jpg",
      uploadDate: "2025-08-04",
      duration: "PT2M30S",
      contentUrl:
        "https://contractor-plus-website.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/reshub-how-to-vids/tree-transplanting.mp4",
      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/tree-transplanting/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to move a mature tree without killing it? Here\u2019s how to transplant a tree the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, pick the new spot. Make sure it has good soil, enough space for the tree to grow, and plenty of sunlight. Mark the spot and clear away any grass or debris.\n\nNext, water the tree well. Dig a wide root ball around the tree, keeping as many roots as possible. At the new site, dig a hole the same size and depth as the root ball.\n\nCarefully move the tree to its new home. Set it upright in the hole. Backfill with the soil you dug out, tamping gently to remove air pockets. Water the tree deeply.\n\nStake the tree if it needs support. Add mulch around the base, but keep it away from the trunk. Mulch helps keep the soil moist and cool.\n\nFinally, water the tree often and watch for signs of stress or disease. Adjust the stakes as needed and keep caring for the tree until it\u2019s established.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
