      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/well-pump-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your well pump acting up and you\u2019re not sure what to do next? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair or replace a well pump, so you can get your water flowing again. \n\nFirst, always shut off the power to your well pump at the breaker. Safety comes first. Inspect the wiring and plumbing for any obvious damage or leaks. Look for signs like no water, low pressure, or strange noises.\n\nNext, disconnect the plumbing and electrical connections. Carefully pull the pump out of the well casing. This can be heavy, so get help if you need it. Check the pump, pressure switch, check valve, and wiring for wear, clogs, or electrical issues.\n\nIf you spot a bad part, replace it. Common fixes include swapping out the pressure switch, check valve, or even the whole pump. Make sure any new parts match your system\u2019s specs.\n\nOnce repairs are done, lower the pump back into the well. Reconnect all pipes and wires. Turn the power back on and test the system. Check for leaks, and make sure you have good water flow and pressure.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
