      transcript:
        "Want to give your kitchen a fresh look without a full remodel? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to reface your cabinets step by step, saving time and money.\n\nFirst, remove all cabinet doors, drawers, and hardware. Label each piece so you can put them back easily. Clean every surface to get rid of grease and dust.\n\nNext, sand the cabinet frames and boxes. Fix any dents or damage with wood filler. Wipe everything down so the new veneer sticks well.\n\nNow, measure and cut your veneer or laminate sheets to fit the cabinet faces and sides. Apply adhesive or contact cement, then press the veneer on. Use a roller to smooth out bubbles and make sure it sticks tight. Don\u2019t forget to add edge banding for a clean finish.\n\nOnce the veneer is set, reinstall your cabinet doors and drawers. Attach new handles and hinges, or reuse the old ones if they\u2019re in good shape. Adjust everything so it lines up perfectly.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Touch up any spots and clean up the area. Your cabinets now look brand new!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
