      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix loose or broken tiles without calling a pro? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair tile adhesive and get your floor looking new again. \n\nFirst, remove any damaged or loose tiles. Use a chisel or putty knife to gently lift them out, being careful not to crack the good tiles around them. Clear away all debris so you have a clean workspace.\n\nNext, prep the surface. Scrape off old adhesive and dust. The area should be smooth and level\u2014this helps the new adhesive stick properly.\n\nNow, grab your tile adhesive, also called thinset mortar. Using a notched trowel, spread a thin, even layer over the exposed area. Follow the instructions on the bag for the right thickness.\n\nPress your replacement tiles firmly into the adhesive. Use tile spacers to keep the gaps even. Let the adhesive set\u2014usually about 24 hours, but check your product\u2019s label.\n\nOnce set, mix your grout and press it into the joints between tiles. Wipe away extra grout with a damp sponge.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Make sure tiles are level and clean up any leftover grout. That\u2019s it\u2014your tile repair is done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
