      transcript:
        "Want to stop roof leaks before they start? Here\u2019s how to install a drip edge the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to prep, measure, and install a roof drip edge for a watertight finish.\n\nFirst, lift the shingles along the roof edge and remove any old drip edge or debris. Check the wood decking underneath for damage. Make sure the surface is clean and ready for new material.\n\nNext, measure the entire roof edge. Cut your aluminum drip edge sections to fit. Dry-fit them along the eaves and rakes, overlapping each joint by at least two inches. This overlap keeps water from sneaking in. Double-check that everything lines up for proper water runoff.\n\nNow, nail the drip edge in place. Use roofing nails every 8 to 10 inches. Once it\u2019s secure, lay the shingles back over the drip edge. Press them down and nail as needed to meet your local building codes.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve just protected your roof from water damage. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
