      transcript:
        "Want to make your old hardwood floors look brand new? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to finish hardwood floors like a pro. \n\nFirst, clear the room. Move out all furniture, cover vents, and clean the floor. This keeps dust out of your finish. \n\nNext, sand the floor. Start with coarse grit, then medium, then fine. This removes the old finish and smooths the wood. After sanding, vacuum and wipe the floor with tack cloths to get rid of dust. \n\nIf you want a new color, now\u2019s the time to stain. Let it dry fully. Then, apply your first coat of polyurethane or sealer. Use a disposable applicator for a smooth finish. \n\nAfter the first coat dries, lightly buff the floor. Apply one or two more coats, letting each dry completely. Keep the room well-ventilated the whole time. \n\nThat\u2019s it! Your floors will look amazing and last for years. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
