      transcript:
        "Did you know a poorly installed dryer vent can be a fire hazard? In this video, you'll learn how to install a dryer vent safely and efficiently, step by step. \n\nFirst, plan your vent route. Find the shortest, straightest path from your dryer to the outside. Gather your materials: a dryer vent kit, flexible aluminum duct, hose clamps, exterior caulk, and mounting screws. \n\nNext, mark where the vent will exit your wall or floor. Cut the opening carefully. Attach the exterior vent hood, making sure it's sealed tight with caulk to keep out weather and pests. Secure it with mounting screws.\n\nNow, connect the ductwork. Attach one end to your dryer and the other to the vent hood. Use hose clamps to secure both ends. Try to keep the duct as straight as possible\u2014fewer bends mean better airflow. Support the duct if needed so it doesn't sag.\n\nFinally, test your system. Run the dryer and check for strong airflow outside. Look for any leaks and fix them. Clean up your work area and make sure everything meets local safety codes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
