        "A leaking roof can turn into a disaster fast\u2014here\u2019s how to stop it in its tracks. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to handle an emergency roof repair step by step, so you can protect your home until a pro can make permanent fixes.\n\nFirst, stay safe. Use a sturdy ladder and check your roof for missing shingles, holes, or obvious leaks. Gather your materials: asphalt shingles, roofing felt, nails, roof cement, flashing, and a tarp. Don\u2019t forget gloves and safety gear.\n\nNext, clear away any debris from the damaged area. Use roofing cement to seal cracks or holes. If the damage is big, lay a tarp over the spot. Pull it tight and secure it with nails or heavy boards, making sure it won\u2019t blow away in bad weather.\n\nGo inside and check for water leaks. Dry any wet spots and set out buckets if needed. Keep an eye on the area for more leaks.\n\nFinally, clean up your tools and leftover materials. Take photos of the damage for insurance. Plan a follow-up with a roofing contractor for a permanent fix.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
