      transcript:
        "Is your sprinkler system not turning on or off? It could be a bad valve\u2014and you can fix it yourself! In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to replace a 1-inch sprinkler valve, from shutting off the water to testing your new install. \n\nFirst, turn off the main water supply to your sprinkler system. Open a valve or drain to relieve any pressure. Find the faulty valve\u2014usually in a valve box in your yard.\n\nNext, disconnect the wiring from the old valve. Unscrew or carefully cut out the old valve using a PVC cutter. Clean the pipe ends so they\u2019re smooth and ready for the new valve.\n\nNow, wrap Teflon tape on threaded fittings. Dry-fit your new valve, using PVC couplings or elbows if needed. Apply PVC primer and cement to the pipe and fittings, then connect everything. Reattach the wiring, matching the colors as before.\n\nLet the glue set for a few minutes. Turn the water back on, activate the sprinkler zone, and check for leaks. Make sure the new valve opens and closes as it should.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
