        "Want to give your front door a fresh new look in just a few hours? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to paint your front door like a pro, from prep to cleanup. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: exterior paint and primer, painter\u2019s tape, a drop cloth, sandpaper, and a brush or roller. Remove all hardware from the door, like handles and locks. Clean the door with soap and water to get rid of dirt and grease. Let it dry, then sand the surface to help the paint stick. Wipe away dust, and use painter\u2019s tape to protect glass and trim.\n\nNext, apply a coat of primer. Use smooth, even strokes and cover the whole door. Let the primer dry as directed\u2014usually about 30 minutes.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to paint. Start with the first coat, using a brush for details and a roller for flat areas. Let it dry, then add a second coat for a rich, lasting finish. Wait for the paint to dry fully.\n\nFinally, peel off the tape, put the hardware back on, touch up any missed spots, and clean up your tools and drop cloth.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
