      transcript:
        "Want to set fence posts that last for years? Watch this before you start! In this video, you'll learn how to install wood fence posts the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, measure and mark where each post will go along your fence line. Use a tape measure and stakes to keep everything straight. Grab a post hole digger and dig each hole about one-third the length of your post deep\u2014usually 2 to 3 feet\u2014and about 10 to 12 inches wide. Add a few inches of gravel at the bottom for drainage.\n\nNext, set your pressure-treated wood posts in the holes. Make sure each post is straight and lines up with the others. Pour in your concrete mix around the post, then add water. Use a level to double-check the post is plumb. Let the concrete set for a few hours.\n\nOnce the concrete starts to harden, backfill the rest of the hole with soil. Tamp it down tight to keep the post steady. Double-check that all posts are secure and ready for your fence panels.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
