      transcript:
        "Is your flat roof leaking or showing signs of wear? Let\u2019s walk through how to repair it step by step, so you can protect your home or building. \n\nFirst, inspect your flat roof. Look for blisters, cracks, or ponding water. Clean off all debris and loose material\u2014this helps new materials stick. \n\nNext, repair any damaged spots. Cut out blisters or cracks. Apply roofing cement, then patch with modified bitumen membrane. Seal all seams and edges tightly. Use roof primer and adhesive for extra hold. \n\nNow, apply a protective coating. Roll or brush it over the repaired areas and the whole roof. Make sure to let it dry fully, especially if your climate is humid. \n\nFinally, do a last inspection. Check that all repairs are watertight. Clean up tools and dispose of old roofing material safely. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
