        "Is your chimney leaking or showing signs of water damage? Don\u2019t ignore it\u2014chimney flashing repair can save you thousands in future repairs. In this video, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to repair chimney flashing step by step.\n\nFirst, inspect the area where your chimney meets the roof. Look for cracked, loose, or rusted flashing. Gather your materials: aluminum flashing, roofing cement, galvanized nails, silicone caulk, and an ice & water shield membrane. Make sure your ladder is secure before you start.\n\nNext, carefully remove the old flashing and any debris. Clean the area well so the new materials will stick properly.\n\nNow, cut and fit your new aluminum flashing around the chimney. Secure it with galvanized roofing nails. Seal every seam with roofing cement to keep water out. Add the ice & water shield membrane for extra protection.\n\nFinally, apply silicone caulk to all joints and check for any gaps. Clean up your work area and dispose of old materials safely.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
