      transcript:
        "Did you know a simple hot water heater checkup can save you hundreds in repairs? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to maintain your hot water heater step by step. First, turn off the power at the breaker and close the cold water valve. This keeps you safe while you work. Next, connect a hose to the drain valve at the bottom of the tank. Open the valve and let the water drain out. Flush the tank with fresh water to clear out any sediment. Once it\u2019s empty, check the anode rod and the temperature-pressure relief valve. If they\u2019re worn or corroded, replace them. Use pipe thread sealant on any new parts. Drop a drain pan tablet in the pan to help prevent odors. When you\u2019re done, close the drain, refill the tank, and turn the power and water back on. Check for leaks and make sure everything heats up as it should. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
