      transcript:
        "Ever wondered why your GFCI outlet keeps tripping or won\u2019t reset? Today, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to repair or replace a GFCI outlet safely and easily. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your circuit breaker. Double-check that the power is off by using a voltage tester. Remove the outlet cover and look for any loose wires or visible damage.\n\nNext, press the test and reset buttons on the GFCI. If it still doesn\u2019t work, the outlet may be faulty. Carefully disconnect the wires, noting where each one goes. If the wires are loose, tighten them. If the outlet is bad, swap it for a new GFCI outlet. Use wire connectors and electrical tape to secure the connections. Attach the new outlet, screw on the cover plate, and make sure everything is snug.\n\nNow, turn the breaker back on. Test the outlet by pressing the test and reset buttons. If it works, you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
