        "Is your skylight leaking or foggy? You can fix it in just a few steps! \n\nIn this video, you'll learn how to repair a skylight, from inspection to final testing, so you can stop leaks and protect your home.\n\nFirst, inspect your skylight for cracks, leaks, or damaged flashing. Gather your tools and materials: a skylight flashing kit, roofing sealant, replacement glass pane, roofing shingles, and fasteners. Clear the area around the skylight for safe access.\n\nNext, carefully remove any old or cracked sealant from the skylight edges and flashing. Clean all surfaces well\u2014this helps the new sealant stick and keeps water out.\n\nNow, replace any broken glass, flashing, or hardware. Use a high-quality roofing sealant around the skylight and flashing. Make sure every seam is sealed tight to prevent future leaks.\n\nOnce repairs are done, test your work. Spray water over the skylight to check for leaks. If it\u2019s watertight, clean up the area and safely dispose of any debris.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
