        "Ever wondered how easy it is to fix a broken door knob yourself? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair or replace a door knob like a pro. \n\nFirst, grab your tools and a replacement door knob. Start by removing the old knob. Unscrew both sides and gently pull the knob and faceplate off the door. Keep the screws and hardware in a safe spot in case you need them later.\n\nNext, inspect the latch and strike plate. If they're worn or damaged, swap them out for new ones. Clean the area and make sure the holes in the door are clear of dust and debris. This helps your new knob fit perfectly.\n\nNow, install the new knob. Slide the latch into the edge of the door, then line up the knobs on both sides. Insert and tighten the screws. Make sure everything feels snug. Finally, test the knob and lock to be sure it turns and latches smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
