        "Ever wondered how to fix damaged bricks and make your wall look new again? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair bricks the right way. \n\nFirst, clear your work area and remove any loose or broken bricks. Clean out the old mortar from the joints so the new bricks will stick well. This takes about 1 to 2 hours.\n\nNext, mix up fresh Type N mortar, following the instructions on the bag. Set your replacement bricks in place, making sure they line up with the old ones. This step usually takes 3 to 4 hours for 100 bricks.\n\nNow, fill the joints with mortar and use a pointing tool to smooth them out. Wipe off any extra mortar from the brick faces so everything matches. This finishing step takes 2 to 3 hours.\n\nFinally, let the mortar cure. Mist the area with water to help it set, then inspect your work to make sure it\u2019s strong and looks good. This last step takes another 2 to 3 hours.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
