      transcript:
        "Want to turn your garage into a beautiful living space? In this video, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to convert a garage step by step, including what materials you\u2019ll need and how long each stage takes. \n\nFirst, start with planning and permits. Check your local building codes, draw up your plans, and get the right permits. This usually takes 20 to 30 hours but is crucial for a legal, safe conversion.\n\nNext, move to framing and insulation. Use 2x4 lumber to frame new walls, add windows or doors, and install R-13 batt insulation to keep the space comfortable. This step takes about 40 to 50 hours.\n\nNow, handle electrical, plumbing, and HVAC. Run new wiring, install outlets and recessed lights, and extend plumbing if you\u2019re adding a bathroom or sink. Install a mini-split HVAC system for heating and cooling. Plan for 50 to 60 hours here.\n\nAfter that, it\u2019s time for drywall, flooring, and finishes. Hang drywall, tape and paint, lay down subfloor and laminate flooring, and add baseboards and trim. This takes 60 to 70 hours.\n\nFinally, schedule your final inspection, fix any issues, and clean up. In 10 to 15 hours, your new living space is ready to use!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
