      transcript:
        "Did you know a simple window seal repair can save you big on energy bills? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to fix a damaged window seal step by step, so you can keep your home comfortable and efficient.\n\nFirst, inspect your window. Look for cracked, peeling, or missing sealant. Use a putty knife or scraper to remove any old caulk and debris. Wipe the area clean with a rag\u2014this helps the new sealant stick.\n\nNext, use painter\u2019s tape to mask off the edges for a neat job. Grab your window sealant\u2014silicone or polyurethane works best. Cut the tip at a 45-degree angle, load it into a caulk gun, and apply a steady bead along the seams and edges. Smooth it out with your finger or a tool for a tight, even seal.\n\nLet the sealant cure for at least 30 minutes, or as the label says. Once dry, peel off the tape and check for any gaps. Wipe away any extra sealant for a clean finish.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
