      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely cap a gas line and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn the exact steps to cap a gas line, from shutting off the gas to testing for leaks. \n\nFirst, always turn off the main gas valve. Make sure the area is well-ventilated. Use a gas detector to double-check there are no leaks before you start. \n\nNext, disconnect the appliance or fixture from the gas line. Clean the threads on the open pipe. Apply pipe thread sealant or Teflon tape to the threads. Then, screw on a brass or steel gas pipe cap. Tighten it securely with a wrench.\n\nNow, turn the gas supply back on. Use a leak detection solution or soapy water to check the capped line for leaks. Watch for bubbles or use a gas detector. If you see bubbles or smell gas, turn off the gas and tighten the cap. Always follow your local safety codes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
