      transcript:
        "Thinking about wiring your own hot tub? Here\u2019s what you need to know to do it safely and up to code. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process for hot tub electrical wiring, from planning to final inspection.\n\nFirst, always start with planning and permits. Check your hot tub\u2019s manual for electrical needs, figure out the load, and get the right permits from your local authorities.\n\nNext, shut off your main power. Measure and install 1-inch PVC electrical conduit from your main panel to the hot tub spot. Make sure you follow local electrical codes for depth and placement.\n\nNow, pull your wires through the conduit. Use 6 AWG copper THHN wire for power and 8 AWG for ground. Install a 50-amp GFCI spa panel close to the tub, then connect the wires to both your main panel and the hot tub\u2019s control box. Double-check all connections are tight and correct.\n\nFinally, schedule an inspection with your local officials. Test every connection, make sure the GFCI works, and confirm everything is safe and code-compliant.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
