      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/copper-pipe-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a leaking copper pipe without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to repair a copper pipe step by step, so you can save money and avoid water damage. \n\nFirst, shut off your main water supply and drain the pipes. Clear the area where you\u2019ll be working and gather your tools\u2014copper pipe, couplings, lead-free solder, flux, emery cloth, and a pipe cutter.\n\nNext, mark the damaged section of pipe. Use your pipe cutter to remove it. Clean the ends of the remaining pipe with emery cloth until they\u2019re shiny\u2014this helps the solder stick.\n\nNow, fit your new copper pipe section in place with couplings. Brush on flux to all joints. Heat each joint with a torch, then touch the solder to the seam. The solder should melt and flow into the joint. Let everything cool, then check your work.\n\nFinally, turn the water back on and look for leaks. If it\u2019s dry, you\u2019re done! Clean up your tools and workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
