      transcript:
        "Is your water heater not heating up? The fix might be easier than you think. \n\nToday, I\u2019ll show you how to replace a water heater element step by step. \n\nFirst, safety comes first. Turn off the power at the breaker. Then, shut off the water supply to the heater. Attach a hose to the drain valve and empty the tank\u2014this usually takes about 20 minutes.\n\nNext, remove the old element. Disconnect the wires from the heating element. Use an element wrench to unscrew and pull out the faulty element. Take your time\u2014don\u2019t force it.\n\nNow, install the new element. Wrap the threads with Teflon tape for a tight seal. Place the new gasket or O-ring, then screw in the new element and tighten it. Reconnect the wires.\n\nClose the drain, turn the water supply back on, and let the tank fill up. Once it\u2019s full, restore power at the breaker. Check for leaks and make sure the heater works.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
