      transcript:
        "Want to make your walls look brand new? Let\u2019s walk through how to install sheetrock step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn exactly what you need, how to do it, and how long it takes.\n\nFirst, clear your work area and gather all your materials: sheetrock panels, joint compound, drywall screws, paper tape, and corner bead. Inspect the framing and mark your stud locations. This helps you line up the panels perfectly.\n\nNext, measure your walls and ceilings. Mark your cut lines on the sheetrock, then use a utility knife or saw to cut each panel to fit. Take your time\u2014accurate cuts make the job easier.\n\nNow, hang the sheetrock. Lift each panel into place and fasten it to the studs with drywall screws. Stagger the seams for extra strength. Make sure everything is tight and flat.\n\nAfter hanging, it\u2019s time for taping and mudding. Apply paper tape over the seams, then cover with joint compound. Feather the edges and let it dry. You\u2019ll need a couple of coats for a smooth finish.\n\nFinally, sand the dried compound until the surface is seamless. Clean up all dust and debris so you\u2019re ready for paint or texture.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
