      transcript:
        "Want to build a strong retaining wall that lasts for years? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to build a concrete block retaining wall, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, clear your site and mark out the wall\u2019s layout. Excavate a trench deep and wide enough for your wall, based on your soil conditions. This is key for stability.\n\nNext, pour in about two tons of gravel for the base. Compact it well and make sure it\u2019s level. This gives your wall a solid foundation.\n\nNow, start laying your first row of concrete blocks. Check for level as you go. Stagger each new row, and use block adhesive to lock them in place. As you build, lay a 4-inch perforated drainage pipe behind the wall and backfill with gravel. This prevents water buildup and keeps your wall strong.\n\nOnce the wall is up, finish backfilling with soil. Compact it, add topsoil or landscaping, and clean up the site. Inspect your wall for stability before you\u2019re done.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
