      transcript:
        "Did you know a clean roof can add years to its life and boost curb appeal? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to safely and effectively clean your roof like a pro. \n\nFirst, get your materials ready: roof cleaning solution, plastic sheeting, scrub brushes, and a safety harness kit. For a 1,000 square foot roof, you\u2019ll need about 5 gallons of cleaning solution, 2 rolls of plastic sheeting, 2 scrub brushes, and 1 safety harness kit.\n\nStart with site preparation. Clear the area around your house, set up ladders or scaffolding, and always use a safety harness. Protect your landscaping and cover any outdoor furniture with plastic sheeting.\n\nNext, remove loose debris from the roof and gutters. Use a broom or blower to clear away leaves, branches, and moss. Collect all waste for proper disposal.\n\nNow, mix your roof-safe cleaning solution as directed. Apply it evenly to the roof, focusing on stained or mossy areas. Let it sit for the time recommended by the manufacturer.\n\nAfter that, gently rinse the roof with low-pressure water. Scrub any stubborn stains with your brushes. Be careful to keep runoff away from storm drains.\n\nFinally, inspect the roof for missed spots or damage. Clean up all materials, make sure gutters and downspouts are clear, and restore the area to its original condition.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
