        "Is your door sticking, sagging, or showing signs of rot? Let\u2019s fix that door frame fast and make it look new again! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a damaged door frame step by step, using simple tools and materials. \n\nFirst, check the frame for cracks, rot, or warping. Grab your wood filler, replacement jamb, screws, shims, caulk, and paint. Next, carefully remove any broken or rotted wood with a pry bar and saw. Clean out all debris so you have a solid base to work with.\n\nNow, cut and fit your new wood pieces or fill small gaps with wood filler. Secure everything with screws or nails. Sand the area smooth, and use a level to make sure the frame is straight and plumb. \n\nFor the finishing touches, prime and paint or stain the repaired area to match the rest of the frame. Reinstall any hardware you removed, and check that the door opens and closes smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
