        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/roof-inspection/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Did you know a simple roof inspection can save you thousands in repairs? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to inspect your roof safely and spot problems before they get worse. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: rent a sturdy ladder, use a safety harness kit, and have something to take notes and photos. Always put safety first\u2014never skip the harness.\n\nStart with a visual assessment. Walk around your home and look up at the roof. Check for missing shingles, debris, or any visible damage. Use binoculars if you have them.\n\nNext, carefully climb onto the roof. Walk the surface and inspect flashing, vents, and valleys. Look for cracked, loose, or rusted areas\u2014these are common leak spots, especially after harsh weather.\n\nDon\u2019t forget the gutters. Make sure they\u2019re clear of leaves and debris. Check that downspouts are attached and water flows away from your house.\n\nFinally, take clear photos of any issues. Write a short report with your findings and suggest repairs or maintenance.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
