      transcript:
        "Did you know a clogged or damaged dryer vent can be a hidden fire risk? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely replace a dryer vent in just a few easy steps. First, unplug your dryer and move it away from the wall. Disconnect the old vent hose and remove the exterior vent cover. Clear out any lint or debris from the vent opening\u2014this helps prevent future clogs. Next, attach your new 4-inch flexible aluminum vent duct to the dryer. Secure it tightly with duct clamps. Now, install the new exterior vent hood, making sure it fits snugly to keep out drafts and pests. Use mounting screws and foil duct tape for a solid seal. Once everything\u2019s in place, reconnect your dryer and slide it back. Run a quick test cycle to check for good airflow. Finally, clean up your work area and dispose of the old vent parts properly. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
