      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix your vertical blinds without calling a pro? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to repair vertical blinds step by step, saving you time and money. \n\nFirst, check your blinds for any broken or misaligned slats. Gently unclip and remove any damaged slats from the headrail. Take your time so you don\u2019t break the clips.\n\nNext, grab your replacement slats and any new carrier stems, wands, or chains you need. Install the new slats by clipping them into place. If a carrier stem is broken, swap it out for a new one. Make sure all moving parts, like the chain or wand, are working smoothly.\n\nNow, reattach all the slats to the headrail. Align them so they hang straight. Test the tilt and draw functions to make sure everything works. If anything sticks, double-check your installation.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your blinds should look and work like new. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
