      transcript:
        "Did you know dirty ductwork can lower your air quality and energy efficiency? Today, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to clean your home\u2019s ductwork step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off your HVAC system. Inspect the ductwork for any damage, and cover all vents and registers with plastic sheeting to keep dust out of your rooms. \n\nNext, remove vent covers and access panels. Set up your HEPA vacuum and duct cleaning brushes so you can reach every section of duct. \n\nNow, use the brushes to loosen dust and debris inside the ducts. At the same time, run the vacuum to pull out all the contaminants. This process usually takes two to three hours for a 2,000 square foot home. \n\nAfter the ducts are clean, wash the vent covers, registers, and any accessible HVAC parts. Reinstall everything and make sure all panels are sealed tight. \n\nFinally, turn your HVAC system back on. Check that airflow is strong, and clean up any mess around your work area. Your ductwork is now clean and your air is fresher! \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
