      transcript:
        "Want to replace your old tile and get a flawless finish? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to replace floor tiles step by step, from prep to final cleanup. \n\nFirst, clear the area and move out any furniture. Protect nearby surfaces with drop cloths. Carefully remove the old tiles using a chisel and hammer. Scrape away any leftover adhesive, then clean and level the subfloor. This is key for a smooth install.\n\nNext, plan your tile layout. Dry-fit a few tiles to make sure your pattern looks good and you don\u2019t end up with tiny slivers at the edges. Mix your thinset mortar and spread it evenly with a notched trowel. Set each tile in place, using spacers to keep the gaps even. Check that everything is level as you go.\n\nOnce the tiles are set, let them cure for a few hours. Then, mix your grout and press it into the joints with a rubber float. Wipe away extra grout with a damp sponge. Let the grout cure, then apply sealer if needed. Finally, reinstall any fixtures and give the area a good clean.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
