      transcript:
        "Want to plant a tree that thrives for years? Watch this before you dig! In this video, you'll learn the right way to plant a tree, step by step, so it grows strong and healthy. \n\nFirst, pick a spot with plenty of sunlight and enough space for the tree to grow. Clear away any weeds or debris, and loosen the soil. This helps the roots spread out easily.\n\nNext, dig a hole that's twice as wide as the tree's root ball, but only as deep. Place the tree in the hole. Make sure the root flare\u2014the spot where the trunk widens at the base\u2014is level with the ground. Backfill the hole with the soil you dug out, packing it gently around the roots.\n\nNow, water the tree well to settle the soil. Add a 2 to 3 inch layer of mulch around the base, but keep it a few inches away from the trunk. Mulch helps keep the soil moist and protects the roots from heat and cold.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
