      transcript:
        "Is your well pump failing and you\u2019re not sure where to start? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to replace a submersible well pump safely and efficiently. \n\nFirst, always shut off the power to your well pump at the breaker. Double-check with a voltage tester to make sure there\u2019s no electricity running. Remove the well cap to access the pump assembly.\n\nNext, disconnect the plumbing and electrical wires. Carefully pull the old pump and piping out of the well. Inspect everything\u2014look for worn wires, cracked pipes, or damaged fittings.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install the new pump. Attach your new submersible pump to the poly pipe and secure all fittings, including a check valve and torque arrestor. Connect the new electrical wire and use waterproof connectors and electrical tape. Lower the pump assembly back into the well, making sure not to kink the pipe or wire. Secure the well seal or cap.\n\nFinally, restore power and prime the system. Check for leaks, test water pressure, and make sure the pump runs smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
