      transcript:
        "Want to stop gutter leaks for good? Here\u2019s how to caulk your gutters like a pro. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the exact steps to seal gutter seams and prevent water damage. \n\nFirst, put on gloves and grab some rags. Clean out all leaves, dirt, and old caulk from your gutters and joints. Check for any rust or damage\u2014fix these before you start caulking.\n\nNext, load a tube of gutter sealant into your caulk gun. Apply a steady bead of caulk along every seam, end cap, and joint. Use your gloved finger or a tool to smooth the caulk for a tight, watertight seal.\n\nLet the caulk cure for at least an hour, or as the label says. Once it\u2019s dry, run water through your gutters to check for leaks. If you see any drips, add more caulk as needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
