      transcript:
        "Did you know a broken garage door cable can leave your car trapped? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely replace your garage door cables step by step. First, disconnect your garage door opener and fully open the door. Use locking pliers or clamps to keep it from moving\u2014safety first! Next, release the tension from the springs. Carefully remove the old cables from the bottom brackets and drums. While you\u2019re there, check all the hardware for any signs of wear. Now, grab your new lift cables and attach them to the bottom brackets and drums. Restore the spring tension, then test the door several times. Make sure it moves smoothly and stays balanced. That\u2019s it! You\u2019ve just replaced your garage door cables and saved yourself a service call. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
