      transcript:
        "Did you know hidden mold in your crawl space can ruin your home's air quality? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to safely remove mold from your crawl space and keep it from coming back. \n\nFirst, get ready for safety. Seal off the crawl space with plastic sheeting, set up fans for ventilation, and put on N95 respirators, gloves, and protective coveralls. Clear out any debris so you have safe access.\n\nNext, it's time to tackle the mold. Spray EPA-approved mold remover on all affected surfaces. Use scrub brushes to clean every spot. Remove and bag any materials that can't be cleaned, like insulation or wood that's too far gone. Use contractor-grade disposal bags to keep things contained.\n\nAfter cleaning, dry out the crawl space. Set up fans and a dehumidifier. Run them for 8 to 10 hours, and check humidity levels to make sure the area is completely dry. Mold loves moisture, so this step is key.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Look for any missed spots and treat them. Apply a mold preventative spray, and fix any leaks or drainage issues to stop future mold growth.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
