        "Is your door slamming shut or refusing to close smoothly? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to repair a door closer like a pro. \n\nFirst, inspect the door closer. Look for oil leaks, loose screws, or parts that look out of place. Check if the door is misaligned or if the closer is making strange noises. \n\nNext, grab your adjustment tools and a screwdriver. Tighten any loose mounting screws. If the door is closing too fast or too slow, use the adjustment screws to set the right speed and tension. If you spot damaged seals or a bent arm, replace those parts with new hardware. \n\nFinally, test your work. Open and close the door several times. Make small adjustments until the door moves smoothly and quietly. Clean up your tools and the area. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
