      transcript:
        "Want to make old windows look new again\u2014without replacing them? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to reglaze a window step by step, so you get a tight seal and a clean finish. \n\nFirst, put on safety gloves. Use a putty knife to carefully remove the old glazing putty and any loose glass from the window frame. Take your time\u2014this step usually takes about 40 minutes per window.\n\nNext, clean the frame well. Sand any rough spots, then brush on primer to any bare wood. Let the primer dry completely. This helps the new putty stick and protects the wood.\n\nNow, press fresh glazing putty into the frame. Set your new glass pane in place, then secure it with glazier points. Smooth more putty over the edges for a tight, weatherproof seal. Make sure all sides are covered and the putty is even.\n\nOnce the putty sets, finish with paint for a long-lasting result.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
