        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/lay-sod/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want a lush green lawn\u2014fast? Laying sod is the quickest way to transform bare ground into beautiful grass. In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to lay sod like a pro.\n\nFirst, clear your yard. Remove old grass, weeds, and rocks. Till the soil about 2\u20133 inches deep. Add compost or topsoil if your dirt is thin or sandy. Rake it smooth and level.\n\nNext, grade the soil so water drains away from your house. Lightly water the area to make the ground damp, not muddy.\n\nNow, start laying sod along a straight edge, like a driveway. Place each piece tightly against the next, staggering seams like bricks. Press the edges together\u2014no gaps! Use a sharp knife to trim around trees or flower beds.\n\nOnce all the sod is down, water it deeply. Then, use a lawn roller to press the sod into the soil. This helps the roots connect.\n\nFor the first two weeks, keep the sod moist but not soggy. Stay off the grass until it roots. Mow when it gets about 3 inches tall.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
