      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/toilet-flush-valve-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a toilet that just won't stop running? Today, I'll show you how to replace a toilet flush valve step by step, so you can stop leaks and save water. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply to your toilet. Flush to empty the tank, then soak up any leftover water with a sponge. Next, disconnect the water supply line. Remove the tank from the bowl by unscrewing the bolts underneath. Carefully lift the tank off and set it aside. Now, take out the old flush valve assembly from inside the tank.\n\nGrab your new flush valve kit. Place the new valve in the tank opening, making sure the seals are tight. Secure it with the hardware that comes in the kit. Double-check for a snug fit to prevent leaks.\n\nReattach the tank to the bowl and reconnect the water supply line. Turn the water back on and let the tank fill. Test the flush a few times to make sure everything works and there are no leaks.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
