      transcript:
        "Want to build a wood fence that lasts for years? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a pressure-treated wood fence, from start to finish.\n\nFirst, clear your fence line and mark where each post will go. Double-check your property lines and local codes before you start digging. Gather all your materials: fence panels, posts, concrete, nails or screws, and gate hardware.\n\nNext, dig your post holes about 2 feet deep. Set each 4x4 post in concrete, making sure they\u2019re straight and evenly spaced. Let the concrete cure\u2014this is key for a sturdy fence.\n\nOnce the posts are solid, attach your horizontal rails, then secure the fence panels or pickets. Use a level to keep everything straight and maintain even gaps between boards.\n\nNow, install your gate. Attach the hinges and latch, and make sure the gate swings smoothly. Tighten all hardware for safety.\n\nFinally, trim any extra post height, apply a wood sealant or stain, and clean up the area. Inspect your work to make sure it\u2019s strong and looks great.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
