      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/pipe-soldering/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to make leak-free copper pipe joints that last for decades? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to solder copper pipes like a pro, from prep to testing. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply and drain the pipes. Clean your work area and gather all your tools: copper pipe, fittings, lead-free solder, flux, emery cloth, and a pipe cleaning brush. Safety gear is a must.\n\nNext, cut your pipes to length and deburr the edges. Use emery cloth and a brush to clean the pipe ends and fittings until they're shiny. Dry fit everything to make sure it lines up right.\n\nNow, apply flux evenly to the pipe ends and inside the fittings. Assemble the joints, making sure they're snug and ready for soldering.\n\nHeat each joint with a torch. Touch the solder to the joint\u2014when it melts and flows around, you're good. Let it cool, then inspect for full coverage. Wipe away any extra flux.\n\nFinally, turn the water back on and check for leaks. Test the system under pressure. Clean up your tools and work area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
