      transcript:
        "Want a stunning patio that lasts for years? Here\u2019s how to install pavers the right way, step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to prep your site, lay a solid base, set your pavers, and finish like a pro. \n\nFirst, mark out your patio area. Remove grass and debris, then dig down about 7 inches. Make sure the ground is level and slopes away from your house for drainage.\n\nNext, spread about 4 inches of gravel base. Compact it well with a plate compactor. Add a 1-inch layer of sand on top and level it out. This gives your pavers a stable, even surface.\n\nNow, lay your pavers in your chosen pattern. Keep the gaps even. Use a masonry saw or splitter to cut pavers for the edges. Install edge restraints around the border to keep everything tight.\n\nFor the final touch, pour polymeric sand over the pavers. Sweep it into the joints, then compact the surface again. Rinse off any extra sand and check that everything is level and solid.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
