      transcript:
        "Thinking about upgrading your electrical panel? Here\u2019s what you need to know before you start. In this video, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process to safely upgrade to a 200 amp electrical panel, including the materials, timeline, and key safety tips. \n\nFirst, always shut off the main power and double-check that all circuits are de-energized. Set up safety barriers around your work area. Next, disconnect all branch circuits and carefully remove the old panel. Inspect the wiring and the wall behind the panel to make sure everything meets your local electrical codes.\n\nNow, mount your new 200 amp panel. Connect the main service wires, then reattach each branch circuit. Use a grounding bar kit and 6 AWG copper wire for proper grounding. Install new circuit breakers, wire connectors, and label each breaker clearly with a panel label kit.\n\nOnce everything is connected, schedule an inspection with your local authorities. Make any corrections if needed. Only restore power after you pass inspection.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
