      transcript:
        "Want perfectly smooth walls without the mess? Let\u2019s break down drywall sanding step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to prep, sand, and clean up like a pro\u2014so your walls are ready for paint or primer.\n\nFirst, clear your work area and cover floors and furniture with plastic sheeting. Good ventilation is key, so open a window if you can. Put on a dust mask and gather your sanding sponge, pole sander, and sandpaper.\n\nStart with medium-grit sandpaper on a pole sander or sanding block. Smooth out all seams and screw holes, feathering the edges so they blend into the wall. Take your time\u2014this is where the magic happens.\n\nNext, switch to fine-grit sandpaper for corners, edges, and any spots that need extra attention. Use good lighting to check for rough patches or ridges. Run your hand over the surface to feel for any bumps.\n\nWhen you\u2019re done sanding, vacuum up the dust and wipe down the walls. Remove your plastic sheeting and inspect everything. If it\u2019s smooth and even, you\u2019re ready to prime or paint.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
