      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/drywall-hole-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a hole in your drywall so it looks brand new? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair a drywall hole like a pro. \n\nFirst, get your materials: a drywall patch, joint compound, drywall tape, sandpaper, primer, and touch-up paint. You\u2019ll also need a utility knife and a drop cloth.\n\nStart by preparing the area. Clear the space, lay down your drop cloth, and use the utility knife to clean up the edges of the hole. This helps the patch stick better.\n\nNext, cut your drywall patch to fit the hole. Place it in the opening, then secure it with joint compound and drywall tape. Make sure the patch is flush with the wall. Smooth out the compound so there are no bumps.\n\nLet it dry, then apply another thin layer of joint compound. Once that\u2019s dry, sand it smooth with sandpaper. Wipe away any dust.\n\nFinally, apply primer over the patch, let it dry, and finish with touch-up paint to match your wall.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
