        "Is your electric water heater not heating up? Let\u2019s fix it fast and safely. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair an electric water heater step by step, from shutting off power to testing your work. \n\nFirst, turn off the electricity at the breaker and shut off the water supply to your heater. Let the unit cool down before you start. \n\nNext, attach a hose to the drain valve and empty the tank. Remove the access panels. Check the heating elements, thermostats, and wiring for any visible damage or corrosion. \n\nIf you spot a faulty heating element or thermostat, use the right tools to remove and replace them. Make sure all electrical connections are tight and the new parts are installed correctly. Use wire connectors and a little Teflon tape if needed. \n\nOnce repairs are done, close the drain valve and refill the tank. Restore power at the breaker. Watch for leaks and make sure the heater is working properly. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
