        "Ever wondered how to create an accurate as-built survey for your project? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to document your building exactly as it stands. \n\nFirst, start with a site walkthrough. Review your project scope, gather any existing plans, and walk the site to spot key features and access points. This helps you plan your survey and avoid surprises.\n\nNext, it's time for field measurements. Use a 100-foot measuring tape and a laser distance measurer to record all dimensions. Don't forget to note the locations of utilities and structural elements. Take clear photos with your smartphone for reference. Use graph paper or a field book to sketch and write down everything as you go.\n\nOnce you have your data, move on to drafting. Transfer your notes and measurements into accurate drawings or digital models. Make sure every wall, door, and utility is shown as it really is.\n\nFinally, review your work. Double-check all measurements and drawings for accuracy. Fix any mistakes, then submit your final as-built survey to the right people.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
