      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a cracked tile without damaging the rest of your floor? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair cracked tiles like a pro. \n\nFirst, use a grout saw to carefully remove the grout around the damaged tile. Take your time\u2014this helps protect the tiles next to it. Next, grab a chisel and hammer. Gently tap to lift out the cracked tile. If it\u2019s stubborn, break it into smaller pieces for easier removal.\n\nNow, clean the exposed area. Scrape away old adhesive and vacuum up any dust. The surface should be smooth and debris-free before you move on.\n\nSpread a layer of thinset mortar where the new tile will go. Press the replacement tile into place, using spacers to keep it lined up with the others. Let the adhesive set as the package recommends\u2014usually a few hours.\n\nOnce it\u2019s set, mix your grout and fill the joints around the new tile. Wipe away any extra grout with a damp sponge. When the grout dries, apply a grout sealer to protect your work and match the finish.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
