      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a leaking drain pipe without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair a 4-inch PVC drain pipe like a pro. \n\nFirst, find the damaged pipe and clear the area. Look for leaks or blockages so you know exactly what needs fixing. This usually takes about 30 to 45 minutes.\n\nNext, shut off the water supply. Cut out the bad section of pipe using a saw. Clean the pipe ends so your new parts fit tight. Make sure your replacement pipe and fittings match your existing plumbing. This step takes about an hour.\n\nNow, install the new pipe or coupling. Use PVC primer and cement to seal the joints. Secure everything with pipe hangers or straps. Double-check that all connections are watertight. This part also takes about an hour.\n\nFinally, turn the water back on and check for leaks. Flush the system to make sure it\u2019s working. Clean up your work area and throw away the old pipe safely.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
