      transcript:
        "Want to give your kitchen a fresh new look in just one weekend? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a tile backsplash like a pro. \n\nFirst, prep your wall. Clean and dry the surface, remove any outlet covers, and patch up holes or bumps. A smooth wall helps your tiles stick better.\n\nNext, plan your layout. Measure your backsplash area, mark straight guidelines, and dry-fit your tiles. Cut tiles to fit around outlets and edges using a tile cutter or wet saw.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install. Spread tile adhesive on the wall with a notched trowel. Press each tile into place, using spacers to keep your grout lines even. Work in small sections so the adhesive doesn\u2019t dry out.\n\nOnce the tiles are set, remove the spacers. Mix your grout and press it into the gaps with a rubber float. Wipe off extra grout with a damp sponge and let it cure as recommended.\n\nFor a polished finish, add edge trim and seal the grout if needed. That\u2019s it\u2014your backsplash is done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
