        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/gutter-sealing/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Leaky gutters can cause big headaches, but sealing them is easier than you think! In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to seal your gutters and stop leaks for good. \n\nFirst, grab your supplies: gutter sealant, a cleaning brush, disposable gloves, and some rags. Start by cleaning out all debris from your gutters and downspouts. Look for cracks, holes, or loose joints\u2014these are the spots you'll need to seal.\n\nNext, dry the gutters completely. Use a wire brush to scrub away any rust or old sealant. Wipe everything down so the surface is clean and ready for new sealant.\n\nNow, put on your gloves. Apply gutter sealant to every seam, joint, and damaged area. Smooth it out with your finger or a tool to make sure it covers well and seals tight.\n\nLet the sealant cure as the label says. Once it's dry, run water through your gutters to check for leaks. If you spot any, touch them up with more sealant.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
