        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/install-220v-outlet/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to power big appliances? Here\u2019s how to install a 220-volt outlet safely and step by step.\n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to plan, wire, and test a 220v outlet for your home or job site.\n\nFirst, pick the best spot for your outlet. Make sure it\u2019s close to where you need heavy-duty power, like for a dryer or workshop tool. Choose the right double-pole breaker size for your appliance\u2014usually 30 or 40 amps. Before you touch anything, turn off the main power at your breaker panel.\n\nNext, run 10-gauge, 3-conductor copper wire from your panel to the new outlet location. Use wire staples or clamps to secure the wire along the way. Mount your electrical box at the chosen spot. Strip the wire ends, then connect the black and red wires to the hot terminals, the white to neutral, and the bare copper to ground on your 220v outlet. Attach the outlet to the box and cover it with a plate.\n\nNow, install your double-pole breaker in the panel. Connect the black and red wires to the breaker, white to the neutral bar, and ground to the ground bar. Double-check all connections. Restore power and use a voltage tester to make sure your new outlet works.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
