      transcript:
        "Is your shower leaking or losing pressure? Let\u2019s fix it step by step! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to diagnose, repair, and seal a shower like a pro. \n\nFirst, inspect your shower for leaks, low water pressure, or broken parts. Look for signs like water stains, loose tiles, or a dripping handle. Figure out if the problem is a bad valve, worn gasket, or cracked tile.\n\nNext, turn off the water supply. Remove the showerhead, handle, trim, or any tiles you need to get to the damaged area. Take your time\u2014don\u2019t break anything you don\u2019t have to.\n\nNow, replace what\u2019s broken. Install a new valve, gasket, or tile. Use the right plumbing fittings and make sure everything is tight. Put the showerhead and handle back on.\n\nTurn the water back on and test for leaks. If everything works, seal around the fixtures and tiles with silicone caulk to keep water out.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
