      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/install-circuit-breaker/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely install a new circuit breaker in your home? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to do it right and keep your electrical system safe. \n\nFirst, always start by turning off the main power at your breaker panel. Use a voltage tester to double-check that all power is off. Remove the panel cover to access the breaker slots\u2014take your time and be careful.\n\nNext, grab your new circuit breaker. Insert it into the open slot in the panel. Connect your circuit wire\u2014usually Romex 12/2 or 14/2\u2014to the breaker terminal. Tighten the screw so the wire is secure, and make sure all connections are snug. Use wire connectors and mounting screws as needed.\n\nOnce everything is connected, replace the panel cover. Turn the main power back on. Flip the new breaker to the ON position and test your new circuit to make sure it works.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
