      transcript:
        "Want to make your molding look brand new with a pro-level paint job? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to paint molding so it looks sharp and lasts. \n\nFirst, gather your supplies: trim-grade interior paint, painter\u2019s tape, drop cloths, sandpaper, caulk, and angled brushes. For 200 linear feet, you\u2019ll need about a gallon of paint, two brushes, and one of each other item.\n\nStart with surface prep. Clean the molding, fill any nail holes with caulk, sand smooth, and wipe away dust. This helps the paint stick and look smooth.\n\nNext, tape off the edges and cover floors or walls with drop cloths. This keeps paint only where you want it.\n\nNow, prime the molding. Use a brush to apply primer evenly. Let it dry fully\u2014don\u2019t rush this step.\n\nTime to paint! Use an angled brush for clean lines. Paint in long, even strokes. Let it dry, then add a second coat if needed.\n\nFinally, remove the tape, clean your brushes, and check for any missed spots or touch-ups.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
