      transcript:
        "Want to stop drafts and save on energy bills? Installing a door sweep is a quick fix you can do yourself.\n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to measure, remove, and install a new door sweep for a perfect seal.\n\nFirst, grab a tape measure and check the width of your door. Pick a door sweep that matches the width and fits the gap at the bottom. Most sweeps cost between $8 and $25, plus a set of mounting screws.\n\nNext, if there\u2019s an old sweep, unscrew or pull it off. Clean the bottom edge of the door so the new sweep sticks or fits well.\n\nNow, line up the new sweep with the bottom of the door. Mark where the screws will go. Drill small pilot holes if needed. Attach the sweep using screws or adhesive, making sure it\u2019s snug but not dragging on the floor.\n\nOpen and close the door to check the fit. Adjust if needed. That\u2019s it\u2014your door is now sealed!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
