      transcript:
        "Want to make your stucco look brand new and last for years? In this video, you'll learn exactly how to paint stucco the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, prep your surface. Clean the stucco, fix any cracks with caulk, and scrape off loose paint. This helps your new paint stick and last longer.\n\nNext, mask off windows, doors, and trim with painter\u2019s tape and drop cloths. Then, roll or brush on a masonry primer. This seals the stucco and gives you even color.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to paint. Use a heavy nap roller or sprayer to apply two coats of exterior acrylic paint. Let the first coat dry before adding the second for a strong, even finish.\n\nAfter painting, remove the tape, touch up edges with a brush, and check for missed spots. Make sure every area looks clean and sharp.\n\nFinally, clean your tools and throw away used materials safely. Walk through the project to make sure you\u2019re happy with the results.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
