      transcript:
        "Want to make your home the brightest on the block this Christmas? In this video, you'll learn exactly how to plan and install professional-grade Christmas lighting, step by step. \n\nFirst, start with design and planning. Meet with your client or decide your own style. Measure the areas you want to light\u2014roofs, windows, trees, and walkways. Sketch a simple plan so you know how many lights and materials you\u2019ll need.\n\nNext, gather your materials. For 1,000 linear feet, you\u2019ll need about 10 strands of 100-foot LED lights, 4 outdoor extension cords, 200 light clips, an outdoor timer, and weatherproof electrical tape. Test every light strand before you start\u2014replace any that don\u2019t work.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install. Use light clips to attach lights securely along the roofline, windows, and landscaping. Run extension cords safely, keeping connections off the ground. Use weatherproof tape to seal any exposed plugs. Set up your outdoor timer so the lights turn on and off automatically.\n\nFinally, power everything on. Walk around and check for dark spots or crooked lines. Adjust as needed until your display looks perfect.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
