      transcript:
        "Want to upgrade your floors without glue or nails? Watch this! Today, you'll learn how to install a floating floor step by step, so you can get pro results at home. \n\nFirst, clear out the room and remove the baseboards. Make sure your subfloor is clean, dry, and level. This is key for a smooth install.\n\nNext, roll out your underlayment. Trim it to fit, and make sure the seams are tight and edges touch the walls. This helps cushion the floor and reduce noise.\n\nNow, start laying your flooring planks. Begin in one corner, and use spacers to keep a small gap along the walls for expansion. Stagger the joints as you go for a natural look. Snap the planks together, row by row.\n\nOnce the floor is down, reinstall your baseboards or add quarter round molding. Remove the spacers and give your new floor a good clean.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve got a beautiful floating floor. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
