      transcript:
        "Is your dryer taking forever to dry clothes? Your vent might be the problem! \n\nIn this video, you'll learn how to repair a dryer vent safely and efficiently. \n\nFirst, unplug your dryer and pull it away from the wall. Remove the vent hose from the back and check for lint, damage, or blockages. A clogged vent is a fire hazard and wastes energy.\n\nNext, use a vent brush or vacuum to clean out the hose and the wall duct. If you see any damaged duct sections or loose clamps, replace them with new ones. Make sure everything fits tightly\u2014use duct clamps and foil tape for a secure seal.\n\nNow, reattach the vent hose to the dryer and the wall. Push the dryer back into place and plug it in. Run the dryer to test airflow. If air is moving freely, you\u2019re all set!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
