      transcript:
        "Cracked bathroom tiles? You can fix them like a pro in just a few hours. In this video, you'll learn how to remove damaged tiles, install new ones, and seal everything for a long-lasting finish. \n\nFirst, grab your chisel and hammer. Carefully chip out the broken tiles. Take your time\u2014work slowly to avoid damaging nearby tiles. Once the tiles are out, scrape away the old adhesive. Make sure the surface is smooth and clean before moving on.\n\nNext, mix your thinset mortar. Spread a thin, even layer where the new tiles will go. Press each replacement tile into place, using spacers to keep the lines straight. Double-check that all tiles are level. Let the tiles set for as long as the manufacturer recommends.\n\nNow, it's time to grout. Mix your grout and press it into the gaps between tiles. Wipe away any extra grout with a damp sponge. Let the grout dry, then apply a grout sealer to protect against water and stains.\n\nThat's it! Your bathroom tiles look brand new. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
