        "Did you know a fire door can save lives in an emergency? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a fire-rated door step by step, so you can protect your property and meet code. \n\nFirst, clear your work area and gather your tools. Remove the old door and hardware. Check the opening and frame\u2014make sure they meet your local fire safety standards.\n\nNext, install or reinforce the fire-rated frame. Hang the prehung fire door, following the manufacturer\u2019s instructions. Use fire-rated hinges\u2014usually three per door. Make sure the door is level and swings freely. Check the gaps around the door; they should be even and meet code.\n\nNow, fit the fire-rated hardware. This includes the door closer, lockset, and intumescent seal kit. Install the threshold or sweep at the bottom. Test the door: it should close by itself and latch every time. Double-check that all parts are fire-rated and compliant with your local regulations.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
