      transcript:
        "Want to make your siding look brand new in just a few hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to pressure wash your siding safely and effectively, step by step. \n\nFirst, get your materials: rent a pressure washer, grab some siding-safe detergent, plastic sheeting, and painter\u2019s tape. You\u2019ll also need safety gear like goggles and gloves.\n\nStart with site prep. Move outdoor furniture, cover plants with plastic sheeting, and close all windows. Check your siding for any damage and brush off loose debris.\n\nNext, set up your pressure washer. Attach the right nozzle, connect to a water supply, and put on your safety gear. Always read the manufacturer\u2019s instructions before you start.\n\nNow, apply the detergent using a low-pressure nozzle. Work from the bottom up, and let it sit for about 10 minutes to break down dirt and mildew.\n\nTime to rinse! Switch to a higher-pressure nozzle. Start at the top and work your way down, keeping the nozzle about a foot from the siding. Move in smooth, even strokes to avoid streaks or damage.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Rinse off your plants, remove coverings, and clean up your tools. Dispose of any waste properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
