      transcript:
        "Want to make your old radiator look brand new? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to paint a radiator the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off your radiator and let it cool down. Move any furniture out of the way. Lay down a drop cloth to protect your floors, and use a degreaser or cleaner to wipe off all the dust, dirt, and grease. This helps the paint stick better.\n\nNext, grab a wire brush or sandpaper and lightly sand the radiator. This smooths out rough spots and helps the paint grip. Wipe away any dust. Use painter\u2019s tape to mask off the wall and floor around the radiator so you don\u2019t get paint where you don\u2019t want it.\n\nNow, apply a metal primer if your paint needs it. Let it dry completely. Then, use a high-heat radiator paint\u2014either spray or brush-on. Apply thin, even coats for the best finish. Let the paint dry fully before turning the radiator back on.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
