        "Is your door sticking or not closing right? The problem could be a damaged door jamb\u2014and you can fix it yourself! In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to repair a door jamb step by step, so your door works like new.\n\nFirst, check the door jamb for any cracks, rot, or broken wood. Mark the damaged spots. Use a pry bar and a saw to carefully remove the bad sections. Take your time\u2014don\u2019t damage the surrounding trim.\n\nNext, measure the pieces you removed. Cut new jamb pieces from a replacement kit to match the size. Attach them with wood glue and finishing nails. Make sure everything lines up, so your door opens and closes smoothly.\n\nNow, fill any seams or nail holes with wood filler. Let it dry, then sand the area until it\u2019s smooth. Finish by painting or staining to match the rest of your door frame.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your door jamb is as good as new. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
