      transcript:
        "Did you know a properly installed fire alarm can save lives in seconds? In this video, you'll learn exactly how to install fire alarms safely and up to code. \n\nFirst, start with a site assessment. Walk through your space and decide where alarms should go\u2014usually in every bedroom, hallway, and each floor. Make sure you follow your local fire codes.\n\nNext, gather your materials: smoke or fire alarms, mounting hardware, electrical wire, wire connectors, and batteries. For a standard job, plan for about 10 alarms, 200 feet of wire, and all the connectors and batteries you'll need.\n\nNow, mount the brackets at your chosen spots. If your alarms are hardwired, run 14/2 NM-B wire between units. Use wire connectors to join wires safely. If they're battery-powered, insert fresh batteries before mounting.\n\nOnce installed, connect the alarms to power or insert batteries. If your alarms are interconnected, program them so they all sound together. Test each alarm to make sure it works.\n\nFinally, show everyone how the alarms work and review basic maintenance\u2014like changing batteries and testing monthly. Give them any manuals or paperwork.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
