      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix cracked or damaged plaster walls like a pro? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair plaster walls so they look brand new. \n\nFirst, clear the area and cover your floors and furniture to protect from dust. Scrape away any loose plaster and clean up all debris. \n\nNext, apply a bonding agent to any exposed lath. Mix your plaster patch compound, then fill in holes and cracks. Use a putty knife to smooth the surface so it matches the rest of the wall.\n\nLet the patch dry completely. Then, sand the area until it\u2019s smooth and even. Wipe away any dust with a damp cloth.\n\nNow, apply a coat of primer to the repaired spots. Once it\u2019s dry, paint over the area to match your wall color. Remove your coverings and clean up your tools.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your wall is as good as new. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
