      transcript:
        "Is your window frame rotting or falling apart? Let\u2019s fix it step by step! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a damaged window frame so it looks and works like new. \n\nFirst, inspect the window frame for rot, cracks, or loose trim. Gather your tools and materials: wood trim, wood filler or epoxy, primer, paint, finish nails, and exterior caulk. Clear the area so you have space to work.\n\nNext, carefully remove any rotted wood, old caulk, or damaged trim. Use a pry bar or chisel, and clean the area well. This helps new materials stick and last longer.\n\nNow, fill any gaps or holes with wood filler or epoxy. Let it dry, then sand it smooth. Replace any missing trim with new exterior wood. Nail it in place with galvanized finish nails so it won\u2019t rust.\n\nSeal all seams with exterior caulk. Then, prime the repaired areas and let them dry. Finish with a coat of exterior paint to protect against weather and match your home.\n\nFinally, clean up your workspace and reinstall any hardware you removed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
