      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to replace a leaky drain trap without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to swap out a drain trap step by step, saving you time and money. \n\nFirst, turn off the water supply to your sink. Place a bucket under the trap to catch any water, and lay down towels to protect your cabinet or floor. \n\nNext, use channel locks to loosen the slip nuts on both ends of the old trap. Carefully remove the trap and let any water drain into your bucket. Clean the pipe threads and the area around the connection to make sure your new trap seals tight.\n\nNow, grab your new P-trap, slip joint washers, and nuts. Fit the new trap in place, making sure the washers are seated properly. Hand-tighten the slip nuts\u2014don\u2019t over-tighten, or you could crack the fittings. \n\nTurn the water back on and check for leaks. If you see any drips, tighten the nuts a bit more. Make sure everything is snug and dry.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
