        "Is your brick wall crumbling or losing mortar? You can fix it yourself with tuckpointing! In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to restore your brick joints and make your wall look new again.\n\nFirst, gather your materials: Type N mortar mix, masonry sand, brick cleaner, and a backer rod if your joints are deep. For a 100 square foot wall, you\u2019ll need about five 80-pound bags of mortar, two bags of sand, one gallon of cleaner, and one roll of backer rod.\n\nStep one: Surface preparation. Use a hammer and chisel or an angle grinder to remove all the loose and damaged mortar from the joints. Clean out the dust and debris so the new mortar sticks well.\n\nStep two: Mixing new mortar. Follow the instructions on the bag, and try to match the color and texture of your existing mortar. Adjust the mix if it\u2019s hot or cold outside.\n\nStep three: Applying mortar. Use a pointing trowel to pack the new mortar into the cleaned joints. Press it in firmly and shape it to match the original look of your wall.\n\nStep four: Finishing and cleanup. Let the mortar set, then brush off any extra and clean the brick faces. Mist the joints with water if needed to help the mortar cure strong.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
