      transcript:
        "Did you know you can repair a chipped or cracked bathtub in just a few hours? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to fix your bathtub and make it look like new. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: a bathtub repair epoxy kit, sandpaper, a putty knife, cleaning solution, protective gloves, and painter\u2019s tape. \n\nStart with surface preparation. Clean the bathtub thoroughly to remove soap scum and debris. Dry the area, then sand the damaged spots until smooth. Wipe away dust and tape off the area to protect the rest of the tub.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time for the repair application. Put on your gloves. Mix the epoxy as directed. Use the putty knife to fill chips or cracks, smoothing the surface as you go. Let the compound cure for the time listed in the instructions\u2014usually about an hour.\n\nFinally, for finishing touches, sand the repaired area until it\u2019s flush with the tub. Apply matching paint or finish if needed, then polish the surface so it blends in perfectly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
