      transcript:
        "Want to give your cabinets a fresh, pro-level look without replacing them? In this video, you'll learn how to stain your cabinets step by step, from prep to finish. \n\nFirst, remove all cabinet doors, drawers, and hardware. Lay them out on drop cloths. Clean every surface with a wood cleaner or degreaser to get rid of grease and dirt. Next, lightly sand all surfaces with sandpaper. This helps the stain stick and removes the old finish. Wipe away dust with a clean rag.\n\nTape off any areas you don't want stained. Now, using a brush or rag, apply the stain evenly. Work in the direction of the wood grain. Wipe off any extra stain and let it dry as the product recommends.\n\nOnce dry, apply a clear protective finish like polyurethane. This seals the stain and protects your cabinets. Let it dry fully, following the instructions for your local temperature and humidity.\n\nFinally, reattach all hardware, doors, and drawers. Check for any touch-ups and make sure everything is secure.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
