      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix damaged hardwood floors and make them look brand new? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair hardwood flooring like a pro. \n\nFirst, inspect your floor and mark the damaged boards. Move furniture out of the way and clear the area. Gather your tools: pry bar, saw, replacement planks, adhesive, nails, wood filler, sandpaper, and stain.\n\nNext, carefully remove the damaged boards. Use a pry bar and saw, working slowly to avoid harming nearby planks. Check the subfloor for moisture or damage. Fix any issues before moving on.\n\nNow, cut your new boards to size. Fit them in place, making sure they line up with the rest of the floor. Secure them with finishing nails or adhesive, following your local building codes.\n\nOnce the boards are in, sand the repaired area until it\u2019s smooth and level with the rest of the floor. Apply wood filler to any gaps, let it dry, then sand again if needed. Finish by applying stain and a protective finish to match your existing floor. Let it dry fully before moving furniture back.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
