        "Want to upgrade your bathroom in just a few hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace a frameless glass shower door, step by step. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: a new frameless glass shower door, mounting hardware kit, silicone sealant, and shims or spacers. You\u2019ll also need basic tools like a drill, screwdriver, and level.\n\nStep one: Remove the old shower door. Unscrew and detach the door, then carefully take off the tracks and hardware. Clean the area well\u2014any leftover debris can mess up your new install.\n\nStep two: Install the new tracks and frame. Measure and mark where the tracks go. Drill pilot holes, then attach the tracks and frame securely. Use a level to make sure everything is straight\u2014this is key for smooth door movement.\n\nStep three: Mount the new door. Hang the glass door onto the frame, tighten all fasteners, and adjust until it opens and closes smoothly. Finally, run a bead of silicone caulk along the edges to seal out water. Let it cure before using the shower.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
