      transcript:
        "Cracked or crumbling brick mortar can ruin your wall\u2014and your peace of mind. Today, I\u2019ll show you how to repair brick mortar step by step, so your wall looks strong and new again. \n\nFirst, prep the surface. Use a chisel and wire brush to clean out all the loose mortar and dust from the joints. This helps the new mortar stick. Take your time\u2014this should take about an hour.\n\nNext, mix your mortar. Follow the instructions on the bag, adding water until it\u2019s thick but spreadable. If you\u2019re using a bonding agent, mix it in now for extra strength.\n\nNow, apply the new mortar. Use a pointing trowel to pack the mortar deep into the cleaned joints. Shape it to match the old joints. If you need to replace any bricks, set them in place with fresh mortar.\n\nLet the mortar cure. Mist the joints with water as they set, and wipe off any extra mortar from the brick faces. After a few hours, your repair is done.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
