      transcript:
        "Want to stop gutter leaks for good? Here\u2019s how to install gutter end caps the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to seal up your gutters and prevent water damage in just a few simple steps. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: aluminum end caps, gutter sealant, screws or pop rivets, and your tools. Set up a sturdy ladder and clear out any debris from your gutters so you have a clean workspace.\n\nNext, fit each end cap onto the open end of your gutter. Make sure it sits flush. Apply a bead of gutter sealant along the seams where the cap meets the gutter. This keeps water from sneaking through. Secure the cap with screws or rivets\u2014just a couple will do. Double-check that each cap is tight and sealed all the way around.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Look for any gaps or loose fittings. Wipe away extra sealant and clean up your area. Dispose of any waste properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
