      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely repair a brick lintel and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to replace a damaged brick lintel like a pro. \n\nFirst, set up your work area. Use scaffolding or ladders, clear any obstacles, and cover windows to protect them. Always wear safety gear before you start.\n\nNext, carefully remove the bricks and old mortar above the lintel. Use a chisel or grinder, and make sure to support the structure as required by your local building codes.\n\nNow, take out the damaged lintel. Install a new steel lintel, making sure it's level and well supported. If you live in a wet or coastal area, add corrosion protection to the steel.\n\nReinstall the bricks above the new lintel, matching the old pattern. Use fresh mortar to repoint the joints, so the repair blends in with the rest of the wall.\n\nFinally, clean up the area and remove all debris. Inspect your work to make sure the lintel and masonry are solid and meet local standards.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
