        "Ever wondered how to install a vent pipe that won\u2019t leak or fail inspection? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a 4-inch PVC vent pipe, from planning to final inspection. \n\nFirst, plan your route. Measure and mark where the pipe will run, following local codes. This usually takes about 1 to 2 hours. Next, cut holes in the framing or drywall where the pipe will go. Dry-fit your pipe sections and fittings, making sure there\u2019s a slight upward slope for airflow. This step takes 2 to 3 hours.\n\nNow, assemble the pipe. Use PVC primer and cement on all joints, or clamps if required. Secure the pipe with hangers or straps every few feet. Seal every connection to prevent leaks. This part takes 3 to 4 hours.\n\nFor roof or wall exits, install a flashing boot and vent cap. Make sure the seal is tight and weatherproof. This step takes 2 to 3 hours and must meet code.\n\nFinally, check for airflow, inspect all joints, and clean up the area. You\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
