      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a leaky or clogged kitchen drain without calling a plumber? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair your kitchen drain like a pro. \n\nFirst, clear out everything under your sink. Place a bucket under the drain to catch any water. Inspect the pipes for leaks or clogs\u2014look for water stains, corrosion, or buildup.\n\nNext, loosen the slip nuts on the drain pipes and P-trap. Carefully remove these parts and dump any water or debris into your bucket. Clean out all the pipes and fittings. Rinse them well to remove grease and buildup.\n\nNow, reassemble the drain. Attach the pipes and P-trap, making sure all connections are tight. Use plumber\u2019s putty or joint compound on threaded joints for a watertight seal. Secure the pipes with hangers or straps if needed.\n\nFinally, run water through the drain. Check every joint for leaks. If everything is dry and draining well, clean up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
