      transcript:
        "Ever wondered if your fuse box is safe\u2014or hiding a big problem? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to inspect a fuse box step by step, so you can spot issues before they become emergencies. \n\nFirst, safety comes first. Turn off the main power supply. Make sure the area is dry and well-lit. Put on gloves and goggles, and use insulated tools.\n\nNext, open the fuse box. Look for any signs of trouble\u2014corrosion, burnt fuses, loose wires, or strange smells. Check that all circuit labels are clear and match the right areas.\n\nNow, test each fuse with a multimeter. If you find a blown or faulty fuse, replace it with the correct type. Tighten any loose connections. When you\u2019re done, make sure all covers are back on securely.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Regular fuse box inspections keep your home or project safe and running smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
