      transcript:
        "Is your toilet leaking or overflowing and you need a fast fix? In this video, you'll learn how to handle an emergency toilet repair step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply valve behind the toilet. This stops more water from leaking or flooding. Next, check for the problem\u2014look for leaks, clogs, or broken parts like the flapper or fill valve. \n\nIf the toilet is clogged, use a plunger or a toilet auger to clear it. For leaks or broken parts, use a toilet repair kit to replace the flapper, fill valve, or flush valve. Swap out the wax ring if you see water at the base. Tighten any loose connections and use plumber\u2019s putty or sealant where needed. \n\nOnce repairs are done, turn the water back on. Flush the toilet a few times to make sure everything works and there are no leaks. Finally, clean up the area. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
