      transcript:
        "Want a rock-solid basement floor that lasts for decades? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to build a basement floor from start to finish. \n\nFirst, clear out your basement area. Remove all debris and make sure the ground is level. Lay down a 6 mil poly vapor barrier\u2014this keeps moisture from coming up through the concrete.\n\nNext, set up your concrete form boards around the edges. Double-check your measurements. Place #3 rebar or wire mesh across the area for strength. Tie the rebar together and make sure it\u2019s raised off the ground so it sits in the middle of the slab.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to pour. Mix your 4-inch concrete slab mix and pour it evenly. Use screeds to level the surface, then floats to smooth it out. Don\u2019t forget to add expansion joint material where needed to prevent cracks.\n\nLet the concrete cure for at least 36 hours. Keep it moist if needed. Once it\u2019s set, remove the forms and finish the surface as you like.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
