      transcript:
        "Want to give your roof a sharp, finished look\u2014and protect it from water damage? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to install new roof fascia boards, step by step. \n\nFirst, remove the old fascia boards. Use a pry bar and be careful not to damage the rafters. Check the rafters for any rot or damage. If you find any, repair or replace those sections before moving on.\n\nNext, measure the roof edges. Cut your new fascia boards\u2014either primed wood or PVC\u2014to fit. Before installing, apply a primer or sealant to all sides of the boards. This helps protect against moisture. Let them dry fully, especially if you live in a humid area.\n\nNow, install the fascia boards. Use galvanized nails or screws to attach them to the rafters. Make sure each board is level and the joints are tight for a clean, professional look.\n\nAfter the boards are up, seal all joints and fastener holes with exterior caulk. Then, paint the fascia with a quality exterior paint. Finally, clean up your work area and dispose of old materials properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
