      transcript:
        "Did you know hidden mold after water damage can ruin your home and your health? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to safely clean up water damage and remove mold like a pro. \n\nFirst, inspect the area for water damage and visible mold. Put on N95 respirators, gloves, and protective coveralls. Seal off the space with plastic sheeting and set up fans or a HEPA air scrubber to keep spores from spreading.\n\nNext, remove any standing water using a pump or wet vacuum. Dry out all surfaces with dehumidifiers and fans. Check moisture levels to make sure everything is really dry.\n\nNow, scrub hard surfaces with detergent and water to remove mold. Throw away anything porous, like drywall or carpet, that can't be cleaned. Spray all affected areas with a mold remediation cleaner to kill any remaining spores.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Make sure all mold is gone. Fix any leaks and replace damaged materials. Set up moisture control to prevent mold from coming back.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
