        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/gutter-inspection/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Did you know clogged gutters can ruin your roof and foundation? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to inspect your gutters safely and spot problems before they get expensive. \n\nFirst, gather your tools: a sturdy ladder, work gloves, and safety glasses. Place your ladder on flat, solid ground right under the gutters you want to check. Always make sure it\u2019s stable before climbing up.\n\nNext, put on your gloves and start a visual inspection. Look for sagging, rust, or loose fasteners. Remove any leaves, twigs, or debris by hand or with a small scoop. Work your way along the gutter, section by section.\n\nOnce the debris is gone, grab a garden hose. Flush water through the gutters and downspouts. Watch for leaks, slow drainage, or water spilling over the sides. If you spot any blockages or leaks, mark them for repair.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Regular gutter inspections keep your home safe and dry. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
