        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/bathtub-surround-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your bathtub surround cracked, leaking, or just looking tired? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair or replace a bathtub surround like a pro. \n\nFirst, remove the old surround. Cut away the caulk with a utility knife, unscrew or detach any fixtures, and carefully pull off the damaged panels. Make sure to dispose of the debris according to your local rules.\n\nNext, prep the wall. Clean the area with a surface cleaner and let it dry. If you see any water damage, fix it now. The wall should be smooth and solid before you continue.\n\nNow, install the new surround panels. Dry-fit each panel to check the fit. Apply construction adhesive to the back, then press the panels firmly onto the wall. Use screws or anchors if needed, especially if your kit recommends it. Make sure all seams and edges are tight.\n\nFinally, seal everything up. Run a bead of waterproof caulk along all seams and corners. Reinstall your fixtures, and double-check that all connections are tight and leak-free.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
