      uploadDate: "2025-08-04",
      duration: "PT2M1S",
      contentUrl:
        "https://contractor-plus-website.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/reshub-how-to-vids/thermostat-troubleshooting.mp4",
      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/thermostat-troubleshooting/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your thermostat not working and you\u2019re not sure where to start? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to troubleshoot your thermostat and get your heating or cooling back on track. \n\nFirst, check if your thermostat has power. If it\u2019s blank or unresponsive, replace the batteries if it uses them. Make sure the settings are correct\u2014set it to heat or cool, and adjust the temperature above or below the current room temp to trigger the system.\n\nNext, turn off the power at the breaker. Remove the thermostat cover. Look at the wiring. Are any wires loose or corroded? Tighten any loose connections and replace corroded wires using wire connectors and a bit of electrical tape if needed. Double-check that each wire is in the right terminal.\n\nNow, turn the power back on. Set the thermostat to your desired temperature and see if your system responds. If the temperature reading seems off, check your manual for calibration steps. If nothing works, it might be time for a replacement thermostat.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
