      transcript:
        "Is your thermostat not heating and you\u2019re not sure what to do next? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to troubleshoot and fix a thermostat that isn\u2019t turning on the heat. \n\nFirst, check if your thermostat has power. If it uses batteries, swap them out for fresh ones. Make sure the display is on and the settings are switched to heating mode. \n\nNext, head to your circuit breaker. Look for any tripped breakers and reset them if needed. Also, check your furnace switch and make sure the furnace door is closed tight\u2014many systems won\u2019t run if the door isn\u2019t secure.\n\nNow, remove the thermostat cover. Look at the wiring connections. Are they tight and secure? Try raising the temperature to see if the furnace kicks on. If nothing happens, your thermostat might need replacing, or you may need to call a pro.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
