        "Want to give your walls a high-end look without breaking the bank? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install picture frame molding like a pro, step by step.\n\nFirst, measure your walls and mark out where you want each frame. Use a level and pencil for straight lines. Plan your layout and gather all your tools and materials: molding, finishing nails, wood filler, caulk, and paint or stain.\n\nNext, cut your molding pieces to size. Use a miter saw to get clean 45-degree corners. Sand the edges smooth, then dry-fit each frame on the wall to check the fit.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install. Apply adhesive to the back of each piece, press it onto the wall, and secure with finishing nails. Make sure everything is level. Fill nail holes and seams with wood filler or caulk. Let it dry.\n\nFor the finishing touches, sand any filled spots, then paint or stain your molding. Clean up your workspace and inspect your frames for a smooth, professional finish.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
