      transcript:
        "Want to stop water damage and boost your home's curb appeal? Today, I'll show you how to install steel gutters step by step, so you can protect your property and get pro results.\n\nFirst, prep your site. Remove any old gutters, check the fascia boards for rot, and measure your roofline. Mark where your gutters and downspouts will go.\n\nNext, cut your steel gutter sections to fit. Attach end caps, join sections with connectors, and pre-drill holes for your hangers or brackets. This makes mounting much easier.\n\nNow, install the brackets along the fascia, spacing them about every two feet. Hang your gutters, making sure they slope slightly toward the downspout\u2014about a quarter inch every ten feet. Secure everything with screws. Attach your downspouts and elbows, then seal all joints with caulk to prevent leaks.\n\nFinally, test your system with water. Check for leaks or misalignment, and fix as needed. Clean up all debris and dispose of old materials properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
