        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/stone-walkway-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your stone walkway cracked, uneven, or just looking tired? In this video, you'll learn how to repair a stone walkway step by step, so it looks great and lasts for years. \n\nFirst, inspect your walkway. Look for loose, cracked, or sunken stones. Mark the damaged spots, gather your tools, and clear away any debris.\n\nNext, carefully lift out the damaged stones. Clean them off, then dig out the old base material if needed. Add fresh gravel base, about 2-3 inches deep, and compact it well. Make sure the surface is level and slopes slightly for drainage.\n\nNow, reset your stones. Place them back in position, checking that they're even with the rest of the walkway. Fill the joints with polymeric sand or mortar mix. Sweep the material into the gaps, then compact it to lock the stones in place.\n\nFinally, sweep off any extra sand or mortar. If you used sand, lightly mist the walkway with water to set it. Inspect your work, clean up the area, and you're done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
