        "Want to make your outdoor furniture look brand new in under two hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to pressure wash your outdoor furniture the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, move your furniture to an open area. Take off all cushions and accessories. Sweep away any loose dirt or leaves. Lay down plastic sheeting to protect the ground.\n\nNext, mix a mild pressure washer detergent with water. Use a soft bristle brush or a sprayer to apply the solution to every surface. Let it sit for a few minutes to break up the grime.\n\nNow, set up your pressure washer. Pick a nozzle that\u2019s safe for furniture\u2014usually a 25- or 40-degree tip. Hold the wand about two feet away and spray each piece evenly. Don\u2019t get too close, or you might damage the finish.\n\nFinally, rinse everything with clean water. Let the furniture air dry before putting the cushions back on.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
