      transcript:
        "Is your roof decking soft, sagging, or showing signs of water damage? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair roof decking safely and efficiently. \n\nFirst, set up ladders and safety gear. Clear debris from the area and cover any landscaping or valuables near your roof. Safety always comes first.\n\nNext, remove the old shingles or roofing material. Pull up nails and carefully cut out any damaged decking sections. Take your time to avoid damaging the surrounding roof.\n\nNow, measure and cut new 5/8\" CDX plywood panels. Secure them to the roof framing, making sure each panel lines up with the existing structure. Use galvanized roofing nails for a strong hold.\n\nOnce the new decking is in place, install 30 lb roofing felt as underlayment. Add drip edge and flashing along the edges for extra protection. Replace the shingles or roofing material, sealing all seams and fasteners to keep water out.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Make sure everything is secure and weatherproof. Clean up all debris and check that the site is safe.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
