      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely relocate a gas line without costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to move a gas line, from shutoff to final inspection. \n\nFirst, always turn off the main gas supply and ventilate the area. Clear out any obstacles so you have safe access to the gas line. Next, carefully disconnect the old gas line using the right tools. Cap any open ends to prevent leaks, and remove the sections you need to move.\n\nNow, install the new CSST gas pipe. Route it to the new location, using elbows, couplings, and tees as needed. Secure the pipe with support straps every few feet. Apply pipe sealant or thread tape to all connections for a tight, leak-free fit. Don\u2019t forget to install a new shutoff valve if needed.\n\nOnce everything is in place, use a pressure test gauge to check for leaks. If your local code requires it, schedule an inspection. When you pass, turn the gas back on and test all appliances. Finally, patch any walls or floors you opened and clean up the area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
