      transcript:
        "Want to save money and energy with a new solar water heater? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to replace your old solar water heater step by step. \n\nFirst, shut down the system. Turn off the power and water supply, let everything cool, and drain all water from the tank and solar collectors. This keeps things safe and mess-free.\n\nNext, remove the old heater. Disconnect all plumbing and electrical lines, take off the mounting hardware, and carefully lift out the old unit.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install the new system. Set the new 80-gallon solar water heater in place. Attach the insulated copper piping, connect the circulation pump, controller, and sensors. Make sure all fittings are tight and up to code.\n\nOnce installed, refill the system and restore power. Check for leaks and test the heater to make sure it\u2019s working right.\n\nFinally, clean up the area and dispose of the old heater and materials properly. Give the owner clear maintenance instructions.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
