      transcript:
        "Did you know a simple well cap can protect your water from dangerous contamination? Today, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to replace and install a sanitary, vented well cap\u2014step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off power to your well pump for safety. Clean around the wellhead to keep dirt out. Use the right tools to carefully remove the old well cap. \n\nNext, inspect the well casing for cracks or debris. Clean the sealing surface so the new cap fits tight. If you see any damage, fix it before moving on. \n\nNow, place the new well cap on the casing. Make sure it sits flat. Use stainless steel bolts or screws to secure it, tightening them evenly for a good seal. If you need a riser, cut and attach PVC pipe with pipe sealant or Teflon tape. \n\nFinally, drop in chlorine tablets to disinfect the well, following local guidelines. Restore power and check for leaks. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
