        "Ever wondered how to safely tear out just part of a building without making a mess? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to do selective demolition step by step. \n\nFirst, review your project plans and walk the site. Mark exactly what needs to go\u2014walls, fixtures, or finishes\u2014so you don\u2019t damage anything you want to keep. This takes about 3 to 4 hours.\n\nNext, prep the area. Shut off all utilities\u2014water, gas, and electric. Put up dust barriers and lay down floor protection to keep the rest of the space clean and safe. Don\u2019t forget your PPE: gloves, masks, and eye protection. This setup usually takes 4 to 6 hours.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time for demolition. Use hand tools and reciprocating saws to carefully remove only what\u2019s marked. Work slow and steady to avoid damaging nearby areas. This part can take 18 to 20 hours for 1,000 square feet.\n\nFinally, sort and bag up debris, load it into a dumpster, and clean the site. Follow local rules for disposal. This cleanup takes about 4 to 5 hours.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
