      transcript:
        "Is your brick patio looking uneven or full of broken bricks? Let\u2019s fix it step by step so it looks brand new. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a brick patio, from removing damaged bricks to finishing with a smooth, sturdy surface.\n\nFirst, inspect your patio and mark any bricks that are cracked, loose, or uneven. Clear away debris and gather your tools, replacement bricks, sand, and mortar.\n\nNext, carefully lift out the damaged bricks. Clean out the old sand or mortar underneath. Check the base\u2014if it\u2019s not level, add or adjust gravel or sand until it\u2019s flat and stable.\n\nNow, place your new or cleaned bricks into the repaired area. Make sure they line up with the rest of the patio. Tap each brick down gently and check that everything is level as you go.\n\nOnce all bricks are in place, sweep polymeric sand into the joints. Compact the surface, then lightly mist with water to set the sand. Finish by cleaning up and disposing of debris properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
