      transcript:
        "Want to turn your backyard into a fun zone with a tire swing? In this video, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to install a safe, sturdy tire swing from start to finish. \n\nFirst, pick a healthy tree with a strong, horizontal branch at least 8 inches thick. Make sure the area is clear and the branch is solid\u2014safety first!\n\nNext, gather your materials: a clean tire, about 30 feet of heavy-duty rope, an eye bolt with washer and nut, a tree protection strap or swing hanger, and two carabiners or quick links. Drill a few holes in the bottom of the tire for drainage, then attach the eye bolt through the tire and secure it tightly.\n\nThread the rope through the eye bolt and tie a strong knot, like a double bowline. Protect the tree by wrapping a strap or hanger around the branch, then attach the rope using your carabiners. Adjust the swing so it hangs about 12 to 18 inches off the ground.\n\nFinally, test the swing for stability and supervise the first few uses. Now you\u2019ve got a classic tire swing everyone can enjoy!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
