        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/kitchen-vent-cleaning/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your kitchen vent hiding years of grease and grime? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to deep clean your kitchen vent like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, safety comes first. Turn off the power to your vent. Gather your supplies: degreasing cleaner, scrub brushes, disposable cloths, protective gloves, and plastic sheeting. Lay the plastic sheeting over your counters and stove to protect them from drips and mess.\n\nNext, remove the vent cover and filters. Use a vacuum or a brush to clear out loose dust and debris from all the parts you can reach. This makes the deep cleaning much easier.\n\nNow, soak the vent cover and filters in a degreasing cleaner. Scrub them well with your brushes to break down stubborn grease. Wipe the inside of the vent with your cleaning cloths and more degreaser. Make sure everything is fully dry before you put it all back together.\n\nFinally, reassemble the vent, restore power, and enjoy a cleaner, safer kitchen.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
