        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/wallpaper-removal-and-painting/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to remove old wallpaper and get perfect painted walls? Today, I\u2019ll show you every step to transform your space, from prep to cleanup. \n\nFirst, clear the room. Move furniture, cover your floors with drop cloths, and tape off trim. Take off outlet covers and switch plates so nothing gets missed.\n\nNext, score the wallpaper with a blade, then spray on wallpaper remover solution. Let it soak, then gently peel off the paper. Scrape off any glue left behind and wash the walls clean.\n\nNow, check for damage. Patch holes with joint compound, sand rough spots, and make sure the surface is smooth. Once dry, roll on a coat of primer to help the paint stick.\n\nTime to paint! Use quality brushes and rollers. Apply two coats, letting each dry fully. Touch up the trim for a crisp finish.\n\nFinally, pull up the drop cloths, reinstall fixtures, and move your furniture back. Clean up any mess and enjoy your fresh new walls.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
