      transcript:
        "Want to install base cabinets like a pro, even if you\u2019ve never done it before? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install three base cabinets, from prep to finishing touches. \n\nFirst, clear out your workspace. Remove any old cabinets and make sure your walls and floors are clean and level. This helps your new cabinets sit straight and look great.\n\nNext, measure and mark where each cabinet will go. Use a level to draw a straight line on the wall for the cabinet tops. Find the wall studs\u2014this is where you\u2019ll anchor the cabinets for strength.\n\nNow, set your first cabinet in place. Use shims to get it perfectly level and plumb. Secure it to the wall studs with cabinet screws. Add the next cabinet, shim and level it, then screw it to the first cabinet and the wall. Repeat for the third cabinet. Always double-check your alignment as you go.\n\nOnce all cabinets are in, install the toe kicks. Adjust the doors and drawers so they open smoothly. Clean up your workspace and inspect all fastenings. Your cabinets are now ready for countertops!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
