        "Want to build a garden fence that lasts for years? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a sturdy wood garden fence, from planning to finishing touches. \n\nFirst, measure your property lines and mark where the fence will go. Always call to check for underground utilities before you dig. Clear away any plants or debris along the fence line.\n\nNext, dig holes for your posts\u2014usually about 8 feet apart. Set each 4x4 post in concrete, making sure they\u2019re straight and at the right height. Let the concrete cure fully before moving on.\n\nNow, attach your fence panels or pickets to the posts. Use galvanized nails or screws, and check that everything is level and evenly spaced.\n\nInstall your gate and hardware kit. Make sure the gate swings smoothly and latches securely. Adjust the hardware if needed.\n\nFinally, inspect the whole fence for stability. Apply a wood sealer or stain if you want extra protection. Clean up all leftover materials and debris.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
