      transcript:
        "Is your window trim rotting or falling apart? Let\u2019s fix it fast and make it look new again! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair exterior window trim step by step. \n\nFirst, inspect your window trim for damage, rot, or loose spots. Gather your tools and materials: wood trim, wood filler, paint or stain, caulk, and galvanized finish nails. Protect the area with drop cloths.\n\nNext, carefully remove any damaged trim using a pry bar and utility knife. Pull out old nails and scrape away old caulk. Clean the area so it\u2019s ready for new trim.\n\nNow, measure and cut your new trim pieces to fit. Attach them with galvanized finish nails, making sure everything lines up nicely.\n\nFor the finishing touches, fill nail holes with wood filler, caulk the seams, and sand any rough spots. Prime and paint or stain the new trim to match your house.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your window trim is repaired and protected. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
