      transcript:
        "Is your garage door creaking or sticking? It might be time to replace those old hinges. In this video, you'll learn how to safely replace garage door hinges step by step. \n\nFirst, unplug your garage door opener and make sure the door is closed. This keeps you safe and the door steady. Gather your new hinges, bolts or screws, a socket wrench, screwdriver, and some lubricant.\n\nNext, support the door panels so they don\u2019t shift. Carefully unscrew and remove the old hinges, one at a time. Keep a hand on the panel as you work to prevent it from moving.\n\nNow, line up your new hinge in the same spot. Attach it with new bolts or screws, and tighten them securely. Repeat this for each hinge you\u2019re replacing.\n\nOnce all new hinges are in, spray a little lubricant on the moving parts. Reconnect your garage door opener and test the door. It should move smoothly and quietly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
