        "Is your storm door sticking, rattling, or letting in drafts? Let\u2019s fix it fast and make it work like new! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a storm door step by step, from inspection to final testing. \n\nFirst, inspect your storm door. Look for loose handles, broken hinges, worn weatherstripping, or cracked glass. Make a list of what needs fixing. \n\nNext, remove any damaged hardware\u2014like handles, hinges, or the door closer. Use a screwdriver to take out old screws. Install your new hardware kit, making sure everything is tight and lines up right. \n\nNow, adjust the door so it opens and closes smoothly. If it\u2019s sagging or scraping, realign it and tighten the hinges. Replace or add weatherstripping around the frame to seal out drafts. Adjust the door closer so it shuts gently, not with a bang. \n\nFinally, test the door several times. Make sure it swings and latches easily. Clean up your tools and toss out old parts. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
