        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/soundproof-wall-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to block out noise and create a peaceful space? Here\u2019s how to install a soundproof wall step by step. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to plan, build, and finish a soundproof wall that really works.\n\nFirst, clear your workspace and measure the wall. Mark your studs and outlets. Gather all your materials: soundproof drywall, mineral wool insulation, acoustic sealant, resilient channels, screws, joint compound, and tape.\n\nNext, check if you need extra framing. Fit mineral wool batts tightly between the studs. Seal every gap with acoustic caulk to stop sound leaks.\n\nNow, attach resilient channels across the studs. These help break up sound vibrations. Mount your soundproof drywall on top, staggering the seams. Use acoustic sealant around all edges and openings.\n\nTape and mud the drywall joints. Sand them smooth, then prime and paint. Don\u2019t forget to seal around outlets with acoustic putty pads.\n\nFinally, inspect for any gaps or weak spots. Test the wall for sound reduction. Clean up and dispose of waste properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
