      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/door-adjustment/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your door sticking, sagging, or just not closing right? In this video, you'll learn how to adjust a door so it opens and closes smoothly\u2014no more annoying jams or gaps. \n\nFirst, inspect the door and frame. Look for spots where the door rubs, gaps around the edges, or loose hinges. Check the latch and frame for any obvious problems.\n\nNext, grab a screwdriver or drill. Tighten all the hinge screws. If any screws are stripped, replace them. Adjust the strike plate if the latch doesn't line up. Use wood shims behind the hinges if the door is still misaligned. This helps level the door in the frame.\n\nSpray a little lubricant on the hinges to stop squeaks and help the door move easier.\n\nNow, test the door. Open and close it a few times. Make small tweaks to the hinges or hardware until the door swings and latches perfectly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
