      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to install emergency lighting that keeps people safe when the power goes out? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to install emergency lights, from planning to final testing. \n\nFirst, start with a site assessment. Walk through your building and decide where emergency lights are needed\u2014think exits, hallways, and stairwells. Make sure your plan meets local safety codes.\n\nNext, gather your materials: LED emergency fixtures with battery backup, 12-gauge electrical wire, wire connectors, mounting hardware, and electrical boxes. For a standard job with 10 fixtures, you'll need about 400 feet of wire and 40 connectors.\n\nNow, run your wiring. Use the right gauge and follow electrical standards for your area. Mount each fixture securely, connect the wires using connectors, and install the electrical boxes as needed.\n\nOnce everything is wired, test each emergency light. Check that the battery backup works and that all units turn on when the main power is off. Document your results for inspection.\n\nFinally, show staff how to use and maintain the system, then clean up your work area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
