      transcript:
        "Want to give your cabinets a fresh, pro-level look without replacing them? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repaint your cabinets for a smooth, lasting finish. \n\nFirst, remove all cabinet doors, drawers, and hardware. Use a good degreaser to clean every surface\u2014paint won\u2019t stick to grease or grime. \n\nNext, sand all the cabinet surfaces. This removes the old finish and helps the new paint grip. Wipe away dust, then use painter\u2019s tape to protect walls and counters. \n\nNow, apply a high-quality primer. Cover every surface and let it dry completely. This step is key for a smooth, even paint job. \n\nOnce the primer\u2019s dry, paint your cabinets with thin, even coats. Let each coat dry before adding the next. Two coats usually look best. \n\nFinally, reattach the hardware, put the doors and drawers back, and clean up your workspace. Check for any spots that need a quick touch-up. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
