      transcript:
        "Did you know a simple weather seal can save you big on energy bills? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace your garage door weather seal step by step. \n\nFirst, raise your garage door. Carefully pull off the old weather seal from the bottom edge. Use a scraper or putty knife to remove any leftover adhesive and dirt. Make sure the surface is clean for the new seal to stick well.\n\nNext, measure the width of your garage door. Mark your new weather seal to match this length. Use a utility knife or strong scissors to cut it to size.\n\nNow, slide or press the new seal into the track at the bottom of the door. If your door uses nails or screws, attach the seal securely along the entire edge. Make sure there are no gaps\u2014this keeps out drafts, water, and pests.\n\nTest the door to make sure it opens and closes smoothly. That\u2019s it! Your garage is now better protected from the elements.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
