      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely move a hot tub without breaking the bank\u2014or your back? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to relocate a hot tub, from prep to reconnection. \n\nFirst, assess both the current and new locations. Measure doorways and paths, and clear anything in the way. Make sure the new spot is level and strong enough to hold the hot tub.\n\nNext, turn off the power at the breaker. Disconnect all electrical connections and drain the water completely. Remove any plumbing, following your local codes.\n\nNow, it's time to move. Use two moving dollies or carts, heavy-duty straps, and plenty of blankets or plastic sheeting to protect the tub and your floors. Get help\u2014hot tubs are heavy! Carefully lift and roll the tub to its new home, watching for tight corners and steps.\n\nOnce in place, reconnect the electrical and plumbing using the right kits and PVC fittings. Fill the tub with water and check for leaks or issues before turning it on.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
