      transcript:
        "Cracked or crumbling brick walls? You can fix them yourself with the right steps. In this video, you'll learn how to repair a masonry wall from start to finish.\n\nFirst, clear the area around the damage. Remove any loose debris and scrub the wall clean. This helps the new mortar stick well.\n\nNext, mix fresh Type N mortar as the bag says. Use a chisel to remove old, damaged mortar joints to a uniform depth. Take your time\u2014clean joints make for a stronger repair.\n\nNow, replace any broken bricks. Apply mortar to the joints and set the new bricks in place. Use a trowel to repoint the wall, packing the mortar tightly and shaping the joints to match the rest of the wall.\n\nLet the mortar set. Mist the area with water to help it cure. Clean up your tools and sweep away any leftover mortar. Dispose of debris as your local rules require.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
