      transcript:
        "Want to add a bathroom or laundry to your basement? Here\u2019s how to install basement plumbing the right way. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn the key steps, materials, and tips for a smooth basement plumbing installation.\n\nFirst, plan your layout. Review your local building codes, sketch out where drains, vents, and water lines will go, and mark everything on the floor. Don\u2019t forget to get your permits before you start.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time for trenching and rough-in. Cut the concrete and dig trenches for your drain and vent pipes. Lay 2-inch PVC drain pipes with the right slope\u2014about a quarter inch per foot. Use PVC fittings like elbows and tees, and secure everything tightly.\n\nNow, install your water supply. Run 3/4-inch PEX pipes to each fixture. Add shut-off valves and connect to your main water line. Pressure test the system to check for leaks before you close anything up.\n\nFinally, connect your fixtures\u2014like toilets, sinks, and showers. Use the right drain kits and flanges. Schedule an inspection with your local authorities to make sure everything\u2019s up to code.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
