        "Did you know a clogged attic vent can spike your energy bills and damage your home? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to clean attic vents safely and thoroughly, step by step. \n\nFirst, gather your supplies: protective sheeting, disposable gloves, dust masks, cleaning brushes, vacuum bags or filters, and a mild cleaning solution. Lay down protective sheeting to keep your attic clean. Put on gloves and a dust mask for safety.\n\nSet up a stable ladder and make sure the attic is safe to enter. Turn off any attic fans and check for hazards like exposed wires or pests before you start.\n\nNext, inspect each attic vent for dust, debris, or blockages. Use a vacuum with a fresh bag or filter to remove loose dust. For stubborn dirt, scrub with a cleaning brush and a mild cleaning solution. If you have compressed air, use it to blow out hard-to-reach spots in the ductwork.\n\nOnce all vents are clean, reinstall the covers. Turn the attic fan back on and check for good airflow. Make sure nothing is blocking the vents. Clean up your workspace and exit the attic safely.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
