      transcript:
        "Want to finish your basement like a pro? Here\u2019s how to install drywall step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn exactly what materials you need, how much time it takes, and the right way to get the job done. \n\nFirst, clear out your basement and gather your supplies: drywall sheets, screws, joint compound, tape, and corner bead. Check the framing and add insulation or a vapor barrier if your local code requires it. This prep takes about 6 to 8 hours.\n\nNext, measure and cut your drywall sheets. Hang them on the walls and ceiling, screwing them into the studs and joists. This step usually takes 20 to 24 hours for a 1,000 square foot basement.\n\nNow, tape all the seams and cover them with joint compound. Don\u2019t forget to fill screw holes too. Let each coat dry before adding the next. Plan for 18 to 20 hours here.\n\nOnce dry, sand everything smooth. Check for any rough spots and touch up as needed. This takes 8 to 10 hours.\n\nFinally, clean up all dust and debris. Do a final inspection to make sure your drywall looks great and is ready for paint. That\u2019s another 2 to 3 hours.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
