      transcript:
        "Is your window stuck or slamming shut? You might need a window balance repair. In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to replace window balances step by step, so your windows open and close smoothly again. \n\nFirst, unlock your window and carefully lift out the sash. Take your time\u2014don\u2019t force it, and be careful not to crack the glass or scratch the frame. Set the sash aside on a soft surface.\n\nNext, look at the old window balances. Most windows use either spiral or block and tackle balances. Unscrew or unclip the old balances from the frame. Grab your new balances and install them, following the manufacturer\u2019s instructions. Use new mounting screws for a secure fit. A quick spray of lubricant on the moving parts can help your window glide better.\n\nNow, reinstall the sash into the frame. Make sure it sits evenly. Test the window by opening and closing it a few times. If it moves smoothly and stays in place, you\u2019ve done it right!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
