      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to replace old, cracked grout and make your tiles look brand new? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to remove and replace grout like a pro. \n\nFirst, grab your tools: a grout removal tool, new grout, sealer, sponges, and a bucket. Start by using a grout saw or oscillating tool to carefully scrape out the old grout between your tiles. Take your time\u2014don't rush, and be careful not to chip the tiles. This usually takes about two hours for a 100 square foot area.\n\nNext, clean out all the dust and debris from the joints. Use a vacuum or brush, then wipe the area with a damp sponge. This step is key for a strong bond.\n\nNow, mix your new grout as the package says. Using a rubber float, press the grout into the joints, working in small sections. Make sure every gap is filled. This part takes two to three hours.\n\nOnce the grout is in, wipe off the excess with a damp sponge. Shape the grout lines for a smooth, even look. Let the grout cure as recommended\u2014usually about an hour.\n\nFinally, apply grout sealer to protect your work from moisture and stains. And that's it\u2014your tiles look fresh and your grout is built to last!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
