      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a damaged brick pillar and make it look brand new? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair a brick pillar, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, inspect the pillar. Look for loose or broken bricks and clear the area around the pillar. Gather your tools and materials: replacement bricks, Type N mortar mix, masonry sand, rebar, brick ties, and waterproofing sealant.\n\nNext, carefully remove the damaged bricks and old mortar using a chisel and hammer. Clean the exposed surfaces and joints. This helps the new mortar stick well.\n\nNow, mix fresh mortar. Set your new bricks in place, making sure they line up with the rest of the pillar. Use mortar between each brick and tool the joints for a smooth, even look. If needed, add rebar and brick ties for extra strength.\n\nLet the mortar set. Mist the area with water to help it cure. Check the pillar for stability and clean up any leftover debris. Finally, apply a waterproofing sealant to protect your repair.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
