      transcript:
        "Is your sprinkler system wasting water and money because of hidden leaks? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to find and fix leaks in your sprinkler lines, step by step. \n\nFirst, do a full system inspection. Walk along your sprinkler lines and look for wet spots, pooling water, or broken sprinkler heads. Check pipes and valves for cracks or obvious leaks.\n\nNext, pressure test the system. Turn on each zone one at a time. Watch for sudden drops in water pressure or uneven spray patterns\u2014these are signs of hidden leaks.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to pinpoint the leak. Feel the soil for soggy areas and listen for hissing sounds. Use leak detection dye in suspicious spots, or rent an acoustic leak detector for hard-to-find leaks. Mark the leak locations with flag markers.\n\nOnce you\u2019ve found the leaks, repair or replace any damaged pipes, fittings, or sprinkler heads. After repairs, turn the system back on and check again to make sure all leaks are fixed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
