      transcript:
        "Thinking about upgrading your kitchen with a new wall oven? Let\u2019s walk through exactly how to install a 30-inch electric wall oven, step by step.\n\nFirst, always start safe. Turn off the power at the breaker. Double-check with a voltage tester. Then, disconnect the wiring and carefully slide out the old oven from the cabinet.\n\nNext, prep your space. Measure the cabinet opening to make sure your new oven fits. Adjust the supports if needed. Check that your electrical box, wire, and breaker meet the oven\u2019s requirements\u2014usually 10-gauge copper wire and a 240V double-pole breaker.\n\nNow, bring in the new oven. With help, lift it into place. Secure it with mounting screws and brackets. Run flexible conduit for the wiring, and connect everything according to local codes. Double-check all connections.\n\nFinally, restore power at the breaker. Test all oven functions to make sure it heats up and works right. Check that the oven is level and secure. Clean up your work area, and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
