      transcript:
        "Want cleaner water at home or on the job? Installing a carbon filter is easier than you think. In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a carbon filter for your water system.\n\nFirst, gather your materials: a carbon filter unit, mounting brackets, flexible ducting, hose clamps, and sealant or tape. You\u2019ll also need basic tools like wrenches and Teflon tape. Shut off the water supply and clear the area where you\u2019ll be working.\n\nNext, mount the filter housing securely to the wall or support. Use the brackets and hardware provided. Measure and cut your pipes or ducting to fit. Connect the inlet and outlet lines to the filter. Wrap Teflon tape around any threaded connections to prevent leaks. Tighten everything with your wrenches.\n\nNow, turn the water supply back on. Check all connections for leaks. Flush the filter as the manufacturer recommends to clear out any carbon dust. Finally, clean up your work area and dispose of packaging properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
