      transcript:
        "Want to make your old hardwood floors look brand new\u2014without a full refinish? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to recoat hardwood floors step by step, so you get pro results and save money.\n\nFirst, clear the room. Move out all furniture, rugs, and anything else on the floor. Sweep and vacuum every inch, then use a floor cleaner or degreaser to get rid of any dirt or grease.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time for light sanding. Use a buffer or sanding screen pads to gently scuff the surface. This removes small scratches and helps the new finish stick. After sanding, wipe the floor with tack cloths to pick up all the dust.\n\nNow, tape off baseboards with painter\u2019s tape. Pour your water-based polyurethane finish into a tray. Using a clean applicator pad or roller, apply a thin, even coat across the floor. Work in small sections and follow the wood grain. Check the manufacturer\u2019s instructions for drying times and coverage.\n\nLet the floor dry and cure for at least 3 to 4 hours. Keep the area well-ventilated and stay off the floor until it\u2019s fully set.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your hardwood floors are refreshed and protected.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
