      transcript:
        "Want to install a new door that fits perfectly and swings smooth? In this video, you'll learn how to install a pre-hung door step by step, with pro tips for a flawless finish.\n\nFirst, remove the old door and trim. Use a pry bar and screwdriver. Clean the opening and check that the framing is level and square. This is key for a good fit.\n\nNext, set your pre-hung door unit into the opening. Use shims on the sides and top to make sure the frame is plumb and level. Check the gap around the door\u2014aim for even spacing. Secure the frame with finishing nails or screws through the jamb, right where the shims are. Test the door. It should swing and latch easily.\n\nNow, install your door casing trim. Nail it in place, then fill nail holes with wood putty or caulk. Make any final hinge or latch tweaks. Clean up, and check that the door opens and closes smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
