      transcript:
        "Want to boost your home's curb appeal and value with a new front porch? In this video, I'll show you exactly how to plan and build a front porch addition, step by step. \n\nFirst, start with planning and permits. Draw up detailed porch plans, pick your materials, and get the right permits from your local building department. This usually takes 8 to 12 hours, but it's crucial to avoid headaches later.\n\nNext, prep your site and foundation. Clear the area, mark your layout, and dig for footings or set piers. Pour concrete according to your local codes. This step takes about 16 to 20 hours.\n\nNow, it's time for framing. Use pressure-treated lumber to build the frame, install posts, beams, and joists. Make sure everything is level and secure. This part takes 24 to 28 hours.\n\nAfter framing, install your decking boards, build the stairs, add railings, and construct the roof. Use composite decking for low maintenance, and make sure all railings and steps meet safety standards. This final step takes 20 to 24 hours.\n\nDon't forget the finishing touches: flashing, waterproof membrane, and paint or stain to protect your porch for years to come.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
