      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to complete a mortgage survey for your property? In this video, you'll learn the exact steps and materials needed to get a mortgage survey done right. \n\nFirst, gather all your property documents\u2014like deeds, site plans, and any old surveys. Double-check who owns the land and where the legal boundaries are. This usually takes about 1 to 2 hours.\n\nNext, head to the site with your tools. You'll need 20 surveyor stakes, 20 survey flags or markers, 4 boundary pins, and materials to prepare your survey map. Set up your equipment, mark the boundaries, and look for any structures or encroachments. Take careful notes and measurements. This on-site work takes about 3 to 4 hours per lot.\n\nFinally, analyze your data and prepare a detailed survey map and report. Make sure it meets your lender's requirements. This last step takes about 2 hours.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
