        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/air-quality-testing-for-mold/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Worried about hidden mold in your home or job site? Here\u2019s how to test your air quality for mold, step by step. \n\nFirst, gather your supplies: an air sampling pump, three mold air sample cassettes, lab analysis forms, and personal protective equipment. Make sure to seal off windows and doors in the area you\u2019re testing. This keeps outside air from messing up your results.\n\nNext, put on your PPE. Set up the air sampling pump and follow the kit instructions. Take samples from at least three spots\u2014focus on places with visible mold or musty smells. Each sample should go into its own cassette.\n\nLabel each sample clearly and fill out the lab forms. Ship everything to a certified lab for analysis.\n\nOnce you get your results, review the mold spore levels and types. If the report shows high levels or dangerous mold, plan for professional remediation or more testing.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
