      transcript:
        "Want cleaner water straight from your tap? Here\u2019s how to install a water filter faucet in under two hours. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn step-by-step how to add a dedicated water filter faucet to your kitchen sink.\n\nFirst, gather your tools and materials: a water filter faucet, flexible supply line, mounting hardware, and Teflon tape. Shut off the water supply and clear out the space under your sink so you can work easily.\n\nNext, if you have an old faucet or soap dispenser in the way, disconnect and remove it. If there\u2019s no hole for the new faucet, carefully drill one in your sink or countertop. Make sure it\u2019s the right size for your new faucet.\n\nNow, install the new water filter faucet. Secure it from underneath with the mounting hardware. Connect the filter system to your cold water line, then attach the flexible supply line to the new faucet. Use Teflon tape on threaded connections to prevent leaks.\n\nTurn the water supply back on. Check all connections for leaks. Flush the filter as recommended by the manufacturer. Finally, clean up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
