      transcript:
        "Want to stop gutter leaks for good? Here\u2019s how to install gutter outlets the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to mark, cut, and fit gutter outlets for a leak-free finish.\n\nFirst, measure and mark where you want each outlet on your gutter. Use a hole saw or tin snips to cut an opening that matches your outlet size. Take your time\u2014clean cuts make a big difference.\n\nNext, insert the gutter outlet into the hole. Make sure it fits snug. Secure it with aluminum screws or rivets. Then, seal all the edges with silicone sealant to keep water from sneaking through.\n\nNow, attach your downspout to the outlet. Double-check that everything lines up. Run water through the gutter to test for leaks and make sure it drains right.\n\nThat\u2019s it! If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
