      transcript:
        "Want a rock-solid floor that lasts? Here\u2019s how to build a subfloor the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process to install a sturdy subfloor for your next project.\n\nFirst, clear your work area. Remove all debris and make sure the ground is level and dry. Mark your layout lines so you know exactly where everything goes.\n\nNext, install your floor joists. Measure and cut each 2x8 to fit. Space them according to your local building code, usually 16 inches on center. Secure each joist with joist hangers and check that they\u2019re level.\n\nNow, lay down the sill gasket on top of the foundation to prevent moisture. Then, cut your 3/4-inch tongue and groove plywood panels to size. Stagger the seams for strength. Apply construction adhesive to the joists, then set each panel in place. Fasten them with subfloor screws, leaving a small gap between panels for expansion.\n\nSeal all seams and screw holes with adhesive or sealant. Inspect the subfloor for any movement or squeaks. Make sure everything meets local codes.\n\nFinally, clean up the area. Remove tools and sweep the floor so it\u2019s ready for the next step\u2014installing your finished flooring.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
