        "Ever wondered how to install a drain pipe that never leaks? Today, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process for a solid, code-compliant drain pipe installation.\n\nFirst, start with planning and marking. Review your plumbing plans, measure out your pipe runs, and mark the wall or floor where the new drain pipe will go. Gather all your materials: 4-inch PVC pipe, elbows, fittings, pipe cement, hangers, and gravel bedding.\n\nNext, cut your pipe sections to the right length. Dry-fit all the pieces together, making sure you have the right slope for drainage\u2014usually a quarter inch per foot. Adjust your layout to meet local plumbing codes.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to assemble. Prime and glue each pipe and fitting, or use the right connectors for metal pipes. Secure every joint and support with hangers or straps. Double-check that every connection is tight and leak-free.\n\nFinally, test your work. Run a water or air pressure test to check for leaks. Fix any issues, then schedule your inspection if your area requires it.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
