        "Ever wondered how to install a pot filler faucet above your stove without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to do it yourself, safely and efficiently. \n\nFirst, shut off your main water supply. Clear the area and cover your counters to protect them. Next, measure and mark where you want the pot filler. Cut a small access hole in the wall. Run a dedicated half-inch copper water line from your main supply to this spot. Use elbows and fittings to navigate around studs, and don\u2019t forget to add pipe insulation.\n\nNow, install the mounting bracket securely to the wall framing. Attach a shut-off valve to the end of your water line. Make sure all fittings are tight and use plumber\u2019s tape and sealant to prevent leaks.\n\nMount the pot filler faucet onto the bracket. Connect it to the water line. Turn the water supply back on and check for leaks. Make sure the faucet swings and aligns properly over your stove.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
