      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to replace a circuit breaker panel safely and efficiently? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process, from shutting off the power to testing your new panel. \n\nFirst, always start with safety. Turn off the main power supply and double-check that all circuits are de-energized. Use lockout and tagout procedures to make sure no one turns the power back on while you work.\n\nNext, label every existing circuit so you know where each wire goes. Disconnect all the branch wires, remove the breakers, and carefully detach the old panel from the wall.\n\nNow, mount your new 200-amp panel. Transfer and secure all the branch wires, install your new main breaker and branch circuit breakers, and make sure to add a grounding bar kit and connect your copper ground wire. Follow your local codes for grounding and bonding.\n\nOnce everything is in place, restore power and test each circuit to make sure it works. Double-check your labels, and arrange for a final inspection as required by your local regulations.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
