        "Want a classic fence that\u2019s fast to build and easy on the wallet? Let\u2019s walk through how to install a split rail fence, step by step. \n\nFirst, measure and mark your fence line. Use stakes and string to keep it straight, and double-check your property lines. Mark where each post will go, spacing them evenly.\n\nNext, dig your post holes. Use a post hole digger to make holes deep and wide enough for each post\u2014usually about a third of the post\u2019s length. Adjust for your soil type if needed.\n\nNow, set your posts. Drop each post in, check that it\u2019s straight with a level, and backfill with gravel or concrete for stability. Let them set if you use concrete.\n\nOnce the posts are solid, install your rails. Slide each rail into the slots or holes in the posts. Make sure they\u2019re level and adjust for any slopes in your yard.\n\nFinally, walk the fence. Tighten any loose connections and clean up the area. Dispose of debris properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
