      transcript:
        "Want to clear your site fast and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to clear a construction site the right way. \n\nFirst, assess and mark your site. Survey the area, mark property lines, and flag any trees or structures you want to keep. Always check for underground utilities before you start digging.\n\nNext, remove all vegetation and debris. Use chainsaws, brush cutters, or heavy equipment to clear trees, stumps, and brush. Sort what you can recycle and dispose of the rest according to local rules.\n\nNow, it's time for excavation and grading. Remove the topsoil, rocks, and level the ground. Make sure the site slopes for proper drainage and compact the soil to prevent settling later.\n\nFinally, install erosion control. Lay down erosion control fabric, set up silt fences, and stabilize exposed soil. Schedule an inspection to make sure you meet all environmental standards.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
