      transcript:
        "Want to install box gutters that last for years and never leak? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install box gutters like a pro. \n\nFirst, clear your work area and set up ladders or scaffolding. Measure your roof edge carefully and mark where each bracket and outlet will go. Accurate measurements are key for a watertight fit.\n\nNext, cut your box gutter sections and downspouts to the right length. Pre-drill holes for fasteners and get your joints ready for sealing. Double-check that everything matches your layout.\n\nNow, install the brackets along your marks. Secure each box gutter section in place, connecting joints with gutter sealant. Attach the downspouts and elbows, making sure the gutter slopes slightly toward the outlets for proper drainage.\n\nApply waterproof sealant to every joint and seam. Run water through the system to check for leaks and make sure it drains away from your building.\n\nFinally, clean up the area and inspect your work. Make sure everything meets local codes and manufacturer guidelines.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
