      transcript:
        "Cracks in your brick foundation? Here\u2019s how to fix them the right way. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a brick foundation step by step, from prep to finish. \n\nFirst, clear the work area and remove any debris. Inspect the foundation for loose bricks, cracks, or crumbling mortar. This helps you spot all the problem areas before you start. \n\nNext, carefully chisel out the damaged bricks and old mortar. Take your time\u2014don\u2019t disturb the good bricks around them. \n\nNow, it\u2019s time to rebuild. Mix fresh Type N mortar in a disposable tub. Apply a bonding agent to the area, then set your new bricks in place. Make sure they line up with the old ones and keep the joints even. Fill the joints with mortar and smooth them out. \n\nLet the mortar cure for at least 12 hours. Once it\u2019s dry, inspect your work for stability and clean up the site. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
