      transcript:
        "Thinking about rebuilding your deck? Here\u2019s what it really takes to do it right. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process to rebuild a 200 square foot deck, including the materials, timeline, and key tips for a safe, long-lasting result.\n\nFirst, start with demolition and site prep. Remove all old boards, railings, and any damaged framing. Clear away debris and check the foundation. Make sure it meets your local building codes.\n\nNext, move on to framing and structural work. Install or repair your posts, beams, and joists. Use pressure-treated lumber for durability. Double-check that everything is level and secure. Anchor posts with concrete and use joist hangers for extra strength.\n\nNow, install your new deck boards. Lay them out with small gaps for drainage. Fasten each board with deck screws and trim the edges for a clean look.\n\nAfter that, add railings and stairs. Use a railing kit for safety and style. Make sure everything is firmly attached and meets local safety standards.\n\nFinally, finish up. Sand any rough spots, apply a sealant or stain, and do a final inspection to make sure your deck is safe and up to code.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
