      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/emergency-leak-detection/national-average",
      transcript:
        "A hidden water leak can destroy your home before you even know it\u2019s there. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to find and stop an emergency leak fast, step by step.\n\nFirst, do a quick assessment. Check your plumbing, ceilings, and floors for wet spots or water stains. If you see active leaking, shut off the main water supply right away.\n\nNext, use a moisture meter or an electronic leak detector to find the exact spot where water is escaping. Mark the area so you know where to work.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time for a temporary fix. Use a pipe repair clamp, plumber\u2019s epoxy putty, or Teflon tape to seal the leak. Place buckets or towels under the area to catch any dripping water and prevent more damage.\n\nFinally, take photos and notes of what you found. Write down your recommendations for a permanent repair or call a pro if needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
