        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/tile-caulking/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to make your tile joints look flawless and last longer? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to caulk tile like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: sanded caulk, painter\u2019s tape, rags or sponges, and latex gloves. For every 100 linear feet, you\u2019ll need about two tubes of caulk, one roll of tape, and a pack of rags.\n\nStart with surface preparation. Clean the tile joints well\u2014remove any old caulk or debris. Make sure the area is dry. This helps the new caulk stick and seal properly.\n\nNext, apply painter\u2019s tape along both sides of the joint for a crisp line. Cut the tip of your caulk tube at a 45-degree angle. Load it into your caulking gun. Squeeze out a steady bead of caulk along the joint. Don\u2019t rush\u2014keep it even.\n\nNow, smooth the caulk with a wet finger or a caulking tool. This gives you a neat, professional finish. Wipe away any extra caulk with a damp rag.\n\nFinally, let the caulk cure as the manufacturer recommends. Keep the area ventilated. Once it\u2019s dry, remove the tape and clean up.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
