        "Thinking about swapping out your old dishwasher? Here\u2019s how to do it safely and right. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to remove your old dishwasher and install a new one, step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off the power at the breaker and turn off the water supply under the sink. Disconnect the drain hose and water line, then unplug or disconnect the electrical wiring. Carefully slide out the old dishwasher and set it aside.\n\nNext, clean the space and check your connections. Make sure the electrical box, water line, and drain hose are in good shape and meet your local codes. Lay down a towel to catch any water spills.\n\nNow, get your new dishwasher ready. Attach the installation kit\u2014hoses, clamps, and fittings. Use Teflon tape on threaded connections and plumber\u2019s putty where needed. Slide the new unit into place, making sure it\u2019s level. Connect the water supply, drain hose, and electrical wiring. Secure the dishwasher to the countertop or cabinet.\n\nFinally, turn the power and water back on. Run a test cycle to check for leaks and make sure everything works.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
