      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely frame a load-bearing wall that stands the test of time? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to frame a strong, code-compliant load-bearing wall. \n\nFirst, review your structural plans and mark the wall location on the floor and ceiling. Double-check all measurements and make sure you\u2019re following your local building codes. \n\nNext, prepare your materials. Cut your 2x4 studs, pressure-treated bottom plates, and header beam to size. Gather your fasteners, construction adhesive, metal joist hangers, and Simpson Strong-Tie brackets. Stage everything close to your work area for easy access.\n\nNow, start framing. Secure the bottom and top plates to the floor and ceiling. Use construction adhesive and 16d framing nails for extra strength. Install your studs, spacing them 16 inches on center, and make sure they\u2019re plumb. Set your header beam in place above any openings, using joist hangers and brackets for support.\n\nOnce the frame is up, double-check all connections. Add blocking or bracing where needed. If required, schedule an inspection with your local building department.\n\nFinally, clean up the site. Remove debris and organize your tools so the area is safe for the next phase.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
