        "Did you know a hidden gas leak could put your home at serious risk? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely inspect your gas lines and spot problems before they become emergencies. \n\nFirst, shut off the main gas supply. Make sure the area is well-ventilated and all gas appliances are turned off. Safety first!\n\nNext, do a visual inspection. Look closely at all exposed gas lines, joints, and connections. Check for rust, corrosion, cracks, or any signs of damage. Make sure pipes are properly labeled and supported.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time for leak testing. Use a gas leak detection solution\u2014apply it to all fittings and joints. Watch for bubbles, which mean there\u2019s a leak. If you have a gas detector, use it for extra safety. \n\nDocument everything you find. Once you\u2019re sure it\u2019s safe, restore the gas supply following all safety rules for your area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
