      transcript:
        "Want a leak-proof roof that lasts? Here\u2019s how to install a roof membrane the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process to install TPO, PVC, or EPDM roof membranes, from prep to final inspection.\n\nFirst, clear the roof. Remove old materials, sweep away debris, and fix any damage. The surface must be clean and dry for the membrane to stick.\n\nNext, measure your roof and cut the membrane sheets. Leave enough for overlaps and around pipes or vents. Double-check your cuts to match your roof\u2019s shape.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install. Apply adhesive or use fasteners as the manufacturer recommends. Roll out the membrane, making sure it\u2019s flat and smooth. Seal the seams with heat welding or approved tape to keep water out.\n\nAfter that, focus on the details. Install flashing around edges, vents, and any roof penetrations. This step is key for a watertight finish.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Check all seams and flashing. Do a water test if needed. Clean up the site and make sure everything meets local codes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
