        "Want to install a wall-mounted sink that looks great and saves space? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to do it right, from prep to final touches. \n\nFirst, shut off your water supply. Mark the sink height on your wall and use a stud finder to locate the studs\u2014this is where your sink will anchor for strength. Gather your sink, mounting bracket, faucet, supply lines, P-trap, shutoff valves, silicone caulk, and all fasteners.\n\nNext, install the mounting bracket. Make sure it\u2019s level and screw it directly into the studs using heavy-duty anchors and fasteners. This is key for safety and stability.\n\nNow, hang the sink on the bracket. Attach the faucet and connect the supply lines to your shutoff valves. Install the P-trap and drain assembly, making sure all connections are tight. Use silicone caulk around the edges for a watertight seal.\n\nFinally, turn the water back on. Check for leaks and test the sink. Wipe down the area and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
