      transcript:
        "Is your heating system ready for the cold months ahead? In this video, you'll learn how to do a full heating system tune-up, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the power to your heating unit. Inspect the system for leaks, rust, or worn parts. Make sure everything meets your local safety codes. \n\nNext, clean the burners, blower, and vents. Replace the air filter with a new one\u2014this is key for good air quality. Don\u2019t forget to clean out any dust or debris from ducts you can reach. \n\nNow, restore power. Test your thermostat and replace the batteries if needed. Make sure the system cycles on and off correctly. Check airflow and confirm all safety controls work as they should. \n\nYou\u2019ll need a new air filter, thermostat batteries, cleaning supplies, and lubricant for moving parts. Plan for about two hours per system. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
