      transcript:
        "Is your fence looking tired or worn out? Let\u2019s bring it back to life with a simple maintenance routine you can do yourself. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to inspect, repair, prep, and refinish your wood fence step by step.\n\nStart by walking along your fence. Look for loose boards, rusted nails, or any signs of damage. Clear away dirt, leaves, and any plants growing on or near the fence using a stiff brush or a hose. This helps you see what needs fixing.\n\nNext, grab your tools. Tighten or replace any loose nails or screws. Swap out broken boards with new ones. If you see any leaning sections, straighten them and secure the posts.\n\nNow, prep the surface. Sand down rough spots and peeling paint. Remove any old stain or paint if needed. Make sure the wood is dry and smooth before moving on.\n\nFinally, apply a fresh coat of exterior wood stain or paint. Use a brush, roller, or sprayer for even coverage. Let it dry fully before touching or hanging anything on the fence.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
