      transcript:
        "Want to heat your home efficiently and evenly? Hydronic heating could be your answer. In this video, you'll learn how to install a complete hydronic heating system, step by step.\n\nFirst, plan your system. Assess your heating needs, design the layout, and gather all your materials\u2014like a hydronic boiler, PEX tubing, circulator pumps, manifolds, thermostats, and insulation.\n\nNext, install the piping and radiators. Run your supply and return lines, mount radiators or lay underfloor PEX tubing, and secure every connection. Make sure you follow local building codes.\n\nNow, set up the boiler. Place it in a safe spot, connect it to your piping, and install the circulator pumps, zone valves, and expansion tank.\n\nFill the system with water. Purge all air from the lines, check for leaks, and test every component to make sure it works right.\n\nFinally, do a full inspection. Adjust your controls, set the thermostats, and show the user how to operate the system safely and efficiently.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
