        "Want to make your floors look finished and professional? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install quarter round molding step by step. \n\nFirst, measure the perimeter of your room. Mark those lengths on your quarter round molding. Use a miter saw to cut each piece, making sure corners and edges fit tight.\n\nNext, clean the baseboards and floor edges. Remove any dust or debris. Dry fit each piece of quarter round to check the fit before you nail anything down.\n\nNow, install the quarter round. Use finishing nails or a nail gun to secure each piece to the baseboard, not the floor. Make sure every piece sits flush and lines up at the corners.\n\nAfter all the molding is up, fill the nail holes with wood filler. Caulk any gaps between the molding and the baseboard. Once it\u2019s dry, touch up with paint or stain to match your trim.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
