      transcript:
        "Want to make your home the brightest on the block this holiday season? In this video, you'll learn exactly how to plan and hang holiday lights like a pro, step by step.\n\nFirst, start with planning and prep. Meet with your client or family to decide on the design. Measure the areas where you want to hang lights\u2014roofs, gutters, trees, or fences. Test every light strand and extension cord before you start. This saves time and avoids surprises.\n\nNext, gather your materials. For every 100 feet of lights, you'll need one LED light strand, two outdoor extension cords, a pack of 100 light clips or hooks, and one outdoor timer. Make sure all your materials are rated for outdoor use.\n\nNow, it's time to hang the lights. Use the right clips or hooks to attach lights safely to each surface. Secure all connections and keep them weatherproof. Take your time to space the lights evenly and avoid overloading any outlet.\n\nOnce everything is up, inspect your work. Turn on the lights, check for any dark spots, and adjust as needed. Clean up the area and give your client or family some simple maintenance tips, like checking timers and replacing bulbs if needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
