        "Want to give your room a high-end look without breaking the bank? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install cornice molding like a pro, step by step.\n\nFirst, measure every wall where you\u2019ll install molding. Mark your stud locations and plan your corner cuts. Gather your tools: a miter saw, tape measure, level, construction adhesive, finishing nails, caulk, and paint.\n\nNext, cut your cornice molding to size. Use a miter saw for clean, accurate angles\u2014especially for corners. Test-fit each piece before you move on.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install. Apply construction adhesive to the back of the molding, or use finishing nails to secure it to the wall and ceiling. Make sure each piece is level and the joints are tight.\n\nFor a flawless finish, fill nail holes and seams with caulk. Once dry, sand smooth. Then, paint or finish the molding to match your decor. Clean up your workspace and inspect your work for quality.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
