      transcript:
        "Are your gutters sagging or overflowing every time it rains? In this video, you'll learn how to realign your gutters for perfect drainage and a leak-free system. \n\nFirst, inspect your gutters. Look for sagging, bad slopes, or damage. Measure the full length and mark any problem spots. This helps you plan where to adjust or replace hangers.\n\nNext, remove the gutter sections and downspouts as needed. Clean out any debris from the gutters and fascia. Gather your new hangers, screws, sealant, and straps.\n\nNow, realign the gutters. Adjust or replace hangers so the gutter slopes slightly toward the downspouts\u2014about a quarter inch drop for every 10 feet. Reinstall the gutter sections, making sure they're secure and straight.\n\nSeal all the joints and connections with gutter sealant. Finally, test your work by running water through the gutters. Check for leaks and make sure water flows smoothly to the downspouts.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
