      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to replace a broken window glass yourself and get a perfect, weather-tight seal? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install new window glass like a pro. \n\nFirst, put on safety gloves and carefully remove any old or broken glass from the window frame. Use a putty knife to scrape away old glazing putty and check the frame for any damage. Clean the frame well so the new glass will fit snugly.\n\nNext, measure the window opening precisely\u2014measure both width and height, and subtract about 1/8 inch for expansion. Order your glass cut to size, or cut it yourself if you have the tools. Before installing, dry-fit the glass in the frame to make sure it fits perfectly.\n\nNow, apply a thin bead of glazing putty or silicone caulk around the frame. Gently set the new glass pane in place. Use glazing points or clips to hold the glass securely. Press them in every 6 inches along the edge. Smooth more putty or caulk over the edges for a tight, weatherproof seal. Let it cure as directed.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your window is as good as new. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
