        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/corroded-pipe-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your water pipe leaking or showing signs of corrosion? Don\u2019t panic\u2014fixing a corroded pipe is easier than you think. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to safely remove and replace a damaged copper pipe section, step by step.\n\nFirst, shut off the main water supply and drain the lines. This keeps your workspace dry and safe. Next, inspect the corroded pipe to see how much needs replacing. Mark the damaged section.\n\nNow, use a pipe cutter or hacksaw to remove the bad pipe. Make sure your cuts are straight and the edges are clean. Use an emery cloth or cleaning brush to prep the ends for a good seal.\n\nMeasure and cut your new copper pipe. Attach couplings or fittings to both ends. Apply flux, then solder the joints for a watertight connection. Don\u2019t forget to add pipe insulation to protect against future corrosion.\n\nFinally, turn the water back on and check for leaks. If everything looks good, you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
