      transcript:
        "Ever wondered exactly where your property ends and your neighbor\u2019s begins? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to complete a lot line survey step by step, so you can mark your boundaries with confidence.\n\nFirst, gather your property documents, any old surveys, and plat maps. Check your local rules\u2014some areas have strict requirements for surveys.\n\nNext, head to your property with your materials: 8 surveyor stakes, 16 survey flags, 4 rebar pins, and a can of marking paint. Look for any existing property markers. Use a measuring tape or, for best results, a surveyor\u2019s transit or GPS tool to measure the boundaries. Mark each corner with a rebar pin and a stake, then flag the lines and spray paint for visibility. Take notes and photos of everything you find.\n\nBack at your desk, compare your measurements to the official records. Use mapping software or graph paper to draw your updated lot lines. Double-check for any differences or errors.\n\nFinally, write up a report. Include your map, all measurements, and any issues you found. Make sure it meets your local standards.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
