        "Is your fiber cement siding cracked or damaged? You can fix it yourself and make your home look new again. In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair fiber cement siding the right way.\n\nFirst, inspect the area. Look for damaged boards and mark them. Clear away any debris so you have space to work. Gather your tools, new siding planks, galvanized nails, flashing tape, caulk, and touch-up paint.\n\nNext, remove the damaged siding. Use a pry bar and hammer to gently pull off the bad boards. Take out any nails or screws. Be careful not to break the good siding around it.\n\nNow, install the new boards. Measure and cut your fiber cement planks to fit. Slide them into place and fasten with galvanized nails. Make sure the boards are straight and spaced like the rest of your siding.\n\nAfter that, seal all the seams with exterior caulk. Let it dry, then prime and paint the new boards to match your house. Clean up your tools and any leftover scraps.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
