      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to install a window screen that fits perfectly and keeps bugs out? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to build and install a window screen from scratch. \n\nFirst, measure your window opening. Write down the width and height. Gather your materials: a window screen frame kit, screen mesh, spline (that\u2019s the rubber cord), four frame corners, and pull tabs. You\u2019ll also need a utility knife, a spline roller, and a tape measure.\n\nNext, cut the frame pieces to match your window size. Connect the corners to build the frame. Test-fit it in the window to make sure it\u2019s snug but not too tight.\n\nNow, lay the screen mesh over the frame. Use the spline roller to press the spline into the groove, locking the mesh in place. Trim off any extra mesh with your utility knife. Attach the pull tabs so you can easily remove the screen later.\n\nFinally, pop the finished screen into your window. Check that it fits and sits flat.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
