      transcript:
        "Want your hot tub to last longer and stay crystal clear? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process for professional hot tub maintenance. \n\nFirst, always turn off the power. Drain the hot tub completely. Use a hot tub filter cleaner and a soft cloth to scrub the shell and filters. This removes buildup and keeps your water fresh.\n\nNext, inspect all the parts. Check the jets, pumps, and heater. Look for leaks, worn parts, or anything that seems off. Make sure everything meets local safety standards.\n\nNow, refill your hot tub with clean water. Test the water using hot tub test strips. Add a sanitizer like chlorine or bromine. Balance the pH with a pH balancer, and adjust alkalinity and calcium hardness as needed. Use a spa shock treatment to keep the water safe and clear. Test again to confirm the water is balanced before turning the power back on.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
