      transcript:
        "Ever wondered exactly where your property ends and your neighbor\u2019s begins? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to complete a property boundary survey step by step, so you know your land\u2019s true limits.\n\nFirst, gather your documents. Find your property deed, plat, and any old surveys. Review the legal description and get your tools ready: surveyor stakes, flagging tape, rebar pins, and spray marking paint.\n\nNext, head to your property. Look for any existing boundary markers. Use a measuring tape or survey equipment to check the property lines. Mark each corner with a stake and rebar pin, then flag and spray paint them so they\u2019re easy to spot.\n\nBack at your desk, compare your field notes to the legal documents. Draw an updated boundary map, making sure everything matches up. Document your findings clearly.\n\nFinally, deliver the survey report and map to the client. Walk them through your findings and answer any questions about their property lines.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
