      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/iron-filter-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Tired of rusty water stains and metallic taste in your home? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a whole-house iron filter system, step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off your main water supply. Pick a spot near your main line for the filter, and gather your tools and materials: the iron filter system, bypass valve kit, flexible connectors, PVC or PEX pipe and fittings, gravel and filter media, drain tubing, pipe insulation, mounting hardware, and Teflon tape.\n\nNext, cut into your main water line. Install the bypass valve so you can service the filter later. Connect the iron filter system, making sure all fittings are tight and match your plumbing type. Use Teflon tape on threaded joints to prevent leaks. Add gravel and filter media as the manufacturer recommends.\n\nAttach the drain line tubing for backwashing, and insulate any exposed pipes. Mount the filter securely with brackets.\n\nNow, slowly turn the water back on. Check every connection for leaks. Flush the system as directed, then test your water to make sure the iron is gone.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
