        "Want to make your home's exterior look fresh without a full repaint? In this video, you'll learn how to do a professional exterior paint touch up, step by step. \n\nFirst, prep your surfaces. Clean the area with a brush or pressure washer to remove dirt, mildew, and loose paint. Let it dry completely. \n\nNext, sand any rough or peeling spots. Feather the edges so the new paint blends in. Apply primer to any bare wood or patched spots. This helps the paint stick and last longer. \n\nNow, it's time to paint. Use a brush or roller to apply matching exterior paint. Blend the edges into the old paint for a seamless look. Let the first coat dry, then add a second if needed. \n\nFinally, inspect your work. Touch up any missed spots. Clean your brushes, throw away used materials, and store leftover paint for future touch ups. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
