        "Did you know you can repair a damaged bathtub liner in just a few hours and save hundreds? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to fix cracks, chips, or holes in your bathtub liner so it looks and works like new. \n\nFirst, clean the entire liner with a non-abrasive cleaner. Make sure you remove all soap scum and dirt. Inspect the liner closely for any cracks, chips, or loose spots.\n\nNext, sand the damaged areas with assorted grit sandpaper. Wipe away all dust and debris, then dry the liner completely. Use masking tape to protect the edges and nearby surfaces.\n\nNow, mix your epoxy adhesive or repair compound as directed. Apply it to the cracks or holes, smoothing it out so it\u2019s level with the rest of the liner. Let it cure for the time listed on your repair kit\u2014don\u2019t rush this step!\n\nOnce cured, sand the repaired spots until smooth. Remove the masking tape and clean up any leftover materials. Your bathtub liner is now ready for use!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
