        "Want to make your yard look sharp and stay tidy? Let\u2019s install landscape edging the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to plan, dig, and set up edging for a clean, professional look.\n\nFirst, measure and mark where you want your edging. Use a garden hose or string to outline curves and straight lines. This helps you see the final shape before you start digging.\n\nNext, dig a trench along your marked lines. Make it deep and wide enough for your edging\u2014usually about 4 to 6 inches deep. Remove any grass, roots, or rocks so the base is smooth and stable.\n\nNow, lay your edging into the trench. Adjust it so it follows your lines perfectly. Secure it with stakes or anchors every few feet to keep it in place. If you\u2019re using weed barrier fabric, lay it down before backfilling.\n\nFinally, backfill the trench with soil. Press the soil down firmly to hold the edging steady. Clean up the area, and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
