      transcript:
        "Want to strip old paint off your cabinets without damaging the wood? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to safely and effectively strip paint from cabinets, so you\u2019re ready for a fresh new finish. \n\nFirst, remove all cabinet doors, drawers, and hardware. Lay down plastic drop cloths to protect your floors, open windows for ventilation, and put on rubber gloves and a respirator mask. Safety first!\n\nNext, use a brush to apply a chemical paint stripper to all cabinet surfaces. Follow the instructions on the label and let it sit for the recommended time so it can break down the paint.\n\nOnce the paint softens, gently scrape it off with a plastic scraper. Wipe away any residue with clean rags. For stubborn spots, use steel wool pads to get into corners and grooves.\n\nAfter all the paint is removed, clean the cabinets with water or a neutralizer to get rid of any leftover stripper. Let everything dry completely.\n\nFinally, lightly sand the surfaces to smooth the wood and remove any last bits of paint. Inspect your work to make sure you didn\u2019t miss any spots. Now your cabinets are ready for a new look!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
