      transcript:
        "Did you know a clogged carbon filter can ruin your water quality fast? In this video, you'll learn how to replace a carbon filter step by step, so your water stays clean and safe. \n\nFirst, turn off the water supply to your filtration system. Open a faucet nearby to relieve any pressure. Find the carbon filter housing and get your tools ready. \n\nNext, unscrew the filter housing. Take out the old carbon filter and throw it away. Clean the inside of the housing with mild soap and water. Rinse it well. Now, insert the new carbon filter, making sure it sits straight and snug. Replace the O-ring or gasket if needed, and use a little Teflon plumber\u2019s tape on the threads for a tight seal.\n\nScrew the housing back on securely. Turn the water supply back on and check for leaks. Run water for a few minutes to flush the new filter and clear out any loose carbon. Make sure everything is working right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
