      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to add a new light switch without calling an electrician? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely install a single pole light switch from start to finish. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker panel. Always double-check with a voltage tester to make sure the power is off. Mark the spot on your wall where you want the new switch.\n\nNext, cut an opening for the electrical box. Run Romex 14/2 wire from your power source or light fixture to the new switch location. Make sure the wire is long enough\u2014about 25 feet is typical for one switch.\n\nInstall the single gang electrical box in the wall. Strip the wire ends, then connect the black (hot) wire to one brass screw on the switch, and the white (neutral) wire to the other. Attach the ground wire to the green screw. Use wire connectors and wrap connections with electrical tape for safety.\n\nSecure the switch in the box, screw on the cover plate, and restore power at the breaker. Test your new switch to make sure it works.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
