      transcript:
        "Want to turn your basement into usable space with a new wall? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to build a basement partition wall, from layout to finishing touches. \n\nFirst, measure and mark where your wall will go. Snap chalk lines on the floor and ceiling. Cut your 2x4s for the top and bottom plates. Use pressure-treated lumber for the bottom plate to prevent moisture damage. Secure the plates to the floor and ceiling with construction adhesive and screws or anchors.\n\nNext, stand up your wall studs every 16 inches. Nail or screw them in place. If you need electrical, install boxes and run wiring now. Then, add R-13 insulation batts between the studs for sound and energy control.\n\nHang drywall sheets on both sides of the wall. Cut out for outlets as you go. Fasten the drywall with screws every 12 inches along the studs.\n\nTape the seams with paper tape and cover with joint compound. Let it dry, sand smooth, and repeat as needed. Once smooth, prime and paint your new wall.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
