      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a drain leak without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair a leaking drain pipe and stop water damage fast. \n\nFirst, find the leak. Look under your sink or in the basement and check all pipes and joints for drips or water stains. Figure out exactly where the water is coming from.\n\nNext, shut off the water to the area. Clear out anything under the sink or around the pipes. Put down a bucket or towels to catch any leftover water.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to repair. Remove the damaged pipe or fitting. Clean the pipe ends with a rag. Use new PVC pipe, couplings, and a replacement P-trap if needed. Apply plumber\u2019s putty or joint compound to the threads, and wrap Teflon tape around them. Connect everything tightly, making sure the pipes line up straight. Use pipe hangers or straps to support the new pipe.\n\nTurn the water back on. Run water through the drain and check every joint for leaks. Wipe up any water and make sure the repair looks good and dry.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
