        "Are your gutters sagging or leaking every time it rains? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to reinforce your gutters so they last for years. \n\nFirst, clean out all debris and leaves from your gutters. Take a close look for any sagging, rust, or damage\u2014these are the spots that need extra support.\n\nNext, check all the gutter brackets. Tighten any loose ones, and add new hanger brackets every two to three feet, especially in weak areas. Use stainless steel screws for a strong hold.\n\nNow, seal every seam and joint with gutter sealant. For extra strength, install gutter screws or rivets at the joints. Make sure your gutters are sloped correctly so water flows to the downspouts.\n\nFinally, run water through the gutters to check for leaks and proper flow. Make any final tweaks, then clean up your work area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
