      transcript:
        "Is your radiant floor heating leaving you cold in spots? In this video, you'll learn how to diagnose and repair a radiant floor heating system step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off the power and access the manifold. Inspect for leaks, airlocks, or zones that aren't heating. Use leak detection dye if needed to spot hidden leaks. \n\nNext, repair or replace damaged PEX tubing with a repair kit. Swap out any faulty manifold fittings, thermostats, pumps, or valves. Make sure all new parts match your system. \n\nNow, bleed air from the system. Refill with water and pressurize to the manufacturer's specs. Watch for leaks and check that the pressure stays steady. \n\nFinally, restore power and test each heating zone. Make sure the floor heats evenly. Patch the floor if needed, clean up, and dispose of waste safely. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
