      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a damaged drywall corner so it looks brand new? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair a corner bead like a pro. \n\nFirst, remove any loose drywall, old joint compound, and the damaged corner bead. Use a utility knife and a putty knife to clean up the area. Sand the surface so it\u2019s smooth and ready for new material.\n\nNext, measure and cut a new metal corner bead to fit the corner. Secure it in place with drywall screws or nails, making sure it lines up perfectly with the wall.\n\nNow, apply joint compound over the corner bead. Use a drywall knife to feather the edges so it blends into the wall. Let it dry, then sand it smooth. You may need to add a second or third coat for a perfect finish, sanding between each coat.\n\nFinally, wipe away any dust, prime the area, and paint to match the rest of your wall. Your corner should look seamless!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
