        "Did you know a dirty return vent can ruin your air quality and spike your energy bills? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to clean your return vent like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off your HVAC system for safety. Lay down disposable drop cloths to protect your floors, and put on gloves and a mask. Gather your supplies: coil cleaner, microfiber cloths, a vacuum, and a new air filter.\n\nNext, unscrew and remove the vent cover. Keep the screws in a safe spot. Check the cover for dust and debris.\n\nNow, vacuum inside the vent opening and the area around it. Use a microfiber cloth to wipe down the vent cover and the inside surfaces. If you see stubborn grime, spray a little HVAC coil cleaner and wipe again.\n\nReplace the old air filter with a new one. Then, reattach the vent cover securely. Turn your HVAC system back on and check the airflow to make sure everything\u2019s working right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
