      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to demolish an old barn, step by step? In this video, you'll learn exactly how to plan, prepare, and safely tear down a 1,200 square foot barn. \n\nFirst, start with a site assessment. Inspect the barn for hazards, get your permits, and disconnect all utilities. Set up temporary fencing and clear the area for safety. This takes about 8 to 10 hours.\n\nNext, salvage any reusable materials like doors, windows, or beams. If you find hazardous materials like asbestos or lead paint, follow your local rules for safe removal. This step usually takes 16 to 20 hours.\n\nNow, it's time for the main event: structural demolition. Use an excavator and the right demolition tools. Start with the roof, then move to the walls, and finally the foundation. Always follow safety protocols. This part takes 40 to 45 hours.\n\nFinally, sort the debris for recycling or disposal. Load it into dumpsters and clean up the site, making sure the ground is restored as required. Plan for 10 to 12 hours for this final step.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
