      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to safely demolish a retaining wall? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process, from prep to cleanup, so you can tackle this project with confidence. \n\nFirst, start with site preparation and safety. Clear everything around the wall and set up safety barriers. Make sure all utilities are marked and protected\u2014never skip this step. This should take about 2 to 3 hours.\n\nNext, it's time for demolition. Use a mini excavator with a breaker to carefully take down the wall, starting at the top and working your way down. Wear your personal protective equipment, and use dust control like a water sprayer. Remove debris as you go to keep the site safe. This part usually takes 8 to 10 hours for 100 feet of wall.\n\nFinally, collect all debris and load it into a 10-yard disposal bin. Use plastic sheeting to contain dust and debris. Clean up the site, level the ground, and make sure everything is safe for future work. This cleanup step takes about 3 to 4 hours.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
