        "Did you know a damaged gutter or fascia can ruin your roof fast? In this video, you'll learn how to repair your gutter and fascia step by step, so your home stays protected. \n\nFirst, inspect your gutters and fascia. Look for rot, cracks, or sagging. Remove any debris, and set up your ladder and safety gear. Gather all your tools and materials before you start.\n\nNext, carefully remove the damaged gutter sections and fascia boards. Use a pry bar and screwdriver. Be gentle to avoid damaging your roof or siding. Dispose of the old materials safely.\n\nNow, measure and cut your new fascia boards. Attach them with exterior wood screws. Then, install the new aluminum gutter sections. Use gutter hangers or brackets every few feet for support. Make sure everything lines up and is secure.\n\nSeal all joints and seams with exterior caulk. Test the gutters by running water through them to check for leaks. Finally, clean up your work area and make sure everything meets local building codes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
