      transcript:
        "Want to make your bathroom look brand new with a tiled tub surround? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a tile tub surround like a pro. \n\nFirst, prep your surface. Remove the old surround, clean the walls, and fix any damage. Install cement backer board using screws and fasteners to create a solid, waterproof base.\n\nNext, plan your tile layout. Dry-fit your tiles to see how they\u2019ll look. Mix thinset mortar and spread it on the wall with a notched trowel. Press each tile into place, using spacers for even grout lines. Cut tiles as needed for corners and edges.\n\nOnce the tiles are set, it\u2019s time to grout. Apply grout between the tiles, wipe away the excess, and let it cure. Then, seal the grout to protect against moisture.\n\nFinish up by running silicone caulk along all seams and corners. Clean the area, reinstall fixtures, and your new tub surround is ready to use!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
