      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely remove old wood siding without damaging your home? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to remove wood siding like a pro. \n\nFirst, get your materials ready: heavy-duty contractor bags, pry bars, dust masks, gloves, and plastic sheeting. You\u2019ll need these for safety and cleanup.\n\nStart with site preparation. Clear the area around your house, set up ladders or scaffolding, and put on your safety gear. This takes about 2 to 3 hours but makes the job much safer.\n\nNext, remove any exterior trim, light fixtures, and downspouts attached to the siding. Take your time\u2014this prevents damage and gives you full access to the wood panels.\n\nNow, use your pry bar and nail puller to detach the wood siding boards. Work from the top down, and be careful not to damage the sheathing underneath. This step can take 6 to 7 hours for 500 square feet.\n\nFinally, inspect the exposed sheathing for any damage, pull out leftover nails, and clean up all debris. Use your contractor bags and plastic sheeting for safe disposal.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
