        "Want to give your cabinets a high-end look without replacing them? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to glaze your cabinets step by step, so you get a pro finish every time. \n\nFirst, take off all cabinet doors and hardware. Clean every surface with a degreaser, then lightly sand to help the glaze stick. Lay down drop cloths and tape off areas you don\u2019t want to paint.\n\nNext, apply a fresh coat of paint or primer. Let it dry fully\u2014this is key for a smooth finish.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to glaze. Use a brush or foam applicator to spread the glaze in small sections. Wipe off the excess with a lint-free rag, working until you get the look you want. Take your time\u2014this is where the magic happens.\n\nCheck for any uneven spots. Blend and touch up corners or crevices so everything looks even.\n\nFinally, let the glaze cure. Reinstall your hardware and doors, and clean up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
