      transcript:
        "Want to make your walls look brand new? Here\u2019s how to install drywall like a pro, step by step. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to prep, hang, tape, and finish drywall for a smooth, paint-ready wall.\n\nFirst, clear your work area and gather your materials: drywall sheets, screws, joint compound, paper tape, and corner bead. Check your wall framing\u2014make sure it\u2019s solid and meets local building codes.\n\nNext, measure and cut your drywall sheets. Fasten them to the framing with drywall screws, making sure seams line up and you cut out for outlets or fixtures.\n\nNow, tape all the seams with paper tape. Cover seams and screw heads with a first coat of joint compound. Smooth it out and let it dry\u2014drying time depends on your local climate.\n\nOnce dry, add more coats of joint compound as needed, sanding between each coat for a smooth finish. Check for any bumps or dents. When it\u2019s perfect, your wall is ready for paint or texture.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
