        "Is your deck hiding dangerous rot that could cost you big? In this video, you'll learn how to spot, remove, and repair deck rot step by step. \n\nFirst, inspect your deck. Look for soft spots, discoloration, or crumbling wood on boards, joists, and posts. Mark any damaged areas. Clear away debris and gather your tools: pry bar, saw, new pressure-treated boards and joists, galvanized screws, wood preservative, flashing tape, adhesive, and disposal bags.\n\nNext, carefully remove all rotted wood. Use a pry bar and saw to take out damaged boards and framing. Bag up the debris and dispose of it according to your local rules.\n\nNow, measure and cut new pressure-treated lumber to fit. Install the new boards and joists, securing them with galvanized screws. Apply wood preservative to cut ends and flashing tape over joists for extra protection. Use construction adhesive for added strength. Make sure everything is level and meets your local building codes.\n\nFinally, seal or stain the new wood to match your deck. Check for stability, clean up the area, and dispose of waste properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
