      transcript:
        "Want a garage floor that lasts for years and looks great? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to install a new garage floor step by step, from prep to finish. \n\nFirst, clear out your garage. Sweep up dust, degrease any oil spots, and patch cracks or holes. This takes about 6 to 8 hours, but it\u2019s key for a smooth finish.\n\nNext, roll out a 6 mil poly vapor barrier to block moisture. Lay it flat and overlap the seams. Mark your layout lines and gather all your materials: ready-mix concrete, wire mesh, expansion joints, anchor bolts, and sealer. This setup takes 4 to 5 hours.\n\nNow, install the floor. Pour your 4000 psi concrete, about 3.7 cubic yards for a 400 sq ft garage. Place wire mesh for strength and set expansion joints every 10 feet. Don\u2019t forget anchor bolts if you need them. Smooth the surface and let it set. This step takes 12 to 14 hours.\n\nFinally, let the floor cure for at least 24 hours. Apply a concrete sealer for protection. Reinstall baseboards and move your stuff back in. Cleanup takes 8 to 10 hours.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
