        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/gutter-slope-adjustment/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wonder why your gutters overflow even when they're clean? Today, I'll show you how to fix that by adjusting your gutter slope for perfect drainage. \n\nFirst, inspect your gutters for standing water or slow drainage. Use a level to check the current slope\u2014mark where the downspouts should be for the best flow.\n\nNext, carefully remove the gutter hangers and fasteners along the section you need to adjust. Lower the gutter to a safe height so you can work comfortably.\n\nNow, it's time to set the right slope. Aim for at least a quarter inch drop for every 10 feet of gutter, sloping toward the downspout. Use a string line and level to get it just right.\n\nOnce the slope is set, reattach the gutters with new or existing hangers. Make sure everything is secure and the slope is consistent. Seal all joints and connections with caulk to prevent leaks.\n\nFinally, flush the gutters with water to test the flow and check for leaks. Clean up your tools and any debris.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
