      transcript:
        "Thinking about replacing your porch? Here\u2019s what it really takes to do it right. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process to replace a porch, from demolition to finishing touches, plus what materials and time you\u2019ll need.\n\nFirst, start with demolition and site prep. Remove the old porch, clear away debris, and check the foundation for any damage. This usually takes 6 to 8 hours. Make sure your work area is safe and up to local standards.\n\nNext, move on to foundation and framing. Repair or pour new concrete footings if needed. Install your support posts and build the frame using pressure-treated lumber. Double-check that everything is level and meets your local building codes. This step takes about 12 to 16 hours.\n\nNow, install the decking and railings. Lay down new decking boards, secure them to the frame, and add your railing system and steps. Use weather-resistant materials that fit your climate. Plan for 10 to 12 hours here.\n\nFinally, add the roof or awning if needed, plus trim and any paint or sealant. Match the style of your home for a polished look. This last step takes 8 to 10 hours.\n\nFor materials, you\u2019ll need pressure-treated lumber, concrete, galvanized fasteners, railings, stair parts, post anchors, and joist hangers. Expect about 48 labor hours for a 100 square foot porch.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
