      transcript:
        "Is your window frame soft, cracked, or letting in drafts? You might need a window jamb repair! In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to fix or replace a damaged window jamb step by step. \n\nFirst, inspect the window jamb for rot or damage. Remove any trim or casing around the window so you can see the full jamb. Gather your tools and materials: wood jamb stock, wood filler or epoxy, primer and paint, finish nails or screws, and caulk.\n\nNext, cut out any rotted or broken wood. Measure and cut new jamb pieces to fit. Secure them in place with finish nails or screws. For small holes or cracks, use wood filler or epoxy. Make sure all surfaces are smooth and level before moving on.\n\nNow, sand the repaired areas. Prime and paint or stain the jamb to match the rest of your window. Reinstall the trim or casing. Finally, clean up your work area and check that the window opens and closes smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
