      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to replace your main water line? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process, from shutting off the water to restoring your yard. \n\nFirst, turn off the main water supply and let everyone know. Find your existing water line and main shutoff valve. Mark the dig area, following your local utility guidelines to avoid hitting other lines.\n\nNext, dig a trench along the path of the old water line. Be careful not to damage other utilities. Remove the old pipe and check the trench for any issues.\n\nNow, lay your new PEX water line pipe. Use brass fittings and a new main shutoff valve. Make sure all joints are tight and use pipe tape and sealant. Insulate the pipe and use trenching sand or backfill for support. Always follow your local plumbing codes.\n\nBefore you cover it up, pressurize the new line and check for leaks. Schedule an inspection if your area requires it. Fix any leaks before moving on.\n\nFinally, backfill the trench, compact the soil, and restore your landscaping or pavement. Clean up the area so it\u2019s safe and looks good.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
