      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to make old brickwork look brand new? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to repoint masonry the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, you\u2019ll learn how to prep your surface. Use a chisel or grinder to remove all loose or damaged mortar from the joints. Clean out the dust and debris\u2014this helps the new mortar stick.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time to mix your mortar. Use Type N mortar mix and masonry sand. Add water and mix until it\u2019s smooth and workable. If your joints are deep, insert a backer rod before adding mortar.\n\nNow, fill the joints with fresh mortar using a pointing trowel. Press it in firmly and shape the joints to match the old ones. Take your time\u2014this step is key for a strong, neat finish.\n\nFinally, mist the area with water to help the mortar cure. Wipe off any extra mortar from the bricks and check your joints for a clean, even look.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
