      transcript:
        "Did you know a simple inspection could save your home from dangerous radon gas? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to inspect a radon mitigation system step by step. First, do a visual check. Look at the fan, pipes, and vent for cracks, leaks, or anything out of place. Next, make sure the fan is running. Listen for odd noises and check airflow at the vent outside. Then, inspect all seals and caulking. If you see gaps or old caulk, reseal them. Also, check that all warning labels are easy to read and in the right spots. Finally, test the system\u2019s manometer. The liquid should show a pressure difference. If you have a radon test kit, use it to confirm levels are safe. That\u2019s it! A full inspection in about two hours. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
