      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/air-duct-inspection/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what's really hiding inside your air ducts? Today, I'll show you how to inspect your air ducts step by step, so you can spot problems before they get worse. \n\nFirst, do an initial assessment. Spend about 20 to 30 minutes visually checking all accessible ducts. Look for dust buildup, mold, or any damage. Pay attention to odd smells or weak airflow\u2014these are warning signs.\n\nNext, test your HVAC system. Turn it on and check airflow from every vent. Use a basic tool like a manometer or even a simple thermometer to compare air pressure and temperature at different vents. This helps you find blockages or leaks.\n\nNow, for a detailed inspection. Open vent covers and use a flashlight or an inspection camera. Look deep inside the ducts for dust, debris, or mold. Wear disposable gloves and a dust mask for safety. Take notes or photos of anything unusual.\n\nFinally, write down your findings. If you see heavy buildup or damage, recommend cleaning or repairs. Share your report with the property owner and discuss next steps.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
