      transcript:
        "Is your bathroom drain slow or leaking? Let\u2019s fix it fast and right. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a bathroom drain step by step, from prep to testing. \n\nFirst, clear the area around your drain. Lay down towels or a bucket to catch any water. Gather your tools: PVC pipe, fittings, plumber\u2019s putty, a hacksaw, and Teflon tape.\n\nNext, remove the drain cover. Unscrew it or gently pry it off. Pull out any hair or debris you see. Check the drainpipe for blockages or cracks.\n\nNow, clean the drain. Use a drain snake to clear clogs. If you see worn gaskets or seals, replace them. Apply plumber\u2019s putty around the new drain assembly for a watertight seal. If the pipe is damaged, cut out the bad section and replace it with new PVC pipe and fittings. Use Teflon tape on threaded joints.\n\nFinally, reassemble the drain. Put the cover back on. Run water to check for leaks. Clean up your workspace. Your bathroom drain should now work like new.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
