        "Want to make your roof last longer and stay leak-free? Watch this! Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a roof ridge the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, get your materials ready: ridge cap shingles, roofing nails, sealant, and underlayment. For a 100-foot ridge, you\u2019ll need about 100 feet of each material, 800 nails, and 2 tubes of sealant.\n\nStep one: Prepare the ridge area. Remove any old ridge caps and clear away debris. Check for damage\u2014fix anything before moving on.\n\nStep two: Install the underlayment or ridge vent. Lay it along the ridge, making sure it\u2019s straight and secure. This keeps water out and helps your roof breathe.\n\nStep three: Position your ridge cap shingles. Start at one end, overlap each shingle, and nail them down tight. Follow the manufacturer\u2019s instructions for spacing and overlap.\n\nStep four: Seal and inspect. Use roofing cement on all exposed nails and joints. Look for gaps or loose spots\u2014fix them now to prevent leaks.\n\nThat\u2019s it! If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
