      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to reroute pipes without making a mess or missing a step? In this video, you'll learn the exact process to reroute plumbing pipes safely and efficiently. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply. Inspect your current pipes and plan the new route. Mark the walls or floors where you'll need access, and always check your local plumbing codes.\n\nNext, open up the walls, floors, or ceilings along your planned path. Carefully remove the old pipes and fittings, making sure not to damage the surrounding structure.\n\nNow, it's time to install the new pipes. Cut your PEX pipe to size, connect with elbow fittings and couplings, and secure everything with pipe clamps or hangers. Don't forget to add pipe insulation and use Teflon tape or sealant on threaded joints. Install shutoff valves where needed.\n\nOnce everything is in place, turn the water back on. Check every joint for leaks and make sure the water flows properly. Finally, patch up any walls or floors you opened, restoring them to their original condition.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
