      transcript:
        "Did you know a flood zone survey can save you thousands in future repairs? In this video, you'll learn exactly how to complete a flood zone survey step by step. \n\nFirst, start with a site assessment. Visit your property and gather topographic data. Review any existing maps and look for water bodies or drainage features that could affect flood risk.\n\nNext, measure elevations. Use surveyor field equipment to record ground elevations and the heights of any important structures. This helps you understand how water might flow or collect on your land.\n\nThen, analyze the flood risk. Compare your data with official floodplain maps. This will show you which parts of your property are in a flood zone and how serious the risk is.\n\nFinally, prepare your report. Summarize your findings, include maps, and make recommendations for flood protection. Don\u2019t forget to get a flood elevation certificate if needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
