      transcript:
        "Want to stop leaks and protect your roofline for years to come? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace your gutters and fascia boards step by step. \n\nFirst, remove the old gutters and fascia. Carefully unscrew and detach everything, making sure to clear away all fasteners and debris. \n\nNext, inspect the exposed rafter tails and roof edge. If you see any rot or damage, replace or repair the wood before moving on. A solid base is key for a long-lasting job.\n\nNow, measure and cut your new primed pine fascia boards. Attach them securely along the roof edge, making sure they\u2019re level and all joints are sealed tight.\n\nTime to mount your new aluminum gutters. Use hangers or brackets every few feet, and make sure the gutters slope slightly toward the downspouts for good drainage. Seal all joints and downspout connections with caulk to prevent leaks.\n\nFinally, check the alignment, test water flow, and tighten all fasteners. Clean up the area and dispose of old materials properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
