      transcript:
        "Is your brick fireplace looking cracked or worn out? Let\u2019s fix it step by step! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a brick fireplace like a pro, from inspection to cleanup. \n\nFirst, inspect your fireplace. Look for loose or damaged bricks and crumbling mortar. Clear out any debris and cover nearby surfaces to protect them.\n\nNext, use a chisel and hammer to carefully remove the damaged bricks and old mortar. Clean out the joints so new bricks will fit snugly.\n\nNow, mix up some Type N mortar. Set your replacement bricks in place, making sure they line up with the old pattern. Fill the joints with mortar and use a pointing tool to smooth them out. If you\u2019re fixing the firebox, use special firebricks.\n\nLet the mortar set. Then, tool the joints for a clean finish and wipe away any extra mortar with a masonry cleaner. Finally, tidy up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
