      transcript:
        "Want to make your home warmer and save on energy bills? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install drywall insulation step by step, so you can do it right the first time.\n\nFirst, clear your work area. Move furniture, cover the floors, and make sure you have all your tools and materials ready\u2014like fiberglass batt insulation, vapor barrier, support wire, staples, and a utility knife.\n\nNext, install the insulation. Fit the fiberglass batts snugly between the wall studs. Make sure there are no gaps\u2014this keeps your home well insulated. Use staples or support wire to hold the insulation in place, following your local building codes.\n\nNow, hang your drywall panels. Measure and cut each sheet to fit. Attach them to the framing with screws or nails. Stagger the seams and make sure each panel is flush and secure.\n\nFinally, tape and finish the seams. Apply joint tape and compound over the seams and screw heads. Smooth it out with a drywall knife and let it dry for a seamless look.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
