      transcript:
        "Cracked bricks can ruin your curb appeal and let in water\u2014let\u2019s fix that fast! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair brick cracks step by step, so your wall looks solid and lasts longer. \n\nFirst, prep the surface. Use a wire brush and chisel to remove any loose mortar, dust, or debris from the crack. Make sure the area is clean and dry before you start. \n\nNext, mix your mortar. Follow the instructions on the bag for the right consistency. Use a pointing trowel to press the mortar deep into the crack. Fill it completely, packing it tight for a strong repair. \n\nNow, finish the job. Smooth the mortar so it matches the existing joints. Wipe away any extra mortar from the bricks. Let the repair cure undisturbed for a few hours, or as long as the manufacturer recommends. \n\nFor best results, use a matching brick and consider sealing the area with masonry sealer once it\u2019s dry. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
