      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to move a heavy spa without damaging it or your property? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to safely move a spa from one location to another. \n\nFirst, start with a site assessment. Measure your spa and plan the best route for moving it. Clear any obstacles at both the pickup and delivery sites to make sure you have easy access.\n\nNext, drain all the water from the spa. Disconnect the electrical and plumbing connections. Secure any loose parts so nothing gets damaged during the move.\n\nNow, it's time to load the spa. Use moving blankets and heavy-duty furniture dollies to protect and lift the spa. Wrap it in plastic wrap and use ratchet straps to keep it secure. Lay down plywood sheets to protect surfaces as you move the spa out. Carefully load it onto your transport vehicle.\n\nTransport the spa to the new location. Once there, unload and position it exactly where you want. Reconnect the electrical and plumbing, refill with water, and test all the functions to make sure everything works.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
