      transcript:
        "Want to make your kitchen safer and more functional with a pro-level electrical install? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to wire a kitchen the right way. \n\nFirst, always start by planning. Review your electrical plans, mark where outlets, switches, and appliances will go, and most importantly\u2014shut off power at the main panel. Safety first!\n\nNext, it\u2019s time for wiring and box installation. Run 12/2 NM-B electrical wire to each outlet, switch, and appliance location. Install electrical boxes\u2014use at least 12 for a standard kitchen. Make sure to follow local codes for spacing and height. Use Romex connectors to secure wires entering each box.\n\nNow, connect your devices. Install duplex receptacles\u2014at least 8 for countertop and general use. Use GFCI outlets near sinks for safety. Mount your switches and lighting fixtures, and label each circuit in the panel. Don\u2019t forget to use wire nuts and electrical tape for secure connections.\n\nOnce everything\u2019s in place, schedule an inspection if needed. Restore power and test every outlet, switch, and light to make sure they work safely.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
