      transcript:
        "Want to upgrade your bathroom lighting in under two hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely install a new vanity light, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker box. Double-check the light switch to make sure the power is off. Remove the old vanity light by unscrewing it and disconnecting the wires. Always keep track of which wire is which\u2014usually black to black, white to white, and ground to ground.\n\nNext, attach the new mounting bracket to the electrical box. Use a level to make sure it\u2019s straight, then tighten the screws so it\u2019s secure.\n\nNow, connect the new fixture\u2019s wires to the house wires using wire connectors. Match the colors: black to black, white to white, and green or bare copper to ground. Tuck the wires neatly into the box. Mount the new vanity light onto the bracket, secure it with the provided hardware, and install the bulbs.\n\nTurn the power back on and test your new light. That\u2019s it! If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
