      transcript:
        "Thinking about replacing your kitchen cabinets? Here\u2019s how to do it right, step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to remove old cabinets, prep your space, install new cabinets, and finish the job like a pro. \n\nFirst, empty all your cabinets and disconnect any plumbing or electrical lines. Carefully unscrew and remove the old cabinets from the walls. Check the wall for any damage and repair it if needed.\n\nNext, patch any holes and fix the drywall. Mark where the wall studs are, and make sure your walls and floors are level. This is key for a smooth install.\n\nNow, start installing your new cabinets. Begin with the upper cabinets. Secure them to the studs, making sure everything is level and lined up. Then, install the base cabinets the same way. Follow the manufacturer\u2019s instructions for best results.\n\nFinally, add the hardware\u2014pulls, knobs, and hinges. Adjust the doors and drawers so they open smoothly. Reconnect any utilities, clean up the area, and dispose of the old cabinets properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
