      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely install electrical wiring in your home? Today, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process to wire a 1,000 square foot space, from planning to final testing. \n\nFirst, plan your layout. Review local electrical codes, sketch a wiring diagram, and mark where outlets, switches, and lights will go. Gather all your materials: NM-B wire, boxes, outlets, switches, wire nuts, tape, cover plates, and staples.\n\nNext, run your cables. Drill holes in studs and joists, then pull the NM-B wire through, routing it to every marked outlet, switch, and fixture. Secure the wire with staples, but don\u2019t pinch it.\n\nNow, install your boxes and devices. Mount electrical boxes at each location. Strip the wire ends, then connect outlets, switches, and fixtures. Use wire nuts and electrical tape for safe, tight connections. Double-check that everything matches your diagram and local codes.\n\nFinally, connect the new circuits to your breaker panel. Label each breaker, then test every outlet, switch, and light. Make sure everything works and meets code.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
