      transcript:
        "Want to install a ceiling fan but not sure how to wire it safely? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install ceiling fan wiring like a pro. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker and double-check with a voltage tester. Clear your workspace and gather your tools and materials: 14/2 NM-B wire, a fan-rated ceiling box, wire connectors, a single pole switch, switch box, cover plates, and drywall patch material.\n\nNext, remove the old light fixture and electrical box. Install a fan-rated box, making sure it\u2019s firmly attached to a joist or support brace. This is crucial for safety\u2014ceiling fans are heavy!\n\nNow, run new 14/2 wire from your wall switch to the ceiling box. Follow your local electrical codes. Connect the wires: black to black (hot), white to white (neutral), and ground to ground. If your fan has a light, connect the extra wire as needed.\n\nInstall the switch and cover plates. Restore power and test the fan and light. Patch any drywall holes and clean up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
