      transcript:
        "Want to give your home a stone or brick look without the heavy price tag? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install masonry veneer step by step, so you can get pro results on your next project.\n\nFirst, prep your wall. Clean it well, fix any damage, and make sure it\u2019s dry. Next, install a weather-resistant barrier to keep moisture out. Attach metal lath over the barrier for the mortar to grip.\n\nNow, mix your mortar as the bag says. Lay out your veneer stones or bricks on the ground to plan your pattern. This helps you avoid too many cuts and keeps things looking natural.\n\nTime to install! Spread mortar on the wall and the back of each piece. Press each stone or brick into place, using spacers for even joints. Check your work often with a level to keep everything straight.\n\nOnce the veneer is up, fill the joints with grout or mortar using a grout bag. Tool the joints for a clean finish and wipe off any extra mortar before it dries.\n\nLet the mortar cure as recommended. Do a final check for gaps or loose pieces and touch up as needed. That\u2019s it\u2014your new masonry veneer is ready to impress!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
