      transcript:
        "Want to install a vinyl window like a pro and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to replace an old window with a new vinyl unit, from removal to finishing touches. \n\nFirst, remove the old window. Take off the interior trim, unscrew any fasteners, and carefully pull out the old window. Check the opening for damage and clear out any debris.\n\nNext, prepare the opening. Make sure it\u2019s level and square. Fix any damaged framing. Apply flashing tape to the sill and sides to keep water out.\n\nNow, install your new vinyl window. Set it in the opening. Use shims to get it plumb and level. Fasten it securely. Fill any gaps with low-expansion spray foam for insulation. Open and close the window to make sure it works smoothly.\n\nFinally, seal and finish. Reinstall the interior trim. Caulk the exterior edges to keep out drafts and water. Clean the glass. Dispose of the old window and materials properly. Double-check your work for a tight, clean fit.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
