        "Did you know a simple device can protect your water from contamination? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a sprinkler backflow preventer, step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off your main water supply. Open a faucet to relieve pressure, then clear the area where you\u2019ll work. Safety first!\n\nNext, cut and clean the supply pipe. Dry-fit your 1-inch double check valve backflow preventer and brass fittings. Use PVC primer and cement to join the pipes. Make sure the preventer sits upright and follows your local code. Secure all connections tightly.\n\nNow, slowly turn the water back on. Check every joint for leaks. Test the backflow preventer to make sure it\u2019s working right. If your area needs an inspection, schedule it now.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve protected your home and water supply. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
