        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/door-stop-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever had a door slam into your wall? Let\u2019s fix that in under 15 minutes! Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a door stop, step by step, so you can protect your walls and keep your doors in check. \n\nFirst, gather your tools and materials: a door stop (wall or floor mount), mounting screws and anchors, a drill, screwdriver, pencil, and measuring tape. Make sure you have everything ready before you start.\n\nNext, decide where you want the door stop. Open the door gently and see where it would hit the wall or floor. Mark that spot with a pencil. If you\u2019re mounting into drywall or concrete, use a drill to make a small pilot hole. This helps the screw go in straight and keeps the wall from cracking.\n\nNow, line up the door stop with your mark. Use the screws and anchors to secure it in place. Tighten it with your screwdriver until it\u2019s snug. Give the door a gentle push to make sure the stop works and nothing moves.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve just protected your wall and made your door safer. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
