      transcript:
        "Want to give your walls a fresh, modern look in just a weekend? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install shiplap like a pro. \n\nFirst, measure your wall and mark the studs. Remove any outlet covers and baseboards so you have a clean surface to work with. \n\nNext, cut your shiplap boards to fit. Sand the edges smooth, then paint or stain them. Let them dry completely before moving on.\n\nNow, start at the bottom of your wall. Use a level to keep your boards straight. Attach each board with a nail gun, making sure to hit the studs. Stagger the seams for a natural look, and keep the spacing even as you go up the wall.\n\nOnce all the boards are up, fill any nail holes with wood filler. Touch up the paint, then reinstall your trim and outlet covers. Clean up, and step back to admire your new shiplap wall!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
