        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/sod-laying-service/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want a lush green lawn\u2014fast? Here\u2019s how to lay sod like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, clear the area. Remove all grass, weeds, and debris. Level and grade the soil so water drains away from your house. This takes about 3 to 4 hours for 1,000 square feet.\n\nNext, condition the soil. Loosen the top few inches and add topsoil if needed. Mix in starter fertilizer for healthy roots. Rake it smooth and water lightly. This step takes 2 to 3 hours.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to lay the sod. Start along a straight edge. Place each roll tightly, staggering the seams like bricks. Trim the edges for a perfect fit. Press seams together\u2014no gaps! This takes 4 to 5 hours.\n\nAfter laying, water the sod deeply. Use a lawn roller to press the sod into the soil. This helps roots grow fast. Check for any uneven spots. Allow 1 to 2 hours for this step.\n\nFinally, clean up and give your new lawn some love. Remove extra materials and debris. Water daily for the first week. Avoid heavy use until the sod is rooted.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
