        "Ever wondered how to replace an undermount sink without calling a pro? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to swap out your old undermount sink for a new one. \n\nFirst, turn off the water supply under your sink. Disconnect the drain and water lines. Carefully remove any mounting clips or brackets, then gently detach the old sink from the countertop. Take your time\u2014undermount sinks are often glued in place.\n\nNext, scrape off any old silicone or adhesive from the underside of the countertop. Clean the area well. Check for any damage. Now, dry-fit your new sink to make sure it lines up with the cutout.\n\nApply a bead of silicone sealant around the edge of the sink opening. Position the new sink underneath the countertop. Secure it with new mounting clips or brackets. Wipe away any extra sealant. Let the silicone set for at least an hour.\n\nFinally, reconnect the drain assembly and water supply lines. Turn the water back on and check for leaks. Tighten connections if needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
