        "Is your garage door sagging or flexing when it opens? Let\u2019s fix that with a quick strut installation! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to reinforce your garage door with struts for better strength and smoother operation. \n\nFirst, gather your tools: three 8-foot garage door struts, self-tapping screws, mounting brackets, a drill, and a socket set. Disconnect the garage door opener and make sure the door is fully closed for safety. \n\nNext, lift the first strut and position it along the top section of the door. Align it so it sits straight and covers the full width. Use self-tapping screws or bolts to secure the strut to the door, spacing the screws evenly. Repeat this for the other struts if your door needs more support. \n\nOnce all struts are attached, reconnect the opener. Manually open and close the door to check for smooth movement. Tighten any loose fasteners and clean up your work area. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
