      transcript:
        "Thinking about upgrading your circuit breaker panel? Here\u2019s how to do it safely and efficiently, step by step. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn exactly what\u2019s involved in replacing an old breaker panel with a new 200 amp panel, including the materials, timeline, and key safety tips.\n\nFirst, always start by shutting off the main power supply. Double-check that every circuit is de-energized, and set up safety barriers around your work area. Safety comes first.\n\nNext, label every existing circuit in your old panel. Carefully disconnect all wiring, then remove the old panel from the wall. Make sure you follow your local electrical codes during this step.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install the new panel. Mount it securely, transfer and connect each circuit, and install new breakers as needed. Use the right copper grounding wire and electrical wire\u2014Romex 12/2 and 10/2 are common choices. Secure all wiring and double-check your connections.\n\nOnce everything\u2019s in place, schedule an inspection with your local authorities. Make any adjustments they require. When you pass inspection, restore power and test your circuits.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
