      transcript:
        "Tired of foggy windows and hidden moisture ruining your view? In this video, you'll learn how to remove window moisture and keep it from coming back. \n\nFirst, check your windows for condensation or water between the panes. Move any furniture or curtains out of the way so you have clear access and good airflow.\n\nNext, grab a dry, absorbent cloth and wipe down the glass, frames, and sills. For stubborn moisture, use a fan or dehumidifier in the room to help dry things out faster.\n\nNow, let's stop the problem from coming back. Inspect the window seals for any gaps or cracks. If you find any, apply butyl sealant or replace the glazing bead as needed. You can also add weatherstripping for extra protection.\n\nFinally, improve ventilation by opening windows when you can, or use exhaust fans to keep humidity low.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
