      transcript:
        "Ever notice small bumps or circles on your walls or ceiling? That\u2019s a nail pop, and fixing it is easier than you think. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair nail pops step by step, so your walls look smooth and new again.\n\nFirst, find all the nail pops in your room. Look for raised spots or tiny cracks. Move furniture out of the way and cover your floors to keep dust off your stuff.\n\nNext, grab some drywall screws. For each nail pop, drive a screw about an inch above and below the pop to secure the drywall to the framing. Remove any loose nails you find. Then, spread joint compound over the area. If the crack is big, press in some drywall tape for extra strength.\n\nLet the compound dry. Once it\u2019s dry, sand the area smooth with sandpaper. Wipe away dust, then brush on primer. When that dries, touch up with paint to match your wall.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your wall is as good as new. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
