      transcript:
        "Want to upgrade your bathroom in just a few hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace an old toilet step by step, so you can do it right the first time. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply to your toilet. Flush to empty the tank, then disconnect the water line. Remove the old toilet by loosening the bolts at the base and lifting it out. \n\nNext, clean the area around the drain flange. Check for any damage to the flange or floor. If it\u2019s all good, you\u2019re ready for the new toilet. \n\nPlace a new wax ring on the flange. Carefully set the new toilet in place, lining up the holes with the bolts. Press down to seal the wax ring, then tighten the bolts evenly. Don\u2019t overtighten\u2014just enough to keep it steady. \n\nReconnect the water supply line and turn the water back on. Check for leaks around the base and at the supply line. Finally, run a bead of caulk around the base for a clean finish. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
