      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to replace a garbage disposal flange without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a new garbage disposal flange step by step. \n\nFirst, unplug your garbage disposal and disconnect it from the sink. Loosen the mounting hardware and carefully remove the old flange. Clean the sink opening well\u2014any old putty or debris can cause leaks.\n\nNext, grab your new flange and roll out a rope of plumber\u2019s putty. Press the putty around the underside of the flange. Insert the flange into the sink opening and press down firmly. From underneath, use the mounting hardware kit to secure the flange tightly. Make sure it\u2019s snug, but don\u2019t overtighten.\n\nNow, reconnect your garbage disposal to the new flange. Tighten all the connections and restore power. Run water and check for leaks. If you see any drips, tighten the connections a bit more.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
