      transcript:
        "Want to save water and boost your faucet\u2019s performance in just 15 minutes? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to quickly replace a faucet aerator, step by step. \n\nFirst, remove the old aerator. Grip the end of your faucet and twist the aerator off by hand. If it\u2019s stuck, use pliers, but be gentle. Once it\u2019s off, clean any dirt or debris from the faucet threads.\n\nNext, grab your new aerator. If your kit includes plumber\u2019s tape, wrap a little around the faucet threads for a better seal. Screw the new aerator on by hand. If needed, use pliers to tighten, but don\u2019t overtighten\u2014just snug is enough.\n\nNow, turn on the faucet and check for leaks. Make sure the water flows smoothly. If you see drips, tighten the aerator a bit more or adjust the tape.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve just installed a new faucet aerator and improved your water flow. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
