      transcript:
        "Want to make your old brick look brand new in just a few hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to pressure wash brick safely and effectively. \n\nFirst, clear the area. Move furniture, plants, and anything else out of the way. Cover nearby surfaces with plastic sheeting and seal electrical outlets with painter\u2019s tape to protect them from water.\n\nNext, pre-treat any stained or dirty spots. Spray a brick-safe cleaning solution and let it sit for about 15 minutes. This helps loosen up dirt and mildew.\n\nNow, set up your pressure washer. Use a wide-angle nozzle and keep the pressure under 1,500 PSI to avoid damaging the brick. Hold the wand about a foot away and spray in smooth, even strokes. Work from the top down, and don\u2019t rush\u2014this usually takes 2 to 3 hours for 1,000 square feet.\n\nAfter washing, rinse the brick with clean water. Check for any missed spots or damage. If needed, repeat the cleaning on stubborn areas.\n\nFinally, remove all coverings, put furniture back, and throw away any waste. Let the brick dry completely before using the area again.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
