      transcript:
        "Want to make your porch last for years, rain or shine? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to waterproof your porch like a pro. \n\nFirst, sweep and wash the porch to get rid of dirt, debris, and mildew. Let it dry completely\u2014this is key for a strong bond.\n\nNext, check for cracks or damaged spots. Fill them with an exterior-grade patching compound and smooth it out. Let repairs cure as recommended for your climate.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time for the waterproofing membrane. Use a roller or brush to apply a liquid waterproofing membrane. Cover every inch, paying extra attention to seams and edges. For extra protection, add a second coat if your area gets a lot of rain.\n\nDon\u2019t forget the details: use polyester reinforcing fabric for weak spots, sealant for edges and joints, and a backer rod for wide gaps. Mix in a non-slip additive to keep the surface safe when wet.\n\nLet the membrane cure fully. Then, inspect for any missed spots or thin areas. Touch up as needed. Now your porch is ready for anything!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
