      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a damaged ceiling texture so it looks brand new? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair ceiling texture like a pro. \n\nFirst, clear the area and cover your floors and furniture. Use a putty knife or scraper to remove any loose or damaged texture from the ceiling. This prep work takes about an hour but makes a big difference.\n\nNext, patch the damaged spots with joint compound. Feather the edges so it blends in, let it dry, then sand it smooth. Once dry, apply a coat of primer to the repaired areas. This helps the new texture stick and look even.\n\nNow, it's time to apply the texture. Mix your texture spray or hopper mix to match the existing ceiling finish. Use a sprayer or brush to blend the new texture into the old. Let it dry completely.\n\nFinally, paint the repaired section to match the rest of your ceiling. Remove all coverings and clean up your tools and space.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
