      transcript:
        "Want to safely extend a gas line and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn the exact steps and materials needed to run a new gas line, from planning to inspection. \n\nFirst, plan your route and check local codes. Get permits from your city or county before starting. Next, shut off the main gas supply and ventilate the area. Clear your workspace for safety.\n\nFor materials, you'll need black iron gas pipe, fittings, thread sealant or Teflon tape, a shutoff valve, pipe hangers, a flexible gas connector, and leak detection solution. Measure and cut your pipe to fit the planned route. Use fittings and sealant to connect each section. Secure the pipe with hangers every few feet.\n\nInstall a shutoff valve at the start of the new line. Attach the flexible connector at the end if needed. Once installed, pressurize the line and use leak detection solution to check every joint. If you find bubbles, tighten the connection and retest.\n\nFinally, schedule an inspection with your local building department. Only turn the gas back on after you pass inspection.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
