      transcript:
        "Want to know how to install a water main the right way? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to install a new water main, from planning to final inspection. \n\nFirst, assess your site. Mark all utility lines and get the permits you need. Plan your trench route based on local codes and your property layout.\n\nNext, start trenching. Dig to the required depth, usually below the frost line. Lay down pipe bedding gravel for support. Place your 1-inch PVC water main pipe in the trench. Use the right pipe fittings\u2014elbows, tees, and couplings\u2014at each turn or connection.\n\nInstall a brass curb stop valve where you need to control water flow. Run tracer wire along the pipe for easy future locating. If needed, add pipe insulation to protect against freezing. Seal all joints with pipe tape or sealant.\n\nConnect the new pipe to the municipal supply and your building inlet. Test for leaks before backfilling. Fill the trench in layers, compacting as you go.\n\nFinally, schedule an inspection with your local authorities. Restore the surface and clean up the site.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
