        "Ever wondered how to mount a garbage disposal without calling a pro? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to safely mount a new garbage disposal under your sink. \n\nFirst, unplug the old disposal or turn off the power at the breaker. Remove the drain trap and disconnect the mounting hardware under your sink. Make sure the area is clear and dry before you start.\n\nNext, grab your mounting bracket kit, plumber\u2019s putty, and mounting screws. Apply a ring of plumber\u2019s putty around the sink drain opening. Press the new flange into place, then attach the mounting ring and hardware from below. Tighten everything so you get a watertight seal\u2014no leaks!\n\nNow, lift the garbage disposal up and twist it onto the mounting ring until it locks. Reconnect the drain pipes and make sure all connections are snug. Restore power, then run water and test for leaks. Turn on the disposal to check that it works smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
