      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/roof-ice-dam-removal/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ice dams can destroy your roof and cause leaks fast\u2014here\u2019s how to stop them before they do. In this video, you\u2019ll learn step-by-step how to safely remove ice dams from your roof and gutters. \n\nFirst, get your safety gear ready. Set up your ladder on solid ground and mark off the work area to keep everyone safe. Next, inspect your roof edges and gutters. Look for thick ice buildup and any signs of water getting inside.\n\nNow, start removing the ice. Use a roof rake to pull snow off the roof, working from the edge up. Don\u2019t chip at the ice\u2014spread calcium chloride pellets in a sock or pantyhose and lay it across the dam. This melts the ice without hurting your shingles. For thick ice, you may need to rent a steam machine.\n\nAfter the ice is gone, clear out your gutters and downspouts. Remove any debris or leftover ice so water can flow freely. Finally, check for any roof damage and clean up your materials, following local disposal rules.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
