        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/point-of-entry-water-filter-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want cleaner water for your whole house? Here\u2019s how to install a point of entry water filter system, step by step. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to set up a filter that treats all the water coming into your home. We\u2019ll cover the tools, materials, and the exact process you need.\n\nFirst, shut off your main water supply. Open a few faucets to relieve pressure. Pick a spot near your main water line that\u2019s easy to reach for future filter changes.\n\nNext, measure and cut about 10 feet of your main pipe. Deburr the ends so they\u2019re smooth. Install shut-off valves on both sides of where the filter will go. Attach mounting brackets to the wall to hold the filter securely.\n\nNow, mount the filter housing. Use Teflon tape and sealant on all threaded connections. Connect the inlet and outlet pipes to the filter, making sure all fittings are tight to prevent leaks.\n\nTurn the water back on. Flush the filter as the manufacturer recommends. Check every connection for leaks and make sure water flows well throughout your home.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
