      transcript:
        "Want to build a concrete wall that lasts for decades? In this video, I\u2019ll show you every step to install a strong, code-compliant concrete wall. \n\nFirst, clear your site and mark out the wall lines. Make sure the ground is level and compacted\u2014this is key for a stable foundation. Set up your formwork using sturdy lumber, following your local building codes.\n\nNext, dig and pour the footing. Place No. 4 rebar in the trench for reinforcement. Double-check that everything is straight and secure before the concrete sets.\n\nNow, assemble the wall forms and position your rebar inside. Pour ready-mix concrete in sections, and use a concrete vibrator to get rid of air pockets. This gives you a smooth, solid wall.\n\nAfter pouring, keep the concrete moist so it cures strong. Wait at least 24 hours, then carefully remove the forms. Inspect the wall for cracks or defects, and fix anything that doesn\u2019t meet code.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
