      transcript:
        "Want to install a new hollow core door and make it look pro? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to replace an old door with a new hollow core slab, step by step. \n\nFirst, take off the old door. Unscrew the hinges, remove the knob and strike plate, and check the frame for any damage. Clean up the opening so you have a smooth surface to work with.\n\nNext, measure the door opening. Mark your new hollow core door for any trimming\u2014remember, always measure twice and cut once. Use a circular saw or hand saw to trim the door to fit. Test fit it in the frame to make sure it swings freely and has even gaps on all sides.\n\nNow, attach your new hinges to the door. Line them up with the old hinge spots on the frame, or mark new ones if needed. Screw the hinges in place. Install the door knob and strike plate, following the manufacturer\u2019s instructions. Hang the door on the frame, check for smooth operation, and make any final tweaks.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve got a fresh, perfectly fitted hollow core door. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
