      transcript:
        "Want to stop mold before it starts? Here\u2019s how to install mold-resistant drywall the right way.\n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process to protect your walls from moisture and mold.\n\nFirst, clear your work area, cover the floors, and make sure there\u2019s good airflow. Bring in all your materials\u2014mold-resistant drywall, screws, joint compound, tape, and corner beads.\n\nNext, check the wall framing for any damage or signs of moisture. Fix any issues and install a vapor barrier or sealant to keep future mold out.\n\nNow, measure and cut your drywall panels. Hang them on the walls and ceilings, making sure the seams are tight and everything lines up. Use drywall screws to secure each sheet.\n\nAfter hanging, apply drywall tape over the seams. Cover with mold-resistant joint compound, let it dry, then sand it smooth for a seamless finish.\n\nFinally, inspect your work for any flaws. Touch up as needed, clean up all debris, and leave the space spotless.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
