      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/kitchen-demolition/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to demo a kitchen safely and efficiently? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to demolish a kitchen, protect your home, and get ready for a remodel. \n\nFirst, shut off the water, gas, and electricity to your kitchen. Remove all appliances and clear out the cabinets. Set up plastic sheeting and floor protection to keep dust and debris from spreading. \n\nNext, take down cabinets, countertops, sinks, and plumbing fixtures. Carefully disconnect and cap all utility lines to meet local codes. \n\nNow, remove any remaining appliances, vent hoods, and backsplashes. Pry up the flooring\u2014whether it's tile, vinyl, or hardwood\u2014being careful not to damage the subfloor. \n\nThen, take down drywall, soffits, and any non-load-bearing walls. Remove insulation and dispose of everything according to your local waste rules. \n\nFinally, haul away all debris using contractor trash bags and a dumpster. Sweep, vacuum, and check for any leftover nails or hazards. Your kitchen is now ready for renovation! \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
