        "Ever wondered how to build a strong, beautiful masonry arch that stands the test of time? Today, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process to construct a masonry arch, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, clear your work area and set up scaffolding if needed. Mark out your arch dimensions on the support wall. Gather all your materials: face bricks, mortar mix, rebar, centering form materials, and waterproofing membrane.\n\nNext, build your centering form. Use sturdy lumber and plywood to create a wooden arch that matches your design. Secure it tightly\u2014this form will support your bricks as you build.\n\nNow, mix your mortar. Start laying bricks or stones over the centering form, working from both sides toward the middle. Keep your joints even and use rebar for extra strength if needed. The keystone goes at the very top\u2014this locks the arch in place. Check your alignment as you go.\n\nLet the mortar cure for the recommended time. Then, carefully remove the centering form. Inspect your arch for stability and clean up the site.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
