      transcript:
        "Did you know a dirty exhaust vent can hurt your air quality and even cause fires? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to clean your exhaust vent like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the power to your exhaust fan. Gather your supplies: a vent cleaning brush kit, vacuum bags or filters, disinfectant cleaner, protective gloves, and drop cloths. Set up your work area and put on gloves and a dust mask for safety.\n\nNext, remove the vent cover and the fan assembly. Use your vacuum and brush to clear dust and debris from the fan blades, motor, and vent housing. Take your time\u2014this step usually takes about 30 to 40 minutes.\n\nNow, clean the vent duct itself. Use a flexible brush or a vacuum attachment to reach inside and remove built-up lint and dust. Once everything is clean, reinstall the fan and vent cover. Turn the power back on and test the fan to make sure it\u2019s working right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
