        "Want to stop your gutters from sagging or leaking? Here\u2019s how to install gutter hangers the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process to secure your gutters and keep water flowing where it should. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: gutter hangers, screws or fasteners, a tube of sealant, a sturdy ladder, a drill, and your safety gear. Before you start, inspect your gutters for any damage or sagging. Fix any issues now to avoid problems later.\n\nNext, measure and mark where each hanger will go. Space them according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions\u2014usually every 2 to 3 feet, but check for your local weather needs. Mark the spots along the gutter.\n\nNow, install the hangers. Secure each one to the fascia board with the right screws. Make sure the gutter slopes slightly toward the downspout for good drainage. Take your time\u2014proper slope is key.\n\nOnce all hangers are in, check the alignment. Tighten all fasteners and make sure hangers are evenly spaced. Adjust as needed for strong, even support.\n\nFinally, clean up your work area. Remove any debris and tools. Do a final inspection to make sure everything is stable and secure.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
