        "Want gutters that last a lifetime and boost curb appeal? Let\u2019s walk through how to install copper gutters, step by step. \n\nFirst, set up your ladders and inspect the fascia. Measure your roofline to figure out exactly how much gutter and how many downspouts you\u2019ll need. Remove any old gutters before you start.\n\nNext, cut your copper gutters and downspouts to the right lengths. Attach end caps, outlets, and corners. Pre-fit everything to make sure it lines up perfectly.\n\nNow, install your hangers or brackets along the fascia. Secure the copper gutters, making sure they slope slightly toward the downspouts for good drainage. Seal all joints and corners to prevent leaks.\n\nAttach the downspouts to the outlets, then fasten them to the wall. Make sure water will flow away from your foundation. Double-check the alignment and secure all straps.\n\nFinally, test the water flow. Look for leaks and make any fixes. Clean up all debris and dispose of old materials properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
