      transcript:
        "Thinking about moving your electrical panel? Here\u2019s what you need to know before you start. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process to safely relocate an electrical panel, including what materials you\u2019ll need and how long it takes.\n\nFirst, plan your new panel location. Make sure it meets local code and get any permits you need. Before you touch anything, shut off the main power supply for safety.\n\nNext, label every circuit in your current panel. Carefully disconnect all the wires, then remove the old panel from the wall.\n\nNow, mount your new panel in the chosen spot. Use the right mounting hardware. Reroute your copper wires through conduit, using the correct fittings and connectors. Secure everything tightly. Install new circuit breakers and connect each circuit, following your local electrical codes. Don\u2019t forget to install a grounding rod and wire for safety.\n\nOnce everything\u2019s in place, schedule an inspection with your local authorities. Make any changes they ask for. When you get approval, restore the power and test your circuits.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
