      transcript:
        "Is your central heating system leaving you in the cold? In this video, you'll learn how to repair a central heating system step by step, from diagnosis to final testing. \n\nFirst, assess the system. Inspect the thermostat, look for error codes, and check for any obvious faults. Next, test each component\u2014boiler, radiators, pumps, and valves. Use diagnostic tools to find out which part isn\u2019t working right.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time for repairs. Replace faulty parts like the thermostat, blower motor, ignition control module, or air filter. Fix any leaks and check all wiring and connectors. Make sure every repair meets local safety standards.\n\nAfter repairs, refill the system with water. Bleed the radiators to remove trapped air and restore the right pressure.\n\nFinally, run a full heating cycle. Make sure everything works smoothly. Give the system a final check and share maintenance tips with the homeowner.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
