      transcript:
        "Did you know dirty air ducts can spread dust and germs all over your home? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to sanitize your air ducts step by step, so you can breathe easier. \n\nFirst, gather your supplies: EPA-registered disinfectant, a fogger or sprayer, protective gear, and plastic sheeting with tape. You\u2019ll also need brushes and a vacuum for cleaning.\n\nStart by turning off your HVAC system. Cover all vents with plastic sheeting and tape to keep dust contained. Inspect the ductwork for debris or mold, and find any access points you\u2019ll need for cleaning.\n\nNext, use specialized brushes and a vacuum to loosen and remove dust and dirt from every accessible duct and vent. Take your time\u2014this usually takes about two hours for a 2,000 square foot home.\n\nNow, put on your gloves, mask, and goggles. Use your fogger or sprayer to apply the EPA-approved disinfectant inside the ducts. Let it sit for the recommended dwell time to kill germs and mold. Finally, reattach the vent covers and turn your HVAC system back on.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
