        "Want to know how to install a hydronic heating system that keeps your home warm and efficient? In this video, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process to get it done right, from planning to final inspection.\n\nFirst, plan your system. Figure out your heating needs, pick the right boiler, pumps, and tubing, and design your layout. Make sure you have all permits and materials ready.\n\nNext, install the piping and radiators or underfloor PEX tubing. Secure every connection and follow your local building codes.\n\nNow, set up the boiler. Place it in a safe spot, connect it to your piping, and add the circulator pumps, zone valves, expansion tank, and air separator.\n\nFill the system with water. Purge all the air from the lines, then pressure test to check for leaks.\n\nFinally, start up the system. Make sure heat is distributed evenly, adjust your thermostats, and do a final inspection to meet code.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
