      transcript:
        "Is your roman shade stuck or sagging? Let\u2019s fix it fast and make it look new again! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a roman shade step by step, including what materials you need and how to do the job right.\n\nFirst, take down the roman shade from its brackets. Lay it flat on a table and check for broken lift cords, cracked plastic rings, or any fabric damage. Look closely\u2014these are the most common problems.\n\nNext, replace any damaged lift cords. Thread the new cord through the rings, following the original path. Swap out any broken plastic rings and tighten any loose stitching. If the cord lock mechanism is worn out, install a new one. Make sure all parts are secure so the shade will move smoothly.\n\nNow, put the shade back up using the mounting brackets. Test the raising and lowering action. Adjust the cords or rings if the shade isn\u2019t hanging straight or moving easily.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
