      transcript:
        "Want to control your home's temperature from anywhere? Let\u2019s install a WiFi thermostat in just a few steps. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to safely remove your old thermostat, wire in a new smart model, and get it online fast.\n\nFirst, turn off power to your HVAC system at the breaker. Safety first! Remove the old thermostat cover and base. As you disconnect each wire, label it by its terminal letter\u2014this makes wiring the new unit much easier.\n\nNext, mount the new WiFi thermostat base to the wall using the included hardware. Connect each labeled wire to the matching terminal on the new base. If you need extra wire, use 18/5 low voltage wire and wire connectors. Once everything\u2019s secure, snap on the thermostat face and restore power at the breaker.\n\nNow, follow the on-screen setup to connect your thermostat to WiFi. Test both heating and cooling to make sure everything works. Finally, check that you can control the thermostat from your phone or tablet.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
