      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely and efficiently demolish a patio? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to tear out an old patio and get your space ready for something new. \n\nFirst, clear the area. Remove all furniture, plants, and debris. Set up safety barriers and gather your tools\u2014think sledgehammers, pry bars, and wheelbarrows. Don\u2019t forget safety gear: heavy-duty contractor bags, dust masks, and work gloves.\n\nNext, start surface removal. Break up concrete, pavers, or decking with the right equipment. Load all debris into contractor bags or directly into your dumpster. For a 400 square foot patio, plan for about 24 hours of labor.\n\nAfter the surface is gone, move to the subbase. Dig out any gravel, sand, or soil underneath. Watch for hidden utilities\u2014always follow your local guidelines if you find any wires or pipes.\n\nFinally, handle debris disposal and cleanup. Haul everything to an approved facility. Sweep and level the area so it\u2019s clean and ready for your next project.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
