      transcript:
        "Want to install wall cabinets like a pro and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to install wall cabinets safely and securely. \n\nFirst, measure your wall space and mark where each cabinet will go. Use a stud finder to locate the studs\u2014these are what will hold the weight. Mark the stud locations clearly. Gather your cabinets, mounting screws, shims, and a touch-up kit before you start.\n\nNext, install a temporary ledger or support rail along your marked line. This will hold the cabinets up while you work. Drill pilot holes into the studs. With a helper, lift the first cabinet onto the support rail. Secure it to the wall using cabinet mounting screws, making sure it's level and plumb. Add the next cabinet, clamp them together, and screw them to each other for a tight fit. Use shims to adjust for any uneven spots.\n\nOnce all cabinets are up, attach the doors and hardware. Adjust the hinges so everything lines up. Remove the support rail, caulk any gaps, and clean up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
