        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/electrical-panel-grounding/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Did you know a single missed step in grounding your electrical panel can put your whole home at risk? Today, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to ground an electrical panel safely and up to code. \n\nFirst, always start by turning off the main breaker. Use a voltage tester to double-check that the power is off. Open the panel and look for an existing ground bar or space to add one.\n\nNext, head outside and drive two ground rods into the earth, at least six feet apart. Use a sledgehammer or a ground rod driver. Attach a grounding electrode clamp to each rod. Now, run a 6-gauge bare copper wire from the first rod to the second, then into your panel. Secure the wire with clamps and fasteners, keeping it tight and neat.\n\nInside the panel, connect the ground wire to the ground bar kit. Make sure all connections are tight. Once everything\u2019s secure, turn the power back on. Use a multimeter to test for proper grounding\u2014look for a low resistance reading.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
