      transcript:
        "Ever wonder how to tackle a demolition cleanup without missing a step? In this video, you'll learn exactly how to clean up after demolition, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, gather your supplies: heavy-duty contractor trash bags, a 10-yard dumpster, dust masks, work gloves, brooms, shovels, and a wheelbarrow. Safety first\u2014put on your gloves and dust mask before you start.\n\nStep one: Debris Collection. Spend 4 to 6 hours gathering and sorting all debris. Separate materials for disposal or recycling, following your local rules.\n\nStep two: Bulk Removal. For the next 6 to 8 hours, load debris into your dumpster or containers. Keep walkways clear and handle heavy items safely.\n\nStep three: Detailed Cleaning. Take 3 to 4 hours to sweep, vacuum, and wipe down every surface. Remove dust, nails, and small debris so the area is ready for the next phase.\n\nStep four: Final Inspection & Disposal. Spend 2 to 3 hours checking for leftover debris. Make sure everything is disposed of properly and you meet local waste rules.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
