        "Is your window lock stuck or broken? Let\u2019s fix it fast and make your home secure again! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair or replace a window lock step by step. \n\nFirst, check the lock for damage or if it\u2019s just out of alignment. Clear the area around your window so you can work safely. Grab your new window lock, mounting screws, a screwdriver, and a little lubricant.\n\nNext, unscrew and remove the old lock. Clean the spot where the lock sits. If the lock is just loose, realign it and screw it back in. If it\u2019s broken, swap in the new lock and secure it tightly with the screws.\n\nNow, test the lock. Open and close the window a few times. If it sticks, add a bit of lubricant. Make any final tweaks, then clean up your tools and the area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
