      transcript:
        "Cracked kitchen tiles making your floor look old? Let\u2019s fix them step by step, so your kitchen looks brand new again. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to remove damaged tiles, prep the surface, install new tiles, and finish with perfect grout lines.\n\nFirst, use a chisel and hammer to gently pry up the broken or loose tiles. Be careful not to damage the surrounding tiles. Clean away all the old adhesive and debris so the area is smooth.\n\nNext, make sure the subfloor is dry and even. Spread thinset mortar with a notched trowel, covering the area where the new tiles will go.\n\nNow, press your replacement tiles firmly into the mortar. Line them up with the existing tiles. Use tile spacers to keep the grout lines even.\n\nOnce the mortar sets, mix your grout and press it into the gaps between the tiles. Wipe away any extra grout with a damp sponge. Let the grout cure as the package says.\n\nFinally, check that all tiles are level and the grout lines look good. Clean up the area and throw away any debris.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
