        "Want to give your room a polished look in just one weekend? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install cove molding like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, measure every wall where you want molding. Write down the lengths, add them up, and mark where the wall studs are. Plan your layout, and note where you\u2019ll have inside and outside corners.\n\nNext, cut your cove molding to size. Use a miter saw for clean, angled cuts at the corners. Sand the edges smooth, then dry-fit each piece along the wall to make sure everything lines up.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install. Attach the molding to the wall and ceiling using finishing nails or a strong adhesive. Make sure the joints at the corners are tight, and secure every piece along the way.\n\nFor the finishing touches, fill any nail holes or seams with wood filler or caulk. Once it\u2019s dry, sand it smooth. Then, paint or stain the molding to match your room. Don\u2019t forget to clean up your workspace!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
