        "Calculate materials & costs to trim repair at https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/trim-repair/national-average\n\nIn this video, we show you exactly how to repair and replace damaged wood trim in your home or on the job. You'll learn how to assess the damage, remove old trim, cut and install new pieces, and finish with sanding and painting for a seamless look. We break down the tools and materials you'll need, including primed wood trim, wood filler, caulk, finishing nails, and paint or stain. Whether you're a homeowner tackling a DIY project or a contractor looking for a refresher, this guide will help you get professional results. Like, follow, and let us know your questions in the comments!",
