      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to repair damaged trim and make it look brand new? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to replace and finish wood trim like a pro. \n\nFirst, inspect your trim for damage and measure how much you need to replace. Gather your materials: primed wood trim, wood filler, caulk, finishing nails, and paint or stain. Remove any old nails or fasteners and clean the area.\n\nNext, carefully pry off the damaged trim. Use a miter saw to cut new pieces to the right length and angle. Take your time\u2014accurate cuts make a big difference.\n\nNow, install the new trim. Secure it with finishing nails or adhesive. Make sure all joints are tight. Fill nail holes and seams with wood filler or caulk for a smooth finish.\n\nOnce the filler dries, sand everything smooth. Wipe down the trim, then apply primer if needed. Finish with paint or stain to match your existing trim.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
