      transcript:
        "Want to upgrade your utility sink with a new faucet in under two hours? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a utility sink faucet, even if you\u2019ve never done it before. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply valves under your sink. Open the old faucet to relieve any pressure, then disconnect the supply lines. Remove the old faucet and clean the sink surface so your new faucet seals tight.\n\nNext, place your new utility sink faucet into the mounting holes. Secure it from underneath with the hardware that came in the box. Now, attach your hot and cold supply lines to the faucet. Use plumber\u2019s putty or Teflon tape on the threads to prevent leaks. Tighten all connections, but don\u2019t overdo it\u2014hand-tight plus a quarter turn is usually enough.\n\nTurn the water supply back on. Run both hot and cold water, and check every connection for leaks. If you spot a drip, tighten the fitting a bit more. Make sure the faucet works smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
