      transcript:
        "Tired of bugs sneaking through your torn porch screen? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to repair your porch screen step by step, so you can enjoy your space again. \n\nFirst, remove the old screen and any damaged spline from the frame. Take your time and clean the frame well\u2014this helps the new screen fit tight. \n\nNext, measure each porch opening. Cut your new screen mesh a little bigger than the opening, so you have some overlap. \n\nNow, lay the new screen over the frame. Use a spline roller to press the screen into the groove, then roll in the new spline to hold it tight. Trim off any extra screen for a clean look. \n\nCheck all the edges. If you find any loose spots, press them in again. Make sure the screen is smooth and tight. \n\nFinally, throw away the old screen and clean up your tools and work area. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
