      transcript:
        "Want to make your closet more organized in under an hour? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a closet rod the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, measure the height and width where you want your closet rod. Use a level and pencil to mark the bracket spots on both walls. This keeps your rod straight and clothes off the floor.\n\nNext, grab your drill. At each mark, drill pilot holes. If you\u2019re not hitting a stud, use wall anchors for extra strength. Then, screw the rod brackets firmly into place.\n\nNow, set the rod into the brackets. Double-check with your level to make sure it\u2019s straight. Press down gently to test stability. If it wobbles, tighten the screws or adjust the brackets until it\u2019s solid.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve got a sturdy closet rod ready for action.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
