      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to install a peephole in your door without hiring a pro? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to add a door viewer for better security in just a few easy steps. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: a peephole viewer, the right size drill bit, and a little silicone sealant. You\u2019ll also need a drill and a tape measure.\n\nStep one: Mark the peephole location. Measure and mark the spot on your door at a height that works for everyone in your home\u2014usually about 5 feet from the floor.\n\nStep two: Drill the hole. Use your drill with the correct bit size for your peephole. Drill slowly and keep the drill level to avoid splintering the door. Go halfway from one side, then finish from the other for a clean hole.\n\nStep three: Install the peephole. Insert the lens from the outside, then screw the inside piece on from the inside. Tighten it by hand. Add a tiny bead of silicone sealant around the edge if you want extra weather protection.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve just made your door safer in under 30 minutes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
