        "Is your well pump acting up and you\u2019re not sure if it\u2019s the pressure switch? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely replace a well pressure switch step by step. \n\nFirst, always start by shutting off power to the well pump at your breaker panel. Safety first\u2014never work on live wires. Next, remove the cover from the pressure switch. You\u2019ll see the wiring and contacts inside.\n\nTake a close look at the switch. If you spot corrosion, debris, or any damage, it\u2019s time for a replacement. Carefully disconnect the wires, noting where each one goes. Unscrew and remove the old switch. Wrap Teflon tape on the threads of your new switch, then install it in place. Make sure it\u2019s tight, but don\u2019t overdo it.\n\nReconnect the wires using new wire connectors if needed, and secure everything with electrical tape. Put the cover back on. Now, restore power at the breaker. Test your system by running water and watching the pressure cycles. If everything runs smoothly, you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
