        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/emergency-faucet-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your faucet leaking and you need a fast fix? In this video, you'll learn how to repair a faucet in an emergency, step by step. First, shut off the water supply under your sink. Turn the valves clockwise until the water stops. Next, check where the leak is coming from\u2014usually the handle or spout. Grab a screwdriver and remove the faucet handle. Take out the old cartridge or washer. Replace it with a new one that matches your faucet. Don\u2019t forget to use plumber\u2019s tape on any threads to prevent leaks. Swap out any worn O-rings or seals too. Put the handle back on and tighten the screw. Now, turn the water back on slowly. Watch for leaks as the water flows. If everything looks good, wipe down the area and you\u2019re done! If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
