      transcript:
        "Want to upgrade your windows without a full remodel? Watch how to install a retrofit window step by step. \n\nFirst, clear the area around your window and remove any blinds or curtains. Take careful measurements of the window opening\u2014accuracy here is key for a good fit.\n\nNext, remove the old window. Gently pry off the interior stops and sashes. Take out any hardware, but be careful not to damage the frame or wall.\n\nNow, dry-fit your new retrofit vinyl window to make sure it fits. Apply a bead of exterior caulk around the opening. Set the window in place, then secure it with screws or fasteners as the manufacturer recommends. Use shims to keep the window level and plumb.\n\nAfter the window is set, fill any gaps with spray foam insulation. Reinstall or add interior trim if needed. Finish by applying exterior caulk around the window and cleaning up the area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
