      transcript:
        "Want to build a concrete ramp that lasts? Here\u2019s how to do it right, step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to prep, reinforce, pour, and finish a concrete ramp for any home or business. \n\nFirst, mark out your ramp area and clear away any debris. Excavate the ground to the right depth, then set your 2x4 form boards. Make sure your slope meets local accessibility codes\u2014this is key for safety.\n\nNext, add a layer of compacted gravel for a solid base. Lay out No. 4 rebar or mesh for strength, tying it together and checking that your forms are straight and secure.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to pour. Mix your ready-mix concrete and fill the forms evenly. Use a screed to level the surface, then shape the edges and apply a broom finish for traction. Don\u2019t forget to add expansion joint material where needed.\n\nLet the concrete cure for at least 16 hours. Once it\u2019s set, carefully remove the forms. Inspect your ramp for smoothness and make sure it meets code.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
