        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/roof-sealant-application/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to make your roof last longer and stop leaks for good? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to apply roof sealant like a pro. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: two 5-gallon buckets of elastomeric or acrylic roof sealant, two gallons of roof cleaner, one roll of polyester fabric, masking tape and plastic sheeting, and two sets of disposable brushes or rollers.\n\nStart by cleaning the roof. Remove all dirt, debris, and any old sealant. Use a roof cleaner and let it dry. Inspect for damage or moisture\u2014fix any issues before moving on.\n\nNext, prep your sealant. Stir it well. Use masking tape and plastic sheeting to protect areas you don\u2019t want sealed. Apply a thick, even coat to all seams, joints, and around roof penetrations with a brush or roller. For extra strength, embed polyester fabric into the wet sealant over seams or cracks.\n\nLet the sealant cure as the manufacturer recommends\u2014usually a few hours. Once dry, check for missed spots and touch up as needed. This ensures a watertight finish.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
