      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a stuck old window and make it work like new? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace a window sash cord step by step. \n\nFirst, remove the window stops and carefully lift out the sash. Use a utility knife to cut and remove the old sash cord. Be gentle so you don\u2019t damage the wood frame or sash.\n\nNext, thread your new sash cord\u2014cotton or nylon\u2014through the pulley at the top of the window. Tie it securely to the sash weight inside the frame. Make sure the weight moves up and down smoothly. Repeat this for both sides of the window.\n\nNow, reattach the sash to the new cords. Set the sash back into the frame and reinstall the window stops. Test the window to make sure it opens and closes easily. If it sticks, adjust the cord tension or check the pulleys.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve just restored your window\u2019s smooth operation. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
