      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/well-cap-replacement/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Did you know a faulty well cap can let in pests and contaminate your water? In this video, you'll learn how to safely replace a well cap step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off power to your well pump. This keeps you safe while you work. Clear away any dirt or debris around the wellhead so you have a clean area to work in.\n\nNext, remove the old well cap. Use a wrench or screwdriver to loosen and take out the bolts or screws. Carefully lift off the old cap, making sure nothing falls into the well opening.\n\nNow, it's time to install the new well cap. Place it over the well casing and line it up with the bolt holes. Use new stainless steel bolts and hardware to secure it tightly. Apply sanitary sealant around the edge for a watertight fit. This keeps out bugs, dirt, and rain.\n\nFinally, disinfect the area with a safe solution to keep your water clean. Turn the power back on and check that everything is sealed and secure.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
