      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to safely replace a gas line? In this video, you'll learn the exact steps and materials needed for a professional gas line replacement. \n\nFirst, always shut off the main gas supply and ventilate the area. Use a gas detector to make sure there\u2019s no gas present. Clear out any obstacles so you have safe access to the work area.\n\nNext, disconnect all appliances from the old gas line. Carefully unthread and remove the old pipe. Check all fittings and valves for any signs of damage or corrosion.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install the new gas line. Measure and cut your CSST gas pipe to fit. Use the right pipe fittings\u2014like elbows and tees\u2014and secure every connection with thread sealant or Teflon tape. Mount the pipe with straps or hangers, and if it\u2019s underground, add tracer wire for safety.\n\nOnce installed, pressurize the new line and check for leaks using a gas leak detector or soapy water. Schedule an inspection if your local code requires it.\n\nFinally, reconnect your appliances, turn the gas back on, and test everything to make sure it works. Clean up the area and dispose of old materials properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
