      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a damaged stone wall and make it look brand new? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair a stone wall like a pro. \n\nFirst, inspect your wall and mark any loose or broken stones. Clear away debris and gather your tools: replacement stones, mortar mix, sealer, backer rod, and joint tools. \n\nNext, carefully remove the damaged stones and scrape out the old mortar. Clean both the stones and the wall surface\u2014this helps the new mortar stick. \n\nNow, mix up fresh mortar. Reset the cleaned stones in place, making sure they line up with the rest of the wall. Fill the joints with mortar and smooth them out with your joint tools. Wipe away any extra mortar before it dries. \n\nLet the mortar set for a few hours. Mist the area with water to help it cure strong. Once dry, brush the joints for a neat finish. Clean up your site and check your work. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
