        "Want to make your stucco look brand new without damaging it? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely pressure wash stucco step by step. \n\nFirst, get your materials: rent a pressure washer, grab a stucco-safe detergent, plastic sheeting, painter\u2019s tape, and a couple of drop cloths. \n\nStart with surface prep. Move outdoor furniture, cover plants, and protect outlets with plastic and tape. Check your stucco for cracks\u2014patch any damage before you start washing.\n\nNext, mix your mild detergent with water. Use a garden sprayer or a low-pressure nozzle to apply it evenly. Let it soak for 10 to 15 minutes so it can break down dirt and stains.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to pressure wash. Use a wide-angle tip and keep the nozzle at least 18 inches from the wall. Work from top to bottom in smooth, even strokes. Don\u2019t rush\u2014take your time to avoid damaging the stucco.\n\nFinally, rinse everything with clean water. Check for any missed spots or damage and touch up as needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
