      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/stone-step-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Cracked or loose stone steps can be a real safety hazard\u2014let\u2019s fix them the right way! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair stone steps so they look great and last for years. \n\nFirst, inspect your steps. Find any loose or broken stones and gather your tools: replacement stone treads, mortar mix, bonding agent, backer rod, and sealer. \n\nStart by carefully removing the damaged stones. Use a hammer and chisel to lift them out. Clean away old mortar and debris so the new stones will bond well. \n\nNext, mix fresh mortar according to the bag instructions. Brush bonding agent onto the clean surface. Place a backer rod in any deep joints. Set the new stone treads in place, pressing them firmly into the mortar. Check that each step is level and lines up with the others. \n\nSmooth the joints with a trowel and wipe away extra mortar. Let the steps cure for at least 24 hours. Finally, apply a sealer to protect your repair from weather. Block off the area while it dries. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
