      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely wire a dishwasher and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to install the electrical for a dishwasher, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, always shut off power at the breaker and double-check with a voltage tester. Clear out the area where you'll be working so you have safe, easy access. \n\nNext, run 12/2 NM electrical cable from your junction box to the dishwasher space. You'll need about 15 feet. Install an electrical box and use a Romex connector to secure the cable. Strip the wires, then connect them according to your dishwasher's manual\u2014usually black to black, white to white, and ground to ground. Use wire connectors and wrap with electrical tape for safety. Make sure all connections are tight and meet your local code.\n\nNow, restore power at the breaker. Test the dishwasher to make sure it powers up and runs correctly. Check that the unit is grounded and secure it in place. Finally, install all covers and make sure everything looks neat and safe.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
