      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to bring an old stone foundation back to life? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair a stone foundation the right way. \n\nFirst, clear the area around your foundation and remove any debris. Inspect the stones and mortar closely\u2014look for cracks, loose stones, or crumbling joints. This tells you exactly what needs fixing.\n\nNext, use a chisel and hammer to carefully remove all damaged mortar and any unstable stones. Be gentle so you don\u2019t disturb the good parts of the wall.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to rebuild. Reset any loose stones, making sure each one is level and fits tightly. Mix up Type N masonry mortar and fill all the gaps, matching the original look. Use a bonding agent for extra strength, and if you have big gaps, add a backer rod first.\n\nOnce the stones are set, let the mortar cure. Mist it with water if it\u2019s drying too fast. Clean off any extra mortar from the stones. Finally, check your work\u2014everything should be solid and stable.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
