      transcript:
        "Is your brick column crumbling or leaning? Let\u2019s fix it step by step! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a damaged brick column the right way, from prep to finish. \n\nFirst, inspect the column for loose or broken bricks. Use a hammer and chisel to carefully remove damaged bricks and scrape out old mortar. Clean the area so new bricks will bond well.\n\nNext, pick replacement bricks that match your column. Mix Type N mortar until it\u2019s thick but workable. Lay a bed of mortar, set each new brick in place, and use a level to keep everything straight. Add brick ties if needed for extra strength.\n\nOnce the bricks are in, fill all the joints with fresh mortar. Use a jointer tool to smooth the lines and wipe away any extra mortar with a damp sponge. Let the mortar cure for at least a day.\n\nFinally, check the column for stability. Clean up the area and throw away debris properly. For extra protection, brush on a water repellent sealer.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
