      transcript:
        "Want to install a utility sink and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to install a utility sink, from prep to final testing. \n\nFirst, shut off your water supply. Clear the area where the sink will go and gather your tools and materials: the sink, faucet, P-trap and drain kit, water supply lines, shutoff valves, mounting hardware, PVC pipe and fittings, and plumber\u2019s putty or sealant.\n\nNext, install the shutoff valves on your water lines. Attach the water supply lines to the faucet. Mount the sink securely to the wall or floor, following your local building codes. Connect the drain kit and P-trap to the sink, then attach the drain to your existing plumbing using PVC pipe and fittings. Use plumber\u2019s putty or sealant on all threaded connections to prevent leaks.\n\nFinally, turn the water back on. Check every connection for leaks. Run water through the sink and make sure it drains properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
