      transcript:
        "Worried about frozen pipes bursting and flooding your home? In this video, you'll learn how to safely find, thaw, and repair frozen pipes step by step. \n\nFirst, find the frozen pipe. Look for spots with no water flow, bulges, or frost. Turn off your main water supply before you start. Check for any cracks or leaks\u2014if you see water, you\u2019ll need to repair that section.\n\nNext, thaw the pipe. Use a hair dryer, heat lamp, or towels soaked in hot water. Start near the faucet and work your way back. Never use an open flame\u2014it\u2019s a fire risk and can damage the pipe.\n\nIf you find a burst section, cut out the damaged pipe. Replace it with new copper pipe and fittings. Use solder and flux to join the pieces. Secure the pipe with hangers or straps. Once done, slowly turn the water back on and check for leaks.\n\nFinally, insulate the repaired pipe with a sleeve to help prevent future freezing. Patch up any drywall you had to open.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
