        "Want to keep water out and protect your home\u2019s walls? Here\u2019s how to install siding flashing the right way. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to prep, measure, install, and seal siding flashing for a watertight finish.\n\nFirst, clear the work area. Remove any old siding or debris. Check the sheathing for damage and make sure the wall is clean and dry.\n\nNext, measure where you need flashing\u2014around windows, doors, and corners. Mark your cut lines and use tin snips to cut the flashing to size. Always wear gloves for safety.\n\nNow, install the flashing. Start at the bottom and work your way up. Overlap each piece by at least two inches to direct water away from the wall. Secure the flashing with nails or screws, spacing them about every 12 inches.\n\nAfter all flashing is in place, seal every seam and fastener with exterior-grade caulk. This keeps water from sneaking in. Finally, inspect your work to make sure everything is tight and up to code.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
