      transcript:
        "Want to make your stone surfaces look brand new without damaging them? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to pressure wash stone safely and effectively, step by step.\n\nFirst, gather your materials: rent a pressure washer, get stone-safe detergent, plastic sheeting, painter\u2019s tape, scrub brushes, and safety gear like gloves and goggles.\n\nStart with site preparation. Clear away debris, move any outdoor furniture, and cover nearby plants or electrical outlets with plastic sheeting and painter\u2019s tape. This protects everything around your work area.\n\nNext, pre-treat the stone. Apply the stone-safe detergent evenly and let it soak for about 10 minutes. While it soaks, set up your pressure washer. Use a wide-angle nozzle\u2014never a narrow one\u2014to avoid damaging the stone.\n\nNow, pressure wash the stone. Hold the nozzle about a foot away and use steady, overlapping strokes. Focus extra time on stained or mossy spots, but don\u2019t linger too long in one place.\n\nFinally, rinse everything with clean water. Check for any missed spots and repeat if needed. Remove the coverings and inspect your work.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
