      transcript:
        "Leaky gutter joints can cause big headaches, but fixing them is easier than you think. In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair gutter joints and stop leaks for good. \n\nFirst, inspect your gutter joints for leaks or damage. Remove any leaves or debris, and clean the area well so the sealant will stick. Next, if you can, carefully take apart the gutter sections at the joint. Dry all surfaces and scrape away any old sealant or rust. This gives you a clean surface for a strong repair.\n\nNow, apply gutter sealant evenly to both sides of the joint. Reattach the gutter sections, then secure them with screws or a joint connector. Wipe away any extra sealant for a neat finish. If you see any holes, use an aluminum patch and sealant to cover them.\n\nFinally, run water through the gutter to check for leaks. Touch up any spots as needed, and make sure everything is watertight. Clean up your work area, and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
