      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix damaged stone veneer and make it look brand new? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair stone veneer like a pro. \n\nFirst, remove any loose or broken stones and clean the exposed surface. Make sure there's no dust, debris, or old mortar left\u2014this helps the new stones stick well.\n\nNext, mix your mortar as the bag says. Apply mortar to both the wall and the back of each replacement stone. Press each stone firmly into place, keeping the spacing even as you go.\n\nOnce the stones are set, fill the joints with grout using a grout bag or trowel. Tool the joints for a smooth, uniform look, and wipe off any extra mortar from the stone faces.\n\nLet everything cure for at least 16 hours without touching it. Finally, inspect your work for stability and clean up the area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
