        "Want to upgrade your kitchen or bathroom in under an hour? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a faucet sprayer step by step, even if you\u2019ve never done it before. \n\nFirst, gather your tools and materials: a faucet sprayer kit, a flexible supply line, Teflon tape, an adjustable wrench, and a towel. Make sure you can reach the water shut-off valves under your sink.\n\nNext, turn off the water supply. Open the faucet to relieve any pressure, and lay down a towel to catch drips.\n\nNow, unscrew the aerator or cap from your faucet. Attach the sprayer diverter where the aerator was, then connect the sprayer hose. Wrap Teflon tape around the threads to prevent leaks. Tighten everything with your wrench, but don\u2019t overdo it.\n\nTurn the water supply back on. Test the sprayer and check all connections for leaks. If you see drips, tighten the fittings a bit more.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
