      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely fix a blown fuse in your home? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair a fuse box, so you can get your power back on fast and safely. \n\nFirst, always start with safety. Turn off the main power supply to your house. Use a voltage tester to double-check there\u2019s no electricity in the box. Put on insulated gloves to protect yourself.\n\nNext, open the fuse box. Look for any fuses that look burnt or broken. Check for any signs of melted wires or damaged parts. Find the fuse that\u2019s causing the problem.\n\nNow, use a fuse puller to carefully remove the bad fuse. Grab a new fuse with the same rating and snap it into place. If you see any loose wires, use wire connectors and electrical tape to fix them. Make sure everything is tight and safe.\n\nPut the panel cover back on and screw it in. Turn the main power back on. Test your circuits to make sure everything works.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
