      transcript:
        "Want to install a drywall ceiling like a pro? Watch this before you start! \n\nIn this video, you'll learn every step to install a drywall ceiling, from prep to a smooth, paint-ready finish.\n\nFirst, clear your work area and gather all your materials: 1/2 inch drywall sheets, drywall screws, joint compound, paper tape, and corner bead. Mark your ceiling joist locations with a pencil. Make sure all electrical and plumbing work is done before you begin.\n\nNext, lift each drywall sheet to the ceiling and fasten it to the joists using drywall screws. Stagger the seams for extra strength. For a 500 square foot ceiling, you'll need about 13 sheets and 2 pounds of screws.\n\nOnce the panels are up, apply paper tape over all seams. Cover the seams and screw holes with the first coat of joint compound. Let it dry.\n\nApply more coats of joint compound, letting each dry before sanding. Sand everything smooth so your ceiling is ready for paint.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
