      transcript:
        "Is your cellular shade stuck or sagging? Let\u2019s fix it fast and save you money! \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a cellular shade step by step, from removal to reinstallation.\n\nFirst, carefully remove the shade from the window. Gently lift it out of the mounting brackets\u2014don\u2019t force it, or you might damage the headrail or fabric.\n\nNext, inspect all the parts. Look for broken cords, worn-out cord locks, cracked end caps, or missing handles. Replace any damaged parts with new ones. You\u2019ll need a replacement cord, cord lock mechanism, mounting brackets, end caps, and a plastic pull handle. Use a screwdriver and scissors for most repairs. Thread the new cord through the shade, secure it to the cord lock, and snap on any new end caps or handles.\n\nOnce everything\u2019s fixed, reinstall the shade. Slide it back into the brackets and make sure it clicks into place. Test the shade by raising and lowering it a few times. Adjust the cord tension if needed so it moves smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
