        "Did you know a dirty bathroom vent can hurt your air quality and even your health? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to clean your bathroom vent like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the power to your bathroom vent at the breaker. Safety first! Lay down a drop cloth to keep your bathroom clean. \n\nNext, remove the vent cover. Wash it with soap and water to get rid of dust and grime. While it dries, use a vent cleaning brush or a vacuum with a hose attachment to clean the fan and the inside of the vent. Don\u2019t forget to wear protective gloves and, if needed, replace the vent filter for better airflow. Spray disinfectant cleaner to kill germs and freshen things up.\n\nOnce everything is clean and dry, put the vent cover back on. Turn the power back on and test the fan. You should notice stronger airflow and a fresher bathroom.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
