        "Did you know a loose garage door bracket can put your whole door at risk? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install garage door brackets the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, gather your tools and materials: two garage door brackets, eight lag screws, two metal reinforcement plates, a drill, a level, and your safety gear. Always check the manufacturer\u2019s instructions before you start.\n\nNext, measure and mark where the brackets will go on your garage door. Use a tape measure for accuracy, and mark the spots with a pencil. Drill pilot holes at each mark\u2014this helps the screws go in straight and keeps the door from splitting.\n\nNow, attach the brackets using your lag screws and drill. Place a metal reinforcement plate behind each bracket for extra strength. Use your level to make sure everything is straight, then tighten all the screws securely.\n\nFinally, test your work. Open and close the garage door by hand. Make sure the brackets are solid and nothing rubs or catches. Double-check all connections and adjust if needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
