      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely hook up a new gas line in your home or project? In this video, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process to install a gas line, from planning to leak testing. \n\nFirst, start with a site assessment. Inspect your current gas setup, pick the best spot for your appliance, and plan the pipe route. Always follow your local codes for safety.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time for pipe installation. Measure and cut your black iron gas pipe. Thread the ends, then use elbows, tees, and couplings to assemble the line. Apply pipe thread sealant to every joint. Install a shutoff valve where you can easily reach it. Use pipe hangers or straps to secure everything along the route.\n\nNow, connect your appliance with a flexible gas connector. Before turning on the gas, brush leak test solution on every joint. Slowly open the shutoff valve and watch for bubbles\u2014bubbles mean leaks, so tighten and retest as needed. Once you\u2019re sure there are no leaks, you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
