      transcript:
        "Is your lawn looking dry, or are your sprinklers wasting water? Let\u2019s fix that with a simple sprinkler system maintenance routine. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to inspect, clean, repair, and test your sprinkler system like a pro.\n\nFirst, turn off the water supply. Walk around and check every sprinkler head, valve, and pipe for damage or leaks. Clear away any dirt or grass so you can see all the parts.\n\nNext, clean each sprinkler head. Remove any clogs and adjust the spray pattern so water covers your lawn evenly. If you spot broken nozzles or worn seals, swap them out for new ones.\n\nNow, turn the water back on. Run each zone one at a time. Watch for leaks, low pressure, or heads spraying the wrong way. Replace any faulty parts\u2014like heads, pipes, or connectors\u2014using Teflon tape and pipe sealant for tight, leak-free joints.\n\nFinally, check your irrigation controller. Update the schedule for the season and test both manual and automatic cycles to make sure everything works right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
