      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to replace a toilet water line without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a new toilet water supply line step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off the main water supply. Flush the toilet to empty the tank, and put down towels or a bucket to catch any leftover water. \n\nNext, use an adjustable wrench to disconnect the old supply line from both the shut-off valve and the toilet tank. Check the fittings for any signs of rust or damage.\n\nNow, grab your new flexible supply line. Attach one end to the shut-off valve and the other to the toilet tank. Hand-tighten both ends, then use your wrench to make sure they\u2019re snug, but don\u2019t over-tighten.\n\nTurn the water supply back on. Watch all the connections closely for leaks. If you see any drips, tighten the fittings a bit more. Wipe up any spills and make sure the area is clean and dry.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
