      transcript:
        "Want to double your closet space in just a few hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a closet organizer step by step, so you get a perfect fit and a pro finish. \n\nFirst, clear out your closet. Take out all clothes and shelves. Measure the width, height, and depth to make sure your new organizer will fit. \n\nNext, mark your wall. Find the studs with a stud finder and mark them. Use a level to draw layout lines for where each shelf and rod will go. This keeps everything straight and strong. \n\nNow, assemble your organizer kit. Follow the instructions to put together shelves, rods, and brackets. Mount the main supports to the wall, screwing into studs when you can. Use wall anchors for extra support if needed. Attach all shelves and rods, making sure everything is tight and level. Add finishing trim for a clean look. \n\nFinally, adjust the shelves and rods to your liking. Put your clothes and items back in. Enjoy your new, organized closet! \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
