      transcript:
        "Tired of cleaning out clogged gutters every season? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install gutter screens and keep your gutters flowing free. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to measure, cut, and install aluminum gutter screens step by step.\n\nFirst, gather your materials: aluminum gutter screens, mounting clips or fasteners, sheet metal screws, a ladder, gloves, and basic tools. Start by inspecting and cleaning your gutters. Remove all leaves and debris so water can flow properly.\n\nNext, measure the length of your gutters. Cut the screens to fit using tin snips or a utility knife. Double-check your measurements to make sure each piece will cover the gutter completely.\n\nNow, install the screens. Snap or screw them onto the gutters, following the manufacturer\u2019s instructions. Make sure each section overlaps slightly and is firmly attached. Use mounting clips or screws as needed for a secure fit.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Look for any gaps or loose spots. Clean up your work area and dispose of any leftover debris or packaging.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
