      transcript:
        "Thinking about replacing your central heating system? Here\u2019s exactly how it\u2019s done, step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off all power and fuel to your old system. Drain it completely, then check your pipes and radiators to make sure they\u2019ll work with the new unit. \n\nNext, remove the old furnace, radiators, and any connected pipes. Be sure to follow local rules for safe disposal. \n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install your new furnace\u2014gas or electric. Connect all the pipework, upgrade or replace radiators if needed, and hook up the thermostat and controls. Use quality ductwork, sheet metal plenums, and flexible connectors for a tight, safe fit. Don\u2019t forget the gas or electrical hookup, condensate drain, return air grilles, and supply registers. \n\nOnce installed, refill the system, bleed out any air, and check for leaks. Test the furnace and balance the radiators so every room heats evenly. \n\nFinally, do a full inspection. Show the owner how to use the controls, hand over all paperwork, and explain basic maintenance. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
