        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/replace-galvanized-pipes/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Did you know old galvanized pipes can ruin your water and your wallet? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to replace galvanized pipes with modern PEX piping. \n\nFirst, shut off your main water supply and drain the pipes. Clear out the area so you can reach all the plumbing. Gather your tools and materials\u2014PEX pipe, fittings, crimp rings, insulation, shutoff valves, support clamps, and transition fittings.\n\nNext, use pipe wrenches and saws to cut and remove the old galvanized pipes. Be careful not to damage walls or floors as you work.\n\nNow, measure and cut your new PEX pipe. Use elbows, tees, and couplings to fit everything together. Secure each joint with crimp rings and make sure to use transition fittings where PEX meets old pipe. Add pipe insulation and support clamps to keep everything in place.\n\nOnce installed, turn the water back on. Check every joint for leaks and flush the system to clear out debris. Make sure water flows well everywhere.\n\nFinally, clean up the area, dispose of old pipes, and do a final inspection to meet local codes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
