      transcript:
        "Want to save big on energy bills with a hybrid water heater? In this video, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to install a 50-gallon hybrid water heater, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the power and water supply. Drain your old water heater, disconnect the plumbing and electrical, and carefully remove the old unit. \n\nNext, move your new hybrid water heater into place. Make sure there\u2019s enough space around it for airflow. Connect the flexible water connectors and dielectric unions to prevent corrosion. Install the PVC drain line for condensate, and hook up the electrical whip or disconnect kit, following your local codes. Don\u2019t forget to add an expansion tank if your system needs it, and insulate the pipes to save even more energy.\n\nNow, fill the tank and check for leaks. Restore power, set up the controls, and make sure the system runs smoothly. \n\nFinally, clean up the area, dispose of the old heater properly, and walk the homeowner through the basics of using their new hybrid water heater.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
