      transcript:
        "Want to make your doors and windows look sharp and finished? In this video, you'll learn how to install architrave molding like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, measure the frames around your doors or windows. Mark the lengths on your architrave molding, then use a mitre saw to cut each piece at the right angle for clean, tight joints.\n\nNext, check the wall surfaces. If they're not flat, sand them down. Dry fit your architrave pieces around the frame to make sure everything lines up perfectly.\n\nNow, apply adhesive to the back of each piece. Press them into place, then secure with finishing nails or pins. Double-check that your corners and joints are tight and neat.\n\nOnce the architrave is fixed, fill any nail holes or gaps with wood filler. Let it dry, then sand everything smooth. Wipe away dust so the surface is ready for primer and paint.\n\nThat's it! Your architrave is installed and ready to finish. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
