      transcript:
        "Want to build strong, long-lasting concrete stairs? Watch this before you start! In this video, you'll learn how to install a 5-step, 4-foot wide concrete stair from start to finish. \n\nFirst, clear your work area and mark out the stair dimensions. Excavate the ground as needed. Set up your form lumber, making sure each step is level and the slope is correct.\n\nNext, cut and lay out your rebar. Place it inside the forms for strength, and secure it well. Double-check all your measurements and reinforce the forms so they don\u2019t move when you pour concrete.\n\nNow, mix your ready-mix concrete to the right consistency. Pour it into the forms, filling each step evenly. Use a tool or tap the forms to remove air pockets.\n\nOnce poured, screed and trowel the surface for a smooth finish. Shape the stair edges and use a broom to add traction. Let the concrete cure undisturbed. After curing, apply a concrete sealer for protection.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
