      transcript:
        "Want to give your home a stunning stone look without the guesswork? In this video, you'll learn how to install a stone facade step by step, from prep to finishing touches. \n\nFirst, prep your wall. Clean it well, fix any damage, and cover it with a weather-resistant barrier. This keeps moisture out and helps the stone stick. \n\nNext, attach metal lath over the barrier. Secure it with masonry nails or screws. Then, spread a scratch coat of mortar over the lath. Let it cure\u2014this gives the stones something to grip. \n\nNow, it's time for the stone. Start at the bottom and work your way up. Use mortar to set each piece, cutting stones as needed for a tight fit. Keep your joints even for a pro look. \n\nOnce all stones are in place, fill the joints with grout. Tool the joints for a clean finish and wipe off any extra mortar. Finally, clean the stone surface and inspect your work. For extra protection, apply a masonry sealer. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
