        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/tile-wall-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to make your wall look brand new with tile? Here\u2019s how to install a tile wall step by step.\n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to prep, plan, and install a beautiful tile wall\u2014even if you\u2019re new to tiling.\n\nFirst, get your materials: ceramic wall tiles, thinset mortar, grout, backer board, spacers, edge trim, and waterproofing membrane. For a 100 square foot wall, you\u2019ll need about 100 square feet of tile, 2 bags of mortar, 1 bag of grout, 7 sheets of backer board, 1 bag of spacers, 3 pieces of edge trim, and 2 rolls of membrane.\n\nStart with surface preparation. Clean and dry the wall. Fix any holes or bumps. If needed, install backer board and waterproofing membrane for a solid, water-resistant base.\n\nNext, layout and planning. Measure your wall. Mark level lines and lay out your tiles on the floor first. This helps you avoid tiny slivers at the edges.\n\nNow, tile installation. Spread thinset mortar on the wall with a notched trowel. Press tiles into place, using spacers for even gaps. Cut tiles to fit corners and edges.\n\nAfter the tiles set, it\u2019s time for grouting and cleaning. Fill the joints with grout, wipe off the excess, and clean the tile faces.\n\nFinish up by sealing the grout lines, reinstalling any fixtures, and checking for touch-ups.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
