        "Want to stop water damage before it starts? Let\u2019s walk through how to install a complete gutter system, step by step. \n\nFirst, measure your roofline and plan where your gutters and downspouts will go. This ensures water drains away from your home, not into your foundation. Mark the gutter slope\u2014about a quarter inch drop for every 10 feet\u2014so water flows the right way.\n\nNext, cut your aluminum gutters and downspouts to size. Gather all your parts: hangers, end caps, elbows, outlets, screws, and sealant. Lay everything out before you start.\n\nNow, install the gutter hangers along the fascia, spacing them about every 2 feet. Attach the gutters, making sure they follow your marked slope. Seal the joints and end caps with caulk to prevent leaks.\n\nAttach the downspouts to the outlets, add elbows to direct water, and secure them to the wall. Make sure the water flows away from your foundation.\n\nFinally, test your system with water. Check for leaks and adjust as needed. Clean up your work area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
