      transcript:
        "Want to turn your noisy garage into a quiet retreat? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to soundproof your garage like a pro. \n\nFirst, clear out your garage. Remove everything and clean the walls, ceiling, and floor. Check for any cracks or gaps\u2014these let sound escape.\n\nNext, seal all gaps and cracks. Use acoustic caulk around doors, windows, and outlets. Don\u2019t forget weatherstripping for the garage door.\n\nNow, install your soundproofing materials. Add acoustic insulation batts inside the walls and ceiling. Attach resilient channels to the framing, then cover with 5/8\" Type X drywall. Seal all seams with acoustic sealant for the best results.\n\nUpgrade your garage door by adding insulation panels and a soundproof door sweep. For the floor, lay down thick rubber mats or carpets to block sound from traveling through.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Look for missed gaps and test the noise reduction. Make any needed adjustments.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
