      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/toilet-fill-valve-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wonder why your toilet keeps running or won't fill up right? Today, I'll show you how to replace a toilet fill valve step by step, so you can fix it fast and save money. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply to your toilet. Turn the valve behind the toilet clockwise until it stops. Flush the toilet to empty the tank, then use a towel or sponge to soak up any leftover water.\n\nNext, disconnect the water supply line from the bottom of the tank. Use a wrench if needed. Unscrew the locknut holding the old fill valve in place, then lift the old valve out.\n\nNow, grab your new fill valve. Follow the instructions in the box\u2014usually, you\u2019ll insert it into the hole in the tank, adjust the height so it sits just above the overflow tube, and tighten the locknut underneath. Wrap Teflon tape around the threads of the supply line, then reconnect it to the tank.\n\nTurn the water supply back on. Watch for leaks and adjust the fill level if needed. Make sure the toilet fills and stops at the right level.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
