        "Want sparkling clean windows without streaks or damage? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to pressure wash your windows safely and effectively, step by step. \n\nFirst, gather your supplies: a pressure washer, window cleaning solution, an extension wand, plastic sheeting, and safety gear. Move any outdoor furniture and cover nearby plants to protect them from spray.\n\nNext, inspect your windows for cracks or damaged seals. If you find any, fix them before washing. Spray the cleaning solution on the glass and frames to loosen dirt and grime.\n\nNow, set your pressure washer to a low setting. Start at the top of each window and spray evenly, keeping the nozzle at least a foot away to avoid damage. Use an extension wand for hard-to-reach spots.\n\nAfter washing, rinse the windows with clean water. Dry the glass with a squeegee or lint-free cloth to prevent streaks.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
