        "Did you know dirty air ducts can make your whole house feel dusty and lower your air quality? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to clean your entire duct system step by step, so your home feels fresher and your HVAC runs better. \n\nFirst, turn off your HVAC system. Cover all vents and registers, and move any furniture blocking duct openings. This makes sure you have clear access and keeps dust from spreading. \n\nNext, remove every vent cover and register. Clean them with a vacuum and brush\u2014don\u2019t skip this, or you\u2019ll just blow dust back into the ducts later. \n\nNow, it\u2019s time for the main event: duct cleaning. Use a specialized vacuum and agitation tools to loosen and suck out dust, debris, and any hidden contaminants from the entire duct system. Take your time\u2014this step can take a few hours. \n\nAfter that, inspect and clean the blower, coils, and any HVAC parts you can reach. Look for mold or damage while you\u2019re at it. \n\nFinally, put the vent covers back on, turn the HVAC back on, and test the airflow. Clean up your work area and make sure everything works right. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
