        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/electric-heater-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your electric heater not working and you\u2019re not sure what\u2019s wrong? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to safely diagnose and repair an electric heater step by step. \n\nFirst, always turn off the power at the breaker. Double-check with a voltage tester to make sure there\u2019s no electricity running to the heater. Safety first! \n\nNext, open up the heater and look for any obvious damage\u2014burn marks, loose wires, or broken parts. Use a screwdriver to remove the cover and get a clear view inside. \n\nNow, grab a multimeter. Test the heating element, thermostat, and wiring. If the heating element or thermostat is faulty, replace them with manufacturer-approved parts. For wiring issues, cut and replace damaged wires using 12-gauge wire and secure them with wire connectors. Tighten everything with mounting screws. \n\nOnce repairs are done, reassemble the heater. Restore power at the breaker and turn the heater on. Listen for odd noises and check for any strange smells. If everything runs smoothly, you\u2019re good to go! \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
