      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to install a dishwasher drain without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to connect a dishwasher drain hose step by step, so you can do it yourself and avoid leaks. \n\nFirst, turn off the power and water supply to your dishwasher. Clear out the space under your sink and gather your tools: a drain hose, hose clamps, an air gap if needed, a PVC drain tee or adapter, and plumber\u2019s putty or sealant.\n\nNext, attach the drain hose to the dishwasher\u2019s drain outlet. Secure it tightly with hose clamps. If your local code requires an air gap, install it on the sink or countertop, then connect the hose to the air gap. Otherwise, loop the hose up high under the counter to prevent dirty water from flowing back in.\n\nConnect the other end of the hose to the drain pipe or garbage disposal using a PVC adapter if needed. Make sure all connections are tight and sealed.\n\nNow, turn the power and water back on. Run a short wash cycle and check for leaks under the sink. If you see any drips, tighten the clamps or reseal as needed. Once everything\u2019s dry, clean up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
