      transcript:
        "Did you know a faulty outdoor outlet can be a hidden safety risk? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely replace an outdoor outlet and keep your home protected from the elements. \n\nFirst, shut off the power at your breaker panel. Double-check with a voltage tester to make sure the outlet is dead. Remove the old outlet cover and unscrew the outlet from the box.\n\nNext, connect the wires to your new weather-resistant GFCI outlet. Match the wires\u2014black to brass, white to silver, and green or bare to ground. Use wire connectors and electrical tape for a secure fit. Mount the outlet in an exterior-rated electrical box, then attach an in-use weatherproof cover. Make sure everything is tight and sealed to keep out moisture.\n\nFinally, turn the power back on. Test the outlet to make sure it works and that the GFCI trips properly. Double-check the cover is sealed to protect against rain and snow.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
