      transcript:
        "Is your porch column sagging or rotting? Here\u2019s how to replace it safely and make your porch look new again. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the exact steps and materials you need to swap out a porch column, whether you\u2019re a homeowner or a contractor. \n\nFirst, support the porch roof with temporary bracing\u2014never skip this step. Remove any trim around the old column, then carefully detach and take out the column. Next, inspect the porch base and header for damage. Repair any rot or cracks before moving on. Get your new column, base and cap set, fasteners, adhesive, shims, and paint ready. \n\nNow, set the new column in place. Use shims to make sure it\u2019s perfectly plumb. Secure it to the base and header with structural fasteners and adhesive. Once it\u2019s solid, remove the temporary supports. Finish up by reattaching the trim, caulking the joints, and touching up the paint. Clean up your work area, and you\u2019re done! \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
