      transcript:
        "Is your thermostat set to cool, but your home still feels warm? In this video, you'll learn how to troubleshoot and fix a thermostat that's not cooling. \n\nFirst, check your thermostat settings. Make sure it's set to cooling mode, the temperature is lower than the room, and the fan is set right for your space.\n\nNext, inspect the power. If your thermostat uses batteries, swap them out for fresh ones. Check the wiring behind the thermostat\u2014look for any loose or disconnected wires and tighten them if needed.\n\nNow, move to your HVAC system. Check the circuit breaker to make sure it hasn't tripped. Inspect the air filter\u2014replace it if it's dirty. Go outside and look at the outdoor unit. Clear away any leaves or debris, and make sure nothing is blocking the airflow.\n\nFinally, turn your system back on. Feel for cool air coming from the vents. Listen for any strange noises and watch to see if the system cycles on and off like it should.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
