      transcript:
        "Want a leak-free, pro-looking shower enclosure in just a few hours? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to install a shower enclosure, from prep to final inspection. \n\nFirst, clear out your bathroom and remove any old shower doors or curtains. Clean the shower base and walls\u2014dirt or soap scum can mess up your seal later.\n\nNext, assemble the shower enclosure frame. Follow the manufacturer's instructions closely. Mark your drill holes on the wall, then set the frame in place. Use a level and shims to make sure everything lines up perfectly.\n\nNow, drill pilot holes and secure the frame with the mounting hardware. Carefully install the glass panels or doors. Once everything is in place, run a bead of waterproof silicone caulk along all the edges. This keeps water where it belongs\u2014inside the shower.\n\nFinally, check that the doors open and close smoothly. Inspect all the seals for gaps. Wipe down the glass and hardware, and toss out any packaging according to your local rules.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
