      transcript:
        "Want flawless hexagon tile floors that last? Here\u2019s how to do it right, step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to prep, lay, and finish hexagon tiles like a pro.\n\nFirst, prep your surface. Clean and level the subfloor. Fix any damage and make sure it\u2019s dry and free of dust. This is key for a strong, even tile job.\n\nNext, plan your layout. Mark guidelines and dry-fit your hexagon tiles. This helps you avoid tiny cuts at the edges and keeps your pattern looking sharp.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install. Spread thinset mortar evenly. Set each tile in place, using spacers for perfect joints. Cut tiles as needed to fit along walls or corners.\n\nOnce the tiles are set, mix and apply grout. Press it into the joints, then wipe away the extra with a damp sponge. Clean the tile surfaces well.\n\nLet the grout cure fully. Then, apply a tile sealer to protect your work and make cleaning easier.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
