        "Want to make your garage look brand new with a fresh coat of paint? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to paint your garage interior like a pro. \n\nFirst, clear out everything from the garage. Sweep the floors and cover anything you don\u2019t want painted with drop cloths. Fix any holes or cracks in the walls using spackling compound and sandpaper. This gives you a smooth surface for painting.\n\nNext, use painter\u2019s tape to protect trim, outlets, and edges. If your walls are stained or dark, apply a coat of primer. This helps the paint stick and gives you even color.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to paint. Use rollers for big areas and brushes for corners and edges. Start with the ceiling, then move to the walls. Let the first coat dry, then add a second coat for the best coverage.\n\nWhen you\u2019re done, carefully remove the tape. Touch up any missed spots. Clean your brushes and rollers. Once the paint is dry, move your stuff back in.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
