      transcript:
        "Want to upgrade your bathroom lighting without hiring an electrician? Watch this! In this video, you'll learn how to safely remove an old bathroom light and install a new fixture step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker box. Double-check with a voltage tester to make sure the wires are dead. Remove the old fixture by unscrewing it and disconnecting the wires. \n\nNext, inspect the existing wiring. If needed, replace the electrical box and run new 14/2 NM wire. Attach the mounting bracket that comes with your new fixture. Connect the black wires together, then the white wires, and finally the ground wires, using wire connectors. Make sure all connections are tight and secure. \n\nNow, mount the new fixture to the wall or ceiling using the included hardware. Install the bulbs. Turn the power back on at the breaker and flip the switch to test your new light. If it works, you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
