      transcript:
        "Want to know how to install bathroom plumbing like a pro? In this video, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process to get your bathroom plumbing done right, from rough-in to final testing. \n\nFirst, mark where your toilet, sink, and shower will go. Measure pipe runs and cut openings in the floor and walls. Make sure your layout follows local building codes.\n\nNext, install your water supply and drain lines. Use copper or PEX for water, and PVC for drains. Run pipes to each fixture location, secure them, and connect everything with the right fittings. Double-check that you\u2019re using approved materials for your area.\n\nNow, hook up your fixtures. Connect the toilet, vanity sink, and shower to the supply and drain lines. Install shutoff valves for each. Once everything\u2019s connected, turn on the water and check for leaks. Test each fixture to make sure it works and meets code.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
