      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a broken underground pipe without making a mess? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to repair a damaged underground PVC pipe safely and efficiently.\n\nFirst, find the leak and mark the area. Carefully dig to expose the damaged pipe\u2014take your time to avoid hitting other utilities. Next, shut off the water supply. Cut out the broken section using a pipe cutter or saw. Clean the pipe ends so your new connections will seal tight. Gather your replacement PVC pipe, couplings, and primer and cement that meet your local plumbing codes.\n\nNow, fit the new pipe section in place. Use couplings and primer and cement to secure all joints. Make sure everything is watertight and lines up with code. Turn the water back on and check for leaks. If all looks good, backfill the trench with gravel and soil, compacting in layers to prevent future settling. Don\u2019t forget to add warning tape above the pipe before finishing the backfill.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
