        "Did you know the right cabling can save a tree from splitting in a storm? In this video, you'll learn how to safely install tree cabling to support weak branches and protect your property. \n\nFirst, assess the tree. Look for weak limbs or splits, and decide where cables should go. Plan your hardware and follow your local tree safety rules.\n\nNext, install the hardware. Drill holes at your marked spots. Insert eye bolts or lag hooks, then attach your steel cables using cable grips and thimbles. Make sure everything is tight and secure.\n\nNow, tension the cables. Tighten them enough to support the branches, but not so much that the tree can't move naturally. Adjust as needed and check that everything lines up right.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Trim any extra cable, cover sharp edges, and wrap the tree where needed to protect the bark. Clean up the area so it's safe for everyone.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
