      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/repointing-stone/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to make old stone walls look brand new again? Today, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to repoint stone like a pro. \n\nFirst, you\u2019ll prep the surface. Use a chisel or grinder to remove all loose or damaged mortar from the joints. Clean the stone faces well\u2014this helps the new mortar stick. \n\nNext, mix your mortar. Use Type N mortar mix, masonry sand, and a bonding agent. Try to match the original mortar\u2019s color and texture for the best look. \n\nNow, dampen the joints with water. Pack the fresh mortar into the gaps using a pointing trowel. Shape the joints to match the old ones as you go. Take your time\u2014this step is key for a seamless finish. \n\nFinally, let the mortar cure. Mist the area with water a few times a day to keep it from drying too fast. Wipe off any extra mortar from the stone faces and check that all joints look even and neat. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
