      transcript:
        "Ever stepped on a tile and felt it move under your feet? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to fix loose floor tiles like a pro. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to remove, reset, and re-grout a loose tile, step by step.\n\nFirst, carefully pry up the loose tile using a putty knife or chisel. Take your time\u2014work around the edges to avoid breaking the tile. Once it\u2019s up, scrape off any old adhesive or debris from both the tile and the floor underneath. A clean surface is key for a strong bond.\n\nNext, make sure the floor is dry and level. Apply fresh thinset mortar to the back of the tile or directly onto the floor. Use a notched trowel for even coverage.\n\nNow, press the tile firmly back into place. Use tile spacers if needed to keep it lined up with the others. Let the adhesive set as recommended\u2014usually about 24 hours.\n\nFinally, mix up your grout and fill the joints around the tile. Wipe away any excess with a damp sponge. Let the grout cure fully before walking on the tile.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
