      transcript:
        "Want to upgrade your home bar with a new sink? Watch this before you start! In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a bar sink like a pro.\n\nFirst, shut off the water supply and clear your workspace. Mark the sink cutout on your countertop. Gather your bar sink, faucet, drain assembly, supply lines, P-trap kit, shutoff valves, plumber\u2019s putty or silicone, and mounting hardware.\n\nNext, cut the countertop opening using your marked lines. Test-fit the sink to make sure it sits right. Adjust the opening if needed.\n\nNow, install the faucet and drain assembly onto the sink. Apply plumber\u2019s putty or silicone around the edges. Set the sink in place. Secure it with the mounting hardware.\n\nConnect the water supply lines and shutoff valves. Attach the P-trap and drain pipes. Make sure all fittings are tight and follow local plumbing codes.\n\nTurn the water back on. Check for leaks under the sink and around the faucet. Test the faucet and drain. Clean up your workspace and dispose of any debris.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
