      transcript:
        "Is your garage floor cracked, uneven, or just plain worn out? Today, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to replace a garage floor, step by step. \n\nFirst, clear out your garage. Remove everything, sweep up debris, and check the old floor for damage. Set up safety barriers and make sure the area is well-ventilated.\n\nNext, it\u2019s demolition time. Use a jackhammer or sledgehammer to break up the old concrete slab. Haul away all debris and dispose of it according to your local rules.\n\nNow, prep the subgrade. Level and compact the soil, then add a layer of gravel for drainage. Install forms around the edges to shape your new floor. Lay down a vapor barrier to block moisture, and roll out wire mesh for reinforcement. Don\u2019t forget to set your expansion joints and anchor bolts or dowels.\n\nTime to pour the new concrete. Mix 4000 psi concrete and pour it evenly. Use a screed to level, then smooth the surface with a float and trowel. Apply a curing compound to help the concrete set properly.\n\nFinally, let the concrete cure as recommended\u2014usually a few days. Remove the forms, inspect your work, and clean up the site. Once the floor is ready, move your things back in.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
