      transcript:
        "Did you know a whole house surge protector can save your electronics from costly damage in seconds? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install one safely and step-by-step. \n\nFirst, turn off the main breaker to cut all power. Double-check with a voltage tester to make sure the panel is safe to work on. Clear the area and gather your tools and materials: surge protector, 12-gauge wire, a new circuit breaker, wire connectors, and mounting hardware.\n\nNext, mount the surge protector close to your electrical panel. Follow the manufacturer\u2019s instructions for wiring. Usually, you\u2019ll connect the protector\u2019s wires to a dedicated breaker and the neutral and ground bars. Make sure all connections are tight and meet local electrical codes.\n\nOnce everything\u2019s wired, reinstall the panel cover. Turn the main breaker back on. Check the surge protector\u2019s indicator lights to confirm it\u2019s working. Clean up your workspace, and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
