        "Want to add light and safety to your basement? Here\u2019s how to install a basement egress window, step by step. \n\nFirst, clear the area inside and outside. Remove any old window or cut out the wall section. Check the opening for damage or weak spots\u2014fix these before moving on.\n\nNext, frame the opening to fit your new window. Use pressure-treated wood for durability. Apply a waterproofing membrane around the frame, and add gravel for drainage at the base. This keeps water out and meets code.\n\nNow, set the new window in place. Make sure it\u2019s level. Secure it with fasteners and anchors. Use spray foam insulation around the edges, then seal with flashing tape. Follow the manufacturer\u2019s instructions for your window type.\n\nFinish up by adding trim inside and out. Check for any air or water leaks. Clean up the area and dispose of debris properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
