      transcript:
        "Did you know mold spores can spread in minutes and cause serious health issues? In this video, you'll learn how to safely remove mold spores from your home or job site, step by step. \n\nFirst, assess the area. Inspect every corner for mold and moisture. Once you spot the problem, set up containment. Use plastic sheeting and tape to seal off the area. This keeps spores from spreading to the rest of your space.\n\nNext, gear up. Put on N95 respirators, gloves, and protective coveralls. Safety first! Make sure the area is well-ventilated, but don\u2019t let air blow spores into clean areas.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to remove the mold. Use a HEPA vacuum to clean all surfaces. Wipe everything down with a mold remediation cleaner. For anything too damaged, bag it up in heavy-duty trash bags and dispose of it safely, following local rules.\n\nAfter cleaning, dry the area completely. Use dehumidifiers and fans. Once dry, apply a mold inhibitor to stop mold from coming back.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
