      transcript:
        "Want to make your kitchen brighter and more modern in just one day? In this video, you'll learn how to install new recessed LED lighting in your kitchen, step by step. \n\nFirst, always start by turning off the power at your breaker box. Double-check that the electricity is off before touching any wires. Remove your old fixtures and make sure the wiring is safe. Gather your tools and materials: six LED recessed lights, 14/2 NM wire, a single-pole switch, switch box, wire connectors, electrical boxes, and a faceplate.\n\nNext, install the mounting brackets for each new fixture. Run your 14/2 NM wire from the power source to each light location and to the switch. Connect the wires following the manufacturer\u2019s instructions\u2014white to white, black to black, and ground to ground. Secure each fixture in its box and make sure all connections are tight.\n\nNow, install or upgrade your wall switch. If you want dimmers or smart controls, this is the time to add them. Mount the switch and faceplate, then test each control to make sure it works.\n\nFinally, turn the power back on. Test all your new lights and adjust their positions if needed. Clean up any debris and safely dispose of old fixtures.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
