      transcript:
        "Is your door sticking, sagging, or just not closing right? In this video, you'll learn how to realign a door so it works like new. \n\nFirst, inspect the door and hinges. Look for sagging, sticking, or gaps. Check if any hinge screws are loose or if the hinges look worn out.\n\nNext, grab a screwdriver and tighten all the hinge screws. If any screws are stripped, replace them with new ones. If the door is still off, you may need to adjust the hinge placement or add shims behind the hinges to get the door lined up.\n\nNow, open and close the door a few times. Watch for smooth movement. If it still rubs or doesn't latch, make small adjustments to the hinges or the strike plate until it fits just right.\n\nFinally, make sure the door latches and swings freely. Clean up your tools and any mess.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
