      transcript:
        "Did you know radon can sneak into your home without a trace? In this video, you'll learn how to test your radon mitigation system step by step, so you can keep your home safe. \n\nFirst, prepare the testing area. Close all windows and outside doors in your home for at least 12 hours before you start. Let your heating or cooling system run as usual\u2014this helps get an accurate reading.\n\nNext, set up your radon test device. Place it in the lowest area of your home that people use, like a basement or first floor. Make sure it's at least 20 inches above the floor, away from drafts, outside walls, and anything damp.\n\nNow, start the test. Follow the instructions for your test kit or digital monitor. Let it run for the recommended time\u2014usually a few days for a kit, or as directed for a monitor. When it's done, seal and label the device. If you're using a kit, send it to a certified lab. If you have a digital monitor, check the results right away. Always follow your local safety rules.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
