      transcript:
        "Got a leaky pipe and want to fix it fast\u2014without calling a plumber? In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to patch a damaged pipe step by step, using simple tools and materials. \n\nFirst, find the damaged section of pipe. Shut off the water supply and clear the area so you can work safely. This usually takes about 20 minutes.\n\nNext, dry the pipe completely. Use sandpaper or an abrasive cloth to clean and roughen the area around the leak. Remove any rust or debris\u2014this helps the patch stick well. Wipe the area with a cleaning solvent and let it dry.\n\nNow, put on protective gloves. Open your pipe patch kit or mix your epoxy or pipe repair putty, following the instructions. Apply the patch or clamp over the damaged spot. Make sure it\u2019s tight and secure. Wait for the recommended cure time, then turn the water back on and check for leaks.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve just patched a pipe and saved money. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
