      transcript:
        "Did you know dirty supply vents can ruin your air quality and energy bills? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to clean your supply vents like a pro, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off your HVAC system for safety. Gather your supplies: a HEPA vacuum filter, vent cleaning brush, disinfectant spray, protective gloves, and drop cloths. Put on your gloves and lay down drop cloths to catch dust.\n\nNext, remove the vent covers. Use your vacuum to suck up dust and debris from the covers and the area around each vent. Wipe down the covers with disinfectant spray.\n\nNow, clean inside the ducts. Use a vacuum hose or a vent brush to reach as far as you can into the duct, loosening and removing dust. Take your time\u2014this step is key for better air flow.\n\nOnce you\u2019re done, reinstall the vent covers. Turn your HVAC system back on and check that air is flowing well from each vent.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
