      transcript:
        "Want to build a farm fence that lasts for years? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a strong, reliable farm fence from start to finish. \n\nFirst, plan your site. Walk your property lines, mark where the fence will go, and decide where you want your gates. Clear away any brush or obstacles along the fence line. This usually takes about 6 to 8 hours.\n\nNext, install your posts. Dig holes at regular intervals\u2014usually 8 feet apart. Set each post in concrete or tamped soil, making sure they\u2019re straight and level. This step is key for a sturdy fence and takes 16 to 20 hours for a 1,000-foot fence.\n\nNow, attach your fencing. Unroll the woven wire fencing, stretch it tight, and fasten it to the posts with fence staples. Install your gate at the planned spot. This part takes 20 to 24 hours.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Walk the fence line, check for loose spots, and make sure the gates open and close smoothly. Fix anything that needs it. This last step takes 8 to 10 hours.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
