      transcript:
        "Is your roof leaking at the very top? It could be your ridge cap! In this video, you'll learn how to repair a roof ridge cap step by step, so you can protect your home from water damage. \n\nFirst, inspect the ridge cap for cracks, missing shingles, or loose nails. Gather your materials: ridge cap shingles, roofing nails, roofing cement or sealant, and underlayment. Don't forget your safety gear\u2014always follow local safety rules.\n\nNext, carefully remove the damaged ridge cap shingles and old nails. Clear away any debris. Check the ridge itself for any signs of rot or structural problems. Fix these before moving on.\n\nNow, install the new underlayment along the ridge if needed. Place the new ridge cap shingles, making sure they overlap correctly. Secure each shingle with roofing nails. Work your way along the ridge, keeping everything straight and tight.\n\nFinally, seal all exposed nail heads with roofing cement. Check for any gaps or loose spots. Do a final inspection to make sure everything is watertight.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
