      transcript:
        "Want to upgrade your old light switch in under 30 minutes? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to safely replace a single pole light switch, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker panel. Double-check that the switch is off by testing it\u2014safety first! Remove the cover plate and unscrew the old switch from the electrical box.\n\nNext, carefully disconnect the wires. Inspect them for any damage. If the ends are bent or frayed, trim and straighten them so you get a solid connection.\n\nNow, connect the wires to your new switch. Follow the manufacturer\u2019s instructions\u2014usually, black wires go to brass screws, and the ground wire goes to green. Tighten the screws, tuck the wires back in, and secure the switch and cover plate.\n\nTurn the power back on and test your new switch. That\u2019s it! You\u2019ve upgraded your light switch safely and easily.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
