        "Ever wondered how to safely wire a garbage disposal without calling an electrician? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to wire a garbage disposal, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, always turn off the power at your circuit breaker. Double-check with a voltage tester to make sure the power is off. Gather your tools and materials: 12/2 NM-B electrical wire, an electrical box, wire connectors, an outlet or switch, a cover plate, and cable clamps.\n\nNext, open the disposal\u2019s wiring compartment. Connect the ground wire to the green screw, the white neutral wire to the white lead, and the black hot wire to the black lead. Use wire connectors to secure each connection. Make sure all wires are tight and no copper is exposed. Attach the cable clamp to keep the wire in place, then close the compartment.\n\nNow, restore power at the breaker. Test the disposal by turning it on and off. Check all connections for safety and make sure everything meets your local electrical codes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
