        "Ever wondered how to fix a damaged door casing and make it look brand new? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair door casing like a pro. \n\nFirst, carefully score along the paint and caulk lines with a utility knife. This helps prevent damage to the wall. Use a pry bar to gently remove the old casing from the door frame. Pull out any leftover nails and clean up the area so it\u2019s ready for new trim.\n\nNext, measure the door frame. Mark and cut your new casing boards to size. For corners, make precise miter cuts so everything fits snug. Dry-fit the pieces around the door to check your work before installing.\n\nNow, nail the new casing in place using finishing nails. Fill any nail holes with wood filler. Run a bead of caulk along the seams for a smooth finish. Once it\u2019s dry, sand any rough spots. Finally, paint or stain the casing to match your existing trim.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
