        "Tired of that old popcorn ceiling? Here\u2019s how to remove it and get a fresh, modern look in just a few steps. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to safely remove popcorn texture, repair the ceiling, and paint it like a pro.\n\nFirst, clear the room. Move out furniture and cover floors and walls with plastic sheeting. Don\u2019t forget to turn off power to ceiling lights for safety.\n\nNext, lightly mist the ceiling with water. This softens the popcorn texture. Use a wide scraper to gently remove it. Collect all debris as you go.\n\nOnce the texture is gone, check for any gouges or rough spots. Patch these with joint compound. Let it dry, then sand the ceiling until it\u2019s smooth.\n\nNow, apply a stain-blocking primer. Let it dry fully. Then, use a roller to paint two coats of ceiling paint for a clean finish.\n\nFinally, remove all coverings, reinstall fixtures, and put the furniture back. Make sure to dispose of debris properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
