        "Want to make your home\u2019s exterior pop and last longer? Here\u2019s how to paint your soffit and fascia like a pro. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the exact steps and materials you need for a flawless finish.\n\nFirst, prep your surfaces. Clean the soffit and fascia to remove dirt, mildew, and any loose paint. Use a scrub brush and mild detergent. Once dry, sand the surfaces so the new paint sticks well.\n\nNext, check for damage. Look for rotted wood or cracks. Replace any bad sections, then fill gaps with paintable exterior caulk. Once repairs are dry, brush on a quality exterior primer, especially on bare or patched spots.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to paint. Use a high-quality exterior paint made for soffits and fascia. Apply with a brush or roller for even coverage. Let the first coat dry fully before adding a second coat if needed.\n\nLay down drop cloths, use painter\u2019s tape for clean edges, and don\u2019t forget safety if you\u2019re working on a ladder.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
