        "Is your tree leaning or splitting? You can save it with tree bracing! \n\nIn this video, you'll learn how to brace a tree step by step, using the right tools and materials.\n\nFirst, assess the tree. Look for cracks, splits, or heavy leaning. Decide if bracing is needed. Choose a tree bracing kit, padding, turnbuckles, and eye bolts. You\u2019ll need one kit, one padding, two turnbuckles, and two eye bolts per tree.\n\nNext, plan where to place the hardware. Mark the spots for drilling, usually above and below the weak point. Wrap the trunk with tree protection padding to prevent damage.\n\nDrill holes for the rods or cables. Insert the eye bolts and secure them tightly. Attach the cables or rods, connecting them with turnbuckles. Tighten the turnbuckles until the tree feels stable, but don\u2019t over-tighten.\n\nFinally, inspect all connections. Adjust the tension if needed. Clean up the area and check the tree regularly for any changes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
