      transcript:
        "Is your sprinkler system acting up? The problem might be hidden underground in the wiring. \n\nIn this video, you'll learn how to safely repair or replace damaged sprinkler wires step by step.\n\nFirst, always turn off the power to your sprinkler system. Find the control box and check for any obvious wire damage or corrosion.\n\nNext, use a multimeter to test each wire. Label your zones so you know which wire goes where. Carefully dig and expose the wiring at the valves and controller.\n\nNow, cut out any damaged wire sections. Strip the ends of the good wire. Use waterproof wire connectors or a direct burial splice kit to join new wire sections. Wrap connections with electrical tape for extra protection.\n\nOnce all repairs are done, turn the power back on. Test each sprinkler zone to make sure everything works. Secure all wiring and clean up your work area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
