      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to install bathtub plumbing like a pro? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to replace your old tub and set up new plumbing, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply. Disconnect the old plumbing and carefully remove the old bathtub. Clean the area and check for any damage or mold\u2014fix these before moving on.\n\nNext, install your new drain kit and P-trap. Fit the overflow and connect new copper pipes using the right fittings. Secure everything with pipe hangers and insulate the pipes to prevent heat loss. Don\u2019t forget to use plumber\u2019s putty or sealant on all threaded joints for a watertight seal.\n\nNow, set your new bathtub in place. Make sure it\u2019s level and secure. Connect the drain, overflow, and water supply lines using flexible supply hoses and shutoff valves. Turn the water back on and test for leaks at every connection.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
