      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely wire a circuit breaker panel like a pro? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to install and wire a new breaker panel, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, always shut off the main power supply. Use a voltage tester to double-check that everything is off. Gather your tools, safety gear, and all materials\u2014like your panel, breakers, wire, and connectors.\n\nNext, plan your panel layout. Decide which circuits go where, and label each breaker spot. Route your Romex wires neatly into the panel, following your local electrical codes. Use panel connectors and bushings to protect the wires as they enter.\n\nNow, strip the wire ends. Connect the hot wires to the breakers, the neutral wires to the neutral bar, and the ground wires to the grounding bar. Install each breaker securely in the panel slots.\n\nBefore you finish, double-check every connection. Make sure all screws are tight and wires are secure. Put the panel cover back on, restore power, and test each circuit to be sure everything works right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
