      transcript:
        "Want to give your cabinets a high-end look without a full remodel? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install crown molding on your cabinets for a seamless, professional finish. \n\nFirst, measure your cabinet tops carefully. Write down the lengths and plan where each molding piece will go, including corners and edges. This helps you buy the right amount\u2014usually about 40 linear feet for a standard kitchen.\n\nNext, cut your molding. Use a miter saw for clean, angled cuts that fit together at corners. Sand the edges smooth, then dry-fit each piece on the cabinets to check the fit before you attach anything.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install. Apply wood glue to the back of each molding piece, then press it onto the cabinet. Secure it with finishing nails, making sure the joints are tight and the molding sits flush against the cabinet.\n\nFor a flawless finish, fill any nail holes with wood filler, caulk the seams, and touch up with paint or stain to match your cabinets. Let everything dry, and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
