      transcript:
        "Did you know hidden mold in your air ducts can make your whole house sick? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely remove mold from air ducts, step by step. \n\nFirst, inspect your ductwork. Look for dark spots or musty smells. Wear gloves, N95 masks, goggles, and coveralls for safety. Seal off vents with plastic sheeting and tape to keep mold spores from spreading.\n\nNext, use a HEPA vacuum to clean out loose dust and debris inside the ducts. Then, scrub all accessible duct surfaces with an EPA-registered mold remover. Take your time\u2014thorough cleaning is key.\n\nAfter cleaning, spray an antimicrobial treatment inside the ducts. Use fans or a dehumidifier to dry everything out. Keep humidity low to stop mold from coming back.\n\nReplace your HEPA filters when you\u2019re done. Dispose of all used safety gear and plastic sheeting.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
