      transcript:
        "Is your deck post wobbly or rotting? Let\u2019s fix it fast and safe! \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to replace a deck post step by step, with the right tools and materials.\n\nFirst, remove the old post. Detach any railings or beams connected to it. Take out all fasteners, then carefully pull the damaged post out of its footing. Work slow to avoid damaging the deck structure.\n\nNext, check the footing. If it\u2019s cracked or loose, repair or replace it. Cut your new pressure-treated 4x4 post to the right length. Always treat any cut ends with wood preservative to prevent rot.\n\nNow, set the new post in place. Add a few inches of gravel at the bottom for drainage. Place the post base, then set the post on top. Make sure it\u2019s perfectly plumb using a level. Secure it with galvanized fasteners and hardware. Finally, reconnect the beams or railings, following your local building codes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
