      transcript:
        "Cracked or chipped porcelain tile? Don\u2019t replace the whole floor\u2014fix it fast and make it look new again! \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair damaged porcelain tiles step by step, using the right tools and materials.\n\nFirst, prep the area. Clean the damaged tile and remove any loose debris. Make sure the surface is dry\u2014this helps the repair stick.\n\nNext, use a porcelain repair compound or epoxy. Apply it to the chip or crack with a putty knife. Smooth it out so it\u2019s level with the tile. Let it set as the product instructions say\u2014usually about an hour.\n\nOnce it\u2019s dry, gently sand the area until it\u2019s flush with the rest of the tile. If needed, use touch-up paint to match the color. Finally, apply a grout sealer to protect the repair from moisture and stains.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your tile looks great and is ready for use.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
