      transcript:
        "Want to upgrade your kitchen with a brand new window, but not sure where to start? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to remove an old kitchen window and install a new vinyl replacement window like a pro. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: a 36 by 48 inch vinyl window, exterior trim, interior casing, spray foam insulation, shims, caulk, and fasteners. You\u2019ll also need basic tools like a drill, pry bar, and utility knife.\n\nStep one: Remove the old window. Carefully take off the interior and exterior trim, unscrew any fasteners, and gently pull out the old window. Inspect the opening for any damage and clean the area well.\n\nStep two: Prepare the opening. Check your measurements, repair or level the sill if needed, and dry fit the new window to make sure it sits square and flush.\n\nStep three: Install the new window. Apply flashing tape to the sill and sides. Set the window in place, use shims to level it, and secure it with screws. Fill any gaps with spray foam insulation. Open and close the window to make sure it works smoothly.\n\nStep four: Seal and finish. Run a bead of caulk around the window, reinstall the trim, and clean up your workspace. Dispose of the old window and materials according to your local rules.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
