      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/well-water-line-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a leaking well water line without calling in a crew? Today, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process to repair a well water line safely and efficiently.\n\nFirst, shut off your well pump and main water supply. This stops water flow and lets you work safely. Next, inspect the water line to find the exact spot of the leak. Mark the area so you know where to dig.\n\nNow, carefully dig to expose the damaged section of pipe. Take your time\u2014avoid hitting other utilities or making a big mess. Once the pipe is exposed, cut out the damaged part. Use a new 1-inch polyethylene water pipe and brass compression couplings to replace the bad section. Secure everything with pipe clamps, and wrap the joints with pipe insulation tape to prevent future leaks.\n\nBefore you cover it up, turn the well pump back on and check for leaks. If everything looks good, backfill the trench with gravel and soil, and restore the area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
