      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix damaged brick veneer and make it look brand new? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair brick veneer the right way, from removing old bricks to sealing the finished wall. \n\nFirst, start with surface preparation. Use a chisel and hammer to carefully remove any loose or damaged bricks and mortar from the area you want to repair. Clean out the cavity and brush off dust from the surrounding bricks. This helps the new mortar stick properly.\n\nNext, it's time for brick and mortar installation. Mix fresh Type N mortar according to the bag instructions. Lightly dampen the cavity so the mortar bonds well. Set your replacement bricks in place, matching the pattern of your existing wall. Fill the joints with mortar, then use a jointer tool to smooth and shape the lines. Wipe away any extra mortar before it dries.\n\nNow, let the mortar cure. This usually takes a few hours. Mist the area with water if it\u2019s hot or dry, so the mortar doesn\u2019t dry too fast and crack. Once cured, clean the area and remove any leftover debris. Finish by applying a masonry sealer to protect your repair from water and weather.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
