      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/emergency-burst-pipe-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "A burst pipe can flood your home in minutes\u2014do you know what to do? In this video, you'll learn how to handle an emergency burst pipe repair step by step. First, shut off your main water supply right away to stop the flooding. Inspect the area to see how bad the damage is. Next, open all faucets to drain any leftover water from the pipes. Clear the space around the burst pipe and use towels or buckets to catch drips. Now, cut out the damaged section of pipe with a pipe cutter. Install a slip coupling or a pipe repair clamp for a quick, temporary fix. Make sure the seal is tight and meets local plumbing codes. Once the repair is in place, slowly turn the water back on. Check for leaks at the repair site and run water through nearby fixtures to make sure everything holds. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
