      transcript:
        "Did you know a simple film can make your windows much harder to break? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install security window film step by step, so you can boost safety at home or on the job.\n\nFirst, gather your materials: security window film, application solution, a sharp utility knife, a squeegee, and lint-free cloths. For 100 square feet, you\u2019ll need about one bottle of solution, one pack of blades, and one squeegee.\n\nStart by cleaning the glass with glass cleaner and lint-free cloths. Remove all dust, grease, and debris\u2014this is key for the film to stick well.\n\nNext, measure each window carefully. Cut the film to size, leaving a little extra around the edges for trimming later.\n\nSpray the application solution onto the glass. Peel the backing off the film, then gently place it on the window. Use your squeegee to press out air bubbles and extra solution, working from the center out.\n\nOnce the film is flat, trim the edges with a sharp blade. Press the edges down firmly to seal.\n\nFinally, inspect your work for bubbles or gaps. Clean up the area and throw away any waste safely.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
