      transcript:
        "Want to know how to install a well casing the right way? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to get a safe, secure well casing installed. \n\nFirst, clear your site and set up the drilling rig. Drill the borehole to the depth your local codes require. This usually takes 6 to 8 hours.\n\nNext, lower your steel well casing into the hole. Use casing centralizers to keep it straight and centered. Make sure the casing sits at the right depth. This step can take 8 to 10 hours.\n\nNow, it's time to seal the casing. Mix cement grout and pump it around the outside of the casing. This seals the gap and keeps out contaminants. Plan for 6 to 8 hours for this step.\n\nFinally, flush the well to remove debris. Inspect the casing and seals to make sure everything is tight and meets local standards. This last step takes another 6 to 8 hours.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
