      transcript:
        "Want a lush, green yard fast? Here\u2019s how to resod your lawn step by step. \n\nFirst, you\u2019ll learn how to remove old grass, prep the soil, lay new sod, and care for it so it thrives. \n\nStart by cutting and removing all old sod, weeds, and debris. Loosen the soil about 2-3 inches deep, then rake it smooth and even. \n\nNext, spread 3 cubic yards of topsoil or compost over the area. Mix it into the soil and level everything with a rake. Make sure water will drain away from your house. \n\nNow, lay your new sod. Stagger the pieces like bricks, pressing the edges tightly together. Use a utility knife to trim around curves or obstacles. Secure the sod with landscaping stakes or pins if needed. \n\nRight after laying, water the sod deeply. Then, use a lawn roller to press the sod down for good soil contact. \n\nFor the first two weeks, keep the sod damp and avoid walking on it. This helps the roots grow strong. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
