      transcript:
        "Want a concrete porch that lasts for decades? Here\u2019s how to build it right, step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to prep, form, pour, and finish a concrete porch\u2014so you get pro results, even if it\u2019s your first time.\n\nFirst, clear the area and remove any grass or debris. Mark out your porch with stakes and string. Dig down to the right depth\u2014usually 6 to 8 inches\u2014and make sure the ground slopes away from your house for drainage.\n\nNext, build your forms using 2x4 lumber. Secure them tightly so they don\u2019t move. Add a layer of gravel, about 4 inches deep, and compact it well. This keeps your porch stable and helps prevent cracks.\n\nLay down concrete reinforcing mesh or rebar for strength. Now, mix and pour your ready-mix concrete. Spread it evenly, screed it level, and use a float to smooth the surface. Don\u2019t forget to add anchor bolts and expansion joints where needed.\n\nFinally, add your desired finish\u2014like broom texture or edging. Cover the slab with plastic or curing compound, and let it cure undisturbed. Follow local weather guidelines for best results.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
