        "Want to avoid costly mistakes before you build? Start with a site plan survey. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to survey your lot step by step, and what materials you\u2019ll need. \n\nFirst, do an initial site assessment. Visit your property, walk the boundaries, and look for key features like trees, slopes, or utility lines. Talk with anyone involved to make sure you know the project needs.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time for field measurements. Use surveying tools to measure distances, elevations, and mark out corners. You\u2019ll need about 40 survey stakes, 8 pieces of rebar for corners, 20 wood lath, 20 survey nails, and a roll of flagging tape. Mark each important spot clearly so nothing gets missed.\n\nAfter collecting your data, draft your site plan. Draw property lines, show where utilities run, and note any slopes or features. Double-check that your plan meets local rules and standards.\n\nThat\u2019s it! With the right prep and materials, your site plan survey will set your project up for success.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
