      transcript:
        "Ever wondered why your toilet leaks at the base? It\u2019s probably the gasket! Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace a toilet gasket step by step, so you can stop leaks and avoid water damage. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply behind the toilet. Flush to empty the tank, then disconnect the water line. Use a wrench to unbolt the toilet from the floor. Carefully lift the toilet and set it aside\u2014this is easier with a helper.\n\nNext, put on disposable gloves. Scrape off the old wax ring from the flange using a putty knife. Clean the area well and check the flange for cracks or damage. Make sure the surface is dry and free of debris.\n\nNow, place the new wax ring on the flange. Set new mounting bolts in place if needed. Lower the toilet straight down onto the gasket, lining up the bolts. Press down gently to seal. Tighten the nuts evenly\u2014don\u2019t overtighten or you could crack the porcelain. Reconnect the water supply, turn it on, and flush to check for leaks. Finish by caulking around the base if you want a clean look.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
