        "Ever wondered how to safely install a new breaker box in your home? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to install a breaker box, from shutting off the power to restoring it safely. \n\nFirst, always start by turning off the main power at your utility meter. Double-check with a voltage tester to make sure there\u2019s no electricity. Clear the area where you\u2019ll be working so you have safe, easy access.\n\nNext, mount the new breaker box to the wall. Make sure it\u2019s level and meets your local code for height and clearance. Secure it tightly so it won\u2019t move.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time for wiring. Route the incoming service wires, ground, and neutral into the box. Attach them to the correct terminals. Install your branch circuit breakers, then connect each circuit wire to its breaker. Use copper wire like Romex 12/2 or 10/2, and make sure all connections are tight and follow your local electrical codes.\n\nOnce everything is wired, double-check your work. Label each circuit clearly. If your area requires it, schedule an inspection. After passing inspection, restore power and test each circuit to make sure everything works.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
