      transcript:
        "Want to upgrade your floors without tearing out the old ones? Watch this to learn how to build a floating floor step by step.\n\nIn this video, you'll see how to install a floating floor, from prep to finishing touches. Let's get started.\n\nFirst, clear out the room and remove all furniture. Clean the subfloor well. Check for any bumps or dips\u2014use a level. Fix any uneven spots so your new floor sits flat and stable.\n\nNext, roll out your underlayment across the whole floor. Trim the edges to fit the space. Tape the seams to lock out moisture and help with sound insulation. If your room is prone to moisture, add a moisture barrier under the underlayment.\n\nNow, start laying your floating floor planks in one corner. Snap the planks together, making sure to leave a small gap along the walls for expansion. Stagger the seams so the joints don\u2019t line up\u2014this makes the floor stronger and looks better.\n\nOnce all the planks are down, install quarter round or base shoe molding around the edges to cover the gaps. Add transition strips where the new floor meets other surfaces. Give the floor a good clean, and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
