        "Did you know a leaky roof valley can ruin your whole roof? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a roof valley that keeps water out and your home safe. \n\nFirst, remove all old shingles and underlayment from the valley area. Make sure the decking is clean and free of nails or debris. Next, roll out a waterproof valley liner or ice and water shield along the valley. Overlap the edges and press it down tight to stop leaks before they start.\n\nNow, cut your galvanized steel valley flashing to fit. Lay it in the valley, making sure it lines up for good water flow. Nail it down with roofing nails, but don\u2019t overdrive the nails\u2014just snug enough to hold.\n\nReplace the shingles along the valley, trimming them for a tight fit. Seal all the edges with roofing cement or sealant to keep water out. Finally, inspect your work for gaps or loose spots, and clean up the area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
