      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a leaking water heater drain valve in under two hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to replace a water heater drain valve safely and easily. \n\nFirst, turn off the power or gas to your water heater. Then, close the cold water inlet valve. Attach a hose to the drain valve and run it to a safe drain or outside. Open the valve and let the tank drain completely\u2014this usually takes about 20 minutes.\n\nNext, use a wrench to unscrew and remove the old drain valve. Check the threads for any debris or rust, and clean them up so your new valve will seal tight.\n\nNow, wrap Teflon thread seal tape around the threads of your new drain valve. Screw it in by hand, then tighten it with your wrench. Make sure it\u2019s snug, but don\u2019t over-tighten.\n\nClose the new valve, remove the hose, and turn the cold water back on to refill the tank. Once it\u2019s full, restore power or gas. Check for leaks around the new valve\u2014if it\u2019s dry, you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
