      transcript:
        "Did you know a damaged vent pipe can cause leaks and bad smells in your home? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace a vent pipe step by step, so you can do it right the first time. \n\nFirst, shut off any HVAC or plumbing systems connected to the vent pipe. Clear the work area so you can reach the full length of the pipe. \n\nNext, remove the old vent pipe. Detach any fasteners, cut out damaged sections, and carefully pull out the pipe. Be gentle to avoid damaging nearby walls or ceilings. \n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install the new pipe. Measure and cut your 3-inch PVC vent pipe to fit. Use PVC elbows and fittings for turns. Apply primer and cement to all joints for a tight seal. Secure the pipe with hangers or straps every few feet. If the pipe goes through the roof, install a flashing boot to keep water out. Make sure everything lines up and slopes as required by your local code. \n\nFinally, test your work. Check for leaks, make sure air flows freely, and inspect all connections. Adjust as needed to meet code. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
