      transcript:
        "Want a stunning brick walkway that lasts for years? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a brick walkway like a pro. \n\nFirst, mark out your walkway with stakes and string. Remove any grass or debris, then dig down about 7 inches to make room for the base. Make sure the area is level and clear.\n\nNext, add a 4-inch layer of paver base gravel. Spread it evenly and compact it well. Then, lay down weed barrier fabric to stop weeds from growing through your walkway.\n\nPour a 1-inch layer of paver sand on top. Smooth it out and check for a slight slope so water drains away from your house.\n\nNow, start laying your brick pavers in your chosen pattern. Use a rubber mallet to tap each brick into place. Cut bricks as needed for the edges, and keep the spacing even. Install edging restraints along the sides to keep everything tight.\n\nOnce all the bricks are down, sweep more sand into the joints. Compact the walkway with a plate compactor, then add more sand if needed. Clean off the surface and inspect your work.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
