      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/toilet-seal-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what really keeps your toilet from leaking? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace a toilet seal step by step, so you can stop leaks and avoid costly water damage. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply behind your toilet. Flush to empty the tank, then disconnect the water line. Next, remove the nuts from the toilet bolts and carefully lift the toilet off the floor. Set it aside on an old towel. Scrape away the old wax ring from the flange using a putty knife, and clean the area well.\n\nNow, place your new wax ring or rubber seal onto the flange, making sure it\u2019s centered. If your mounting bolts are rusty, swap them out for new ones. With gloves on, carefully lower the toilet straight down onto the new seal. Press gently to seat it, then tighten the bolts evenly\u2014don\u2019t overtighten or you could crack the base.\n\nReconnect the water line, turn the supply back on, and flush a few times. Check for leaks around the base. If it\u2019s dry, you\u2019re done! Caulk around the base for a clean finish if you like.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
