      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to restore old, damaged brickwork and make it look brand new? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process for professional brick restoration, from start to finish.\n\nFirst, assess the area. Spend 3 to 4 hours inspecting the brickwork for cracks or damage. Clean the surface and gather your tools and materials\u2014like replacement bricks, Type N mortar mix, masonry cleaner, backer rod, and water repellent sealer. Protect nearby surfaces before you begin.\n\nNext, remove the damaged bricks and old mortar. This takes about 6 to 8 hours. Use a hammer and chisel to carefully take out broken bricks. Clean the exposed area so it\u2019s ready for new materials.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install new bricks. Mix your mortar to match the existing color. Lay the bricks, making sure they\u2019re level and spaced evenly. Apply mortar between each brick and tool the joints for a smooth, consistent look. This step usually takes 10 to 12 hours.\n\nLet the mortar cure for 8 to 9 hours. Once it\u2019s set, inspect your work for stability and appearance. Clean up the site and apply a water repellent sealer to protect your restoration.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
