      transcript:
        "Is your baseboard heater not warming up like it should? In this video, you'll learn how to safely repair a baseboard heater and get it working again. \n\nFirst, always turn off the power at the circuit breaker. Safety comes first! Remove the heater cover and look for any obvious damage, dust buildup, or loose wires. \n\nNext, grab a vacuum and clean out dust and debris from the heater fins and housing. Tighten any loose wire connections. Check the thermostat and wiring for signs of wear or corrosion. If you spot any damaged parts, it's time to replace them. \n\nSwap out the heating element, thermostat, or wiring as needed. Use wire connectors and electrical tape to secure your connections. Reassemble the heater, turn the power back on, and test to make sure it heats up properly. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
