      transcript:
        "Is your door not latching right or feeling loose? Let\u2019s fix that strike plate in under an hour! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a door strike plate step by step, so your door closes tight and secure. First, grab a screwdriver and remove the old strike plate from the door frame. Check the area for any damage or worn-out screw holes. If the holes are stripped, fill them with wood filler or use toothpicks and wood glue. Let it dry, then sand the area smooth. Next, line up your new strike plate and secure it with fresh wood screws. Make sure it sits flush with the frame. Test the door\u2014if it doesn\u2019t latch right, adjust the plate until it does. Finish up with a little touch-up paint or stain if needed. That\u2019s it! Your door should now close perfectly. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
