        "Want to make your garage floor look brand new in just a few hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to pressure wash your garage floor the right way. \n\nFirst, clear out your garage. Move cars, tools, and anything else off the floor. Sweep up all the loose dirt and cover any electrical outlets with plastic sheeting for safety.\n\nNext, tackle those tough stains. Apply a concrete-safe degreaser to any oil spots or stubborn marks. Let it sit as the label says, then scrub with a stiff brush to loosen up the grime.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to pressure wash. Set up your pressure washer with a nozzle made for concrete. Work in overlapping passes to make sure you don\u2019t miss a spot. Take your time\u2014this step usually takes about an hour for a standard two-car garage.\n\nWhen you\u2019re done, rinse the floor well to remove all soap and residue. Let the floor air dry before you move anything back in.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
