      transcript:
        "Did you know clogged gutters can cause thousands in water damage? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely and efficiently remove debris from your gutters, step by step. \n\nFirst, gather your tools and safety gear. You\u2019ll need heavy-duty trash bags, disposable gloves, a sturdy ladder, a bucket, a trowel, and safety glasses. Set up your ladder on stable ground and make sure it\u2019s secure before climbing up.\n\nNext, put on your gloves and start removing debris. Use your hands or a trowel to scoop out leaves, twigs, and dirt. Drop everything into your bucket to keep things tidy. As you go, check for any blockages in the gutter or downspouts.\n\nOnce the debris is gone, grab a garden hose and flush out the gutters and downspouts. Watch the water flow\u2014if it backs up, you may have a clog to clear. While you\u2019re up there, inspect for leaks, sagging, or any damage. Make a note of anything that needs repair.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Clean gutters protect your home and save you money. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
