      transcript:
        "Want to make your old retaining wall look brand new in just a few hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to pressure wash a retaining wall safely and effectively. \n\nFirst, get your materials ready: rent a pressure washer, grab some masonry detergent, plastic sheeting, and painter\u2019s tape. You\u2019ll need about four hours for every 100 feet of wall.\n\nStart with site prep. Clear away debris, move anything nearby, and cover plants or outlets with plastic sheeting and tape. This protects everything from water and chemicals.\n\nNext, mix your pressure washing detergent as directed. Apply it evenly to the wall and let it soak for about 30 to 45 minutes. This helps break down dirt, mold, and stains.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to pressure wash. Use the right nozzle\u2014usually a 25-degree tip. Start at the top of the wall and work your way down, keeping the nozzle about a foot away to avoid damage. Move slowly and overlap each pass for a thorough clean. This step takes about 1.5 to 2 hours.\n\nFinally, rinse the wall with clean water. Check for any missed spots and repeat if needed. Remove your coverings and tidy up the area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
