      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely add a power outlet right in your floor? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a floor outlet like a pro. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker box. Pick the perfect spot for your outlet\u2014make sure there\u2019s nothing underneath, like pipes or joists. Mark the spot clearly on your floor.\n\nNext, use a hole saw to cut out the opening. Carefully fish 12/2 Romex wire from your power source to the new hole, following your local electrical codes. Take your time\u2014safe wiring is key.\n\nNow, mount the floor outlet box in the hole. Connect the wires to a tamper-resistant receptacle using wire connectors. Secure everything with mounting screws. Restore power at the breaker, then test your new outlet with a device to make sure it works. Finally, install the cover plate for a clean, finished look.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
