      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a damaged drain pipe without digging up your yard? Today, I\u2019ll show you exactly how drain pipe relining works, step by step. \n\nFirst, start with a camera inspection. Feed the camera into the pipe to spot cracks, roots, or buildup. Once you know what you\u2019re dealing with, clean the pipe thoroughly. Use high-pressure water or mechanical tools to clear out all debris\u2014this step is key for a strong bond later.\n\nNext, measure the length of pipe you need to reline. Mix your epoxy resin according to the instructions. Then, soak the liner with the resin. Insert the liner into the pipe using either the inversion or pull-in-place method. Make sure the liner covers the entire damaged area.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to cure. Let the liner set for 16 to 18 hours, or as the manufacturer recommends. Once it\u2019s cured, do a final camera inspection to check your work. If everything looks good, restore water flow and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
