      transcript:
        "Frozen pipes can burst and flood your home\u2014here\u2019s how to thaw them safely and fast! \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to find frozen pipes, thaw them without damage, and prevent future freezing.\n\nFirst, locate the frozen section. Check for weak water flow and look at exposed pipes in cold spots like basements or crawl spaces. Turn off your main water supply to avoid a burst pipe.\n\nNext, thaw the pipe safely. Use a hair dryer, heat lamp, or wrap warm towels around the pipe. Start near the faucet and work toward the frozen area. Never use an open flame\u2014it\u2019s a fire risk.\n\nOnce thawed, slowly turn the water back on. Watch for leaks and check all faucets to make sure everything works. If you spot a leak, shut off the water and call a pro.\n\nTo prevent freezing again, wrap pipes with insulation or use heat tape.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
