      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/soundproof-drywall-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to block out noise and get real peace and quiet? Let\u2019s walk through how to install soundproof drywall, step by step. \n\nFirst, clear your workspace and remove any old wall coverings. Check the framing\u2014fix anything that needs repair before you start. \n\nNext, apply acoustic sealant to all wall joints. Add soundproof insulation between the studs if you want extra noise control. Then, attach resilient channels or sound isolation clips to the framing. These help stop sound from traveling through the walls.\n\nNow, hang your soundproof drywall panels. Cut them to fit, stagger the seams, and screw them tightly to the channels. This makes a big difference in blocking sound.\n\nTape all the joints, then apply joint compound in thin layers. Sand between coats for a smooth finish. Take your time\u2014this step is key for a seamless look.\n\nFinally, prime and paint the walls. Reinstall your trim, and seal any gaps with acoustic caulk. That\u2019s it\u2014your room is now ready for quiet!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
