      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to blast away stubborn drain clogs with pure water power? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to hydro jet a drain, step by step, so you can clear tough blockages like a pro. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: rent a hydro jetting machine, grab protective gear\u2014gloves, goggles, and boots\u2014plus drain access tools and about 200 gallons of water for every 100 feet of pipe. Safety first: always suit up before you start.\n\nStep one: Inspect the drain. Look for blockages and plan your access. Set up your hydro jetting machine near the drain, making sure all connections are tight and safe.\n\nStep two: Feed the hydro jetting hose into the drain. Turn on the machine and slowly apply high-pressure water. Move the hose through the pipe to break up grease, roots, and debris. Take your time\u2014this usually takes 1.5 to 2 hours for 100 feet.\n\nStep three: When you\u2019re done, flush the drain with clean water to check the flow. Inspect for leaks, then clean up your tools and the area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
