      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to install a sewer drain the right way? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process for a safe, code-compliant sewer drain installation. \n\nFirst, start with a site assessment. Check your existing plumbing, plan your drain route, and get any permits you need. Always mark utility lines before digging.\n\nNext, it's time for excavation. Dig a trench along your planned path, making sure you hit the right depth and slope for proper drainage. Clear out any debris and prep the trench bed with gravel bedding.\n\nNow, lay your 4-inch PVC sewer pipes. Use the right fittings\u2014elbows, tees, and couplings\u2014and secure each joint with PVC glue and primer. Don't forget to install cleanout fittings where required by local code.\n\nBefore you cover anything up, schedule an inspection. Test for leaks and check the slope. Once you get the green light, backfill the trench and compact the soil to prevent settling.\n\nFinally, do a flow test to make sure everything works. Restore the surface and dispose of any leftover materials properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
