      transcript:
        "Want to light up your yard with a post light, but not sure where to start? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a post light safely and correctly.\n\nFirst, mark the spot where you want your post light. Always call your local utility service to check for underground lines before you dig. Clear away any debris or obstacles.\n\nNext, dig a hole deep enough for your post\u2014usually about 2 feet. Place the post in the hole, making sure it\u2019s level. Pour in concrete mix and let it partially set. This keeps your post sturdy for years.\n\nNow, run PVC conduit from your power source to the post. Pull UF-rated electrical wire through the conduit. Connect the wires using wire connectors, and follow your local electrical codes for safety.\n\nMount the light fixture on top of the post. Connect the wiring, install the bulb, and turn on the power to test your new light.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
