      transcript:
        "Is your hydronic heating system not working right? Let\u2019s walk through how to repair it step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to inspect, repair, and restart your hydronic heating system safely and efficiently.\n\nFirst, shut off the power and water to your system. Inspect the boiler, pumps, and all piping for leaks or damage. Look for any faulty parts, like a bad circulator pump or a leaking valve.\n\nNext, repair or replace the broken parts. Swap out any bad zone valves, circulator pumps, or thermostats. Make sure the new parts match your system. Use copper pipe, pipe insulation, and the right fittings. Solder joints with flux for a tight seal.\n\nOnce repairs are done, refill the system with a glycol and water mix. Bleed air from all radiators and lines. Check the pressure and flow to make sure everything is balanced.\n\nFinally, turn the power back on. Test the heating cycles. Watch for leaks and adjust the controls for safe, efficient heat.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
