      transcript:
        "Is your stone mailbox falling apart? Let\u2019s fix it step by step. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a stone mailbox, from removing damaged stones to making it look brand new.\n\nFirst, inspect your mailbox for loose or broken stones. Gather your tools and materials: mortar mix, replacement stones, masonry sealer, metal lath if needed, and brick ties. Clear the area so you can work safely.\n\nNext, carefully remove any loose or damaged stones. Use a chisel and hammer if needed. Clean off old mortar from both the stones and the mailbox structure. This helps the new mortar stick better.\n\nNow, mix fresh mortar according to the instructions. If you need extra support, attach metal lath and brick ties to the mailbox. Start resetting the stones in their original spots. Press them firmly into the mortar and fill the joints evenly. Make sure the stones are level and stable.\n\nLet the mortar set for about an hour. Wipe off any extra mortar from the stone faces. Once everything is dry, check the alignment and apply masonry sealer to protect your work.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
