      transcript:
        "Want to save money and keep your spa warm all year? Let\u2019s walk through how to insulate your spa the right way.\n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process to insulate your spa, boost energy efficiency, and cut down on heating costs.\n\nFirst, prep your site. Clear the area around your spa, disconnect the power, and make sure everything is dry and easy to reach.\n\nNext, remove the spa panels to access the inside. Check for any moisture or damage. Clean all surfaces so the insulation sticks well.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to insulate. Use closed cell spray foam insulation and a vapor barrier. Spray the foam evenly on the spa shell and plumbing. Cover every spot\u2014no gaps! Follow the manufacturer\u2019s instructions for best results.\n\nOnce the insulation is set, put the panels back on. Seal any openings with adhesive or sealant. Make sure everything fits tight to keep the heat in.\n\nFinally, restore power and test your spa. Check for any heat loss. Clean up your work area and dispose of waste safely.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
