      transcript:
        "Want to keep deer out of your yard for good? Watch how to install a strong, long-lasting deer fence step by step. \n\nFirst, plan your site. Measure the area you want to protect and mark the fence line. Pick where your gate will go. Always call 811 to check for underground utilities before you dig, and check your local fence rules.\n\nNext, install your posts. Dig holes about 8 feet apart. Set each metal post in concrete or tamped soil. Make sure they line up straight and are sturdy.\n\nNow, attach the fence mesh. Unroll the 7-foot-high deer fence along your posts. Pull it tight and use fence ties or clips to secure it to each post. If you need a gate, install it now. Double-check that your fence is tall enough to keep deer out.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Walk the fence line, look for gaps, and reinforce any weak spots. Trim off extra mesh and clean up all debris.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
