      transcript:
        "Want to make your steps look brand new in just a couple of hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to pressure wash your steps safely and effectively. \n\nFirst, clear the area. Move any furniture, cars, or debris away from your steps. Cover electrical outlets and any delicate plants nearby with plastic sheeting and painter\u2019s tape. This keeps everything safe from water and cleaning chemicals.\n\nNext, set up your pressure washer. Connect it to a water source and pick the right nozzle\u2014usually a 25-degree tip for steps. If your steps are really dirty, apply a pressure washing detergent. Let it soak in for a few minutes to break up grime.\n\nNow, start washing from the top step and work your way down. Hold the nozzle about a foot away from the surface to avoid damage. Use steady, even strokes. Once you\u2019ve cleaned all the steps, rinse them well with clean water to remove any leftover soap.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your steps should look fresh and clean. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
