      transcript:
        "Want to make your old roof look new and last longer? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to apply a roof coating step by step, so you get pro results and save money.\n\nFirst, you\u2019ll learn how to prep your roof. Start by clearing off all debris, dirt, and any old coatings. Use a roof cleaner and scrub well. Fix any cracks or damaged spots\u2014this helps the coating stick and last.\n\nNext, apply a roof primer if your coating needs it. Use a roller or brush, and make sure you cover the whole area. Let it dry completely before moving on.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time for the main event: applying the elastomeric roof coating. Use a roller or sprayer for even coverage. Don\u2019t forget the edges and seams. For extra strength, add roof fabric reinforcement over problem areas before the final coat.\n\nOnce you\u2019re done, let the coating cure for at least 12 hours. Don\u2019t walk on it while it dries. After curing, inspect the roof for any missed spots and touch up as needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
