        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/construction-staking/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to make sure your building project starts in the right spot? In this video, you'll learn how to do construction staking step by step, so your layout is accurate and ready for inspection. \n\nFirst, review your project plans and check the property boundaries. Walk the site and look for anything that could affect your staking, like trees or slopes. This helps you plan where each stake will go and keeps you in line with local rules.\n\nNext, set up your survey equipment. Mark your main control points and reference benchmarks. These are your guideposts for the whole project, so double-check their locations.\n\nNow, it's time to place your stakes. Use wood stakes, flagging tape, string line, and nails. Mark out building corners, utility lines, and grading limits. Measure twice to make sure every stake is in the right spot.\n\nFinally, verify all your staked points. Write down their locations and create a staking report. This is important for inspections and your project records.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
