      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to build a safe, long-lasting chimney? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process for chimney construction, from foundation to final inspection. \n\nFirst, clear your work area and mark out the chimney footprint. Pour a reinforced concrete foundation\u2014this is key for stability and should take about 6 to 8 hours. Next, start building the chimney stack. Lay clay bricks or concrete blocks in even rows, using Type N mortar mix for strong joints. As you go, install chimney flue liners to guide smoke safely out and meet local building codes. This stage usually takes 24 to 28 hours.\n\nOnce the stack is up, form and pour the chimney crown at the top. Install a chimney cap to keep out rain and debris. Add a flashing kit where the chimney meets the roof\u2014this keeps water from leaking in. This part takes another 6 to 8 hours.\n\nFinally, inspect your work for safety and code compliance. Clean up all debris and tools. That\u2019s it! You\u2019ve built a chimney that\u2019s safe, efficient, and built to last.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
