      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/radon-barrier-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Did you know radon gas can sneak into your home through the floor? In this video, you'll learn how to install a radon barrier step by step, so you can protect your space and breathe easy. \n\nFirst, clear all debris and level the subfloor. Make sure the area is clean and dry\u2014this is key for a good seal. Next, unroll the 10-mil radon barrier membrane. Cut it to fit, and overlap each seam by at least 12 inches. Cover the entire subfloor, with no gaps.\n\nNow, seal every seam and edge with radon-resistant tape. Pay extra attention to spots where pipes or walls meet the floor. Use polyurethane sealant for any tricky areas or penetrations. Secure the edges with a termination bar and fasteners, about every foot along the perimeter.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Look for gaps, tears, or loose edges. Fix any issues, and make sure your installation meets local building codes and radon standards.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
