      transcript:
        "Want to build a custom bookshelf that fits your space perfectly? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to plan, build, and finish a sturdy, beautiful bookshelf. \n\nFirst, measure your space and sketch your bookshelf design. Choose strong 3/4-inch plywood for the main structure and 1x2 hardwood trim for a clean look. Gather your materials: plywood sheets, trim, wood screws, wood glue, primer and paint, shelf pins, and sandpaper.\n\nNext, cut your plywood panels to size. Sand all surfaces smooth and pre-drill holes for easy assembly. Lay out your parts and tools so everything\u2019s ready to go.\n\nNow, assemble the frame. Attach the sides, top, and bottom with wood screws or glue. Add the shelves, making sure everything is level and square. Use shelf pins or brackets if you want adjustable shelves.\n\nFill any holes, sand rough edges, and apply your choice of paint or stain. Let it dry completely before moving the bookshelf.\n\nFinally, position your bookshelf and anchor it to the wall for safety. Clean up your workspace and arrange your books and decor.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
