        "Thinking about switching to a propane water heater? Here\u2019s how to install one safely and efficiently. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process, from removing your old unit to firing up your new propane heater. \n\nFirst, turn off the water and propane supply. Drain your old water heater, disconnect the plumbing and gas lines, and carefully remove the old unit from your space. \n\nNext, bring in your new propane water heater. Set it in place, then connect the water supply lines. Install the venting kit as the manufacturer recommends\u2014this is key for safe operation. Attach the propane gas line using approved fittings, and don\u2019t forget to add a shutoff valve for safety. \n\nNow, check all your connections for leaks. Fill the tank, purge any air from the lines, and ignite the pilot. Make sure everything runs smoothly and meets your local safety codes. Clean up your workspace, and you\u2019re done! \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
