        "Want to install a kitchen gas line safely and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn the exact steps and materials needed for a professional kitchen gas line installation.\n\nFirst, shut off the main gas supply. Assess your kitchen and plan the best route for the new gas line. Make sure you have all permits and materials ready: CSST gas pipe, shutoff valve, fittings, pipe hangers, sealant, and an escutcheon for wall or floor entry.\n\nNext, measure and cut about 30 feet of 1/2-inch CSST gas pipe. Attach the pipe to the shutoff valve, then use proper fittings and connectors to secure each joint. Support the pipe every few feet with hangers to prevent sagging. Use pipe thread sealant or tape on all threaded connections for a tight seal. Install the escutcheon where the pipe passes through walls or floors for a clean finish.\n\nOnce installed, pressurize the line and check every joint for leaks using soapy water or a gas leak detector. If you see bubbles or detect gas, tighten the connections. Schedule an inspection if your local code requires it before turning the gas back on.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
