      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to install a well water line that lasts for years? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to run a new water line from your well to your building, the right way. \n\nFirst, start with a site assessment. Mark your water line route, check for underground utilities, and make sure you have all permits and materials ready. This keeps your project safe and up to code.\n\nNext, it's time for trenching and pipe laying. Dig a trench deep enough to protect the pipe from freezing\u2014usually below the frost line. Lay 1-inch polyethylene water pipe along the route, making sure it slopes gently from the well to the building for good water flow.\n\nNow, connect and seal. Attach the pipe to the well using a brass pitless adapter and check valve. Connect the other end to your building's plumbing. Use quality fittings and clamps, and seal every joint tight to prevent leaks.\n\nBefore you finish, pressure test the line. Check for leaks and make sure the system holds pressure. Once it passes, backfill the trench with sand or clean soil, and restore the surface.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
