      transcript:
        "Is your wood siding looking rough or starting to rot? In this video, you'll learn how to repair wood siding step by step, so your home looks great and stays protected. \n\nFirst, inspect your siding. Look for rot, cracks, or loose boards. Clean the area and gather your tools: pry bar, hammer, saw, nails, wood filler, primer, paint, and caulk.\n\nNext, carefully remove any damaged boards. Use a pry bar and hammer, and be gentle so you don't damage the good siding or the wall underneath.\n\nNow, measure and cut your new siding boards to fit. Make sure they match the old boards. Attach them with galvanized nails or screws, keeping everything lined up.\n\nAfter the boards are in, seal all the joints and gaps with caulk. Fill any small holes with exterior wood filler. Once dry, apply primer to the new wood. Then paint or stain to match your existing siding. This keeps out water and gives a smooth, finished look.\n\nThat's it! Your siding is repaired and ready for any weather. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
