      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how easy it is to fix a broken light switch yourself? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely repair or replace a single pole light switch in just a few steps. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your circuit breaker. Double-check the switch is off, then use a screwdriver to remove the cover plate. \n\nNext, inspect the wiring. Look for loose or damaged wires. If the switch is faulty, disconnect the wires and attach them to a new switch. Make sure each wire is tight and secure. Use wire connectors and a bit of electrical tape for extra safety. \n\nNow, reattach the cover plate. Turn the power back on at the breaker. Test your switch to make sure it works. \n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve just repaired your light switch safely and quickly. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
