      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/hvac-mold-removal/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Did you know hidden mold in your HVAC can ruin your air and your health? Today, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to remove mold from your HVAC system, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the HVAC power. Put on N95 respirators, gloves, and protective clothing. Seal off the work area with plastic sheeting and duct tape to keep mold spores from spreading.\n\nNext, inspect all ducts, coils, and vents for mold. Remove vent covers and vacuum inside the ducts using a HEPA vacuum. Scrub all accessible surfaces with an EPA-approved antimicrobial cleaner. If you find any contaminated insulation, replace it. Don\u2019t forget to swap out old HEPA filters for new ones.\n\nAfter cleaning, spray all cleaned parts with antimicrobial treatment. Use fans or a dehumidifier to dry everything completely. Keep an eye on humidity\u2014mold loves moisture.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve just tackled HVAC mold removal safely and thoroughly. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
