        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/stone-crack-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix cracks in stone so they disappear for good? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair stone cracks like a pro. \n\nFirst, gather your supplies: epoxy or polyurethane crack filler, masonry cleaner, backer rod, painter\u2019s tape, and disposable gloves. \n\nStart by cleaning the cracked area with masonry cleaner. Remove all dirt, dust, and loose pieces. Inspect the crack to see how deep and wide it is.\n\nNext, use a chisel to slightly widen and deepen the crack. This helps the filler bond better. Brush out any dust and rinse the area. Let it dry.\n\nNow, if the crack is deep, push a backer rod into the gap. Tape off the edges with painter\u2019s tape to keep things neat. Mix your epoxy or crack filler as the label says. Wearing gloves, fill the crack completely, pressing the filler in so it reaches all the way down. Smooth the surface to match the stone.\n\nLet the repair cure for the time listed on your product. Once it\u2019s dry, sand or polish the area for a seamless look. Clean up your tools and workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
