      transcript:
        "Want to build a backyard sandbox that lasts for years? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a safe, sturdy sandbox for your kids or clients. \n\nFirst, pick a flat, sunny spot away from trees and roots. Clear away grass, rocks, and debris. Use a shovel and level to make the ground even\u2014this is key for a stable sandbox.\n\nNext, build your frame. Use eight pieces of 2x6 pressure-treated lumber, each 8 feet long. Lay them out in a square, secure the corners with galvanized brackets, and fasten everything with galvanized screws. Double-check that all sides are square and level.\n\nNow, roll out weed barrier fabric inside the frame. This keeps weeds out and sand clean. Cut the fabric to fit, and staple it down.\n\nPour in about 40 bags of clean play sand. Spread it evenly with a rake. Smooth the surface, check for sharp edges, and install a cover if you want extra protection.\n\nFinally, inspect the sandbox for safety\u2014no sharp screws or splinters. Now it\u2019s ready for play!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
