        "Ever wondered how to safely and efficiently demo the inside of a building? Today, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process for a successful interior demolition, from prep to cleanup. \n\nFirst, clear out all furniture and belongings. Set up plastic sheeting and painter\u2019s tape to block off dust, and disconnect any utilities\u2014safety first! Put on your dust mask, gloves, and coveralls before you start. \n\nNext, begin selective demolition. Remove drywall, flooring, and non-load-bearing walls using the right tools. Be careful not to damage anything structural. Take your time\u2014this step can take up to 14 hours for 1,000 square feet.\n\nOnce demo is done, sort and bag all debris using heavy-duty contractor bags. Load everything into your rented dumpster. Recycle materials if you can, and follow your local disposal rules.\n\nFinally, sweep and vacuum the area. Inspect for any hidden damage so the space is ready for the next phase of your project.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
