      transcript:
        "Is your stone patio looking uneven or falling apart? Let\u2019s fix it step by step so it looks brand new. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a stone patio the right way, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, inspect your patio for loose, cracked, or uneven stones. Remove any damaged stones and sweep away debris. Clean the area well\u2014this helps new stones stick and last longer.\n\nNext, check the base. Add or remove gravel or sand to level it out. Use a tamper or plate compactor to make the base solid and flat. This is key for a stable patio.\n\nNow, place your new or existing stones back in. Make sure each stone is level with the others. Tap them gently with a rubber mallet. Fill the joints with polymeric sand or mortar, depending on your patio style.\n\nFinally, sweep off any extra sand or mortar. Mist the patio with water to help the joint material settle. Clean up the area and throw away debris as needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
