        "Is your laundry room always humid or musty? Let\u2019s fix that with a new exhaust fan! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to install a laundry-rated exhaust fan step by step, from planning to final testing. \n\nFirst, pick the right fan for your space and check your local building codes. Gather your tools and mark where the fan will go. Make sure you have access to electrical wiring.\n\nNext, cut an opening in the ceiling or wall for the vent. Install the mounting bracket, then attach the fan housing securely.\n\nNow, connect the fan to power using 14/2 NM-B electrical wire and wire connectors. Run a 4-inch flexible duct from the fan to an exterior vent cap. Use duct clamps to seal all joints tight for best airflow.\n\nFinally, test the fan. Check airflow at the outside vent, install the fan cover, and clean up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
