      transcript:
        "Want to install your dishwasher like a pro and avoid leaks? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to handle dishwasher plumbing installation, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply and disconnect the power. Clear out the space under your sink so you have room to work. Gather your materials: a 6-foot braided stainless steel water supply line, a 6-foot drain hose, a 3/8-inch compression elbow fitting, Teflon plumber\u2019s tape, and two hose clamps. Make sure your existing plumbing matches your new dishwasher\u2019s connections.\n\nNext, connect the water supply line to the shutoff valve. Use Teflon tape on the threads for a tight seal. Attach the drain hose to your sink drain or garbage disposal, and secure it with hose clamps. Make sure both lines are routed without kinks or sharp bends to prevent leaks.\n\nNow, connect the power\u2014either wire it in or plug it into a grounded outlet. Turn the water and power back on. Run a short cycle to check for leaks and make sure everything works right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
