      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to strip old paint off your cabinets without ruining them? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to safely and effectively remove paint from your cabinets, so you\u2019re ready for a fresh new look. \n\nFirst, clear out your cabinets. Take off the doors, remove all hardware, and empty the shelves. Lay down plastic drop cloths to protect your floors, open windows for ventilation, and put on rubber gloves and a respirator mask for safety.\n\nNext, apply a chemical paint stripper or use a heat gun on the cabinet surfaces. Work in small sections. Let the stripper sit as directed, then use a scraper to gently lift off the softened paint. Don\u2019t rush\u2014take your time to avoid damaging the wood.\n\nAfter most of the paint is gone, use steel wool pads or sandpaper to remove any leftover residue, especially in corners and crevices. Wipe everything down with a damp rag to get rid of dust and chemicals.\n\nFinally, inspect your cabinets for any missed spots. Dispose of paint chips and chemical waste safely, following your local rules. Let the cabinets dry completely before you start refinishing.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
