      transcript:
        "Is your central air conditioning unit on its last legs? Here\u2019s how to replace it step by step, so you can keep your home cool and comfortable. \n\nFirst, shut off the power to your HVAC system. Recover any refrigerant safely, then disconnect the electrical wiring and ductwork. Make sure the area is clear and safe to work in.\n\nNext, remove the old unit. Carefully detach it from its base, and check for any damage or debris. Clean the area before moving on.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install the new unit. Set the new air conditioner on a solid pad. Connect the electrical wiring, refrigerant line set, and ductwork. Double-check that all connections meet local codes and the manufacturer\u2019s instructions.\n\nAfter everything is hooked up, evacuate the system and charge it with refrigerant. Restore power and test the system. Check airflow, temperature, and make sure the thermostat and controls work right.\n\nFinally, clean up the work area and dispose of the old unit properly. Do a final inspection to confirm everything runs safely and efficiently.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
