      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix crumbling brick steps and make them look brand new? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair a 3-step brick section like a pro. \n\nFirst, clear away any debris and set up safety barriers around your work area. Gather your tools and materials: about 40 replacement bricks, 2 bags of Type N mortar mix, a quart of concrete bonding agent, joint tooling sand, and some plastic sheeting to protect nearby surfaces.\n\nNext, carefully chisel out the damaged bricks and scrape away old mortar. Clean the exposed surfaces well\u2014this helps the new mortar stick.\n\nNow, mix your mortar according to the instructions. Brush on the bonding agent, then set your new bricks in place, making sure they line up with the existing steps. Fill the joints evenly with mortar and use a joint tool to smooth them out for a clean finish.\n\nWipe away any extra mortar, then let the steps cure undisturbed. Once dry, your steps are safe and ready to use!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
