        "Want your paint job to last longer and look better? Start with a proper power wash! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to power wash your home before painting, step by step. \n\nFirst, prep your work area. Move outdoor furniture, cover plants, and use plastic sheeting and painter\u2019s tape to protect outlets and anything you don\u2019t want wet. This takes about an hour but saves you headaches later.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time to power wash. Fill your washer with about 200 gallons of water and add pressure washer detergent\u2014about 2 gallons for 1,000 square feet. Spray every surface you plan to paint. Focus on removing dirt, mildew, and any loose paint. Take your time\u2014this step usually takes 2 to 3 hours.\n\nAfter washing, let everything dry for at least 2 hours. Once dry, inspect the surfaces. Look for leftover debris or any damage that needs fixing before you start painting.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
