        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/partition-wall-framing/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to frame a partition wall like a pro? Let\u2019s break down the exact steps you need to get it done right. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to lay out, frame, and prep a partition wall for drywall. \n\nFirst, measure and mark where your wall will go on the floor and ceiling. Use a chalk line to snap straight guides\u2014accuracy here makes everything easier. \n\nNext, cut your pressure-treated bottom plate and top plate to length. Secure the bottom plate to the floor and the top plate to the ceiling, following your chalk lines. Use the right fasteners for your subfloor and ceiling type.\n\nNow, measure and cut your 2x4 studs. Place them vertically between the plates, spacing them 16 inches on center, or as your local code requires. Make sure each stud is plumb and nail them in with 16d framing nails.\n\nIf you need a doorway, frame a rough opening. Add a header and jack studs to support the load above the door.\n\nFinally, check all your connections, make sure the wall is straight and secure, and clean up the area. Your partition wall is now ready for drywall.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
