      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/soundproofing-bathroom/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wonder how to make your bathroom truly private and quiet? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to soundproof your bathroom like a pro. \n\nFirst, inspect your bathroom walls, doors, and vents for any gaps or cracks. Remove any fixtures in the way and clean all surfaces\u2014this helps the soundproofing materials stick better.\n\nNext, seal up all gaps with acoustic sealant. Then, install acoustic insulation batts inside the wall cavities. Attach resilient channels to the studs, and hang soundproof drywall over them. Use screws and fasteners to secure everything tightly.\n\nDon\u2019t forget the door! Add weatherstripping around the frame and install a door sweep at the bottom to block sound leaks.\n\nFor plumbing and vents, wrap exposed pipes with acoustic insulation. Install vent baffles or soundproof covers on exhaust fans to keep noise from escaping.\n\nFinally, reinstall any fixtures you removed. Test for sound leaks by closing the door and listening. Make any needed adjustments, then clean up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
