        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/build-concrete-floor/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want a rock-solid concrete floor that lasts for decades? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to build a concrete floor the right way, from prep to finish. \n\nFirst, clear your site and remove any debris. Level the ground and set up sturdy 2x4 form boards to outline your floor. Make sure to add a slight slope if you need drainage.\n\nNext, spread and compact a layer of gravel or crushed stone for a stable base. Roll out a 6 mil poly vapor barrier to block moisture. Then, lay out your rebar or wire mesh for strength\u2014tie it together and keep it raised off the ground.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to pour. Mix your 4000 psi ready-mix concrete and pour it evenly inside the forms. Use shovels and rakes to spread it, then screed the surface with a straight board to get it level.\n\nAfter pouring, smooth the surface with a float. Add texture if you want, and cut control joints to prevent cracks. Keep the concrete moist and covered for several days so it cures strong.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
