      transcript:
        "Want to make your RV look brand new in just a few hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to pressure wash your RV safely and effectively, step by step. \n\nFirst, move your RV to a good washing spot. Close all windows and vents. Check the outside for any damage or sensitive areas\u2014cover those with plastic sheeting to protect them.\n\nNext, grab your pressure washer. Give the RV a quick rinse to knock off loose dirt. Then, spray on an RV-safe detergent. Let it soak for a few minutes so it can break down the grime.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time for the main wash. Start at the top and work your way down. Use the pressure washer to clean every surface, paying extra attention to seams and wheel wells. For stubborn spots, use a soft bristle brush. Rinse everything thoroughly.\n\nFinally, do a last rinse to remove all soap. Check for any missed spots. Dry the RV with microfiber towels, and make sure your work area is clean.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
