        "Ever wondered how to hook up a garbage disposal without calling a plumber? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to install a garbage disposal safely and efficiently. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at the breaker. Clear out the cabinet under your sink and disconnect the drain pipes. If there's an old drain assembly, remove it now.\n\nNext, install the mounting assembly. Attach the mounting ring and flange to the sink drain opening. Use plumber\u2019s putty for a watertight seal, and make sure everything is tight and lined up as the manufacturer suggests.\n\nNow, connect the disposal unit. Mount it to the assembly, then wire it up using an electrical cord kit. Secure the unit, attach the flexible discharge tube, and connect it to your drain system. Use the right plumbing fittings and adapters for a snug fit.\n\nFinally, restore power. Run water and test the disposal. Check all connections for leaks and make sure it runs smoothly. Clean up your workspace, and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
