      transcript:
        "Want a concrete deck that lasts for years? Here\u2019s how to build one the right way, step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to prep your site, pour and finish concrete, and make sure your deck is strong and smooth.\n\nFirst, clear and level your work area. Mark out your deck\u2019s shape and size. Set up 2x4 form boards around the edges, making sure they\u2019re straight and secure. Next, lay down a 4-inch gravel base for drainage. Place No. 4 rebar in a grid pattern inside the forms\u2014this adds strength and prevents cracks. Tie the rebar together with wire.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to pour. Order 4000 psi ready-mix concrete\u2014about 7.5 cubic yards for a 300 square foot deck. Pour the concrete evenly into the forms. Use a screed board to level it, then smooth the surface with a float. Add texture or pattern if you want slip resistance. Don\u2019t forget to install expansion joint material every 8 to 10 feet to control cracking.\n\nLet the concrete cure for at least 36 hours. Keep it moist by misting with water or covering with plastic. Once cured, carefully remove the forms. Inspect the deck for any rough spots and seal the surface with a concrete sealer to protect it from stains and weather.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
