      transcript:
        "Ever had a leaky toilet shut off valve and wondered if you could fix it yourself? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace a toilet shut off valve step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off your main water supply. Flush the toilet to drain out any water left in the tank. Place towels or a bucket under the supply line to catch drips.\n\nNext, disconnect the supply line from the old shut off valve. Use a wrench to loosen and remove the old valve. Clean the pipe threads so your new valve seals tight.\n\nNow, wrap plumber\u2019s tape around the threads. Attach your new 1/4 turn angle stop valve and tighten it with a wrench. Connect a new braided supply line from the valve to the toilet.\n\nTurn the main water back on. Open the new shut off valve and check for leaks. Make sure the toilet fills and works like normal.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
