      transcript:
        "A broken sewer line can turn into a disaster fast\u2014here\u2019s how to fix it right, step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn exactly how to handle an emergency sewer line repair, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, assess the problem. Inspect the sewer line, find the break, and mark all nearby utility lines. Set up safety barriers and gather your tools. \n\nNext, it\u2019s time to dig. Carefully excavate the area to expose the damaged pipe. Watch out for other underground utilities, and make sure your trench is safe and shored up. \n\nNow, repair or replace the line. Cut out the damaged section, then install new 4-inch PVC pipe and fittings. Use primer and cement for strong, leak-free joints. Test the repair for leaks and proper flow before moving on. \n\nFinally, backfill the trench. Add pipe bedding sand, then gravel, and compact the soil. Patch any asphalt or concrete you had to cut, and clean up the site. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
