        "Ever wondered how to move your thermostat without messing up your walls or wiring? Today, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to relocate a thermostat safely and efficiently. \n\nFirst, always start by turning off the power to your HVAC system at the breaker. This keeps you safe. Next, remove the old thermostat from the wall. Label each wire as you disconnect it\u2014this makes reconnecting easy later.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to run new wiring. Use 18/5 thermostat wire and route it through the wall or ceiling to your new location. Secure the wire and follow local electrical codes. You\u2019ll need wire connectors and a low voltage electrical box at the new spot.\n\nOnce the wire is in place, mount the new electrical box and attach the thermostat base. Connect each labeled wire to the right terminal. Screw the thermostat in, snap on the cover, and restore power. Program your thermostat for comfort and test to make sure everything works.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
