      transcript:
        "Did you know a simple sensor can save your garage\u2014and your family\u2014from accidents? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install garage door safety sensors step by step. \n\nFirst, unplug your garage door opener for safety. Clear the area around the tracks so you have room to work. Gather your tools: a sensor kit, low voltage wire, and wire staples or clips.\n\nNext, mount the sensors on each side of the garage door track. Place them about six inches above the floor. Make sure both sensors are at the same height and facing each other directly\u2014this is key for proper operation.\n\nNow, run the low voltage wire from each sensor up to the opener unit. Use wire staples or clips to keep the wire neat and out of the way. Connect the wires to the opener, following the manufacturer\u2019s instructions.\n\nPlug the opener back in. Test the sensors by closing the door and waving an object in front of them. The door should stop or reverse\u2014if not, check the alignment and wiring.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
