      transcript:
        "Want to know how to install a concrete parking lot that lasts for years? In this video, I\u2019ll show you every step, from site prep to final striping, so you can get it done right the first time.\n\nFirst, clear your site and excavate to the right depth. Remove all debris and grade the soil for good drainage. Compact the soil well\u2014this is key for a stable base.\n\nNext, set up your forms using 2x6 lumber or metal. Lay down about 25 tons of 3/4-inch crushed stone and compact it. This gravel base keeps your concrete strong and prevents cracks.\n\nNow, install your rebar\u2014No. 4, half-inch bars work great. Space them evenly for solid reinforcement. Pour 4000 psi ready-mix concrete, about 37 cubic yards for a 3,000 square foot lot. Use screeds and floats to level and smooth the surface.\n\nKeep the concrete moist as it cures. Cut control joints to stop cracks before they start. After curing, remove the forms, clean up, and add striping and signs to meet local codes. Inspect everything for safety and quality.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
