        "Want a stunning, durable countertop you can install yourself? Watch this! In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to install a tile countertop, from demo to final seal. \n\nFirst, remove the old countertop. Disconnect plumbing, take out the old top, and clean the base. Fix or reinforce the surface so it's strong and flat.\n\nNext, measure and mark layout lines. Dry fit your tiles to plan cuts and avoid tiny pieces at the edges. Adjust for the best look.\n\nNow, spread thinset mortar evenly over the surface. Set your tiles in place using spacers. Cut tiles as needed for edges and around sinks. Make sure everything is level and lined up.\n\nOnce the mortar dries, apply grout between the tiles. Wipe away extra grout and clean the tile faces. Check the joints and touch up if needed.\n\nFinally, seal the grout to protect it. Reinstall your sink and plumbing. Caulk the edges for a clean finish. Clean up your workspace and toss any debris properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
