      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a damaged tile wall and make it look brand new? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to repair a tile wall like a pro. \n\nFirst, assess the damage. Check which tiles need replacing and gather matching tiles, thinset mortar, grout, spacers, and a backer board patch if needed. Clear the area and protect nearby surfaces. Good ventilation is important.\n\nNext, carefully remove the broken tiles. Use a chisel and hammer to lift them out, and scrape away old adhesive. Clean the wall so it\u2019s smooth and ready for new tiles.\n\nNow, apply fresh thinset mortar to the wall. Press the new tiles into place, using spacers to keep them even. Let the adhesive set as the manufacturer recommends\u2014usually a few hours.\n\nOnce the tiles are set, mix your grout and press it into the joints. Wipe away extra grout with a damp sponge and smooth the lines. When the grout dries, clean the tiles and inspect your work.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
