      transcript:
        "Mold can destroy your home fast\u2014here\u2019s how to stop it in its tracks. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process to repair mold damage safely and effectively.\n\nFirst, assess the affected area. Look for visible mold and moisture sources. Set up plastic sheeting to contain the space and keep spores from spreading. Always wear N95 respirators, gloves, and protective coveralls for safety.\n\nNext, remove any contaminated materials like drywall or carpet. Clean all surfaces with a mold remediation cleaner. Use a HEPA vacuum to capture loose spores. Place all debris in sealed disposal bags.\n\nNow, dry out the area. Set up air movers and dehumidifiers to bring moisture levels down. This step is key to prevent mold from coming back.\n\nFinally, restore and protect. Repair or replace damaged structures. Apply an anti-microbial sealant to all cleaned surfaces. Make sure to fix any leaks or moisture problems to keep mold away for good.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
