        "Want to save energy and protect your pipes from freezing? Let\u2019s show you how to install pipe insulation the right way.\n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to measure, cut, fit, and seal foam pipe insulation for any exposed pipes.\n\nFirst, measure the length and diameter of every exposed pipe you want to insulate. Write down your numbers, then buy foam pipe sleeves and insulation tape that match your pipe size. You\u2019ll need about 17 six-foot sleeves for 100 feet of pipe, plus a roll of tape and some cable ties.\n\nNext, cut the insulation sleeves to fit each pipe section. Most sleeves are pre-slit\u2014just open them up and snap them over the pipe. Make sure the insulation covers the entire length, including any bends or joints.\n\nNow, seal every seam and joint with insulation tape. Wrap the tape tightly so there are no gaps. Use cable ties to secure the insulation at tricky spots, like elbows or fittings.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Check that every pipe is fully covered and the insulation is snug. Clean up any scraps and throw away packaging according to your local rules.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
