      transcript:
        "Want a rock-solid concrete pad that lasts for years? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a concrete pad the right way, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, mark out your pad boundaries and clear away any grass, rocks, or debris. Excavate the area to the right depth\u2014usually about 7 inches for a 4-inch pad plus gravel base. Make sure the ground is level and compact it well. This gives your pad a strong, stable base.\n\nNext, build your forms using 2x4 lumber. Secure them tightly so they don\u2019t move. Add about 2 tons of 3/4-inch crushed gravel, spread it out, and compact it for drainage and stability.\n\nLay out your rebar grid\u2014No. 3 rebar works great. Tie the bars together and keep them off the ground with small supports.\n\nNow, mix your ready-mix concrete or have it delivered. Pour it into the forms, spread it evenly, and use a screed board to level the surface. Smooth it out with a float, and use an edging tool for clean edges.\n\nFinally, apply a curing compound or cover the pad with plastic. Let it cure undisturbed for at least 8 hours for best strength.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
