      transcript:
        "A gas leak is an emergency\u2014do you know how to fix it fast and safely? In this video, you'll learn the exact steps to repair a damaged gas line, from shutoff to inspection. \n\nFirst, turn off the main gas supply right away and ventilate the area. Use a gas detector or soapy water to find the leak. Next, carefully remove the damaged section of pipe. Use the right tools and always follow local safety codes. \n\nNow, measure and cut your new black iron gas pipe. Attach the right fittings\u2014elbows, couplings, or tees\u2014and use pipe thread sealant on all threads. Secure the new pipe with hangers or supports. Once everything is tight, pressure test the line to make sure there are no leaks. \n\nFinally, slowly turn the gas back on. Check every connection with a gas leak detector solution. Make sure all appliances work, and document your repair for code compliance. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
