      transcript:
        "Ever wonder how to fix ugly drywall seams so they disappear? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair drywall seams like a pro. \n\nFirst, clear the area and remove any loose material from the seams. Lightly sand the edges so you have a clean, smooth surface to work with. This prep takes about 45 minutes but makes a big difference.\n\nNext, grab your joint compound and drywall tape. Spread a thin layer of compound over the seam, then press the tape into it. Smooth out any extra compound with your knife. Let this first coat dry completely\u2014usually about an hour or so.\n\nNow, apply a second coat of joint compound. Feather the edges so it blends into the wall. Once it\u2019s dry, sand the area until it\u2019s smooth and ready for paint. Don\u2019t forget to wipe away dust before priming and painting.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Seamless drywall repairs, done right. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
