        "Want to install a new kitchen door without the headaches? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to replace your kitchen door like a pro. \n\nFirst, remove the old door. Unscrew the hinges and take off the handle. Clear away any old hardware and check the frame for damage. Make sure the opening is clean and square\u2014this helps your new door fit right.\n\nNext, set your new prehung door into the opening. Use shims to keep it level and plumb. Attach the hinges to the frame, then secure the door with finishing nails or screws. Install your new handle or knob set, and any other hardware you need.\n\nNow, test the door. Open and close it a few times. Adjust the shims if it sticks or rubs. Once it swings smoothly, add the door casing or trim around the frame. Fill any nail holes with wood filler or caulk for a clean look. Finish up by applying weatherstripping if needed, and clean your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
