        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/deck-stairs-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to build safe, sturdy deck stairs without guesswork? In this video, you'll learn how to plan, build, and finish a set of deck stairs step by step. \n\nFirst, measure from your deck to the ground. This tells you how many steps you need. Sketch your stair layout and check your local building codes. Gather all your materials: pressure-treated stringers, treads, risers, deck screws, concrete mix, post anchors, and a handrail kit.\n\nNext, mark and cut your stringers to match your rise and run. Treat the cut ends to prevent rot. Test-fit the stringers to make sure they sit level and tight.\n\nNow, secure the stringers to your deck frame and set them on concrete footings. Use metal post anchors for extra support. Make sure everything is level and solid.\n\nAttach your treads and risers to the stringers. Space them evenly and fasten them with galvanized deck screws. Double-check that each step is secure and level.\n\nFinish by adding a handrail or guardrail if needed. Inspect all fasteners and clean up your work area. Make sure your stairs meet safety codes before using them.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
