      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/gas-line-maintenance/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Did you know a hidden gas leak could put your home at risk? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely maintain and repair a gas line, step by step. \n\nFirst, always shut off the main gas supply and ventilate the area. Use your nose\u2014if you smell gas, leave and call the pros. If it\u2019s safe, inspect all visible gas lines for rust, corrosion, or damage.\n\nNext, grab a gas leak detector solution. Brush it onto every joint and fitting. Watch for bubbles\u2014those mean leaks. Tighten any loose fittings. If you spot worn parts, mark them for replacement.\n\nNow, replace any faulty valves, connectors, or pipe sections. Use pipe joint compound or thread seal tape on all new connections. Make sure you use materials rated for gas lines, like black iron or CSST pipe and approved fittings.\n\nOnce repairs are done, slowly turn the gas back on. Check every joint again with leak detector solution. Finally, test all appliances to make sure they work and there are no leaks. Always follow your local safety codes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
