      transcript:
        "Want to stop water from ruining your brick or block walls? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to waterproof masonry step by step, so your walls stay dry and strong for years. \n\nFirst, prep the surface. Use a wire brush and pressure washer to clean off dirt, stains, and loose mortar. Let the wall dry fully\u2014this is key for a good seal.\n\nNext, check for cracks or gaps in the mortar. Fill them with masonry caulk or repair mortar. Smooth it out so the surface is even.\n\nNow, tape off any areas you don\u2019t want sealed. Use painter\u2019s tape and masking materials for clean edges.\n\nTime to apply the waterproofing sealer. Use a roller or sprayer for even coverage. Work in sections and follow the product\u2019s drying times. Don\u2019t miss any spots!\n\nOnce dry, inspect the wall. Touch up any missed areas with more sealer.\n\nFinally, clean your tools and throw away waste safely. Double-check your work to make sure every inch is sealed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
