      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/concrete-garage-floor-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want a garage floor that lasts for decades? Here\u2019s how to install a concrete garage floor the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, clear out your garage and remove any debris. Excavate the area to the right depth, then compact the soil. Add a layer of gravel\u2014this helps with drainage and keeps your slab stable.\n\nNext, build your forms using 2x4 lumber around the edges. Lay down a 6-mil vapor barrier to block moisture. Place wire mesh or rebar for reinforcement\u2014this prevents cracks and adds strength.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to pour the concrete. Order enough ready-mix for a 4-inch slab\u2014about 12 cubic yards for a 400 square foot garage. Pour the concrete evenly, then use a screed to level it. Float the surface smooth, and make sure you have a slight slope for drainage.\n\nAfter pouring, use trowels and edgers for a clean finish. Cover the slab to keep in moisture and let it cure slowly\u2014this is key to preventing cracks and making your floor strong.\n\nOnce the concrete sets, remove the forms. Clean up the site and check for any defects. Dispose of leftover materials properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
