      transcript:
        "Want a lush green lawn fast? Here\u2019s how to install a new lawn the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn every step to get a beautiful yard, from prep to first watering. \n\nFirst, clear the area. Remove old grass, weeds, and debris. Loosen the soil about 3 to 4 inches deep. Take out rocks and roots for a smooth surface.\n\nNext, spread topsoil or compost. Mix it into the soil to boost nutrients. Grade the area so water drains away from your house or patio.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to lay sod or spread grass seed. Place sod rolls tightly together, or rake seeds lightly into the soil. This helps roots make good contact.\n\nWater the new lawn right away. Soak the soil to the root depth. For the first two weeks, keep the area damp but not soggy.\n\nFinally, clean up extra materials and tools. Check for gaps or dry spots and fix them. This helps your lawn grow in thick and even.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
