      transcript:
        "Want perfect, crack-free drywall corners? Here\u2019s how to install corner bead like a pro. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn every step to get strong, clean drywall corners that last.\n\nFirst, prep your workspace. Clear the area, remove dust, and make sure your drywall corners are clean and dry. This helps the bead stick well.\n\nNext, measure each corner. Cut your metal corner bead to fit. Test the fit before you attach it\u2014accuracy here means a better finish later.\n\nNow, install the bead. Hold it tight to the corner and fasten it with drywall screws every 8 to 12 inches. Make sure it\u2019s straight and snug along the whole edge.\n\nTime for joint compound. Apply a thin layer over the bead, feathering the edges out onto the drywall. Let it dry, then sand smooth. Repeat with a second coat if needed for a seamless look.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your corners are protected and ready for paint.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
