        "https://contractor-plus-website.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/og-images/24d0e2cb-7e8f-4bd2-8b45-9e4fe76c3469.jpg",
      uploadDate: "2025-08-04",
      duration: "PT2M35S",
      contentUrl:
        "https://contractor-plus-website.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/reshub-how-to-vids/pipe-insulation-installation.mp4",
      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/pipe-insulation-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to stop pipes from freezing or sweating? Here\u2019s how to insulate your pipes like a pro.\n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn step-by-step how to install foam pipe insulation, from prep to final check.\n\nFirst, inspect all exposed pipes and measure their length and diameter. Write these down so you buy the right size foam insulation, tape, and cable ties. You\u2019ll need about 17 pieces of 1-inch foam insulation for 100 feet of pipe, plus a roll of insulation tape and some cable ties.\n\nNext, clean and dry every pipe. Dirt or moisture will keep the insulation from sticking well.\n\nNow, cut the foam insulation to fit each pipe section. Open the slit, wrap it around the pipe, and press it closed. For corners or joints, cut angles so the pieces fit tight. Seal every seam with insulation tape, especially in cold or humid areas.\n\nSecure the insulation with extra tape or cable ties. Double-check for any gaps or exposed spots, especially at joints and bends.\n\nFinally, clean up scraps, store leftover materials, and review every pipe to make sure it\u2019s fully covered and sealed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
