        "Want to make your old cabinets look brand new without replacing them? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to paint your cabinets like a pro. \n\nFirst, remove all cabinet doors, drawers, and hardware. Label each piece so you can put everything back in the right spot later. Set them aside safely.\n\nNext, clean every surface with a degreaser to get rid of grease and grime. Sand all the doors, drawers, and frames. This helps the paint stick and gives you a smooth finish.\n\nNow, apply a stain-blocking, bonding primer to every surface. Let it dry completely. This step is key for a long-lasting paint job.\n\nOnce the primer is dry, paint your cabinets with two coats of high-quality cabinet paint. Use a brush or roller for even coverage. Let each coat dry before adding the next.\n\nFinally, reattach all the hardware, doors, and drawers. Check for any missed spots and touch up as needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
