      transcript:
        "Want to avoid costly sprinkler repairs this season? Let\u2019s walk through a full sprinkler system startup, step by step. \n\nFirst, inspect your system. Check all sprinkler heads, valves, and pipes for damage or debris. Clear away any dirt or grass, and make sure every part is easy to reach.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time to pressurize and test. Slowly open the main water supply. Don\u2019t rush\u2014this prevents pipe bursts. Manually turn on each zone, one at a time. Watch for leaks, check that every head sprays evenly, and make sure your lawn gets full coverage. Replace any broken heads and use pipe sealant tape if you spot leaks. If a valve isn\u2019t working, swap out the diaphragm and use system lubricant as needed.\n\nFinally, adjust your controller. Set the watering schedule for each zone. Fine-tune run times and tweak sprinkler heads so every area gets the right amount of water.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
