      transcript:
        "Did you know dirty solar panels can lose up to 25% of their power? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely pressure wash your solar panels for maximum efficiency. \n\nFirst, turn off your solar panel system and check the manufacturer\u2019s cleaning guidelines. Safety comes first\u2014set up ladders or harnesses if your panels are on the roof. Clear away any debris and lay down protective sheeting to shield nearby areas.\n\nNext, fill your pressure washer with deionized water and a biodegradable solar panel cleaner. Attach a soft bristle brush. Use low pressure\u2014never high!\u2014and spray at a shallow angle. Gently scrub each panel section by section. This helps avoid damage to the glass or seals.\n\nOnce you\u2019re done, inspect the panels for any leftover dirt or signs of damage. Wipe down the edges and let them dry. Finally, turn the system back on and make sure everything is working right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
