      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to move a light switch without calling an electrician? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to safely move a light switch to a new spot in your home. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker box. Double-check the switch is dead with a tester. Mark the new spot on your wall and plan your wiring route. Make sure there are no pipes or studs in the way.\n\nNext, remove the old switch and gently pull out the wires. Cut the drywall as needed, drill holes, and run your new Romex wire to the new location. Install a new single gang electrical box.\n\nConnect the wires to your new switch, secure it in the box, and add a switch plate cover. Turn the power back on and test the switch. Finally, patch up any drywall holes you made.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
