        "Is your wrought iron fence looking rusty or broken? Let\u2019s fix it step by step so it looks brand new again. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a 20-foot section of wrought iron fence, from assessment to painting. \n\nFirst, inspect your fence for rust, damage, and loose parts. Gather your tools and materials: replacement pickets and rails, welding rods, rust converter, primer, exterior metal paint, and mounting hardware. Clear the area for safe access.\n\nNext, remove all rust and old paint using a wire brush, sandpaper, or grinder. Clean the surface well so new materials stick properly.\n\nNow, repair the fence. Weld or fasten any broken sections. Replace missing pickets or rails. Fill holes or cracks with metal filler. Make sure everything is secure and lines up with the original design.\n\nAfter repairs, apply a rust-inhibiting primer and let it dry. Then, paint the repaired areas or the whole fence with weather-resistant paint.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your fence is strong and looks great again. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
