      transcript:
        "Did you know a fresh under-sink water filter can make your tap water taste brand new? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace your under-sink water filter step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the cold water supply valve under your sink. Open the faucet to relieve any pressure, and clear out the cabinet so you have room to work.\n\nNext, disconnect the tubing from the old filter. Unscrew or unclip the filter housing, then pull out the old filter cartridge.\n\nNow, grab your new filter cartridge. Insert it into the housing, making sure it\u2019s seated properly. Secure the housing back in place, and reconnect all tubing. Use Teflon plumber\u2019s tape on threaded connections to prevent leaks.\n\nTurn the water supply back on slowly. Run the faucet for a few minutes to flush the new filter. Check all connections for leaks. Tighten as needed.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve got clean, filtered water again. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
