      transcript:
        "Want to make your roof strong and weatherproof? Here\u2019s how to install roof sheathing the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process to lay down OSB or plywood panels, fasten them securely, and get your roof ready for shingles. \n\nFirst, clear off the roof deck. Remove any old nails or debris. Check for damaged wood and fix it now. Next, bring up your sheathing panels, nails, adhesive, and drip edge flashing. Keep everything close, but safe from falling.\n\nNow, start laying your panels. Use 4x8 foot OSB or plywood sheets. Stagger the joints so seams don\u2019t line up. Leave a small gap\u2014about an eighth of an inch\u2014between panels for expansion. Fasten each panel to the rafters or trusses with roofing nails or screws. Follow your local building code for spacing and fastener type. Use adhesive or construction glue for extra strength if required.\n\nOnce all panels are down, install any required clips and tape the seams. Double-check that every panel is tight and secure. Walk the roof and inspect your work. Make sure everything meets your local code before moving on to underlayment.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
