      transcript:
        "Cracked or loose tiles around your bathtub? Here\u2019s how to fix them like a pro. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn step-by-step how to repair bathtub tiles, from removal to sealing, so your bathroom looks brand new.\n\nFirst, use a chisel and hammer to carefully remove any damaged tiles. Take your time\u2014avoid breaking nearby tiles. Scrape away old adhesive and grout until the area is clean and smooth.\n\nNext, make sure the surface is dry and dust-free. Apply a layer of thinset mortar or tile adhesive evenly over the exposed area. This helps the new tiles stick properly.\n\nNow, press your replacement tiles into the adhesive. Line them up with the existing tiles and use spacers to keep the grout lines even. Let the adhesive set for about an hour.\n\nOnce the tiles are secure, mix your grout and spread it between the tiles. Wipe away any extra grout with a damp sponge. After the grout dries, apply a waterproof sealant to protect your repair from moisture.\n\nFinally, inspect your work for any uneven spots and clean up the area. Throw away debris and make sure your bathtub is ready to use.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
