        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/masonry-caulking/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to seal your masonry joints like a pro and keep water out for years? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to caulk masonry joints for a clean, watertight finish. \n\nFirst, prep your surface. Remove any old caulk, dirt, or loose debris from the joints. Make sure everything is dry and clean\u2014this helps the new caulk stick better.\n\nNext, use painter\u2019s tape along both sides of the joint. This keeps your lines sharp and protects the brick or stone from extra caulk.\n\nNow, grab your caulk. Cut the tip of the tube at a 45-degree angle and load it into your caulking gun. Squeeze a steady bead of caulk into the joint. For deep gaps, push in a backer rod first. Smooth the bead with a caulking tool or your finger for a neat finish.\n\nLet the caulk cure as the label says. Once it\u2019s set, peel off the tape and check for any missed spots. Touch up if needed to make sure it\u2019s fully sealed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
