        "Ever wondered how to safely tear out a bathroom without making a huge mess? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to demolish a bathroom the right way, from prep to cleanup. \n\nFirst, get your materials ready: heavy-duty trash bags, dust masks, work gloves, plastic sheeting, painter\u2019s tape, saw blades, and floor protection board. These keep you safe and your home clean.\n\nStart with site prep. Shut off the water and electricity. Remove all personal items. Lay down floor protection and seal off the area with plastic sheeting and painter\u2019s tape to keep dust contained.\n\nNext, remove fixtures. Disconnect and take out sinks, toilets, tubs, and cabinets. Always cap off plumbing and electrical lines for safety.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time for tile and wall demo. Use a reciprocating saw and pry bars to carefully remove wall tiles, floor tiles, drywall, and backer board. Wear your dust mask and gloves, and work slowly to avoid damaging what you want to keep.\n\nFinally, clean up. Bag all debris, sweep, and vacuum the area. Make sure the space is clear and ready for the next phase of your remodel.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
