        "Ever wondered what it really takes to replace a main breaker panel safely and efficiently? In this video, you'll learn the exact steps and materials needed to swap out a 200-amp main breaker panel, from shutdown to inspection. \n\nFirst, always start with safety. Notify everyone in the building, shut off the main utility power, and double-check that all circuits are dead. Set up safety barriers around your work area.\n\nNext, label every existing circuit in the old panel. Disconnect all branch wires, remove the breakers, and carefully detach the old panel from the wall.\n\nNow, it's time to install the new panel. Mount it securely, transfer and connect all branch wires, and install your new breakers. Make sure to use proper copper grounding wire and follow local electrical codes for grounding and bonding.\n\nOnce everything is in place, schedule an inspection with your local authorities. Make any adjustments they require. When you get the green light, restore power and test all circuits.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
