      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/well-water-softener-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Tired of hard water ruining your pipes and appliances? Let\u2019s walk through how to install a well water softener, step by step. \n\nFirst, you\u2019ll learn how to plan your setup, connect the system, and test it for perfect results. \n\nStart by shutting off your main water supply. Pick a spot near your main water line and a power outlet. Always check your local plumbing codes before you begin.\n\nNext, cut into the main water line. Install the bypass valve kit, then connect the inlet and outlet pipes. Set your softener tank and brine tank in place, following the manufacturer\u2019s instructions.\n\nNow, hook up the drain tubing and overflow line. Plug in the power supply. Add salt to the brine tank, program the control head, and start up the system. Make sure you follow your local water quality guidelines.\n\nFinally, check for leaks. Run a full regeneration cycle. Test the water to confirm it\u2019s soft, and clean up your work area. Dispose of any waste according to local rules.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
