      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/water-heater-leak-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your water heater leaking and you\u2019re not sure what to do next? In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to fix a water heater leak step by step, so you can stop the drip and save money. \n\nFirst, shut off the power or gas to your water heater. Then, close the water inlet valve. Attach a hose to the drain valve at the bottom of the tank and drain the water safely into a floor drain or outside. This prevents spills and makes repairs easier.\n\nNext, inspect all connections, valves, and the tank itself. Look for loose fittings, worn-out hoses, or a faulty valve. Tighten any loose connections. If you spot a bad valve or hose, replace it with new parts. For minor tank leaks, use plumber\u2019s tape and approved patch materials. Make sure you use the right materials for your plumbing type\u2014copper, PVC, or PEX.\n\nOnce repairs are done, close the drain valve and remove the hose. Open the water inlet valve to refill the tank. Restore power or gas, then check for leaks as the tank heats up. Watch for any drips and make sure everything works as it should.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
