      transcript:
        "Are pests destroying your trees and you\u2019re not sure what to do? In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to safely and effectively control tree pests step by step. \n\nFirst, inspect your trees for signs of trouble\u2014look for holes, chewed leaves, or insects. Take your time, about 20 to 30 minutes, and try to identify the exact pest. This helps you choose the right treatment.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time to treat. Put on your personal protective equipment. Mix your insecticide concentrate as directed, and use a sprayer to cover the affected areas. You can rent spray equipment if you don\u2019t have one. Apply the treatment carefully, following all safety instructions. This step usually takes 45 to 60 minutes for five trees.\n\nAfter a few days, check your trees again. Look for any remaining pests or damage. Remove dead pests and prune any damaged branches. If you still see pests, repeat the treatment. This follow-up takes about 30 to 45 minutes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
