      duration: "PT2M57S",
      contentUrl:
        "https://contractor-plus-website.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/reshub-how-to-vids/concrete-fence-post-installation.mp4",
      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/concrete-fence-post-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want rock-solid fence posts that last for decades? In this video, you'll learn how to install concrete fence posts step by step, from marking your line to setting the posts in concrete. \n\nFirst, measure and mark your fence line. Use stakes and string to keep everything straight. Mark where each post will go, spacing them evenly\u2014usually 6 to 8 feet apart. \n\nNext, grab a post hole digger and dig each hole about 2 feet deep and 10 to 12 inches wide. Add a few inches of gravel at the bottom for drainage. \n\nNow, set your concrete posts in the holes. Use a level to make sure each post is straight and plumb. Mix your ready-mix concrete\u2014one 80-pound bag per hole is typical. Pour the concrete around the post, filling the hole. If you want faster results, add a fast-setting concrete additive. Brace the posts so they stay upright while the concrete sets. \n\nLet the concrete cure for at least 8 hours. Once it's set, remove the braces and check that each post is solid and aligned. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
