      transcript:
        "Want cleaner water straight from your tap in under two hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a point-of-use water filter, step by step. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: the filter unit, two flexible supply lines, a shutoff valve, mounting hardware, Teflon tape, an adjustable wrench, a bucket, and some towels. Clear out the space under your sink so you have room to work.\n\nNext, turn off the cold water supply valve. Place a bucket under the supply line to catch any drips. Use your wrench to disconnect the supply line from the faucet.\n\nNow, mount the filter bracket under the sink. Attach the filter cartridge to the bracket. Wrap Teflon tape around the threads of your fittings to prevent leaks. Connect the inlet and outlet hoses to the filter, following the manufacturer\u2019s instructions. Make sure all fittings are tight and the hoses are aligned properly.\n\nTurn the water supply back on. Flush the filter as recommended by the manufacturer. Check every connection for leaks. Once you\u2019re sure everything\u2019s dry and working, clean up your workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
