      transcript:
        "Did you know a leaking galvanized pipe can waste thousands of gallons of water a year? In this video, you'll learn how to repair a damaged galvanized pipe step by step, so you can stop leaks and protect your home.\n\nFirst, shut off your main water supply. Open a faucet to drain the lines, then clear any obstacles so you can reach the damaged pipe.\n\nNext, use a pipe cutter or reciprocating saw to cut out the bad section. Clean the ends of the remaining pipe\u2014this helps the new connections seal tight.\n\nNow, measure and cut your new galvanized pipe. Apply pipe thread sealant to the threads, then screw on new couplings. Attach the replacement pipe, making sure all fittings are tight. Use pipe hangers or supports to keep everything secure.\n\nFinally, turn the water back on. Check every joint for leaks and make sure water flows smoothly. Tighten any connections if needed.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
