      transcript:
        "Want to avoid costly mistakes when building a fence? Start with a proper fence line survey. In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to survey your fence line step by step, so you get it right the first time.\n\nFirst, gather your documents and tools. You\u2019ll need your property deed, any old surveys, a 100-foot measuring tape, survey stakes, flagging tape, and marking paint. This should take about 30 to 45 minutes.\n\nNext, locate your property corners. Use your documents to find the official boundary markers or monuments. Mark these spots with stakes or flags. Take your time\u2014accuracy here is key. Expect this to take about an hour to an hour and a half.\n\nNow, measure and mark your fence line. Stretch your measuring tape between the corners. Place stakes every 10 to 20 feet, and use string or flagging tape to connect them. Mark the line with paint. Make sure your line follows local rules and doesn\u2019t cross onto a neighbor\u2019s property.\n\nFinally, double-check your work. Measure again, take photos, and write down your findings. This helps with permits and future work. Plan for another 30 to 45 minutes here.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
