        "Want to stop water from pooling around your home\u2019s foundation? Let\u2019s install gutter extensions the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to plan, cut, and install gutter extensions for better drainage. \n\nFirst, assess and prepare your site. Inspect your current gutters, measure where the downspouts are, and clear any debris around the area. Gather all your materials: gutter extension sections, elbows, hangers, screws, adapters, and sealant.\n\nNext, cut your gutter extension pieces to the lengths you need. Attach elbows or connectors as needed, and dry-fit everything to make sure it lines up with your downspouts.\n\nNow, install the extensions. Secure them to the downspouts using screws or brackets. Make sure the extensions direct water away from your foundation\u2014at least 3 to 5 feet is best.\n\nFinally, seal all the joints with caulk or sealant. Test the system by running water through it. Check for leaks and make sure water flows away from your house.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
