        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/window-flashing-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to stop window leaks before they start? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install window flashing the right way, step by step. \n\nFirst, clean and inspect the window opening. Remove all dust and debris, and make sure the surface is dry and damage-free. This is key for a tight seal.\n\nNext, apply self-adhered flashing tape to the sill. Run it up each side a few inches. Press it down firmly\u2014no air bubbles. This keeps water out.\n\nNow, set your window in place. Check that it\u2019s level and plumb. Then, add side flashing tape over the window flanges. Overlap the sill flashing so water drains out, not in.\n\nFinally, install head flashing tape above the window. Overlap the side flashing. Seal all edges and fastener holes with a good polyurethane or silicone sealant. This blocks water from sneaking in.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
