      transcript:
        "Did you know a failed expansion tank can ruin your water heater and cost you big? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace a water heater expansion tank step by step. \n\nFirst, shut off the main water supply and turn off power to your water heater. Open a hot water faucet to relieve pressure, then use the drain valve to let water out of the heater. This takes about 20 to 30 minutes.\n\nNext, use a wrench to disconnect the old expansion tank from the piping. Check the connection for rust or damage. If you see any, clean or replace the fittings before moving on.\n\nNow, wrap plumber\u2019s tape around the threads of the new tank. Attach it to the pipe and tighten it securely. Use dielectric unions if needed to prevent corrosion. Add pipe insulation and a mounting strap for support.\n\nTurn the water and power back on. Check for leaks and make sure everything works right. Always follow your local codes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
