      transcript:
        "Want cleaner, safer water from your well? Here\u2019s how to install a whole house well water filtration system, step by step. \n\nFirst, assess your site. Test your water quality and decide what type of filtration you need. Pick a system that fits your home and check if you need any permits.\n\nNext, get ready for installation. Turn off your well pump and relieve the water pressure. Clear the area where you\u2019ll work. Lay out your filtration system parts and read the instructions.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install. Cut and fit your PVC or PEX pipes. Mount the filtration unit securely. Connect the inlet and outlet lines, using plumber\u2019s tape and sealant to prevent leaks. Add the sediment pre-filter and activated carbon filter cartridges. Install the bypass valve kit so you can service the system later.\n\nOnce everything\u2019s connected, turn the water back on. Check for leaks, flush the system, and test your water quality. Adjust settings if needed.\n\nFinally, clean up the area and show everyone how to maintain the system. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
