      transcript:
        "Want a smooth, durable pool deck that lasts for years? In this video, you'll learn how to install a concrete pool deck step by step, from prep to sealing. \n\nFirst, clear the area around your pool and mark out the deck shape. Remove any debris, then dig down to the right depth. Compact the soil well\u2014this is key for a stable base.\n\nNext, set up your form boards to outline the deck. Use wood or metal forms. Add a 3/4-inch crushed stone gravel base, about 8 tons for 1,000 square feet. Compact it tight. Lay down wire mesh and No. 3 rebar for strength\u2014about 1,000 square feet of mesh and 800 feet of rebar.\n\nNow, pour your 4,000 psi ready-mix concrete\u2014about 12.5 cubic yards. Spread it evenly, screed the surface, and use a float for a smooth finish. Add control joints and texture for slip resistance. Don\u2019t forget expansion joints\u2014about 120 feet for this size deck.\n\nLet the concrete cure for at least two days. Keep it moist and shaded. Once it\u2019s cured, apply a high-quality sealer\u2014about 5 gallons for 1,000 square feet. This protects your deck and keeps it looking great.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
