      transcript:
        "Want to install a gas line for your dryer, but not sure where to start? In this video, I\u2019ll show you the exact steps to safely run a new gas line for a dryer, from planning to leak testing. \n\nFirst, assess your site. Spend about 30 to 45 minutes checking where your dryer will go. Plan the best route for the gas line and make sure you follow your local building codes. Gather all your materials: CSST gas line, shutoff valve, flexible connector, fittings, sealant, and clamps.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time to install. Shut off the main gas supply. Cut and assemble your pipe sections, using approved fittings and Teflon tape or pipe sealant. Securely run about 25 feet of gas line to your dryer spot. Use strapping or clamps to hold the line in place.\n\nNow, connect the gas line to your dryer. Turn the gas back on. Test every connection for leaks with soapy water or a gas detector. If you see bubbles or get a warning, shut off the gas and fix the leak. Only finish when every joint is safe and tight.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
