      transcript:
        "Want to build a strong foundation that lasts? Let\u2019s walk through how to install concrete footings step by step.\n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to prep your site, set forms, reinforce, pour, and finish a concrete footing\u2014so you can do it right the first time.\n\nFirst, mark out your footing layout and clear away any debris. Excavate trenches to the depth and width your local building code requires. This usually takes 2 to 3 hours.\n\nNext, install your form lumber\u20142x6 boards work great. Make sure they\u2019re straight and level. Place No. 4 rebar inside the forms, spaced as your plans call for. Tie the rebar together with tie wire for strength. This step takes about 3 to 4 hours.\n\nNow, pour your ready-mix concrete evenly into the forms. Use a shovel or rod to work out air pockets and make sure the concrete fills every corner. This should take 2 to 3 hours.\n\nFinally, level the surface and smooth the edges. Cover the concrete with plastic or a curing compound to keep in moisture. Let it cure undisturbed for at least 16 hours for best strength.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
