      transcript:
        "Did you know a simple splash block can save your foundation from water damage? Today, I\u2019ll show you exactly how to install gutter splash blocks the right way. First, gather your materials: concrete splash blocks, a couple bags of gravel, a small roll of landscape fabric, gloves, and a level. Walk around your home and find every downspout that needs a splash block. Clear away any leaves or debris so you have a clean spot to work. Next, lay down a small patch of landscape fabric and add a thin layer of gravel where each splash block will go. This helps with drainage and keeps weeds down. Now, place each splash block directly under the downspout. Make sure it slopes away from your house\u2014use your level to check. The goal is to send water away from your foundation. Once all blocks are in place, pour some water through the downspout to test. Watch to see that the water flows off the splash block and away from your home. Adjust if needed. That\u2019s it! If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
