      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a leaking pipe joint without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to repair a pipe joint step by step, so you can save time and money. \n\nFirst, shut off the water supply to the pipe you\u2019re working on. Open a faucet to drain any leftover water, and clear the area so you have room to work safely.\n\nNext, loosen or cut out the damaged joint. Remove any old sealant or debris from the pipe ends. Use pipe primer and cleaner to get the surfaces spotless\u2014this is key for a good seal.\n\nNow, apply pipe joint sealant or tape to the cleaned ends. Fit your new pipe joint coupling and any replacement pipe sections. Tighten the connections, or solder if you\u2019re working with metal pipes. Use pipe clamps or straps to secure everything in place. If you used adhesives, let them cure as the instructions say.\n\nTurn the water back on and check for leaks. That\u2019s it\u2014your pipe joint is repaired!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
