      transcript:
        "A burst water line can flood your home in minutes\u2014do you know what to do? In this video, you'll learn how to handle an emergency water line repair step by step, so you can stop leaks fast and avoid costly damage. \n\nFirst, shut off your main water supply right away. This prevents more flooding and gives you time to assess the damage. Look closely at the pipe to find exactly where the leak is and how much pipe needs replacing.\n\nNext, use a pipe cutter or hacksaw to remove the damaged section. Make sure your cuts are clean and straight, and try not to disturb nearby pipes or fittings.\n\nNow, measure and cut a new piece of copper pipe. Attach it using couplings or press fittings, and use solder and flux if needed. Tighten all connections and add pipe hangers for support. Don\u2019t forget to insulate the new pipe to prevent future problems.\n\nFinally, slowly turn the water back on. Check every joint for leaks and make sure the water pressure is normal. If everything looks good, your repair is done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
