      transcript:
        "Want a smooth, long-lasting concrete walkway? Here\u2019s how to do it right, step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to prep, form, pour, and finish a concrete walkway like a pro.\n\nFirst, mark out your walkway and clear the area. Remove grass, rocks, and dig down about 6 inches. Make sure the ground is level and meets your local code.\n\nNext, set up your forms using 2x4 lumber along the edges. Lay down about 2 tons of gravel base and compact it well. This gives your walkway a solid foundation.\n\nNow, add rebar for strength. Place No. 3 rebar every 2 feet along the walkway. Install expansion joints every 10 feet to prevent cracks.\n\nMix and pour about 3.1 cubic yards of ready-mix concrete for 100 square feet at 4 inches thick. Spread it evenly, level it with a screed, and use an edging tool for clean sides. Finish with a broom for texture so it\u2019s not slippery.\n\nLet the concrete cure for at least 24 hours, keeping it moist if needed. Carefully remove the forms and check for any rough spots. Finally, apply a concrete sealer to protect your new walkway.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
