      transcript:
        "Want a stunning patio that lasts for years? Let\u2019s break down how to install outdoor tile the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn every step to create a beautiful, durable tile patio from start to finish.\n\nFirst, clear your patio area and remove any debris. Make sure the ground is level\u2014this is key for a smooth finish. Compact the soil and add a base layer, like gravel, for drainage.\n\nNext, mix and pour your concrete or mortar base. Use a screed to get it even, then let it partially cure. Check that the surface is flat before moving on.\n\nNow, plan your tile layout. Dry-fit a few tiles to see how they\u2019ll look. Spread polymer-modified thinset mortar, then set your porcelain outdoor tiles in place using spacers. Cut tiles as needed for edges and corners.\n\nOnce the tiles are set, remove the spacers. Mix your outdoor-rated grout and fill the joints. Wipe away extra grout, let it cure, then apply a penetrating sealer to protect your patio from the weather.\n\nFinally, inspect your work, clean the tiles, and dispose of waste properly. Add edge trim for a finished look.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
