      transcript:
        "Want to make your brick or block last longer and look better? Sealing your masonry is easier than you think. In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to seal masonry like a pro.\n\nFirst, clean the surface. Use a stiff brush and mild detergent to scrub away dirt, debris, and loose mortar. Let it dry completely\u2014this is key for a good seal.\n\nNext, inspect for cracks or damaged joints. Fill any small cracks with masonry repair caulk. Let the repairs cure as the product recommends.\n\nNow, protect nearby areas with painter\u2019s tape and plastic sheeting. Pour your masonry sealer into a paint tray. Using a roller or sprayer, apply the sealer evenly. Work in sections and avoid letting the sealer pool up. Make sure you cover every inch.\n\nLet the sealer dry as directed. Once dry, check for missed spots and touch up if needed. That\u2019s it\u2014your masonry is now protected from water and weather!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
