      transcript:
        "Want to install a doorbell that actually works every time you press it? In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to wire a doorbell system from start to finish. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker. Safety first! Find where your transformer will go\u2014usually near your electrical panel or a junction box. Plan the wire route from the doorbell button, to the chime inside, and then to the transformer.\n\nNext, run your doorbell wire. Drill holes if you need to, and fish the 18/2 low-voltage wire through the walls. Use wire staples or clips to keep it neat and secure. Always leave a little extra wire at each spot for easy connections.\n\nNow, connect the wires. Attach them to the doorbell button outside, the chime inside, and the transformer. Use wire connectors for tight, safe joins. Once everything\u2019s hooked up, turn the power back on and test your doorbell. Make sure it rings loud and clear!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
