      duration: "PT2M34S",
      contentUrl:
        "https://contractor-plus-website.s3.us-east-2.amazonaws.com/reshub-how-to-vids/replace-lawn-with-sod.mp4",
      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/replace-lawn-with-sod/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want a lush green lawn\u2014fast? Here\u2019s how to replace your old grass with fresh sod, step by step. \n\nFirst, remove your existing lawn. Use a sod cutter or shovel to clear away all grass, weeds, and debris. Make sure to dispose of everything according to your local rules. This step takes about 8 to 10 hours for 1,000 square feet.\n\nNext, prepare the soil. Loosen it to a depth of 3 to 4 inches. Remove any rocks, then mix in compost or topsoil for healthy roots. Level and grade the area so water drains away from your house. This takes another 6 to 8 hours.\n\nNow, lay your new sod. Stagger the pieces in a brick pattern and press the edges tightly together. Use a roller to make sure the sod touches the soil everywhere. Trim the edges to fit your yard\u2019s shape. This step also takes 8 to 10 hours.\n\nFinally, water the sod right away. Keep it moist for the first two weeks, and avoid walking on it during this time. Plan for 6 to 8 hours of care in the first days.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
