      transcript:
        "Want to install a new thermostat but not sure how to run the wiring? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install thermostat wiring safely and correctly. \n\nFirst, always turn off power to your HVAC system at the breaker. Remove the old thermostat and label each wire by its terminal. This makes reconnecting much easier later.\n\nNext, run your new 18/5 solid copper thermostat wire from the control board to the thermostat location. Use wire staples or clips to secure the wire every few feet, keeping it neat and out of the way. At both ends, connect each wire to the correct terminal\u2014double-check your labels and the wiring diagram.\n\nNow, install a low voltage electrical box if needed, mount your new thermostat, and attach the wires to the matching terminals. Restore power at the breaker, then test your system to make sure everything works\u2014heat, cool, and fan.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
