        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/commercial-demolition/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to demolish a commercial building safely and efficiently? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process and what materials and equipment you'll need for a successful commercial demolition. \n\nFirst, start with a site assessment. Inspect the building, look for hazardous materials like asbestos, and get all the permits required by your local authorities. This usually takes about 10 to 15 hours.\n\nNext, disconnect all utilities\u2014electricity, water, and gas. Set up temporary fencing and dust barriers to keep the site safe and control debris. This prep work takes 8 to 12 hours.\n\nNow, it's time for the main event: structural demolition. Use heavy equipment like a skid steer or excavator to carefully take down the building. Make sure your crew wears proper PPE and follows all safety rules. This step can take 100 to 110 hours for a 5,000 square foot space.\n\nFinally, sort and load the debris into dumpsters, then haul it away for recycling or disposal. Clean up the site to meet local environmental standards. This last step takes about 20 to 25 hours.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
