      transcript:
        "Want to install K-style gutters like a pro and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to install 5-inch K-style aluminum gutters, from prep to final testing. \n\nFirst, set up your ladders and gather all your tools. Measure your roofline to figure out how much gutter and how many downspouts you need. If there are old gutters, remove them now.\n\nNext, cut your K-style gutters to the right lengths. Attach end caps to each end, and use gutter sealant at the seams. Connect sections with connectors, and pre-drill holes for hangers and downspouts.\n\nNow, mount the gutter hangers along the fascia, spacing them about every 5 feet. Make sure the gutters slope slightly toward the downspouts for good drainage. Secure the gutters, then attach the downspouts and elbows. Use screws and sealant to keep everything tight and leak-free.\n\nFinally, flush the gutters with water to check for leaks and make sure water flows to the downspouts. Clean up any debris and dispose of old materials properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
