        "Want perfect grout lines that last? Here\u2019s how to grout tile like a pro. In this video, you\u2019ll learn every step to install grout, from prep to cleanup. \n\nFirst, prep your surface. Clean out all tile joints, remove dust and debris, and make sure tiles are dry and secure. This is key for a strong finish.\n\nNext, mix your grout. Follow the instructions on the bag or tub. Use a rubber grout float to press grout firmly into the joints. Work in small sections so the grout doesn\u2019t dry out too fast.\n\nNow, clean up. After about 10-15 minutes, wipe the tiles with a damp sponge. Rinse the sponge often. Shape the grout lines as you go for a smooth, even look.\n\nLet the grout cure as the manufacturer recommends\u2014usually 24 hours. Then, buff away any haze with a dry cloth. Inspect all joints for gaps or cracks. Once dry, apply grout sealer to protect your work.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
