        "Is your brick walkway uneven or falling apart? Let\u2019s fix it step by step! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair a brick walkway so it looks great and lasts for years. \n\nFirst, inspect your walkway. Look for loose, sunken, or broken bricks. Mark the problem spots, grab your tools, and clear away any debris.\n\nNext, carefully lift out the damaged bricks. Set them aside. Remove the old sand or gravel underneath. Add fresh gravel or sand, then level and compact the base so it\u2019s solid and even.\n\nNow, reset the bricks in their original pattern. Use a rubber mallet to tap each brick into place. Make sure the surface is flat and the joints are tight as you go.\n\nFor the final step, sweep sand into the joints between the bricks. Compact the walkway, add more sand if needed, and sweep again. Clean up the area and dispose of debris properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
