        "Want to know how to install kitchen plumbing like a pro? In this video, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process to get your kitchen water lines, drains, and fixtures set up right. \n\nFirst, shut off the main water supply. Disconnect any old plumbing and clear out the area so you have room to work safely.\n\nNext, install your new supply and drain lines. Use PEX or copper pipes for water, and PVC for drains. Run lines to the sink, dishwasher, and fridge. Secure everything with pipe hangers and supports. Make sure to follow local plumbing codes.\n\nNow, hook up your fixtures. Connect the faucet, garbage disposal, dishwasher, and any other appliances. Use shut-off valves and supply lines for each. Seal all joints with plumber\u2019s putty or sealant. Test for leaks as you go.\n\nFinally, turn the water back on. Check every connection for leaks and make sure the drains work. Clean up your workspace, and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
