      transcript:
        "Did you know a bad underlayment can ruin your whole roof\u2014even if your shingles look fine? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to replace roof underlayment step by step, so your roof stays leak-free and strong. \n\nFirst, strip off all old shingles and underlayment. Use a roofing shovel or pry bar, and toss debris in a dumpster. Check the roof deck for rot or soft spots. Replace any damaged wood\u2014this is key for a solid base.\n\nNext, roll out your new synthetic underlayment. Start at the bottom edge, overlap each row by at least 4 inches, and fasten it with roofing nails. Use roof deck tape on seams for extra protection. Install drip edge along the eaves and rakes to keep water out.\n\nSeal around vents and edges with roofing sealant. Finally, install new shingles or roofing material, making sure everything lines up and is nailed down tight.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
