      transcript:
        "Is your deck feeling bouncy or unsafe? You might have damaged joists hiding underneath. In this video, I\u2019ll show you how to repair deck joists step by step, so your deck is safe and strong again. \n\nFirst, inspect all the joists under your deck for rot, cracks, or insect damage. Remove any decking boards in the way and clear the area. Gather your materials: pressure-treated joists, galvanized joist hangers, structural screws, construction adhesive, and deck flashing tape.\n\nNext, carefully remove the damaged joists using a pry bar and saw. Clean and level the support area. Check for any other hidden issues before moving on.\n\nNow, cut your new joists to the right length. Treat the cut ends with wood preservative to prevent future rot. Install the new joists using galvanized hangers and structural screws. Make sure each joist is spaced and aligned according to your local building codes. Use construction adhesive for extra strength, and apply flashing tape to protect against moisture.\n\nFinally, reinstall the decking boards, fastening them securely. Inspect the whole deck for stability and safety. Clean up your work area and dispose of debris properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
