      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely repair a damaged stone lintel and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to replace or repair a stone lintel like a pro. \n\nFirst, set up your work area. Use scaffolding or ladders for safe access. Clear the space and put on your safety gear. Protect nearby surfaces and always follow your local safety rules.\n\nNext, remove the damaged material. Carefully chip away loose mortar and any broken stone with a hammer and chisel. Before you go further, use temporary supports to hold up the structure above the lintel. This is critical for safety and required by building codes.\n\nNow, it's time for the stone repair or replacement. Cut and fit your new stone lintel, or patch the old one with a compatible material. Set the lintel in place, making sure it's level and well-supported. Use steel reinforcement bars if needed, following your local guidelines.\n\nFinish up by repointing the joints. Mix fresh mortar and fill the gaps around the lintel. Tool the joints for a clean look, wipe away excess, and let it cure. Inspect your work to make sure it meets code.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
