      transcript:
        "Want cleaner water fast? Here\u2019s how to replace your reverse osmosis system like a pro. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the exact steps to remove your old system and install a new 5-stage reverse osmosis filter under your sink.\n\nFirst, shut off the water supply and open the faucet to relieve pressure. Disconnect all tubing and fittings. Carefully remove the old system from under the sink.\n\nNext, mount the new filter assembly in place. Use the included hardware and make sure it\u2019s secure. Connect the flexible supply tubing to the feed water adapter or valve. Attach the drain saddle valve to your drain line. Wrap threaded fittings with Teflon tape to prevent leaks.\n\nInstall the storage tank and the new faucet, following the manufacturer\u2019s instructions. Double-check all connections.\n\nNow, turn the water supply back on. Flush the system as recommended\u2014usually by running water through it for several minutes. Check for leaks at every connection. Finally, test the water flow and taste to make sure everything works perfectly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
