        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/install-sink-plumbing/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to install sink plumbing without calling a pro? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to hook up a new sink, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: a sink drain assembly, P-trap kit, two supply lines, two shutoff valves, pipe fittings, and plumber\u2019s putty or Teflon tape. Shut off the water supply and clear your workspace. Lay out all your tools and parts so you\u2019re ready to go.\n\nNext, install the drain and faucet. Place plumber\u2019s putty under the drain flange, insert it into the sink, and tighten the drain assembly from below. Make sure all gaskets and washers are in place for a watertight seal. Then, mount the faucet according to the manufacturer\u2019s instructions.\n\nNow, connect the water supply. Attach the shutoff valves to the water lines, then connect the hot and cold supply lines from the valves to the faucet. Use Teflon tape on threaded connections to prevent leaks. Install the P-trap under the sink, connecting it to the drain and the wall pipe. Tighten all fittings by hand, then snug them with pliers.\n\nTurn the water back on and check for leaks. Run both hot and cold water, and inspect every connection. Tighten as needed. If everything\u2019s dry, you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
