      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to mark out an easement on your property the right way? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process for a professional easement survey, from paperwork to final map. \n\nFirst, gather all your property documents\u2014deeds, plats, and any old surveys. Review them carefully to spot any existing easements or legal notes about your land.\n\nNext, head out to the site. Use surveyor stakes and flags to mark property lines and the easement area. Bring a can of marking paint to highlight boundaries. Take careful measurements and record all the details you\u2019ll need for your map.\n\nBack at your desk, draft a clear survey map showing the property lines and the easement. Print out a set for your records. Write a short report that explains your findings and confirms you followed local rules.\n\nFor a typical one-acre survey, plan on about eight hours of work and materials like stakes, flags, paint, and map printing.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
