      transcript:
        "Did you know a cracked foundation can threaten your whole house? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to repair foundation masonry step by step, so you can protect your home or job site. \n\nFirst, clear the work area and remove any debris. Inspect the foundation for cracks or damage, and mark all the spots that need repair. Safety first\u2014wear gloves and eye protection.\n\nNext, use a wire brush and chisel to clean out cracks and old mortar. Get rid of all loose material and dust. This helps the new mortar stick well.\n\nNow, mix Type N masonry mortar as the bag says. Use a trowel to fill cracks and gaps, smoothing the surface for a clean finish. For bigger repairs, set new concrete blocks and add rebar for strength. Don\u2019t forget to use a bonding agent for better adhesion.\n\nLet the mortar cure as recommended. If needed, install steel bars or mesh to reinforce the repair. Once cured, apply a waterproofing sealant to protect against moisture.\n\nFinally, inspect your work for stability. Clean up all tools and debris. Your foundation should now be solid and safe.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
