        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/brick-facade-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a damaged brick facade and make it look brand new? Today, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process to repair a brick facade, from prep to cleanup, so you can do it right the first time.\n\nFirst, get your materials ready: replacement bricks, Type N mortar mix, masonry cleaner, backer rod, and brick ties. For a 100 square foot area, you\u2019ll need about 100 bricks, 4 bags of mortar, and the rest as listed.\n\nStart with surface preparation. Clean the brick face with masonry cleaner, remove any loose mortar, and check for damaged bricks. Set up safety barriers and gather your tools.\n\nNext, carefully chisel out the old, crumbling mortar and any broken bricks. Take your time\u2014don\u2019t damage the good bricks around them.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to install new bricks. Mix fresh mortar, set the bricks in place, and use a backer rod if needed for wide joints. Repoint the joints to match the existing pattern. Make sure everything lines up and looks even.\n\nLet the mortar cure. Mist the joints if needed to help it set. Clean off any extra mortar from the brick faces. Finally, clear away debris and take down your safety barriers.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
