      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to fix a damaged brick arch and make it look brand new? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair a brick arch the right way. \n\nFirst, inspect the arch for cracks, loose bricks, or crumbling mortar. Use a chisel and brush to remove any loose material. Clean the area well\u2014this helps the new mortar stick.\n\nNext, carefully take out any damaged bricks. Mix up Type N mortar until it\u2019s smooth. Set your new face bricks in place, matching the pattern of the old arch. Use brick ties and a steel lintel for extra support if needed. Fill the joints with fresh mortar, shaping it to match the original look.\n\nLet the mortar cure for several hours. Mist the area with water if it\u2019s hot or dry to prevent cracking. Once cured, clean off any extra mortar from the brick faces. Finally, check the arch for strength and apply a masonry sealer to protect your work.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
