      transcript:
        "Want to know how to install an oil heater safely and efficiently? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to install an oil-fired heater system, from start to finish.\n\nFirst, assess your site. Check your heating needs, pick a safe spot, and make sure there's enough ventilation and clearance. This keeps your installation up to code and safe.\n\nNext, mount the oil heater. Use sturdy brackets or stands, and double-check that everything is stable and level in your chosen area.\n\nNow, connect the fuel line and electrical wiring. Run copper fuel lines from the oil tank to the heater, install shutoff valves, and make all electrical connections. Test for leaks and make sure everything meets local codes.\n\nAfter that, it's time to test and calibrate. Prime the system, start the heater, and watch it run. Adjust the thermostat and safety controls for the best performance.\n\nFinally, do a full inspection. Check all connections, make sure the system runs safely, give the user instructions, and clean up the workspace.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
