      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/garbage-disposal-leak-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is water leaking under your sink from the garbage disposal? Let\u2019s fix it fast and stop the mess! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to find and repair a garbage disposal leak step by step.\n\nFirst, unplug the disposal for safety. Clear out everything under the sink so you can see all the parts. Use a flashlight to check where the leak is coming from\u2014look at the top flange, the side connections, and the bottom of the unit.\n\nIf you see water around the sink flange, tighten the mounting bolts. If the leak is at a pipe joint, tighten the hose clamps or connections. For worn gaskets or old plumber\u2019s putty, remove the old material and replace it with new plumber\u2019s putty or a fresh gasket kit. If the drain pipe is cracked, swap it out for a new one.\n\nOnce everything is tight and replaced, plug the disposal back in. Run water and turn on the unit. Watch closely for any leaks. If it\u2019s dry, you\u2019re done! Clean up the area and put your items back.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
