      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/roof-deck-replacement/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your roof deck rotting or sagging? Here\u2019s how to replace it step by step. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to safely remove and replace a roof deck, what materials you\u2019ll need, and how long each step takes.\n\nFirst, strip off all old roofing and damaged decking. This usually takes 8 to 10 hours. Make sure to follow your local rules for debris disposal and check the structure underneath for any hidden damage.\n\nNext, repair or replace any bad rafters or joists. The framing must be solid and level. Clean the area so it\u2019s ready for new decking. This step takes about 6 to 8 hours.\n\nNow, install your new CDX plywood panels. Stagger the seams for strength and fasten them down with roofing nails and construction adhesive. Check that everything lines up and meets your local building codes. This part takes 10 to 12 hours.\n\nAfter that, roll out roofing felt underlayment and install drip edge flashing at all edges and joints. Seal everything well to keep water out. Plan for 6 to 8 hours here.\n\nFinally, inspect your work, clean up all waste, and make sure everything passes code before you start installing new shingles. This last step takes 2 to 3 hours.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
