      transcript:
        "Want to make your kitchen cabinets open and close like new? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install concealed cabinet hinges step by step. \n\nFirst, remove the old cabinet doors and hinges. Use a screwdriver to unscrew each hinge. Label each door so you know where it goes later. Clean the cabinet frames and doors to get rid of dust and grease.\n\nNext, mark where your new hinges will go. Measure carefully on both the cabinet frame and the door. Use a pencil to mark the spots. Drill pilot holes for the screws. If your hinges need a cup hole, use a drill bit made for hinge cups.\n\nNow, attach the new hinges to the doors. Line up the hinges with your marks and screw them in. Then, hold the door in place and screw the other side of the hinge to the cabinet frame. Repeat for each door.\n\nFinally, adjust the hinges so the doors hang straight and open smoothly. Test each door to make sure it works right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
