      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to patch a tile floor so it looks brand new? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to patch up to 10 tiles, step by step, with pro results. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: replacement tiles, thinset mortar, grout, tile spacers, and sealer. You\u2019ll also need basic tools like a chisel, trowel, sponge, and bucket.\n\nStart with surface preparation. Remove the damaged tiles using a chisel. Scrape away all old adhesive until the area is smooth and dry. This step takes about 30 to 45 minutes but is key for a strong patch.\n\nNext, it\u2019s time for tile installation. Spread a thin layer of thinset mortar on the patch area. Place your new tiles, using spacers to keep them even. Press each tile firmly and wipe away any extra mortar. This part should take about an hour.\n\nOnce the mortar sets, move on to grouting and finishing. Fill the gaps with grout, then wipe the tiles clean with a damp sponge. Let everything dry, then check that your patch matches the rest of the floor. For extra protection, apply a sealer.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve patched your tile floor like a pro. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
