      transcript:
        "Want a stone floor that looks amazing and lasts for years? Let\u2019s break down exactly how to install a stone floor, step by step. \n\nFirst, clear out your space. Remove old flooring, clean the subfloor, and make sure it\u2019s level and dry. This is key for a smooth install.\n\nNext, plan your layout. Dry fit your stone tiles, making cuts as needed so everything fits perfectly. Take your time here\u2014good planning means fewer mistakes.\n\nNow, mix your thinset mortar and spread it evenly. Set each stone tile in place, using spacers for even joints. Work in small sections so the mortar doesn\u2019t dry out. Let the tiles cure as recommended.\n\nOnce the tiles are set, it\u2019s time to grout. Press grout into the joints, then wipe away the extra with a damp sponge. Clean the stone surface well to avoid haze.\n\nFinally, apply a stone sealer to protect your floor. Inspect your work, fix any issues, and let the floor cure fully before regular use.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
