      transcript:
        "Want to save money and boost comfort by replacing old windows? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to replace ten old windows with new, energy-efficient ones. \n\nFirst, clear the area and remove any blinds or curtains. Carefully measure each window opening\u2014accurate sizing is key for a good fit. \n\nNext, pry off the trim and cut through any old caulk. Gently remove the old windows. Check the framing and sills for damage, and repair anything you find before moving on.\n\nNow, install your new vinyl replacement windows. Place each window in the opening, use shims to level it, and secure it with screws. Fill any gaps with window insulation foam. Make sure each window opens and closes smoothly, and check for a tight seal.\n\nFinish by applying exterior and interior caulk around the frames. Reinstall the trim, and touch up paint or stain as needed. Double-check that all seals are tight for maximum energy savings.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
