      transcript:
        "Did you know a few damaged shower tiles can lead to big water problems? In this video, you'll learn how to repair shower tiles step by step, so your bathroom stays safe and looks great. \n\nFirst, remove the cracked or loose tiles. Use a chisel and hammer to carefully chip them out. Clean away all the old adhesive and grout so the surface is smooth.\n\nNext, check the exposed area for water damage or mold. If you find any, dry it out or repair it before moving on. Then, apply a waterproof membrane patch to protect the wall from future leaks.\n\nNow, it's time to install the new tiles. Spread thinset mortar on the wall, press your replacement tiles into place, and use spacers to keep the gaps even. Let the tiles set as the manufacturer recommends.\n\nOnce the tiles are set, fill the joints with grout. Wipe away any extra grout with a damp sponge. After the grout cures, apply a grout sealer to keep out moisture and stains.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
