      transcript:
        "Is your bathtub leaking and you\u2019re not sure where to start? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to find and fix a bathtub leak, so you can stop water damage fast. \n\nFirst, find the source of the leak. Check around the tub, faucet, drain, and even the floor nearby. Look for wet spots, cracks, or old, peeling caulk. Mark any problem areas you see.\n\nNext, turn off the water supply. Remove any old caulk or damaged drain parts. If the drain assembly or gasket is worn out, swap it for a new one. Use plumber\u2019s putty or silicone caulk to seal around the drain and any cracks. If you spot a leaky pipe, you may need to replace a section of PVC pipe and fittings. If you can\u2019t reach the pipes, consider installing an access panel for future repairs.\n\nLet the sealant dry as recommended. Then, turn the water back on and run the tub. Watch closely for leaks. If it\u2019s dry, clean up your tools and make sure the area is safe to use.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
