      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/concrete-basketball-court-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to build your own concrete basketball court? Here\u2019s how to do it step by step, from start to finish.\n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to plan, prep, and pour a pro-style basketball court in your backyard or for your next project.\n\nFirst, clear and level your site. Mark out the court boundaries\u2014standard is 30 by 50 feet. Set up sturdy form boards around the edges to hold the concrete in place.\n\nNext, dig down about 8 inches. Compact the soil, then add a 4-inch layer of gravel. This helps with drainage and keeps your slab stable. Use about 8 tons of gravel for a full-size court.\n\nLay out your rebar grid\u2014No. 3 rebar, spaced evenly, about 600 linear feet total. This gives your slab strength and helps prevent cracks.\n\nNow, pour your ready-mix concrete. You\u2019ll need about 15 cubic yards for a 4-inch thick slab. Spread it out, screed it level, and finish the surface with a broom or trowel for grip. Don\u2019t forget to add expansion joints every 10 feet to control cracking.\n\nLet the concrete cure for at least 24 hours. Protect it from rain and sun. Once cured, paint your court lines with durable striping paint\u2014about 2 gallons should do it. Finally, install your basketball hoop system.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve got a solid, long-lasting basketball court ready for action.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
