        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/roof-storm-damage-replacement/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Did a storm wreck your roof? Here\u2019s how to replace it step by step. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to assess storm damage, gather materials, and install a new roof the right way.\n\nFirst, inspect your roof for damage. Look for missing shingles, leaks, or soft spots. Take photos and note what needs replacing.\n\nNext, get your materials. You\u2019ll need asphalt shingles, underlayment, nails, drip edge, ice and water shield, sealant, plywood for decking, ridge cap shingles, flashing, and a dumpster for debris. Make sure you have enough for your roof size\u2014usually measured per 1,000 square feet.\n\nPrepare the site. Remove any debris and set up safety gear. Secure permits if your area requires them.\n\nNow, strip off the old roof. Remove damaged shingles, underlayment, and flashing. Clear everything down to the decking.\n\nInstall new underlayment and ice and water shield. Lay down the drip edge, then start installing shingles from the bottom up. Add flashing around chimneys and vents. Finish with ridge cap shingles and sealant for a watertight finish.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Make sure everything is secure and meets local codes. Clean up all debris and check for leftover nails.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
