      transcript:
        "Is your drip irrigation system wasting water or not working right? In this video, you'll learn how to repair a basic drip irrigation system step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the water supply. Walk along your drip lines and look for leaks, clogs, or broken emitters. Mark any spots that need fixing.\n\nNext, cut out any damaged tubing with sharp scissors or a tubing cutter. Replace faulty emitters, connectors, or couplings. Use barbed fittings to join new tubing sections. Plug any unused holes with goof plugs. If your filter or pressure regulator looks dirty or worn, swap them out for new ones. Wrap threaded connections with Teflon tape to prevent leaks.\n\nNow, turn the water back on. Watch for leaks and make sure water flows evenly from each emitter. Adjust or flush emitters as needed for even coverage.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
