      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to replace a toilet tank without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a new toilet tank step by step, saving you time and money. \n\nFirst, gather your tools and materials: a new toilet tank, tank-to-bowl gasket kit, tank bolts and washers, a water supply line, plumber\u2019s putty or sealant, an adjustable wrench, and a towel. Make sure your new tank matches your toilet model.\n\nNext, turn off the water supply valve behind the toilet. Flush to empty the old tank, then disconnect the water supply line. Use your wrench to remove the bolts holding the tank to the bowl. Carefully lift the old tank off and set it aside.\n\nNow, place the new gasket on the flush valve opening of your new tank. Set the tank onto the bowl, lining up the bolt holes. Insert the new bolts and washers, then tighten them evenly\u2014don\u2019t overtighten, or you could crack the porcelain.\n\nReconnect the water supply line and hand-tighten the fittings. Turn the water back on and let the tank fill. Check for leaks around the bolts and connections. Adjust the fill valve if needed so the water stops at the right level.\n\nThat\u2019s it! You\u2019ve installed a new toilet tank. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
