        "Want a stunning stone patio that lasts for years? Here\u2019s how to build one step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn exactly how to install a stone patio, from prep to finishing touches. \n\nFirst, mark your patio boundaries and clear the area. Remove grass, debris, and dig down about 6-8 inches. Make sure the ground is level and slopes away from your house for drainage.\n\nNext, lay down a weed barrier fabric to stop weeds from growing up through your patio. Spread a 4-inch layer of gravel base, then compact it well. Add a 1-inch layer of sand on top and compact again for a smooth, stable surface.\n\nNow, start laying your stone pavers in your chosen pattern. Fit them tightly together, and use a rubber mallet to tap them level. Cut stones as needed to fit the edges. Install edging restraints around the patio to keep everything in place.\n\nFinally, sweep polymeric sand into the joints between stones. Compact the surface one last time, then rinse off any extra sand. Inspect your work and clean up the area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
