        "Want your spa to feel brand new every time you use it? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to do a full spa maintenance service, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the power to your spa. Inspect the shell, jets, and all components for any damage or buildup. Then, drain all the water completely. This takes about 20 to 30 minutes.\n\nNext, scrub the spa surfaces with a surface cleaner. Clean the jets and remove any debris. Take out the filter, rinse it well, and use a filter cleaner. If the filter looks worn out, replace it with a new one. This cleaning step should take 40 to 50 minutes.\n\nNow, refill your spa with fresh water. Turn the power back on. Use a water test kit to check the pH and sanitizer levels. Add chlorine or bromine, pH increaser or decreaser, and shock treatment as needed. Make sure the water is balanced and safe before you use the spa. This last step takes about 30 to 40 minutes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
