        "Is your garbage disposal making strange noises or just not working? In this video, you'll learn how to troubleshoot and fix common garbage disposal problems, step by step. \n\nFirst, always turn off the power at the breaker before you start. Safety first! Grab a flashlight and look under your sink for any obvious blockages or leaks around the disposal unit.\n\nNext, use a hex wrench or disposal tool to turn the disposal from underneath. This can help free up any jams. Remove any debris you find inside the chamber. Then, press the reset button on the bottom of the unit to reset the motor.\n\nNow, turn the power back on. Run some water and test the disposal. Watch and listen for leaks or odd sounds. If you see any leaks, tighten the connections under the sink. Make sure everything is working safely before you finish.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
