      transcript:
        "Want to know how to install a propane heating system safely and efficiently? In this video, I\u2019ll show you the step-by-step process, from planning to final walkthrough. \n\nFirst, assess your site. Figure out your heating needs, pick the right size furnace and tank, and make sure you have enough space and ventilation. Clear the area and get any permits you need.\n\nNext, place your 500-gallon propane tank on a solid concrete pad. Follow all safety codes for distance and clearance. Attach the propane regulator and connect the copper gas line to your building. Double-check all fittings for a tight, secure fit.\n\nNow, install the furnace. Connect the propane lines, set up the venting kit, and wire in the thermostat. Use flexible gas connectors and pipe fittings to make sure everything is sealed and supported.\n\nBefore you fire it up, pressure test the gas lines and check for leaks. Adjust the system for best performance and make sure it meets local safety standards.\n\nFinally, walk through the system with the homeowner. Show how to use it, review safety tips, and clean up the site. Hand over all documentation and answer any questions.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
