        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/sediment-filter-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want cleaner water and fewer plumbing problems? Installing a sediment filter is easier than you think. In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to install a sediment filter on your main water line. \n\nFirst, gather your materials: a sediment filter housing, filter cartridge, mounting bracket with screws, plumbing fittings, and Teflon tape. You\u2019ll also need basic tools like wrenches and a bucket. \n\nStart by shutting off your main water supply. Open a faucet to relieve any pressure in the line. Next, mark where you want to install the filter. Cut the main water pipe at that spot. Fit the filter housing in place, making sure the flow arrow matches your water direction. Use Teflon tape on all threaded connections to prevent leaks. Secure the housing with the mounting bracket and screws. \n\nNow, connect the plumbing fittings. Double-check everything is tight. Turn the water supply back on slowly and check for leaks. Finally, flush the filter as the manufacturer recommends to clear out any debris. Once the water runs clear, you\u2019re done! \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
