      transcript:
        "Is your thermostat completely dead and your home stuck at the wrong temperature? In this video, you'll learn how to troubleshoot and fix a thermostat that won't turn on. \n\nFirst, check if your thermostat has power. Look for a blank display. Head to your electrical panel and make sure the HVAC circuit breaker isn't tripped. Flip it off and back on if needed.\n\nNext, check the thermostat settings. Make sure it's set to heat or cool, and the temperature is right. If your thermostat uses batteries, swap them out for fresh ones. Sometimes, dead batteries are the only problem.\n\nIf it still won't turn on, it's time to check the wiring. Turn off power at the breaker. Remove the thermostat cover. Look for any loose or disconnected wires. Tighten them with a screwdriver and use wire connectors if needed. Put the cover back on, restore power, and test the thermostat.\n\nIf none of these steps work, you may need a replacement thermostat or new wiring. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
