      transcript:
        "Want to install concrete curbing that lasts for years? In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to do it right, from prep to finish. \n\nFirst, mark out your curbing line and clear away grass or debris. Dig a shallow trench along the edge, making sure the base is level and packed down tight. \n\nNext, set up your forms using 2x4 lumber. Secure them well so they don\u2019t move. Lay in your rebar for strength\u2014space it evenly along the trench. \n\nNow, mix your concrete to a thick, workable consistency. Pour it into the forms, filling them all the way. Use a trowel to shape and smooth the top, keeping everything even. \n\nAdd finishing touches like edging or texture. Cover the curbing to keep it moist and let it cure for a few days\u2014this is key for strength. \n\nOnce the concrete sets, carefully remove the forms. Check for any rough spots and clean up the area. Dispose of waste properly. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
