      transcript:
        "Clogged gutters can cause big water damage\u2014let\u2019s stop that today! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to flush your gutters step by step, the right way. \n\nFirst, gather your tools: a sturdy ladder, gloves, a gutter scoop, a hose with a spray nozzle, and safety goggles. Set up your ladder on solid ground and put on your safety gear before you start.\n\nNext, remove all the leaves and debris from your gutters by hand or with the scoop. Drop the mess into trash bags or onto a tarp for easy cleanup.\n\nNow, grab your hose and flush water through the gutters and downspouts. Watch for any slow spots\u2014these mean clogs. If you find a blockage, clear it out until water flows freely.\n\nFinally, inspect your gutters for leaks, sagging, or loose fasteners. Make a note of any repairs you need to keep your gutters working right.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
