      transcript:
        "Want to get a smooth, pro-level paint job? It all starts with the right primer application. In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to prep, protect, and prime any room like a pro. \n\nFirst, prep your surfaces. Clean off dust, grease, and loose paint. Patch any holes and sand rough spots. Make sure everything is dry before you start priming.\n\nNext, protect your space. Lay down drop cloths to cover the floors. Use painter\u2019s tape to mask off trim, outlets, and fixtures. This keeps primer splatters off the things you don\u2019t want to paint.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to prime. Stir your primer well. Use a brush for corners and edges, and a roller for big areas. Apply the primer evenly. If the surface needs it, let the first coat dry, then add a second coat.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Look for missed spots or thin areas. Touch up as needed for a solid, even finish.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
