      transcript:
        "Want to replace your old baseboard heater without calling an electrician? Watch this! In this video, you'll learn how to safely remove an old electric baseboard heater and install a new one, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker box. Double-check with a voltage tester to make sure the power is off. Unscrew the old heater from the wall and disconnect the wires. Remove the old unit and set it aside.\n\nNext, inspect the wiring. If the wires look damaged, replace them with new 12/2 NM-B electrical cable. Attach the new heater's mounting brackets to the wall, making sure they're level and secure. Mount the new baseboard heater onto the brackets.\n\nNow, connect the wires using wire connectors and wire nuts, following the manufacturer's instructions. Double-check all connections. Restore power at the breaker and test the heater to make sure it works. Finally, clean up your workspace and dispose of the old heater according to your local rules.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
