      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/fan-balancing-service/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Is your ceiling fan wobbling or making noise? Let\u2019s fix that with a simple fan balancing service! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to balance a ceiling fan step by step, so it runs smooth and quiet. \n\nFirst, turn off the power to your fan. Safety comes first! Inspect the blades and mounting hardware for any loose screws or damage. Use a microfiber cloth and cleaning solution to wipe away dust and debris from the blades and motor housing.\n\nNext, grab a balancing weights kit. Turn the fan blades by hand and look for any that seem out of line. Use the kit to test each blade\u2014attach the test weight to different blades and run the fan to see which one reduces the wobble. Once you find the unbalanced blade, attach the permanent weight as directed in the kit. Adjust the blade positions if needed, making sure they\u2019re all tight and even.\n\nNow, restore power and run the fan at different speeds. Watch and listen for any wobbling or noise. If needed, make small adjustments until the fan spins smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
