        "Want to install a dishwasher water line without calling a plumber? Watch this! In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to connect a new water line to your dishwasher, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off your main water supply. Unplug the dishwasher and clear out the space under your sink so you can reach the plumbing. \n\nNext, install the water supply line. Attach a 6-foot braided stainless steel line to the hot water valve. Use Teflon tape or pipe thread sealant on the threads to prevent leaks. Add a tee fitting if you need to split the water line. Connect the other end of the line to the dishwasher\u2019s water inlet. Make sure all connections are tight. \n\nNow, turn the water supply back on. Check every connection for leaks. Plug in the dishwasher and run a short cycle to make sure everything works and there are no drips. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
