      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely replace your main circuit breaker without calling an electrician? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to swap out a main breaker and get your power back on fast.\n\nFirst, you\u2019ll learn how to power down your panel and prep for safety. Always shut off all branch circuit breakers first. Then, double-check that the main power is off\u2014use a voltage tester to be sure. Wear insulated gloves and safety glasses. Confirm the electrical service is fully disconnected before you touch anything inside the panel.\n\nNext, open the panel cover. Carefully disconnect the wires from the old main breaker. Take your time\u2014these wires are thick and can be tough to handle. Remove the old breaker and inspect the panel and bus bars for any signs of damage or corrosion. If you see anything wrong, stop and call a pro.\n\nNow, install your new 200-amp main breaker. Connect the wires securely using new wire connectors and copper wire if needed. Make sure everything is tight and safe. Replace the panel cover, restore power, and test all your circuits. Check that everything works and meets your local electrical codes.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
