      transcript:
        "Ever wondered what it really takes to safely replace a gas line? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to remove and install a new gas line, including the materials and safety checks you need. \n\nFirst, always shut off the main gas supply and ventilate your workspace. Make sure all appliances are off and gather your tools and safety gear. \n\nNext, disconnect the old gas line. Carefully remove it, checking for any corrosion or damage. Clean the threads and prep your connection points. \n\nNow, measure and cut your new black iron gas pipe. Use pipe thread sealant on all connections. Assemble the pipes with elbows, tees, and couplings as needed. Secure everything with pipe hangers or straps, and install new shutoff valves and flexible connectors. Tighten all fittings to code. \n\nBefore turning the gas back on, do a pressure test to check for leaks. Then, have your work inspected as required by local rules. Only restore gas service after passing inspection. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
