      transcript:
        "Want to add style and light to your walls in under two hours? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a wall sconce safely and easily, step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the power at your breaker. Use a stud finder to locate studs and mark where you want your sconce. Standard height is about 60 inches from the floor, but adjust for your space.\n\nNext, cut an opening for the electrical box at your mark. Run Romex 14/2 wire from your power source to the box. Secure the box to the wall, making sure it\u2019s flush and tight.\n\nNow, attach the mounting bracket to the box. Connect the fixture wires to the house wires\u2014black to black, white to white, and ground to ground\u2014using wire nuts. Tuck the wires in and secure the sconce to the bracket.\n\nTurn the power back on at the breaker. Test your sconce. If it works, install the bulb and shade. Clean up your work area, and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
