        "Ever wondered how to safely install a garbage disposal switch in your kitchen? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to do it right, from start to finish. \n\nFirst, always turn off the power at your breaker panel. Double-check there\u2019s no electricity at the disposal before you start. Gather your tools and materials: a single pole switch, cover plate, electrical box, 14/2 NM wire, and wire connectors.\n\nNext, pick a spot for your switch. Cut an opening in the wall and mount the electrical box securely. Make sure it\u2019s up to your local building codes.\n\nNow, run the electrical wire from your power source to the switch, then from the switch to the disposal. Connect the wires: black to black, white to white, and ground to ground. Use wire connectors and follow all safety guidelines.\n\nOnce everything\u2019s connected, put on the cover plate. Turn the power back on and test the switch. Make sure the disposal turns on and off as it should. Clean up your workspace and double-check all connections are tight and safe.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
