        "Tired of waiting forever for hot water at your faucet? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a water heater recirculation pump, so you get hot water fast and save water every day. \n\nFirst, turn off the power or gas to your water heater. Close the water supply valve, then drain a little water from the tank to relieve pressure. Safety first!\n\nNext, mount the recirculation pump to the hot water outlet on your heater. Use flexible water connectors and install a check valve to prevent backflow\u2014this is required by most local codes. Wrap threads with Teflon tape and use pipe sealant for leak-free joints.\n\nNow, connect the return line or install the under-sink bypass valve, depending on your system. Reopen the water supply and restore power or gas. Set the timer or sensor on your pump to match your household\u2019s hot water needs.\n\nFinally, check every connection for leaks. Turn on a hot water tap and make sure the pump works and hot water arrives quickly. Clean up your workspace and dispose of any old parts or packaging properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
