      transcript:
        "Want to make your floors look stunning with marble tile? Here\u2019s how to install marble tile like a pro, step by step.\n\nFirst, get your materials: marble tiles, thinset mortar, tile spacers, grout, sealer, and backer board. For 100 square feet, you\u2019ll need about 100 sq ft of tile, 3 bags of mortar, 1 bag of spacers, 2 bags of grout, 1 quart of sealer, and 7 sheets of backer board.\n\nStart with surface preparation. Remove old flooring, clean, and level the subfloor. Make sure it\u2019s dry and free of debris.\n\nNext, plan your layout. Mark reference lines and dry fit the tiles. This helps you avoid small, awkward cuts at the edges.\n\nNow, mix your thinset mortar. Spread it evenly with a notched trowel. Set each marble tile in place, using spacers for even gaps. Cut tiles as needed for edges and corners.\n\nLet the mortar cure. Then, apply grout between the tiles. Wipe off excess grout and clean the tile surfaces.\n\nFinally, seal the marble and grout to protect your new floor. Inspect for any issues and make sure everything looks perfect.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
