      transcript:
        "Did you know a leaky roof valley can ruin your whole roof fast? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to repair a roof valley step by step, so you can stop leaks and protect your home. \n\nFirst, inspect the valley for damaged shingles, flashing, or debris. Make sure the area is safe, and gather your tools and materials: galvanized steel valley flashing, roofing underlayment, nails, asphalt shingles, and roofing cement.\n\nNext, carefully remove old shingles, nails, and any damaged flashing from the valley. Clean out all debris so you have a solid base for repairs.\n\nNow, cut and fit new metal flashing into the valley. Secure it with roofing nails, making sure each piece overlaps the next for proper water flow.\n\nAfter that, install new shingles over the flashing. Line them up with the existing rows. Seal all edges and nail heads with roofing cement to keep water out.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Make sure everything is watertight, then clean up the area and remove all debris.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
