      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to replace your garbage disposal without calling a plumber? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to swap out your old garbage disposal and hook up the plumbing, step by step. \n\nFirst, unplug the old disposal and disconnect the drain lines under your sink. Remove the mounting assembly and carefully take out the old unit. \n\nNext, mount your new disposal. Use plumber\u2019s putty to seal the flange, then secure the mounting ring. Attach the discharge tube and, if you have a dishwasher, connect the inlet. Use PVC drain pipes, elbows, and couplings to line up the plumbing. Tighten everything with hose clamps and make sure to use Teflon tape on threaded joints for a leak-free fit. Install the rubber gasket kit where needed.\n\nNow, restore power. Run water and turn on the disposal. Check every joint and seal for leaks. Make sure the unit runs smoothly and quietly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
