        "Did you know sediment buildup can ruin your water heater and spike your energy bills? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to remove sediment from your water heater step by step. \n\nFirst, turn off the power to your water heater. If it\u2019s electric, switch off the breaker. For gas, set the thermostat to 'pilot.' Next, close the cold water inlet valve on top of the tank. This keeps things safe while you work.\n\nNow, grab a hose and connect it to the drain valve at the bottom of the tank. Run the other end to a floor drain or outside. Open the drain valve and let the water flow out. Be careful\u2014the water can be hot! Once the tank is empty, briefly open the cold water valve to flush out any leftover sediment. Keep flushing until the water runs clear.\n\nWhen you\u2019re done, close the drain valve and remove the hose. Open the cold water inlet to refill the tank. Once it\u2019s full, restore power or turn the gas back on. Check for leaks around the drain valve. That\u2019s it\u2014your water heater is clean and ready to go!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
