      transcript:
        "Is your main drain backing up or leaking? Here\u2019s how to repair it step by step. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to assess, repair, and restore a main drain line safely and efficiently. \n\nFirst, inspect the main drain for blockages or damage. Find the cleanout access and clear the area\u2014move anything in the way and make sure it\u2019s safe to work. This usually takes about 1 to 2 hours.\n\nNext, use a drain snake or similar tool to clear any clogs. If the pipe is damaged, carefully cut out the bad section. Collect all debris and dispose of it properly. This step can take 3 to 4 hours.\n\nNow, it\u2019s time to repair. Measure and cut new 4-inch PVC pipe to fit. Use PVC couplings and primer and cement to join the new pipe to the old. Make sure all connections are tight and the pipe is straight. This part takes 4 to 5 hours.\n\nFinally, flush the system to check for leaks. Make sure water drains smoothly. Restore the area and double-check that everything meets local plumbing codes. This last step takes about an hour.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
