        "Ever wondered how to fix a broken drain pipe without calling a pro? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to repair a broken PVC drain pipe step by step. \n\nFirst, find the damaged pipe. Turn off the water supply and check how much pipe needs replacing. \n\nNext, cut out the broken section using a saw or pipe cutter. Make sure your cuts are straight and the edges are smooth. Clean up the area so it\u2019s ready for the new pipe.\n\nNow, measure and cut your new PVC pipe to fit. Dry-fit the pipe, couplings, and elbow to make sure everything lines up. Use PVC primer and cement on all joints, then connect the new pipe and fittings. Secure the pipe with hangers or straps so it won\u2019t move.\n\nTurn the water back on and check for leaks. If everything looks good, patch up any surfaces you had to open up.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
