      transcript:
        "Want a lush, green lawn fast? Here\u2019s how to remove old sod and install new grass the right way. In this video, you\u2019ll learn the step-by-step process, what materials you need, and how long each step takes.\n\nFirst, mark out your area and clear away any debris. Use a sod cutter or shovel to remove the old grass and weeds. Rake the soil until it\u2019s smooth and even\u2014this takes about 4 to 6 hours for 1,000 square feet.\n\nNext, loosen the topsoil and mix in compost or soil conditioner. Level the area to help your new sod grow strong and drain well. This step takes 2 to 3 hours.\n\nNow, lay your fresh sod rolls tightly together in a staggered pattern. Press the seams and trim the edges for a perfect fit. Use a roller to make sure the sod touches the soil everywhere. This part takes another 4 to 6 hours.\n\nFinally, water the new sod deeply and keep it moist for the first day. Avoid walking on it while it settles\u2014about 12 hours of care.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
