      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to safely wire a breaker panel and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn the step-by-step process to wire a breaker panel like a pro. \n\nFirst, always start by shutting off the main power supply. Double-check with a voltage tester to make sure there\u2019s no electricity flowing. Set up safety barriers and gather your tools. Review your local electrical codes before you begin.\n\nNext, plan your panel layout. Decide where each circuit will go and label your breakers. Route your wires through the panel knockouts, using clamps to secure the cables. Make sure each wire is long enough to reach its breaker or bus bar.\n\nNow, strip the insulation from your wires. Connect each branch circuit wire to its breaker. Attach the neutral and ground wires to their bus bars. Tighten all terminals and double-check every connection to meet code.\n\nInspect your work. Install the panel cover and label each breaker clearly. Schedule an official inspection if your area requires it.\n\nFinally, restore the main power. Test each circuit to make sure everything works and all breakers function properly. Fix any issues right away to keep your home safe.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
