      embedUrl:
        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/soundproof-ceiling-installation/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Want to block out noise from above? Here\u2019s how to install a soundproof ceiling step by step. \n\nIn this video, you\u2019ll learn how to soundproof a ceiling using acoustic insulation, resilient channels, and special drywall. Let\u2019s get started.\n\nFirst, clear the room and cover your floors and furniture. Gather all your materials: acoustic insulation batts, resilient channels, soundproof drywall, acoustic sealant, drywall screws, joint compound, and joint tape.\n\nStep one: Fit acoustic insulation batts tightly between the ceiling joists. Make sure there are no gaps\u2014this is key to stopping sound.\n\nStep two: Attach resilient channels perpendicular to the joists. These metal strips help break the path of vibration, so sound doesn\u2019t travel through the structure.\n\nStep three: Hang your soundproof drywall onto the channels. Use drywall screws to secure it. Then, seal every seam and the edges with acoustic caulk. This keeps sound from sneaking through cracks.\n\nFinish by taping and mudding the joints, just like regular drywall. Let it dry, and you\u2019re done!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
