        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/window-condensation-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Tired of foggy windows and water stains? Let\u2019s fix window condensation for good. In this video, you\u2019ll learn how to repair condensation issues step by step, so your windows stay clear and dry. \n\nFirst, assess and prepare the area. Inspect each window for condensation. Look for fog between the panes or water on the glass. Move any curtains or furniture out of the way so you have space to work.\n\nNext, clean and dry the window surfaces. Wipe down the glass and frames with a dry cloth. If there\u2019s any dirt or mold, use a mild cleaner. Make sure everything is completely dry before moving on. This helps prevent mold from coming back.\n\nNow, seal and improve ventilation. Apply weatherstripping or caulk around the window edges to block out moisture. If you have a broken insulated glass unit, replace it with a new one. Use glazing tape or sealant, setting blocks, and caulk to install the new glass. Finally, improve airflow by using a dehumidifier or installing an exhaust fan nearby. This helps stop condensation from returning.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
