        "https://contractorplus.app/resources/contractor-costs/stone-fireplace-repair/national-average",
      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to bring an old stone fireplace back to life? Today, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to repair a stone fireplace so it looks and works like new. \n\nFirst, assess the fireplace. Look for cracks, loose stones, or crumbling mortar. Clear the area and cover nearby surfaces to protect them from dust. Gather your tools: chisel, brush, mortar mix, replacement stones, firebrick, lath, fasteners, and masonry sealer.\n\nNext, carefully remove any damaged mortar and loose stones with your chisel and brush. Mix fresh mortar according to the instructions. Reset the stones and fill the joints, making sure everything is level and matches the rest of the fireplace. If you need to replace firebricks, do that now.\n\nLet the mortar cure for a few hours. Once it\u2019s set, gently clean the stone surfaces to remove any leftover mortar. Dispose of debris and tidy up the area.\n\nFinally, inspect your work. Make sure all stones are secure and the fireplace looks great. Touch up any spots if needed, and apply masonry sealer for extra protection.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
