      transcript:
        "Did you know a broken garage door spring can leave you stuck at home? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to safely replace garage door extension springs step by step. \n\nFirst, safety is key. Disconnect your garage door opener and clamp the door in place so it can\u2019t move. Put on gloves and safety glasses. Gather your new extension springs, safety cables, mounting hardware, and some lubricant.\n\nNext, release the tension from the old springs. Carefully detach the safety cables, then remove the old springs from both sides of the door. Take your time\u2014springs are under tension and can be dangerous.\n\nNow, install the new extension springs. Attach them to the brackets, then thread the safety cables through the springs and secure them. Double-check that all hardware is tight and everything is lined up.\n\nRemove the clamps. Manually open and close the door to check the balance. If the door feels heavy or uneven, adjust the spring tension until it moves smoothly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
