      transcript:
        "Did you know a simple tree checkup can save you thousands in damage? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to do a full tree health assessment, step by step. \n\nFirst, start with a visual inspection. Spend about 20 minutes looking for dead branches, odd leaf colors, pests, or signs of disease. Check for cracks or wounds on the bark. \n\nNext, move to soil and root evaluation. Use a soil test kit and a moisture meter. Check if the soil is too dry, too wet, or compacted. Look for exposed or damaged roots, and watch for signs of root rot or roots circling the trunk. \n\nFinally, assess the canopy and trunk. Inspect the trunk for cavities, fungal growth, or deep cracks. Look up at the canopy\u2014does it look full and even, or are there bare spots and thinning? \n\nTake notes and photos for your report. This whole process takes about an hour and a half per tree. \n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
