      transcript:
        "Ever wondered how to stop your toilet tank from leaking at the base? Today, I\u2019ll show you how to install a toilet tank to bowl, step by step. \n\nFirst, unpack your toilet tank and bowl. Check for any cracks or damage. Make sure you have all the hardware: a gasket kit, tank bolts and washers, brass nuts, and plumber\u2019s putty or sealant.\n\nNext, place the rubber gasket onto the flush valve outlet on the bottom of the tank. This gasket is what keeps water from leaking between the tank and bowl, so make sure it sits flat and snug.\n\nNow, set the tank onto the bowl. Line up the holes. Insert the bolts with washers from inside the tank, through the bowl, and secure them underneath with brass nuts. Tighten the nuts evenly, a little at a time, switching sides. Don\u2019t over-tighten\u2014just enough to keep the tank steady and level.\n\nReconnect the water supply line. Turn the water back on and let the tank fill. Check for leaks around the bolts and gasket. If you see drips, tighten the nuts just a bit more.\n\nThat\u2019s it! Your toilet tank is now secure and leak-free. If you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
