        "Want to install an aluminum window like a pro and avoid costly mistakes? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to remove an old window and install a new aluminum unit safely and securely.\n\nFirst, remove the old window. Carefully pry out the trim, unscrew the fasteners, and lift out the window. Clean the opening and check for any damage. Make sure the rough opening is level and meets your local building codes.\n\nNext, set your new aluminum window frame in place. Use shims to get it perfectly level and square. Secure the frame with screws or anchors\u2014usually about 12 fasteners for a standard window. Double-check that everything is plumb and square before moving on.\n\nNow, seal and finish. Apply insulation around the frame. Use flashing tape along the edges to keep out water. Run a bead of exterior caulk around the window to seal it tight. Install your interior and exterior trim, then clean the glass and your work area.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
