        "Ever wondered how to replace a well pressure tank without calling a pro? In this video, you'll learn step-by-step how to install a new well tank safely and correctly. \n\nFirst, turn off power to the well pump. Drain the old tank, disconnect all plumbing and electrical lines, and carefully remove the old tank from its spot. \n\nNext, set your new well pressure tank\u201440 to 60 gallons\u2014on a solid, level concrete pad. Use a tank tee kit to connect the inlet and outlet pipes. Install the pressure gauge, relief valve, and ball valve. Wrap all threaded fittings with PTFE thread seal tape to prevent leaks. Attach flexible 1-inch pipe as needed, and make sure all connections are tight and meet local codes.\n\nNow, restore power and fill the tank. Check every joint for leaks. Adjust the pressure switch if needed, and make sure the system cycles on and off correctly. Clean up your work area and dispose of the old tank and materials properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
