      transcript:
        "Want to make your basement warmer, drier, and ready for new floors? Watch how to install a basement subfloor step by step. \n\nFirst, clear out your basement and sweep the floor. Lay down a 6 mil poly vapor barrier to block moisture\u2014overlap the seams and tape them tight. Let it settle flat.\n\nNext, measure and cut pressure-treated lumber for your framing. Lay out sleepers or a grid system across the floor. Use a level to make sure everything is even. Secure the framing to the concrete with Tapcon screws.\n\nNow, add insulation between the framing\u2014rigid foam or mineral wool works best. Place your 3/4-inch tongue and groove subfloor panels on top, staggering the seams. Use construction adhesive and screws to lock them down tight.\n\nFinally, seal all seams and edges with adhesive or tape. Double-check for levelness and make any needed adjustments. Clean up your workspace\u2014now you\u2019re ready for flooring!\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
