      transcript:
        "Want to give your home a fresh, finished look? Replacing trim is easier than you think! In this video, I\u2019ll show you step-by-step how to remove old trim and install new baseboards or casing like a pro.\n\nFirst, carefully pry off the old trim with a pry bar and utility knife. Take your time to avoid damaging your walls or floors. Remove all nails and clean up any debris.\n\nNext, measure each wall where you\u2019ll install new trim. Mark your new trim pieces and cut them to size with a miter saw. Dry fit each piece to make sure everything lines up perfectly.\n\nNow, attach the new trim to the wall using finishing nails or a nail gun. Make sure each piece is level and the joints are tight. Fill any nail holes or seams with wood filler.\n\nFor the finishing touches, sand the filled areas smooth. Caulk along the edges for a seamless look, then paint or stain your trim as you like. Finally, clean up your work area and dispose of the old trim properly.\n\nIf you liked this video, I appreciate the like and follow. If you're a contractor, come check out Contractor Plus. We've built the ultimate operating system for build and service contractors. Thanks for watching!",
